{Nigel Davies: 'In the early 1960s Bobby Fischer experimented with the Black side of the Ruy Lopez. He played a few games with the Classical defence 3...Bc5 and in the 1963 US championship adopted the so-called 'Norwegian Variation' with 3...a6 4 Ba4 b5 5 Bb3 Na5. Fischer was probably attracted to this line by the fact that it gains the two bishops. But meanwhile he loses time and White gains the ascendancy in the center...'} 1. Nf3 Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. g3 d5 4. Bg2 Be7 5. O-O O-O 6. d4 Nbd7 7. Nbd2 { 8.f7 f7 9.d5 +-  8.f7 f7 9.d5 +- Nigel Davies: 'ChessBase: ' 8.f7 f7 9.d5 +-''} b6 $1 {Nigel Davies: 'White was threatening 8.Bxf7+ followed by 9.Qd5+, picking up the rook on a8.'} (7... c6 8. Re1 b6 9. e4 dxe4 (9... Bb7 10. e5 Ne8 11. cxd5 cxd5 12. Bf1) 10. Ng5 Bb7 11. Ngxe4 Rb8 12. Nc3 Rc8 13. Nf3 c5 14. d5) 8. b3 $2 {Nigel Davies: 'After this Black gets ...d7-d5 in when his two bishops become quite dangerous.'} (8. cxd5 exd5 9. Ne5 Bb7 10. Ndf3 (10. Ndc4 Ne4 11. Qc2 f6 12. Bxe4 dxe4 13. Ng4 f5 14. Nge5 Nxe5 15. dxe5 Qd5) 10... c5 11. b3 (11. dxc5 bxc5) 11... a5 {was fine for Black in Emms - Yuneev, Leningrad 1990} {Nigel Davies: 'The attempt to refute Black's play with'} 12. Bb2 $6 {Nigel Davies: 'is refuted by'} Ne4 13. Rc1 Re8 $1 {White's best move is probably} 14. Nxd7 Qxd7 15. Ne5 Qe6 16. Nd3 Bd6 17. dxc5 bxc5 18. e3 a4) 8... Bb7 9. Bb2 c5 10. e3 Rc8 $1 11. Ne5 cxd4 $1 12. exd4 Rc7 13. Qe2 {Nigel Davies: 'The bishop looks badly placed on this square because its activity is inhibited by the pawn on e5.'} Qa8 14. f4 (14. Rfe1 {(Lind - Ernst, Karlskrona 1983) and now} dxc4 {looks fairly equal.} 15. Bxb7 Qxb7 16. bxc4 Nxe5 17. dxe5 Nd7) 14... dxc4 $1 15. Bxb7 (15. bxc4 Bxg2 16. Qxg2 $2 {Nigel Davies: 'is answered by'} Qxg2+ $16 {Euwe Euwe Nigel Davies: 'ChessBase: '' ChessBase: 'Euwe''} {Nigel Davies: 'Euwe has suggested'} 17. Kxg2 {Nigel Davies: 'so as to meet'} Nxe5 {Nigel Davies: 'with'} 18. fxe5 $1 $16 {Euwe Euwe Nigel Davies: '!' '!' Nigel Davies: 'when Black is in a bind because of the difficulties he will have contesting the dark squares (notably c5).' Nigel Davies: 'when Black is in a bind because of the difficulties he will have contesting the dark squares (notably c5). ChessBase: '!' ChessBase: 'Euwe''} Ng4 19. Rf3 Bg5 20. Ne4 { d5=} {White should prefer simply} Rxc4 21. Nxg5 Rc2+ 22. Kh3 h5) 15... Qxb7 16. bxc4 b5 $1 17. c5 (17. Rab1 $1 $40 {Kmoch} bxc4 {Nigel Davies: '??' '??'} 18. Ba3 $19 {Nigel Davies: 'wins the queen.' Nigel Davies: 'wins the queen. ChessBase: '-+''} {Nigel Davies: 'In this position'} Nb6 {Nigel Davies: 'can be answered by'} 19. Bxe7 {Nigel Davies: 'as White is not ready to play Re1+. But now Black takes the initiative on the queenside.'} Rxe7 20. Ndxc4 $15 {  ×b2b3} {Nigel Davies: 'Simply'} Qa6 $142 {Nigel Davies: 'would also have been an improvement on Addison's choice as' Nigel Davies: 'would also have been an improvement on Addison's choice as ChessBase: '''}) 17... Nxc5 18. dxc5 (18. Rfc1) 18... Bxc5+ 19. Rf2 Bxf2+ $1 20. Qxf2 Rc2 { 21... h4 22.h2 g3 23.fg c4 nebst 24... d3+ Euwe  21... h4 22.h2 g3 23.fg c4 nebst 24... d3+ Euwe Nigel Davies: 'Threatening 21... h4 22.Bh2 g3 23.fg c4 followed by 24... d3+.' Nigel Davies: 'Threatening 21... h4 22.Bh2 g3 23.fg c4 followed by 24... d3+. ChessBase: ' 21... h4 22.h2 g3 23.fg c4 nebst 24... d3+ Euwe''} 21. Qd4 (21. Bd4 $1 Ne4 22. Nxe4 Rxf2 $15 {Kmoch} 23. Nxf2 $2 Rd8) 21... Qb6 $1 22. Qxb6 axb6 23. Bc1 Rd8 24. Nf1 (24. Nef3 Rd3 25. Ne5 Rd5 $18 26. Nef3 $2 Ne4 $19 {Nigel Davies: 'But after'} 27. Kf1 (27. Nxe4 $19 {Nigel Davies: 'After'} Rd1+ {Nigel Davies: 'Black can just play'}) 27... Rdxd2 28. Bxd2 Nxd2+ 29. Nxd2 Rxd2 $17 {Kmoch} 30. h4 $145 {Nigel Davies: 'ChessBase: 'RR''} Rh2 31. Kg1 {Nigel Davies: 'White's game falls apart.'} Rb2) 24... Rd1 $1 25. Bb2 Rxa1 26. Bxa1 { 27.fd2  27.fd2 Nigel Davies: 'ChessBase: ' 27.fd2''} Rxa2 $1 {Nigel Davies: 'Before White has time to play 27.Nfd2'} 27. Bd4 Nd5 $1 { f5  f5 Nigel Davies: 'The winning move. Black is going to play ... Nf5, winning the h4 pawn.' Nigel Davies: 'The winning move. Black is going to play ... Nf5, winning the h4 pawn. ChessBase: ' f5''} 28. Nf3 b4 29. N1d2 Kf8 30. Kf1 Rc2 31. Ke1 f6 32. Kd1 Rc8 33. Ke2 Ke7 34. Kd3 Kd7 { 35... g5  35... g5 Nigel Davies: 'ChessBase: ' 35... g5''} 35. Nc4 b5 36. Na5 Nc3 37. Nd2 Kd6 38. Nb7+ (38. Ne4+ {Nigel Davies: 'is met by'} Nxe4 $1 39. Kxe4 Rc2 { 23.de4, 24.fd2} 40. h4 $4 f5+ 41. Ke3 Kd5 42. Bxg7 $19 Ra2 43. Nb3 (43. Nb7 Ra7) 43... Ra3) 38... Kc6 {Nigel Davies: 'After'} 39. Nc5 Kd5 40. Nd7 Na4 {Mit einem gewonnenem Endspiel. Euwe Mit einem gewonnenem Endspiel. Euwe Nigel Davies: 'Black has a winning endgame according to Euwe' Nigel Davies: 'Black has a winning endgame according to Euwe ChessBase: 'Mit einem gewonnenem Endspiel. Euwe''} 0-1

