{Bobby Fischer: 'GAME N. 34 Hanging pawns unhung. Classical theory expounds the danger of "hanging Pawns," but Fischer demonstrates here, in a revolutionary manner, that they are just as often an asset as a liability. Bertok's errors seem insignificant, yet he drifts into a passive position. On the verge of exploiting Black's loose center, he always lacks just the one tempo needed to do so. Meanwhile, using the open b-file as a base of operations, Fischer manages to force White into a defensive posture. In the midst of this Q-side tension, the winning move (21...g5) comes unexpectedly on the opposite wing. '} 1. e4 {Bobby Fischer Bobby Fischer Konikowski Bobby Fischer} e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Bb4 {Charousek,R; Petrosian,T Bobby Fischer: '; A refinement attributed to Petrosian, but actually played by Charousek in the 'nineties - and probably dating back even farther. '} 4. e5 {Bobby Fischer: ', White, having no other good waiting move, is obliged to develop, thus restricting his option of playing this Knight to e2.'} c5 5. Bd2 {Bobby Fischer: ', Back to the main line. The shadow boxing is over. '} Ne7 6. a3 Bxc3 {Bobby Fischer: '; Petrosian usually omits this move (see note to Black's 8th). '} 7. Bxc3 b6 {Tartakover,S Bobby Fischer: '; Tartakover's Defense. '} 8. b4 {Bobby Fischer: ', The best procedure, opening the c-file and preparing Rc1 with pressure on Black's c-pawn.'} Qc7 9. Nf3 cxb4 10. Bxb4 Ba6 {Bobby Fischer: '; The text is drawish, but I had already clinched first prize. '} 11. Bd3 Bxd3 $1 {Bobby Fischer: '; The right post. At b7 this Bishop would block the b-file and obstruct later operations there. '} 12. cxd3 Nbc6 13. Rc1 $2 {Bobby Fischer: ', Producing hanging center Pawns which, in this case, exert a tremendously cramping influence on White's future development.'} Qd7 14. Bd6 Rc8 $1 15. O-O Nf5 16. Rc3 {Bobby Fischer: ', What else is there? Black's center is well-prutected, and he is ready to assume the Q-side initiative with ... a5 and ...Qb4. ' Bobby Fischer: ', What else is there? Black's center is well-prutected, and he is ready to assume the Q-side initiative with ... a5 and ...Qb4. ' Bobby Fischer: ', What else is there? Black's center is well-prutected, and he is ready to assume the Q-side initiative with ... a5 and ...Qb4. ' Konikowski: '?!'} Nxd6 17. exd6 O-O 18. Qc2 Na5 19. Rc7 $2 Rxc7 $1 20. dxc7 Rc8 21. Rc1 f6 $1 $19 {Bobby Fischer: '!' Bobby Fischer: '; Practically forcing the win of a piece. ' Bobby Fischer: '!' Bobby Fischer: '; Practically forcing the win of a piece. ' Bobby Fischer: '!' Bobby Fischer: '; Practically forcing the win of a piece. ' Konikowski: '!'} 22. a4 {Bobby Fischer: ', To break the hammer-lock.'} Nb7 23. g4 Nd6 {Bobby Fischer: '; Black has some temporary discomfort but it's only a matter of time before he consolidates and wins with his extra piece. '} ({Bobby Fischer: 'if'} 23... Kf7 $2) 24. Qc6 {Bobby Fischer: ', Blundering a Pawn.'} Qxc6 $1 {Bobby Fischer: '; Threatening mate. '} 25. Rxc6 Ne8 {Konikowski: '-+'} 26. Rxe6 Kf7 27. Rc6 Rxc7 28. Rxc7+ Nxc7 29. Kf1 a5 {Bobby Fischer: '; Sealing the g-file and neutralizing all threats. '} 30. Ke2 Ne6 31. Ke3 Ke7 {Bobby Fischer: '; White resigns.'} 32. Nd2 Kd6 {Bobby Fischer: 'The lesser evil is'} 33. Nb1 $142 Kc6 34. Nc3 $19 {Bobby Fischer: 'but White is still lost if Black exercises a modicum of caution.'} {Bobby Fischer: 'Not'} Nc7 $2 35. h4 {Bobby Fischer: 'On'} h6 36. h5 b5 37. axb5+ $19 {Bobby Fischer: 'is crushing.' Bobby Fischer: 'is crushing.' Bobby Fischer: 'is crushing.' Konikowski: ''} {Bobby Fischer: 'The following variation gives some insight into the nature of White's problem:'} Nxb5 38. Na4 Nd6 39. Nc3 Nb5 40. Na4 Nd6 41. Nc3 f5 42. f3 $1 (42. Kf4 fxg4 43. Ke5 $1 Nb5 44. Na4 (44. Nxd5 a4 {Konikowski: 'Fischer'} 45. Nb4+ Kd7 $10 {Bobby Fischer: 'etc.)'}) 44... Na3 45. Kf5 Nc2 46. Kg6 {Konikowski: '-+'} Nxd4 47. Kxg7 Nf5+ 48. Kg6 $19 {Bobby Fischer: 'wins.'} {Bobby Fischer: 'if'} g3 49. fxg3 Nxg3 50. Kxh6 $19 {Bobby Fischer: 'wins.'} {Bobby Fischer: 'Best is'} d4 $142 51. Kg6 Nxh5 52. Kxh5 $1 Kb5 $1 53. Nb2 a4 54. Nxa4 Kxa4 55. Kg4 Kb3 {Bobby Fischer: 'with good drawing chances.'} {Bobby Fischer: '(if 24'} 56. Kf4 Kc2 57. Ke4 Kc3) 42... fxg4 43. fxg4 Nb5 44. Na4 Kd6 45. Nc5 $19 {Bobby Fischer: 'and White, completely tied up, must lose material.'} Ke7 {Konikowski} 46. Kf4 $19 {Bobby Fischer: 'if'} Nxd4 47. Ke5 Nc2 48. Kxd5 $1 Ne3+ 49. Kc6 Kf6 50. d4 Kg5 51. d5 $1 Kxg4 52. d6 Nc4 53. d7 {Bobby Fischer: 'White's game is already difficult, e.g.,'} Ne5+ 54. Kb5 Nxd7 55. Nxd7 Kxh5 56. Kxa5 Kg4 57. Ne5+ Kg3 0-1

