1. Nf3 {Postny,E} Nf6 2. g3 b5 3. Bg2 Bb7 4. O-O e6 5. d3 d5 6. Nbd2 Be7 7. e4 O-O 8. Qe2 c5 9. Re1 Nc6 10. c3 (10. e5 Nd7 11. Nf1 $5) 10... a5 11. exd5 (11. e5 Nd7 12. Nf1 {is just a transposition.} {A picturesque mate can be seen after} b4 $4 13. h4 a4 14. a3) 11... exd5 (11... Nxd5 12. Ne4 $1 $16 h6 $40) 12. d4 (12. Nf1 Re8 13. Bg5) 12... Qb6 $6 13. dxc5 $1 (13. Nb3 c4 14. Nc5 Bxc5 15. dxc5 Qxc5 16. Be3 Qd6 17. Nd4 Nxd4 18. Bxd4) 13... Bxc5 14. Nb3 Rfe8 {Postny,E: 'is just a transposition.'} 15. Qc2 (15. Qf1 b4 {White has a strong, long-lasting initiative for the sacrificed material. It is important that Black's king lost its right to castle.}) 15... d4 16. Qf5 $2 {The wrong place for the queen.} (16. Nxc5 Qxc5 17. Bg5 Nd5 {[%cal Ge4d6] White wins a piece back with a continuing initiative.} 18. Rxe8+ $2 Rxe8 19. Rc1 dxc3 $18 {[%cal Gd5e7]} 20. bxc3 $2) (16. Rxe8+ Rxe8 17. cxd4 Nxd4 18. Nbxd4 $2 (18. Qxc5 Nxf3+ 19. Bxf3 Re1+ 20. Kg2 Bxf3+ 21. Kxf3 {½-½ Sakharov,Y-Bannik,A/Kiev 1963/EXT 2003} Qb7+ $1) 18... Bxd4 19. Bf4) 16... Rxe1+ 17. Nxe1 Re8 18. Nf3 (18. Bg5 {Black is completely tied up.} Re5) (18. Bf4 Bf8 19. Nxd4 $1 Nxd4 20. cxd4 Bxg2 21. Nxg2 Qxd4 22. Qxb5) 18... Bd6 19. Bg5 (19. Nbxd4 Nxd4 20. cxd4 Be4 21. Qg5 Qb7) 19... Ne4 (19... dxc3 20. Bxf6 gxf6 21. Qxf6 Re6 22. Qxc3 b4) 20. Re1 (20. Nbxd4 Nxd4 21. Nxd4 (21. cxd4 $18 {The point of 16.h5. 1-0 Kolpakov,M-Nikitin,A/Moscow 1963/EXT 99 (27)} g6 22. Qd7 Bc6 23. Qh3) 21... Re5 $19 {0-1 Rotstein,J-Sakharov,Y/Kiev 1963/EXT 2003 (35)} (21... Bc8 22. Qxb5 Qxb5 23. Nxb5) 22. Qd7 $1) 20... Ne7 {White has not enough resources to harass the black king.} 21. Bxe7 (21. Qd7 Bc6) 21... g6 22. Qh3 dxc3 23. Rxe4 (23. Bxd6 Qxf2+ 24. Kh1 $2 Qxe1+ 25. Nxe1 Nf2+ 26. Kg1 Nxh3+ 27. Bxh3 Rxe1+ 28. Kf2 cxb2) 23... cxb2 24. Re1 Rxe7 25. Rb1 a4 (25... Re2 26. Nfd4) 26. Nbd4 Bxf3 27. Nxf3 Re2 $138 28. Rf1 $1 Rxf2 29. Qc8+ Kg7 30. Qc3+ f6 0-1

