{ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'GAME N. 39 The confrontation. This dramatic meeting between the generations took place on board I after it was rumored that Botvinnik would be given a "rest day" against the American team. But it was fated that Fischer, at last, albeit with Black, would have a crack at the world champion. Walking into a prepared variation, Fischer promptly refutes it. "The reader can guess that my equanimity was wrecked", confesses Botvinnik, whose notes are incorporated here. Nervously, he proceeds to run his still tenable position downhill. But Fischer, instead of nursing his winning advantage, simplifies too quickly and reaches an adjournment where victory is problematical. After a sleepless night of analysis, Botvinnik finds a stunning defense. Fischer engages in a seemingly harmless transposition of moves (51...b5), and falls into a pit - throwing away the win he maintains was still there. ''} 1. c4 {ChessBase ChessBase ChessBase ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer'} g6 2. Nc3 Bg7 3. d4 d6 {"Die Eingebung des Augenblicks. Ich konnte am Leuchten seiner Augen erkennen, daß er für mein Königsindisch gut gerüstet war", schreibt Fischer in seiner berühmten Partiensammlung "My 60 Memorable Games". ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: '; The spur of the moment. I could see by the glint in his eye that he had come well anned for my King's Indian. ''} 4. e4 Nf6 5. f3 {ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: ', The main line, but I don't believe this early development of the Queen can give White anything. ''} O-O 6. Be3 a6 7. Qd2 c6 {Eine deutliche Kampfansage! Die Smyslov-Variante führt in der Regel zu sehr kompliziertem Spiel. Schwarz vermeidet Vereinfachungen und versucht, mit seinen Leichtfiguren Druck auf das weiße Zentrum auszuüben.} 8. Bd3 (8. O-O-O) 8... b5 {ChessBase: 'Smyslov,V' ChessBase: 'Smyslov,V Bobby Fischer: '; Smyslov's Variation. '' Smyslov,V} (8... e5 $1 {!}) 9. Nge2 (9. cxb5 axb5 10. b4 Nbd7 11. Nge2 Nb6 12. O-O Be6 13. a3 Bc4 14. Bc2 Bxe2 15. Qxe2 Nc4) 9... Nbd7 10. O-O (10. Rc1 Rb8 $10 {ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'draws.'' =} (10... e5 11. d5 b4 12. Nd1 c5 $1 {!} 13. g4 h5 14. Nf2) {Damit setzt eine Serie von Schachgeboten ein, die das Ziel haben, den schwarzen König auf schlechte Felder zu drängen. Verlieren würde ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'if''} 11. cxb5 axb5 12. O-O e5 $19 {ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'wins.''} {ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'if''} 13. Rfd1 Bb7 $1 {!} 14. b3 Qe7 15. Bg5 Rfd8 16. Re1 Qf8 17. Bb1 h6 {mit einer theoretischen Remisstellung, Botvinnik ChessBase: '=' '=' '=' ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'leads to a theoretical draw.'' = Botvinnik} 18. Bh4) 10... Rb8 (10... Bb7 $1 {!} 11. cxb5 (11. b3 Rc8 (11... e5 $2 {ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'loses to''} 12. d5 $1 $18 {ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: '!''} {ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'not''} b4 $2 {?} 13. Nd1 $1 {, und der weiße Bauer zieht mit Schach ein: ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'and White queens with check''} c5 14. g4 Kh8 15. Nf2 {ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'or''} Ng8 $2 {?} 16. Ng3) 12. Rab1 e6 13. Nd1 Qc7 14. Nf2 $10 {Fischer ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: '=' Bobby Fischer: 'etc.'' = Botvinnik}) 11... axb5 12. b4 $1 {!}) 11. cxb5 axb5 $1 {!} 12. b4 Nb6 13. a4 {Weiß ist gezwungen, seine Bauernstellung zu schwächen.} bxa4 14. Nxa4 {ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: ', Opening the diagonal for Black's KB can't be right, but White is still striving for an opening advantage.''} Nxa4 15. Rxa4 {'passed pawn'} Bd7 $1 {!} 16. Ra5 Qb6 17. Rb1 { "Als ich mich auf den Kampf mit Smyslov vorbereitete, stellte ich natürlich gründliche Analysen der Smyslov-Variante im allgemeinen und der Diagrammstellung im besonderen an! Hier sah ich, daß die schwarze Dame in Gefahr gerät, gleichgültig, ob sie nach h4 oder f5 geht", schreibt Botvinnik und unterstreicht seine Aussage mit den Varianten 17...h4 18.c2 g5 19.d4! bzw. 17...f5 18.b4 a5 19.d4 und der Drohung 20.g4. ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: '"When I was preparing to meet Smyslov, I, of course, made a thorough analysis of the Smyslov System in general and of the position on the diagram in particular! Here I reckoned that whether the Black Queen went to h4 or f5, it would be in danger; for example,' Bobby Fischer: 'Or''} {ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Alas, my opponent found a third continuation!" (BOTVINNIK.) ''} Rfc8 $1 {Diese einfache Möglichkeit hatte Botvinnik nicht berücksichtigt. Trotzdem besteht für ihn vorerst kein Grund zur Panik. Für den verlorengehenden Bauern erhält er Vorposten auf d6 und c7 sowie ein lebendiges Figuenspiel. ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: '; "A very unpleasant surprise - now White really had to start playing. UP to here I had only had to remember my analysis, though that was not so easy. I had a recollection of the Black Queen being trapped somewhere on the K-side; and following this track I managed to recall the whole variation. At last everything was in order - on the board was the familiar position; then suddenly it was obvious that in my analysis I had missed what Fischer had found with the greatest of ease at the board. The reader can guess that my equanimity was wrecked. However, if you assess 17...Qxf4 from an objective point of view, then although it is the best way out for Black, as you will see from what comes later, his position is still difficult." (BOTVINNIK.) When I made this move, I felt sure he had overlooked it. '' !} 18. Nc3 ({ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Here I break camp with Botvinnik, only to meet at the next diagram. He gives''} 18. d5 {ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'overlooking that White can obtain an immediate draw with''}) 18... Qd8 19. Qa2 Be6 20. Qa3 d5 21. e5 ({ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'if''} 21. Ba6 {?} Rc7 22. Bf4 Nh5 23. Bxc7 Bxd4+ $19 {ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'and White is bombarded with checks which lead to probable mate, certainly win of material.''} {ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'if''} 24. Kh1 {?} Qxc7 $19 {ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'wins.''}) 21... Nd7 {ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: '; "So Black has won a Pawn; but the Knight on c7 and the Pawn on d6 confine his Rooks - and also, White has two Bishops. The first thing White must do is complete his development." (BOTVINNIK.) ''} 22. Na4 Bf5 {ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: '; "A bad mistake; evidently, Black overestimated his possibilities. Of course, he had to prepare the move ...Be5;''} {ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Now White has the two important squares d5 and c5 at his disposal and his spatial advantage becomes crushing." (BOTVINNIK.) Needless to add, I couldn't disagree more. Why should Black return the Pawn? ''} 23. Bxf5 gxf5 {'passed pawn'} 24. Ra6 $2 {Fischer und Botvinnik stimmen darin überein, daß dies der falsche Platz für den Läufer ist, aber bei der Stellungsbeurteilung nach dem richtigen c4 scheiden sich die Geister. ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: ', "Feeble play.'' ?} Rc7 $1 {ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: '; "Apparently, this forces the exchange of the Knight on c7,'' !} (24... Nb6 25. Nc5 (25. Nxb6 $2 Rxb6 $1 {wins.}) 25... Nc4 $19 {ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'wins.''} {not} 26. Qd3 $2 {(ChessBase) Bobby Fischer} e6) 25. Rc1 $2 {Nach diesem zweiten Fehler in Serie wird die weiße Lage schon hoffnungslos. ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: ', This really took me aback.''} Qc8 26. Ra5 e6 27. Bd2 Bf8 {ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: '; "The simplest.''} 28. f4 $19 {ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: ', Just leads to a dead lost ending.''} Kh8 (28... Nb6 $19 {ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'is decisive.''}) ({ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'if''} 28... f6 $2 {?}) 29. Nc5 Nxc5 (29... Nb6 30. Na6 Nc4 $1 {ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'is the pause that refreshes - White is checkless - if'' !} 31. Rxc4 dxc4 32. Nxb8 Qxb8 33. Ra8) 30. dxc5 Qd8 31. Qd3 Qd7 {Nahezu forciert hat sich diese Stellung nach den beiden Fehlern im 24. und 25.Zug ergebn. Der Minusbauer und die zerfledderte Bauernstellung machen die Lage des Anziehenden hoffnungslos, zumal (vorläufig) auch alle Übergänge in ein Turmendspiel aussichtslos sind.} 32. Rca1 $6 {Stellt auch noch den Läufer schlecht. ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: ', "A pointless move, since White cannot go into the lost Rook and Pawn ending;''} Rcb7 33. Ra8 Qc8 34. Rxb8 Qxb8 35. Qa3 Kg8 36. Qa4 {ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: ', "White's best practical chance consisted in an exchange of Rooks and a position with his King on d4 (or e3), his Bishop on c2 and his f-Pawn at f4. But all that is impossible.''} Qc7 37. Ra3 h6 38. Qa8 Rb8 {ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: '; "Before this I considered the game completely hopeless for me, but the text move gave me new heart; why had my opponent allowed my Bishop to get to a good post (and the only good one!) at c2?''} 39. Qa5 Qc8 40. Qa6 Be7 {ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: '; "In general terms, d6 is the best square for the King; for then the Knight would not need to defend the b-Pawn and Black would win by advancing his Q-side Pawns. But this maneuver is also not bad." (BOTVINNIK.) ''} (40... Qc7) 41. Qxc8+ { Nach und nach hat Schwarz die Stellung seiner Figuren optimiert und sollte nun am besten irgendeinen unverfänglichen Zug ins Kuvert geben.} Rxc8 $2 {ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: '; "Could have led to an innnediate draw - and just at the very moment \vhen Black was nearing his goal. You see, White was already in zugzwang: against a King move Black plays ...Kh4 and ...Ne6-f4(xh3); if Bb1, the reply ...Rd1 wins; and if the White Rook moves from its place, then ...Rc4 is decisive.''} {Stattdessen wählt Fischer den schwierigen Übergang ins Turmendspiel.} 42. Kf2 Kf8 43. Kf3 $6 {ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: ', "Natural and bad. White is now in danger of defeat again.'' 'passed pawn'} h5 {Noch immer ist sich Fischer offenbar keiner Gefahr bewußt und glaubt an einen leichten Sieg. ?} (43... Ke8) 44. Ke2 Kg7 {Noch eine Ungenauigkeit. Auf g5 steht der schwarze König später nicht gut, dem war mit 44...h6 und 45...g7 Abhilfe zu schaffen. ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: '; "His last chance consisted in improving the position of his King by the maneuver ...Kh6-g7." (BOTVINNIK.) ''} 45. Be1 { Hier wurde die Partie endlich abgebrochen. Wie es scheint, hat Schwarz bei beiderseits bestem Spiel keine Gewinnchancen mehr. Zudem darf man nicht vergessen, daß Botvinnik mit der sowjetischen Mannschaft das beste Analyseteam der Welt zur Seite stand, ganz zu schweigen von seinem eigenen riesigen Erfahrungsschatz. ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: ', "Here Black sealed a move.' Bobby Fischer: 'White's threat is to exchange a pair of Pawns on the Q-side by a5 (for example,' Bobby Fischer: 'The most subtle move was''} {ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'The game was officially "drawn" at breakfast. The Russian team had a table near the American team. Someone inquired of Botvinnik what he thought of the adjourned position. Hardly looking up from his plate, the world champion shrugged, "Nichia" (draw). The word quickly spread, and I overheard someone at the English table saying: "The Russians said Fischer could have won before adjournment..." ''} Kg6 46. Ra7 Bd8 47. Bc3 $1 {In Botvinniks Buch "Meine 25 interessantesten Endspiele" ist nachzulesen, daß Fischer später schrieb, diese Feinheit übersehen zu haben. Erstaunlich, behauptet Fischer doch in seiner ganze 16 Jahre vorher erschienenen Partiensammlung "Dies war die erste Verteidigung, die ich untersuchte!" ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: ', "A very fine idea, found during overnight analysis by Geller. Because if his bad King position Black finds it difficult to mobilize his connected passed Pawns." (BOTVINNIK.) This was the first defense I had considered!''} h4 48. Kd3 $1 {ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: ', I had analyzed mainly 48 f4+ but Botvinnik's line is best and also contains a sly trap. '' !} (48. Be1) (48. h3) 48... h3 49. gxh3 ({ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'or''} 49. g3) 49... Bh4 50. Ke2 {ChessBase: 'Botvinnik,M: ' ChessBase: 'Botvinnik,M:  Bobby Fischer: ', "The weakness of the g-Pawn and the a-Pawn gives White sufficient counterplay." (BOTVINNIK..) '' Botvinnik,M: } Bd8 51. Kf3 { Diese Stellung leitete eine Privatfehde zwischen Fischer und Botvinnik ein. Ist sie remis, oder (nach dem besten Zug 51...d4) für Schwarz gewonnen? 'passed pawn'} (51. Be1 {ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'is easy.''}) 51... Bh4 $2 {ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: '; Originally Botvinnik wrote in Chess Life: "This is a mistake in analysis.'' ?} {Zurück zur Partie. ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Now to return to the dreary (for me) game. ''} 52. Kg2 $1 $10 {Danach ist die Stellung remis, endlich kann Botvinnik zu gelösten Sticheleien übergehen. ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: '!' Bobby Fischer: ', "Now Black is left with two RP's and the draw becomes a question of theory." (BOTVINNIK.)''} Rd8 53. Kf3 (53. Rc7 Ra8 {'-+' Fischer} (53... d4 54. Bd2 Ra8)) 53... Rc8 {ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: '; Botvinnik visibly relaxed. I had played right into his hands. ''} 54. Ke2 Bd8 (54... f6 {!$19} {ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'if''} 55. Re7 {?} fxe5 {ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'or''} 56. Rxe6+ {?}) (54... Kg7 $2) 55. Be1 f6 56. Kf3 (56. exf6 {, und Schwarz kann nicht gewinnen = Kasparov} Bxf6 {?}) 56... fxe5 {Botvinnik: "Der Leser möge sich nicht wundern, daß das Spiel in einem theoretisch unentschiedenen Spielausgang so lange hinausgezögert wird. Es gibt Schachspieler, die sich nach einer von ihnen nicht erwarteten Wendung der Ereignisse nicht leicht umstellen können."} 57. fxe5 $1 {!} Rc7 58. Ra8 Bg5 59. Rg8+ Kh5 60. h4 Bh6 {ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: '; "Generally speaking, this ending would be drawn even without the f-Pawn - any textbook on the endgame will tell you this." (BOTVINNIK) ''} (60... Bc1 $19 {ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'wins.''} 61. Rh8+ $1 {Kasparov !} Kg6 62. h5+ Kg7 63. Ra8) (60... Bxh4 61. Rh8+) (60... Be7) 61. Rh8 (61. Re8 {ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'or''} Ra7 62. Rxe6 $1 {!} Ra3+) 61... Kg6 62. h5+ Kg7 (62... Kxh5 {verteidigen, der eleganteste Remisweg aber sei der vom 13jährigen Garri Kasparov (damals in Botvinniks legendärer Schachschule) gefundene [s.o.]. = Botvinnik} {ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'not''} 63. Bd2 $2 {?}) 63. Ra8 Bg5 64. Ra6 Rc8 (64... Kf7 65. b5 $3 {!!} cxb5 66. c6 $40 {"und der weiße König steht der kommenden Schachlawine schutzlos gegenüber." Diesmal blieb Botvinnik das letzte Wort vorbehalten. Zum einen könne sich Weiß mit ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'and White's King will be without shelter from the coming avalanche of checks.''}) 65. b5 cxb5 66. Rxe6 Bc1 (66... Kf7 67. Rg6 Be7 68. e6+ Kf8 { Diese Stellung hatte Botvinnik in seinen ersten Analysen ("nach beträchtlicher Seelenforschung", Fischer) mit remis abgetan. Der Amerikaner konterte mit ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Botvinnik also reached this position in his analysis independently, and concluded that it was a draw. However, it is precisely here, in this barren wilderness, that Black can wend his way to a win. Correct is''} 69. h6 $1 {!}) (66... Rxc5 67. Rg6+) 67. Bb4 (67. c6 Ba3 {Das Zwischenspiel ist beendet - Weiß hat keine Schachgebote mehr.}) 67... d4 68. Rg6+ {"Erst hier drückte mir Fischer die Hand mit einem Gesicht, das weiß wie die Wand war, und verließ mit nassen Augen den Saal", überschreitet Botvinnik zum Schluß die Grenze des Erträglichen. nach Angaben von Botvinnik und Fischer in Tischbierek "Sternstunden des Schachs, 30 x Olympia" Sportverlag 1993 ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: ', Drawn. " 'Too many mistakes?' the reader may justly ask. Yes, there were rather a lot!" (BOTVINNIK.) ''} Kh7 69. Rd6 $19 {ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'But even after''} Bb2 {ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: '!''} (69... Be3 70. c6 {ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: '!''} f4 71. e6 $1 {ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: '(finally Black has crawled up along the a-file)'' !}) 70. Rd7+ Kg8 (70... Kh6 $1 {!} 71. Bd2+ Kxh5 $1 {!} 72. Rd6 Rh8 $1 {!} 73. e6 (73. c6 $1 {Der schwarze König darf die b-Linie nicht betreten, damit Weiß keine Schachs von hinten geben kann. ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: '(the idea is to keep the King off the b-file so that White's Rook can't check from behind)'' !})) 71. e6 Bc3 72. e7 Re8 (72... Kf7 $19 {ChessBase: '-+' '-+' ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'transposes into the note to Black's 51st.''} 73. Rd8 Kxe7 {ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Was it really true that the adjourned position was lost? Was I mistaken?" (BOTVINNIK.) Botvinnik then went on to give a corrected analysis which, as we shall see, also falls short. 51...Kd4! 52.Rxg6 b5 53.h5 b4''} 74. Rxc8 $1 {ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: '(instead of his previous 54.Kg2)'' !} Bxb4 75. h6 {!}) 73. Rd8 Kf7 74. Rxe8 $10 {ChessBase: 'Botvinnik,M' ChessBase: 'Botvinnik,M Bobby Fischer: 'the White King reaches the Q-side and it is easy to credit the draw."'' = Botvinnik Botvinnik,M} {ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'if''} Kxe8 {ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'or 55 ...Kb3 then''} 75. c6 {ChessBase: ' h5-h6-h7-h8' ChessBase: ' h5-h6-h7-h8 Bobby Fischer: 'followed by h6-h7 is very strong)''  h5-h6-h7-h8} {Nach ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Later in the 1962 Russian Yearbook, he analyzed the entire ending more exhaustively and came to the conclusion, after considerable soulsearching, that it was drawn even against the best line:''} Bxb4 $1 {ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'The bracketed comments are mine. "'' !} 76. c7 {beginnt der Wettlauf der Bauern:} 1/2-1/2

