{ChessCalisthenics: 'C99: Closed Ruy Lopez: Chigorin Defence: 11 d4 Qc7 12 Nbd2 cxd4' Bobby Fischer: 'GAME N. 8 Meat and potatoes. Alekhine said, in his prime, that to wrest a point from him it was necessary to win the same rame three times: once at the beginning, once in the middle, once at the end. No less a tribute may be paid to Keres. Each phase of rhis game is fascinating and hard-fought. Even rhe errors. and there are more than a few. contribute to making it an unusually complete exhibition of two master craftsmen using all the tools of rheir trade. While perhaps unglamorous, there is meat here, and potatoes tao. And it is likely rhat as a result of rhls victory Fisd!er came to be regarded as a serious contender by the leading Soviet Grandmasters - thls was the first time he had defeated one. '} 1. e4 {ChessCalisthenics Bobby Fischer} e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 f5 4. Nc3 fxe4 5. Nxe4 d5 6. Nxe5 dxe4 7. Nxc6 Qg5 8. Qe2 Nf6 9. f4 Qxf4 10. d4 Qh4+ 11. g3 Qh3 12. Bg5 (12. Ne5+ $2 c6 13. Bc4 Be6 14. Bf4 Rd8 {Bobby Fischer: ', The second adjournment There are two technical obstacles facing White:  1) He Cannot exchange Bishops; the ending whore he is two Pawns ahead remains a theoretical draw with Rooks on the board.  2) He cannot exchange Rooks so long as Black's King has access to f6; the ending (even with two extra Pawns) is still a draw with Bishops on the board. '} 15. O-O-O Bd6 16. Rhe1 O-O $2 17. Qf1 $2 {Bobby Fischer: '; This slip is fatal. Keres told me he had reached this position in adjournment analysis, but had forgotten his drawing line-over-the-board.'} Qf5 $1 { g4  g4  g4 Bobby Fischer: ', Headed for g4.'} 18. Bd2 Nd5 19. Qg2 Bxe5 { 64.f7 f7 65.h5 Barcza} 20. dxe5 {? Barcza ? Barcza ChessCalisthenics: '?'} e3 {Bobby Fischer: ', White still can't afford to trade. '} 21. Bxe3 {? Barcza ? Barcza ChessCalisthenics: '??'} Nxe3 $1 22. Bxe6+ Qxe6 23. Rxe3 Qxa2 $1 $18 {Bobby Fischer: '!' Bobby Fischer: ', This makes all the difference. Black's King can no longer set up a blockade on f6. '} 24. Rxd8 Qa1+ 25. Kd2 Rxd8+ 26. Rd3 Rxd3+) (12. Nxa7+ Bd7 13. Bxd7+ Qxd7 14. Nb5 c6 15. Nc3 Bb4 16. Bd2 (16. Be3 O-O 17. O-O Bxc3 18. bxc3 $1 b5 19. c4 bxc4 20. Qxc4+ Nd5 21. Bf4 $18 {Bobby Fischer: 'and queens.'} Ra3 22. Be5 Raf3 23. Rxf3 exf3 24. Rf1 Qf5 25. Rf2 Qg5 26. h3 $1 Qc1+ 27. Qf1 Qe3 28. Qd3 $18 {Barcza}) 16... O-O 17. O-O Qxd4+ {! Barcza ! Barcza ! Barcza Bobby Fischer: ', Back on the right track. '} 18. Be3 Qd6 $1 19. Qc4+ Kh8 {Bobby Fischer: ', Finally the f-Pawn is free to advance. '} 20. Rad1 Qe7 21. a3 Ng4 22. Qxb4 Qxb4 {Bobby Fischer: ', Black resigns.'} 23. axb4 {Bobby Fischer: 'On'} Nxe3 24. Rxf8+ Rxf8 25. Re1 Nxc2 26. Rxe4 b5) 12... a6 13. Ba4 Bd7 14. Bxf6 gxf6 15. Qxe4+ Kf7 $6 {Barcza} 16. Ne5+ {! Barcza} fxe5 {ChessCalisthenics: 'N' Bobby Fischer: '; Black already bas difficulties.'} 17. Rf1+ $2 {Bobby Fischer: ', A superficial plan.'} Ke7 18. Bxd7 Kxd7 19. Rf7+ Ke8 {Bobby Fischer: '; To get out of the pin. '} (19... Be7 20. O-O-O $2 Qe6 21. dxe5+ Kc8) 20. Rxc7 Bd6 (20... Qe6) 21. Rxb7 Rc8 $2 {Bobby Fischer: '; Overlooking White's follow-up.'} 22. O-O-O Qxh2 (22... Rf8 23. dxe5 Be7 24. Qa4+ Kf7) 23. dxe5 {Bobby Fischer: '!'} Be7 (23... Qxc2+ 24. Qxc2 $2 Rxc2+ 25. Kxc2 Bxe5) 24. Rxe7+ Kxe7 25. Qb7+ {Bobby Fischer: ', Regaining the piece. Black's extra Pawn is meaningless in view of hismangled Pawn formation. '} Ke6 $1 {Bobby Fischer: '; An energetic maneuver! This Bishop is headed, if circumstances permit, toward the defense of Black's weakened K-side. '} (25... Rc7 26. Qxc7+ Ke6 27. Rd6+ Kf5 $1 {Bobby Fischer: '; Sacrificing a second Pawn for counterplay on the open c-file.'} 28. Qf7+ Kg4 29. Qf4+ Kh3 30. Qh4+ Kg2 31. Rd2+ Kf1 32. Qxh2 Rd8 33. Qh1#) 26. Qd7+ Kxe5 $1 27. Qd5+ Kf6 $1 {Bobby Fischer: '; Aggressive defense! '} 28. Rf1+ $1 Kg6 29. Qf5+ $1 Kh6 30. Qe6+ Kh5 (30... Kg5 31. Rf5+ $2 {Bobby Fischer: ', Losing a vital tempo, which gives Black time lo rush his King toward the center.'} Kg4 $1 32. Rf4+ Kh5 33. Qg4+ Kh6 $5 {Bobby Fischer: '; A risky selection in time-pressure,' Bobby Fischer: 'aimed against'} 34. Rf6#) 31. Rf5+ $1 Kg4 32. Rf4+ {! Barcza ! Barcza ! Barcza Bobby Fischer: ', A difficult choice.'} Kxg3 $1 (32... Kh5 33. Qg4+ $1 Kh6 34. Rf6#) 33. Qg4# 1-0

