1. e4 c5 2. Nc3 e6 3. Nge2 Nc6 4. g3 d5 5. exd5 exd5 6. d3 Nf6 7. Bg2 Be7 (7... d4) 8. Bg5 d4 9. Bxf6 Bxf6 10. Ne4 Be7 11. Nf4 O-O 12. O-O Re8 13. Qh5 g6 14. Qd5 Bf5 (14... Nb4 15. Qxd8 Rxd8 16. a3 Nc6) (14... Kg7) 15. Rfe1 Kg7 $6 {TH: Although it worked in this game as a one-off, it is not to be recommended.} (15... Nb4 16. Qb3 g5 17. Nh5 Be6 18. c4 f5 19. Nxc5 Bxc5 20. a3 Nc6 21. Rxe6 Rxe6 22. Bd5 Qe7 23. Bxe6+ Qxe6 24. Qxb7) 16. a3 Rc8 17. h3 Qxd5 18. Nxd5 Bf8 19. g4 Be6 {Diagram #} 20. Nef6 (20. Ng5 Bd6 (20... Bd7 21. Nxh7)) (20. Nf4) 20... Red8 21. g5 Bd6 $1 {After this Black's solid position made it almost imposible for White to play for a win.} (21... h6 22. h4 (22. Nf4 Bf5 (22... hxg5 23. Nxe6+ fxe6 24. Rxe6 Kf7 25. Rae1) 23. h4 Bd6) (22. gxh6+ Kxh6 23. Nf4 Bf5 24. Bxc6 Rxc6 25. Ng8+ Kg7 26. Ne7 Rf6) 22... hxg5 23. hxg5 Bd6) 22. Re4 Ne7 23. Rh4 (23. Rae1) 23... Rh8 24. Re1 Nf5 (24... Nxd5 25. Bxd5 Bxd5 26. Nxd5 h6) 25. Rhe4 h6 26. h4 hxg5 (26... Rhd8 27. Bh3 (27. Nf4 Bxf4 28. Rxf4 Nxh4) 27... Bb8 28. Rxe6 fxe6 29. Rxe6) (26... c4 27. Bf1) (26... Bxd5 27. Nxd5) 27. hxg5 Rh4 28. Rxh4 Nxh4 29. Re4 Nf5 (29... Nxg2 30. Kxg2 Bxd5 (30... Bb8 31. Kf3 Rh8 32. Nf4) 31. Nxd5 Rh8 32. Nf6) 30. Nf4 Ba2 (30... Bxf4 31. Rxf4 b6 (31... b5)) 31. N4d5 (31. Bh3 Bxf4 32. Rxf4 Bb1) 31... Bxd5 (31... Bb1 32. Re2 (32. Bh3 Bxc2 33. Bxf5 gxf5 34. Re8 Rb8)) 32. Nxd5 Kf8 33. Kf1 (33. Bh3 Re8 34. Bxf5 gxf5 35. Rh4 Kg7 (35... Re2 36. Rh6) 36. Kf1 (36. Rh6 Re6)) 33... Re8 34. Rxe8+ Kxe8 $1 35. Nf6+ Kd8 36. Bxb7 Bf4 37. Ne4 Bc1 (37... Nd6 38. Nxc5 Bc1 39. Bd5 Bxb2 40. a4) 38. a4 Bxb2 39. Nxc5 Bc1 40. Be4 (40. Ne4 Ke7 41. Bd5 Bf4 42. Kg2 Nd6) 40... Bxg5 $2 (40... Nd6 41. Nb3 $13) 41. Bxf5 gxf5 42. Nb3 Bf6 43. Kg2 Kd7 44. Kg3 Ke6 45. Na5 Be5+ 46. Kh4 Bf6+ $14 47. Kh5 {Sealed move} Kd5 48. Kh6 (48. Nb3 Ke5) 48... Kc5 49. Kh7 Kb4 50. Nc6+ Kc3 (50... Kxa4 51. Nxa7 Kb4 52. Kg8 {is also very bad for Black - Nunn)} Kc3 53. Kxf7 Bh8 54. Kg8) 51. Kg8 Kxc2 52. Kxf7 Bh8 (52... Bh4 {Black has little to show for the two pawns - Nunn.}) 53. a5 (53. Kg8 $140 Bf6 54. Kf7) 53... Kxd3 $1 54. a6 Ke2 55. Nxa7 d3 $1 56. Nc6 d2 57. a7 d1=Q 58. a8=Q Qd5+ 59. Kg6 Qe6+ $14 {Sealed at second adjournment} 60. Kh7 Bc3 (60... Bf6 61. Qa7 Qxc6 {draws.} 62. Qe3+ $145 {is critical.}) 61. Nd8 Qe7+ (61... Qe4 62. Qxe4+ fxe4 {idea ...Kf4 and ...Rg6 maintains equality (Fischer)} 63. Nf7 {favours White according to Boleslavsky, but} Kxf2 64. Nd6 e3 65. Ne4+) 62. Kg6 Qf6+ (62... Bd2 63. f4 $1) (62... Kxf2 63. Qa2+ Kg3 64. Qd5 $13) 63. Kh5 Qh8+ 64. Kg6 Qg7+ 65. Kxf5 Qf6+ 66. Kg4 Qg6+ $1 67. Kf4 Bd2+ 68. Ke5 Bc3+ 69. Kf4 Qd6+ 70. Kf5 Qd7+ 71. Kg5 Qe7+ {Fischer proposed a draw} 72. Kf5 $140 Qf6+ 73. Kg4 Qg7+ 74. Kf5 $1 Qf6+ 75. Kg4 Qg6+ $2 76. Kf4 Bd2+ 77. Ke5 Qg5+ 78. Ke6 $1 $11 Qg4+ 79. Kf7 Qd7+ 80. Kg6 {and the K goes to the queenside drawing (Wade)} 1/2-1/2

