1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Ba4 Nf6 5. O-O Nxe4 6. d4 b5 7. Bb3 exd4 (7... d5) (7... d6) 8. Re1 $146 {Matanovic,A: 'N'} (8. Nxd4 Ne7 9. Re1 (9. Bxf7+ Kxf7 10. Qf3+ Kg8 11. Qxe4 d5) 9... d5 $13 10. Nc6 {Ü 49/(219) Matanovic,A: '- 49/(219)' Ü 49/(219) Ü 49/(219) Ü 49/(219) Matanovic,A: '- 49/(219)'} Nxc6 {- 55/(209)} 11. Bxd5 Bb7 12. Bxe4 Be7 13. Bxc6+ Bxc6 14. Qe2 Kf8) 8... d5 9. Nc3 (9. Nxd4 $18 Nxd4 10. Qxd4 $18 Be6) (9. Bxd5 Qxd5 10. Nc3 $13) 9... Be6 (9... dxc3 10. Bxd5 Bb7 $16 11. Bxe4 (11. Rxe4+ Ne7) 11... Be7 (11... Qxd1 12. Bxc6+) 12. Qe2) 10. Nxe4 dxe4 11. Rxe4 Be7 12. Bxe6 fxe6 13. Nxd4 (13. Rxe6 Qd5 (13... Qd7 14. Qe2 O-O) 14. Qe2 O-O 15. Rxe7 {with very tense end.} {It was possible to start action on the Queens side} Nxe7 {MIKHALCHISHIN: 'it was time to start protecting own pawn.'} 16. Qxe7 $5 Rae8 $1 17. Qxc7 Rf7 18. Qg3 Rxf3 19. gxf3 Re1+ 20. Kg2 Qc4 $16 21. Kh3 Qe6+ 22. Qg4 Qc6 $1) 13... O-O (13... e5 {with repetition.} 14. Qh5+ {was another typical option of fighting against b7-b5.} {MIKHALCHISHIN: 'More active and better was'} g6 15. Nxc6) (13... Qd5 14. Qg4 O-O-O 15. Be3) (13... Nxd4 14. Rxd4 Qxd4 15. Qxd4 Rd8 16. Qg4) 14. Qg4 Nxd4 15. Rxd4 Qc8 16. Re4 $14 { Matanovic,A: ''    Matanovic,A: ''} Rf6 17. Be3 (17. Bf4 $1 Bd6 18. Rae1 $17) (17. Bg5 Rg6 18. h4 h6 $17 19. Qh5 Qe8 20. Bxe7 Rxg2+ 21. Kxg2 Qxh5) 17... Qd7 18. Rd1 Qc6 {MIKHALCHISHIN: 'Diagram '} 19. Bd4 $6 {MIKHALCHISHIN: 'useful move , but Whites' main problem in this position is to include into the game Knight on a3. At this moment it was possible to do ,while pawn c4 is poisoned'} Rg6 20. Qe2 Rd8 21. g3 $6 Qd5 $1 {MIKHALCHISHIN: 'Diagram '} 22. Re1 {MIKHALCHISHIN: '?!' '?!' '?!'} c5 (22... Qxa2 23. b3 Qa5 ({MIKHALCHISHIN: 'More direct attack on the Queens side was preferable'} 23... Rd6 $1 {MIKHALCHISHIN: '!?' '!?' '!?'} 24. Ra1) 24. Rxe6 {with mutual chances.}) 23. Bc3 Rd6 $17 24. Be5 Rd8 25. Bf4 c4 (25... Qxa2 {MIKHALCHISHIN: 'Of course active approach-Russians never go back!'} 26. b3 Qa5 27. Rxe6) (25... Kf7 $13 26. b3) 26. Rxe6 {MIKHALCHISHIN: 'Diagram '} Rxe6 27. Qxe6+ Qxe6 $1 28. Rxe6 Bf6 29. Rxa6 $8 Rd1+ 30. Kg2 Bxb2 $1 (30... Rb1 {was much better chance,eliminating the defence of pawn a2.} 31. a4 {was very unpleasant for Black.} (31. b3 Rb2 32. Ra5 Rxc2 33. Rxb5 Rxa2 {with initiative.} {Maybe better strategy would be attack of the e4 pawn.} 34. bxc4 Rc2) {MIKHALCHISHIN: 'Better was'} 31... Rxb2 $1 (31... b4 {with very tense position.} 32. Rc6 $5 {Two other options were more direct} Rxb2 {Similar idea could be conducted differently} 33. Rxc4 $5 Bc3 34. Bd6) 32. axb5 Rxb5 $1 $17 33. Rc6 c3 34. Re6 Kf7 35. Re2) 31. Rb6 {MIKHALCHISHIN: 'Diagram '} Ra1 $1 {MIKHALCHISHIN: '!?' '!?' '!?'} 32. Rxb5 Rxa2 33. Rc5 Ra4 (33... c3 34. Be5 Ba1 35. Rc7 Rxc2 36. Rxg7+ Kf8 {was close to draw.} 37. Rc7 {was more powerful - young Bobby would play it!}) 34. Be5 Bxe5 35. Rxe5 Ra2 (35... Ra3 36. Re3 Ra2 37. Rc3) 36. Re2 $8 Kf7 $2 (36... Ra3 $11 37. Re3 Ra2 38. Rc3) 37. Kf3 $1 Kf6 38. Ke4 g5 39. Kd4 Kf5 40. f3 (40. Kxc4 Kg4 41. Kb3) 40... c3 41. Rf2 $14 {MIKHALCHISHIN: 'Diagram  White protected everything and their free pawns are ready to run.'} (41. Kxc3 Ra3+ 42. Kd4 {with draw.} Rxf3 43. c4) 41... Ra3 42. Kc4 h5 43. Kb4 Ra8 44. f4 (44. Kxc3 h4) 44... Ke4 45. fxg5 Ke3 46. Rg2 (46. Rf7 Kd2) 46... Kd4 (46... Rc8 47. h4 Kf3 $11 48. Rg1 Kf2 49. Rd1 Kxg3 50. Rd4) 47. Re2 $1 {MIKHALCHISHIN: 'Fischer decides to sacrifice its c pawn and starts to prepare run of another,more dangerous one.'} Rb8+ 48. Ka4 Rg8 49. h4 Rf8 50. Re7 (50. g4 hxg4 51. g6) 50... Rf3 $1 51. Rd7+ {MIKHALCHISHIN: 'Diagram '} Kc4 $2 52. Rc7+ Kd4 53. Rd7+ Kc4 54. Rc7+ Kd4 55. Kb3 $1 Rxg3 56. Rd7+ $1 Ke4 57. Rh7 $18 {MIKHALCHISHIN: 'transposition into winning Rook end.'} Kd4 58. Rxh5 Rg1 59. Rh8 Rb1+ 60. Ka4 Ra1+ (60... Rb2 61. g6) 61. Kb5 Rb1+ 62. Kc6 Rg1 63. Rd8+ Kc4 64. Re8 Kb4 (64... Kd4 65. Re2 Rg4 66. Kd6 Rxh4 67. Rg2) 65. Kd5 $1 Rd1+ (65... Ka3 66. Rb8) 66. Ke6 Re1+ 67. Kf7 {MIKHALCHISHIN: '1-0 '} Rf1+ {was not bad.} 68. Kg6 Rf2 69. h5 Rxc2 70. h6 Rh2 71. h7 c2 {was stiil winning for White.} {MIKHALCHISHIN: 'It was very difficult way to draw'} 72. Rc8 $1 Kb3 73. Kg7 1-0

