{Bobby Fischer: 'GAME N. 10 Milking the cow The Ruy Lopez has been so extensively analyzed that often both players reel off their first twenty moves in two minutes flat. Nevertheless, it gives rise to situations that call for tact and patience. As Bronstein remarked. "When you play the Ruy, it's like milking a cow." Fischer, here, milks the cow to a fare-thee-well. The first twenty-two moves are identical with game number 6. Unzicker then varies with the dubious ...f6. which undermines his e-Pawn and leaves him with weak squares. Retribution, though not swift, is sure. Creating simultaneous threats on both wings. Fischer finally infiltrates on the a-file. Black is so tied up that he cannot defend one of his Pawns when attacked - making defeat imminent. '} 1. e4 {Bobby Fischer} e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Ba4 Nf6 5. O-O Be7 6. Re1 b5 7. Bb3 d6 8. c3 O-O 9. h3 Na5 10. Bc2 c5 11. d4 Nd7 12. d5 (12. dxc5 dxc5 13. Nbd2 Qc7 (13... Bb7) 14. Nf1 Nb6 15. Ne3 Rd8 16. Qe2 Be6 17. Nd5 Nxd5 18. exd5 Bxd5 19. Nxe5 Ra7 20. Bf4 Qb6 21. Rad1 g6 22. Ng4 Nc4 23. Bh6 Be6 24. Bb3 Qb8 25. Rxd8+ Bxd8 26. Bxc4 bxc4 27. Qxc4 Qd6 28. Qa4 Qe7 29. Nf6+ Kh8 30. Nd5 Qd7 31. Qe4 Qd6 32. Nf4 Re7 33. Bg5 Re8 34. Bxd8 Rxd8 35. Nxe6 Qxe6 36. Qxe6 fxe6 37. Rxe6 Rd1+ 38. Kh2 Rd2 39. Rb6 Rxf2 40. Rb7 Rf6 41. Kg3) (12. Nbd2 cxd4 (12... exd4 13. cxd4 Nc6 14. d5 Nce5 15. Nxe5 Nxe5 16. a4 Rb8 17. axb5 axb5 18. f4 Ng6 19. Nf3 Bh4 20. Rf1 Bg3 21. f5 Ne5 22. Ng5 Bh4 23. f6) 13. cxd4 Nc6 14. a3 (14. Nf1 exd4 (14... Nb6 15. b3 Bf6 16. Bb2 Bd7 17. Ne3) 15. Nxd4 Nxd4 16. Qxd4 Ne5 17. Qd1 Bf6 18. Ne3 Be6) 14... exd4 15. Nb3 Nde5 (15... d3) 16. Nfxd4 Bf6) (12. a4 Rb8 13. axb5 axb5 14. dxc5 dxc5 15. Nbd2 Bb7 16. Nf1 Nc4 17. Ne3 (17. b3 Nd6 18. Ne3) 17... Nxe3 18. Bxe3 Qc7 19. Qe2 c4) 12... Nb6 13. g4 (13. Nbd2 f5 (13... Bd7 14. Nf1 Nb7 15. b3 a5 (15... c4)) 14. exf5 Bxf5 15. Bxf5 Rxf5 16. Ne4 Qd7) 13... h5 (13... Bd7 14. Kh2 h5 15. g5) 14. Nh2 (14. gxh5 Bxh3 15. Nh2 Bg5) 14... hxg4 15. hxg4 Bg5 16. Nd2 g6 (16... Bf4 17. Ndf1 (17. Ndf3 g5) 17... g6) 17. Ndf3 Bxc1 (17... Bf4) 18. Qxc1 Kg7 19. Qg5 Nb7 $2 {Gligoric} (19... Qxg5 20. Nxg5 Bd7 (20... Nac4 21. Rab1 (21. b3 Na3 22. Bd1 (22. Bd3 c4) 22... Rh8) 21... Rh8 22. Bd3 Bd7 23. Kg2 Rh6) 21. Kg2 c4 22. Nh3 Nb7 23. f4 f6 24. Kg3 Nc5 25. Nf3 Nba4 26. Rab1 a5 27. Nd2 Rh8 28. Nf2 Nb6 29. Rh1 b4 30. Rxh8 Rxh8 31. b3 cxb3 32. Nxb3 Nxb3 33. Bxb3 Rc8 34. cxb4 Rc3+ 35. Kg2 a4 36. Bd1 exf4 37. b5 a3 38. Bb3 Bxb5 39. Bd1 Rc5 40. Nd3 Bxd3) (19... Bd7) (19... f6) 20. Qxd8 $5 {! Gligoric} Rxd8 21. a4 bxa4 (21... Bd7 22. axb5 (22. a5 Nc4 23. b4 Rh8) 22... axb5 23. b3) 22. Bxa4 Nxa4 {Bobby Fischer: '?'} {Bobby Fischer: 'Unzicker prefers active defense. He eliminates the potential pressure along the h-file, it is true, but at the cost of weakening his e-Pawn. '} 23. Rxa4 {× e5} Bd7 24. Ra2 $1 {Fischer/Gligoric} (24. Raa1) 24... c4 25. Nd2 Bb5 26. Nhf1 $16 { Bobby Fischer: ', Because both flanks are fluid, White, with his two Bishops, is better able to penetrate and exploit the "loose" Pawns. '} (26. Kg2 Rh8 (26... Nc5 27. Rh1 Nd3 28. Nhf1 Nf4+ 29. Kg1) 27. Re3 Nc5 28. Rh3 Rxh3 29. Kxh3 Rh8+ 30. Kg2 f6) 26... Rh8 (26... Nc5 27. Ne3 Nd3 28. Rb1 Rh8) 27. Ne3 {Bobby Fischer: ', If he swaps, White gains the a-file; if he doesn't. White keeps the d-file. '} (27. f3) 27... Rh4 28. Kg2 Rah8 29. Nf3 Rh3 30. Nf1 $1 (30. Raa1 Nc5 31. Rh1 (31. Nd2 Nd3) 31... Rxh1 32. Rxh1 Rxh1 33. Kxh1 Nxe4 (33... Nd3)) 30... Nc5 31. Ng3 {Bobby Fischer: ', Now White must penetrate on either the a- or d-file. Black's e-Pawn has clearly been exposed as a weakling. '} Bd7 (31... Nd3 32. Rh1 Nxf2) 32. g5 f6 {Bobby Fischer: '; Apparently defending everything.'} (32... Bg4) 33. gxf6+ $1 {Bobby Fischer: ', Bringing the Bishop into the game puts additional pressure on Black's overburdened pieces. '} Kxf6 34. Re3 {Bobby Fischer: ', Infiltration! '} (34. Rh1 Rxh1 35. Nxh1 Nxe4 36. Rxa6 Bh3+ 37. Kg1 Rb8 38. Ng3 Nxg3 39. fxg3 Rxb2 40. Rxd6+ Kf5) 34... Ke7 35. Nd2 $1 {Bobby Fischer: ', Simply attacking a Pawn. Curiously, Black is in too much of a straitjacket to do much about it. '} Rh2+ (35... Nd3 36. Rxd3 (36. Nxc4 Rh2+ 37. Kg1 Nf4) 36... cxd3 37. Rxa6 Rf8 38. Ngf1 Rhh8) 36. Kg1 Bb5 37. Ra1 R2h4 38. Kg2 {Bobby Fischer: ', The win is still far from clear. White's major technical problem is creating a passed Pawn on the Q-side while sheltering his King from a perpetual check. '} Rf8 {Bobby Fischer: '; Threatening ...Nxe4. '} 39. Rf3 (39. Rh1 Rxh1 40. Nxh1 Nd3) 39... Rb8 40. Kg1 Ra8 (40... Nd3 41. b3 (41. Rb1 Bd7 42. Nxc4 Nf4) 41... cxb3 42. c4 b2 43. Rb1 Ba4 44. Rxd3 Bc2 45. Ra3 Bxb1 46. Nxb1 Rb4 47. Kg2) 41. Ra5 Rc8 42. Ra3 (42. Ra1 Nd3 43. Rb1 Nf4) 42... Ra8 (42... Nd3 43. Ra2 Ra8) 43. Ra5 Ra7 44. Kg2 Nb7 45. Ra1 a5 (45... Nc5) 46. Ngf1 {Bobby Fischer: ', Step one is completed: White has a passed b-Pawn. '} Nc5 47. Ne3 a4 $8 {Bobby Fischer: '; Forced.'} (47... Nxe4 {Tal,M; Geller,E} 48. Nxe4 Rxe4 49. Rh1 {Rossolimo,N Bobby Fischer: 'is an interesting alternative. (ROSSOLIMO) - Black avoids weakening his d5.'} Rd7 50. Kg3) (47... Nb3 48. Nxb3 cxb3 49. Rg3) 48. Rh3 (48. Rg3 Kf6 $10 {Fischer,R-Matanovic,A Portoroz izt 1958 Bobby Fischer: '=' Bobby Fischer: 'Black's Knight is already prepared to parachute to d3.'} {Bobby Fischer: 'Tal and Geller recommend'} 49. Rf3+ {Bobby Fischer: 'and if'} (49. Rg4)) 48... Rxh3 49. Kxh3 $1 {Gligoric Bobby Fischer: ', The idea is to create another passed Pawn in the center. '} Nd3 50. Ra2 (50. Kg3 Nxb2 51. Nc2) 50... Nxf2+ 51. Kg3 Nd3 {Bobby Fischer: '; Striving to keep the blockade as long as possible. '} 52. Nexc4 Ra8 (52... Rc7 53. Na5 (53. Nb6 $16 {Bobby Fischer: 'White gets an edge after'} Nc5 54. Kf3 Rb7 55. Nbc4 $13 {Bobby Fischer: 'Against Matanovich, at Portoroz, 1958, I tried the inferior'} Rb8) (53. Ne3 Rc8 54. Nd1 Bd7) 53... Rc8 54. c4 $16 {Gligoric} Bd7) 53. Nb6 $1 Ra6 {Bobby Fischer: '; Makes it easy.'} (53... Rh8 {Bobby Fischer: 'is met by'} 54. c4 {Bobby Fischer: 'instituting an awkward pin.'} {Bobby Fischer: 'For analysis of this position see game 6.'} Be8 $1 {Fischer,R-Shocron,G Mar del Plata 1959 Bobby Fischer: 'Fischer,R-Shocron,G; Mar del Plata, 1959.'} 55. Nxa4 Nf4) 54. Nbc4 Nc5 55. Kf3 Ra8 56. b4 Nb3 57. Na3 $1 Bd7 (57... Be2+ 58. Ke3 Bd1 {Bobby Fischer: 'though'} 59. Nac4 $1 $16 { d1-a1-a~ Bobby Fischer: 'followed by Qa1! forces an invasion on the Q-side.'}) 58. Kg2 (58. Ndc4) 58... Bg4 ({Bobby Fischer: 'Black should ease the pressure by'} 58... g5 $142) 59. Nac4 (59. Rb2 $18 {Bobby Fischer: 'if'} Nxd2 60. Rxd2 $18 { Bobby Fischer: 'with a winning attack.'} Rf8 {Bobby Fischer: 'can be met by'} 61. Rd3 {The threat was} Kf6 {Bobby Fischer} 62. c4 Kg5 63. Nb5) 59... Rc8 60. Ne3 (60. Rxa4 Nxd2 61. Nxd2 Rxc3 $1 62. Ra7+ Kf6 $18 {Bobby Fischer: 'wins a piece.'} {Bobby Fischer: 'or'} 63. Kf2) 60... Bd7 61. c4 Rb8 62. b5 Nc5 63. Nd1 Kd8 64. Nc3 Ra8 65. Nf3 {Bobby Fischer: ', Black resigns.'} ({Bobby Fischer: 'On'} 65. Kg3 {Bobby Fischer: '?'} Kc7 $18 {Bobby Fischer: 'forces mate.'} {Bobby Fischer: 'Not'} 66. Kh4 Rh8+ 67. Kg5 Rh2) 65... Kc7 {Bobby Fischer: 'After'} 66. Ng5 Kb6 67. Nf7 Rf8 $18 {Bobby Fischer: 'leads to an elementary win.'} 68. Rf2 (68. Nxd6 Kc7 (68... Rf6 69. Nxa4+ $18 {Bobby Fischer: 'when one of Black's hanging Pawns must fall.'} {Bobby Fischer: 'if'} Nxa4 70. Rxa4 Rxd6 71. Ra6+ Kc5 72. Ra7 $18) 69. Nxa4 Kxd6 (69... Ra8 70. Nf7 Rxa4 71. Rxa4 $1 Nxa4 72. Nxe5) 70. Nxc5 Kxc5 71. Ra7 $18 {Bobby Fischer: 'wins.'} Bg4 $2 72. Kg3 Bf3 73. Rc7+ Kb6 74. Rc6+ Ka5 75. Rxg6 Bxe4 76. Re6 Rf5 77. d6 $1 $18 {Bobby Fischer: '!' Bobby Fischer: 'wins.'}) 68... a3 69. Rf3 (69. Nxd6 Bh3+ (69... Rxf2+ {Bobby Fischer: 'wins.'} {Bobby Fischer: 'If'} 70. Kxf2 $2 Kc7 71. Nf7 Nxe4+ $18 {Bobby Fischer: 'Not'} 72. Nxe4 {Bobby Fischer: '?'} a2 $10 {Bobby Fischer: 'draws.'} {Bobby Fischer: 'On'} 73. Nc5 a1=Q {Bobby Fischer: 'maintains the bind (if'} 74. b6+ $2 Kc8 {Bobby Fischer: ').'} (74... Kxb6 75. Nxd7+ $1 {Bobby Fischer: 'Black should wait around with'} Ka5 $142 {Bobby Fischer: 'How can Black defend the Pawn? '} 76. Ndxe5 $2) 75. b7+ {Bobby Fischer: '?' Bobby Fischer: 'loses a second Pawn after'} Kc7 {Bobby Fischer: 'It's better to refrain from'} 76. b8=Q+ $2 {× e3, a2-g2 Bobby Fischer: 'which weakens the K -field.'} {Bobby Fischer: 'On'} Kxb8 77. Nxd7+ Kb7 78. Ndxe5 Qd4+ 79. Kf3 $18 {Bobby Fischer: 'should win.'} g5 80. d6 $18 {Gligoric} {Sharper and possibly immediately decisive is} Qf4+ $1 {Bobby Fischer}) 70. Kg1 Rxf2 71. Kxf2 Kc7 72. Ne8+ (72. Nf7 Nxe4+ 73. Nxe4 $18 {Bobby Fischer: 'wins.'} {Bobby Fischer: 'if'} a2) 72... Kd8 73. Nd6 Ke7) 69... Bg4 70. Rf2 a2 $18 {Gligoric} (70... Ka5) {Bobby Fischer: 'The best defense was'} 71. Nxa2 {} Nxe4 72. Rf1 Bf5 73. c5+ (73. Nh6 Bh3+) 73... dxc5 1-0

