8. Qc2 Nxb3 19. Qxb3 Be6 20. Qc3 Be5 21. Nxe5 Qxe5 22. Qc2 Rd4) (17. Nd2 Rd8 18. N2f3 (18. Nf5 Bxf5 19. exf5 Be5) 18... Nxb3 19. Qxb3 c5 20. Nf5 Be6 21. Qc2 Be5) (17. Qc2 Rd8 18. Rd1 Nxb3 19. Nxb3 Kh8 (19... Qe7 20. Nc3 Qe5 21. Nd4 Qh2+ 22. Kf1 Be6 23. Nxe6 fxe6 24. Qd3 Rd7 25. Qf3 Rg7 26. Ke2 Rf8 27. Rd3 f5 28. Rf1 b4 29. Nb1 Rxg2) (19... Bh2+ 20. Kh1 Rxd1+) 20. Nc3 Qe7 21. Ne2 c5 22. Ng3 (22. Nxc5 Rg8 23. Rxd6 Qxd6 24. Rd1) 22... Rg8 23. Rxd6) 17... Bxf5 18. exf5 Rad8 19. Qh5 (19. Qg4+ Kh8 20. Nc3 (20. Qh4 Be5 21. Nc3 Rfe8 22. Re3 Rg8 23. Rd1)) 19... Nd3 (19... b4) (19... Be5 20. Nc3 Rd4 21. Re3 Bf4 22. Re2 Bd2 23. Nd1 Bg5 24. g3 Qd6 25. Ne3 Bxe3 26. Rxe3) 20. Re4 Qa7) 16... Ne5 (16... Bc5 17. Qc3 a5 18. Nbd2 (18. a3 Qg3 19. Qxc5 Nxc5 20. Bxf7+ Kxf7 21. fxg3 Nb3 22. Ra2 Be6) 18... a4 19. Bc2 b4 20. Qd3 Ba6) 17. Nbd2 Rd8 ({Black decides to fianchetto his Bishop. The alternative is} 17... c5 18. Qe3 c4 19. Bc2 $16 Bc5 20. Qh6 Qb6 21. a4 Bxf2+ 22. Kh1 Bxe1 23. Rxe1) (17... Kh8 18. Nh4 Rg8 19. Nf5 Bxf5 20. exf5 Rad8) 18. Qe3 $6 Nd3 19. Qh6 Bf4 $13 (19... Nxe1 20. Rxe1 $13 {After a better} Bf4 (20... Be5 $13 {Bishop on h4-d8 diagonal is not best placed. Better was} 21. Nxe5 $14 {From the e3 square Bishop controls both wings.}) 21. Qxf6 Bxd2 {the position is unclear.} ({After} 21... Rxd2 $1 {we can see that the Bishop is not well placed on h4. The position is unclear:} 22. Nxd2 Bxd2 23. Rd1 Ba5 24. Rd3) 22. Bxf7+ $5) (19... Qe7 {is slightly preferable.} {Slightly preferable is} 20. e5) 20. Qxf6 Rd6 21. Qc3 Nxe1 22. Rxe1 Qd8 (22... Rg6 23. Nh4 $14) (22... Bxh3 $16 {Dubious move. Preferable was} 23. gxh3 $14 {Threatenning xd4. The alternative is} Rg6+ 24. Kf1 $5) 23. Re2 Rg6 $6 24. Kh1 ({Unnecessary move which only helps Black. Preferable was a typical} 24. Kf1) 24... Be6 25. Bxe6 fxe6 $13 (25... Rxe6 26. Nb3 (26. Nd4 Bxd2 27. Nxe6 $13 {Of course,} Bxc3 {would be bad because of} 28. Nxd8 {with next h5.} Rxd8 $13 {is an alternative.})) 26. g3 Bh6 $2 (26... Bxd2 $13 27. Rxd2 {is an alternative:}) 27. Kg2 $2 (27. Qxc6 Rc8) (27. Nb3) 27... Rc8 $2 28. e5 $1 $16 (28. Nb3 $13 c5 {Was more sensitive:} 29. Nxc5 b4 $14 {Stronger was} 30. Qd3) 28... Qd5 29. Ne4 Bg7 $2 30. b3 $18 {White is wining. He is a pawn up and his e4 dominates.} Rf8 31. Qc2 Rf4 32. Ned2 c5 33. Re3 Qc6 (33... Bf8 34. Ne4 (34. Rd3 {the position is completely unclear.} {White misses a very strong move} Rd4 $1 {[%csl Yg3][%cal Yg2g3] after which he keeps a slight edge:} 35. Rxd4 cxd4 36. Qd3 ({Preferable was} 36. Qe4 Bb4) 36... Bg7 $14) 34... Be7 {and after a nice}) 34. Ne4 $2 c4 35. bxc4 $2 bxc4 36. Ned2 Bh6 $1 $11 37. Rc3 Rg7 38. Rd3 ({Fischer loses a huge part of his adantage. Better was} 38. Nxc4 $18 {I am sure that in his prime age Fischer would play} Rxf3 {without thinking.} {The alternative is} 39. Rxf3 Rc7) (38. Rxc4 $16 {The position is extremely complex and it is hard to find strong moves. Better was} Rxc4) 38... Qa8 39. Nxc4 Qc6 40. Na3 (40. Rc3 Rxf3 41. Rxf3 Rf7 42. Qe2 Rxf3 $11 43. Qxf3 $5 {Another wrong exchange. After a better} Qxc4 {White has a clear edge.}) 40... Qxc2 41. Nxc2 Ra4 {Although the position is even White has to fight for draw.} 42. Rd8+ Kf7 {Objectively, Rook endgame is even.} 43. a3 Rg6 (43... Bc1 44. Rd1 Bb2 45. Rb1 Bc3 46. Rb3 Rc4) 44. h4 Bf8 45. Ng5+ $6 Ke7 46. Ra8 h6 47. Nh7 Bg7 48. Ra7+ Ke8 49. h5 Rgg4 50. f3 (50. Ne3 {also leads to an even play:} Bxe5 51. Nxg4 Rxg4 52. f4 Ba1 (52... Bxf4 53. Nf6+) 53. Ng5) 50... Rgc4 51. Rxg7 $2 Rxc2+ 52. Kh3 Rxa3 53. f4 Rf2 (53... a5 54. Rg6 (54. f5 exf5 55. e6 Re2 56. Nf6+ Kd8 57. Rd7+ Kc8 $19 {Clear mistake which loses the game. After} 58. e7 {preventing g5, the position is even.} {Unnecessary idea. Easier was} Raa2 59. e8=Q+ Rxe8 $11) 54... Kf7 55. Nf6 Rf2 56. Rxh6 Rxf4 57. Rh7+ Kf8 58. h6 Rff3 59. Rg7) 54. Nf6+ Kf8 55. Rg4 a5 56. Ne4 Rc2 57. Rg6 Re3 58. Nd6 Rcc3 59. Rxe6 Rxg3+ 60. Kh4 Rg1 61. f5 Rc2 62. Re8+ Kg7 63. f6+ Kh7 64. Re7+ Kg8 {More resilient is} 65. Kh3 {although it loses after} Rc3+ {Possible line is:} 66. Kh4 Rc2 67. Kh3 Rc3+ 68. Kh2 Rcg3 (68... Re1) 69. f7+ Kg7 70. Nf5+ Kf8 71. Nxg3 Rxg3 (71... Rxg3 72. Ra7 Re3) 0-1

