1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Ba4 Nf6 5. O-O Be7 6. Re1 b5 7. Bb3 d6 8. c3 O-O 9. h3 Bb7 {Breyer Nagesh,Havanur: 'The Breyer Variation, a favourite of Spassky.'} 10. d4 Na5 (10... exd4 11. cxd4 d5 12. e5 Ne4 13. Nc3 Na5 { 38...c2 39... e4} 14. Bc2 $1 f5 15. exf6 Bxf6 16. Nxe4 dxe4 17. Bxe4 Bxe4 18. Rxe4 c5 19. d5) 11. Bc2 Nc4 (11... exd4 12. cxd4 d5 (12... c5 13. Nbd2 $18) 13. e5 Ne4) (11... c5 {! Olafsson Geller} 12. Nbd2) 12. b3 Nb6 13. Nbd2 {Nagesh,Havanur: 'This plan preventing the freeing advance...c5 was popular in those days.'} (13. dxe5 { 35.e5} dxe5 14. Qxd8 Raxd8 { 36... b3 -+} 15. Nxe5 { 37.b5} Nxe4 16. Bxe4 Bxe4) 13... Nbd7 (13... Re8 $18 {Timman} 14. Bb2 (14. dxe5 dxe5 15. Nxe5 Bc5 (15... Bd6 $18 16. Nef3 Bxe4 $1 $10 (16... Nxe4 $1 17. Nxe4 Bxe4 18. Bg5) 17. Nxe4 Nxe4 18. Qd3 (18. Bxe4 Rxe4 19. Rxe4 Bh2+))) (14. Nf1 $10) 14... Bf8 15. c4) (13... Nfd7 $3) (13... exd4 $2 14. cxd4 $18 c5) 14. b4 (14. Bb2) 14... exd4 (14... a5 15. Nb3) 15. cxd4 a5 (15... c5 16. bxc5 dxc5 17. d5) 16. bxa5 c5 { 17... c5 Nagesh,Havanur: 'Gligoric,Svetozar: '!?'' Nagesh,Havanur: 'A novelty in this position. Otherwise the idea is known. The move indirectly defends e5 and targets White's b-pawn. However, its drawback is that it shuts out the QR.'} (16... Rxa5 17. d5 c5 18. dxc6 Bxc6 19. Nd4 $1) 17. e5 {Nagesh,Havanur: 'Gligoric,Svetozar: '!'' Nagesh,Havanur: 'Indirectly defending the b-pawn.'} dxe5 (17... Ne8) 18. dxe5 {Nagesh,Havanur: 'The battle is for the control of e5 and this move strikes at d6, the heart of its base.'} Nd5 19. Ne4 Nb4 (19... Rxa5 20. Neg5 h6 21. Qd3 g6 22. Ne6 $18 {Olafsson}) (19... Re8) 20. Bb1 Rxa5 21. Qe2 {Nagesh,Havanur: 'Calling into question Black's entire plan initiated with 16...Qb8.'} (21. e6 { 42... c2 -+} fxe6 22. Neg5 (22. Nfg5 Bd5 23. Nxh7 Rf5) 22... Bxf3 23. Nxf3 Bf6) 21... Nb6 $10 {Purdy} (21... Re8 22. Rd1 (22. e6 fxe6 23. Neg5 Bxg5 24. Nxg5 Nf8 25. Qh5 g6) 22... Qc7) 22. Nfg5 Bxe4 (22... h6 23. Nh7 Re8 {'' !} (23... Kxh7 24. Nxc5+) 24. Nhf6+ $3 Bxf6 (24... gxf6 $4 25. Qg4+ $19 {Nagesh,Havanur: '=' '=' '='} Kh8 26. Nd6 (26. Bxh6 Bf8 27. Bxf8 Rxf8 $18 28. Nxf6) 26... Bxd6 27. Qf5 $18 Kg7 28. Bxh6+) 25. Nxf6+ Qxf6 (25... gxf6 26. Qg4+ Kf8 27. Bxh6+ $10 {Timman} Ke7 28. e6 Kd6 $2 29. Qg3+ Kc6 30. Be4+ N4d5 31. exf7 Rh8 32. Bxd5+ { 43.c6 +-}) 26. exf6 $1 {Nagesh,Havanur: '=' '=' '=' Nagesh,Havanur: 'analysis initiated by Olafsson and refined by Timman and Kasparov'} Rxe2 27. Rxe2) (22... g6 23. e6 f5 $18 24. Nf7 $1) 23. Qxe4 g6 {Nagesh,Havanur: '!?' '!?' '!?' Nagesh,Havanur: 'Spassky offers a pawn for active counterplay.'} 24. Qh4 {Nagesh,Havanur: '!' '!' '!'} h5 25. Qg3 (25. g4 Qd4 $1) 25... Nc4 {? Purdy ?!} 26. Nf3 $1 {Nagesh,Havanur: 'Gligoric,Svetozar: '!'' ''} (26. e6 f5 {White has the upper hand, but no clear win according to Timman and Kasparov.} 27. Nf3 (27. Nf7 {Nagesh,Havanur: '!' '!'} Rxf7 28. exf7+ Kxf7 29. Bxf5 gxf5 {+- Byrne/ = Timman} 30. Qf3 $1 $14 {'' ! Gligoric} Kg6 {?!} 31. g4 {! Timman} Qd5 $2 {Nagesh,Havanur: '?!' '?!'}) 27... Qe8 (27... Kg7 28. Qf4) (27... Rf6 28. Bg5 {+- Olafsson} Kh7 { 41... a2  Timman} {Nagesh,Havanur: 'If'} 29. Bxf6 Bxf6 $1 {+- Nej  38.h4, 39.be6 Nagesh,Havanur: '(Nei) preparing h4 followed by Rbe6 forming a mating net should win.'} 30. Bxf5 {+- Olafsson} gxf5 31. Rad1 Nd5 32. e7 Bxe7 $132 {Timman} 33. Rxd5) 28. Nd2) (26. Nxf7 Rxf7 27. Qxg6+ $13 {Timman} Rg7 $1 {!} 28. Qe6+ {!? Shtein} Kh8 29. Qh6+ Kg8 {/+- vgl. Anmerkung zum 29.Zug von Schwarz Timman} {If} 30. Bf5 $2 Ra6 $16 31. Be6+ $4 {runs into} Rxe6 $1 32. Qxe6+) (26. Ne6 {Nagesh,Havanur: 'He had to play'} Bh4 {Nagesh,Havanur: '!' '!' '!' %03'better is'} 27. Nxd8 Bxg3 28. Nb7 Ra7 29. Nxc5 Bxe5) 26... Kg7 ({Nagesh,Havanur: 'Larsen offered'} 26... Nd3 $142 {Nagesh,Havanur: '!' '!' '!' Nagesh,Havanur: 'and it sets more problems for White. However, after'} 27. Bxd3 (27. Rd1 Nxc1) 27... Qxd3 28. Bg5 {+- Nej/ / +- Timman  }) 27. Qf4 {Nagesh,Havanur: 'The point of White's 24th move.'} Rh8 28. e6 f5 {Nagesh,Havanur: 'Gligoric,Svetozar: '!''} (28... Bf6 $18 {Byrne} {Nagesh,Havanur: 'The suggestion of Krogius and Nei'} 29. exf7 {Nej '' ! Polugaevsky} Bxa1 (29... Qd6 30. f8=Q+ Kxf8 31. Qe4 {= Timman} Qd7 {?} 32. Bg5 Ra6 33. Bxf6 $17 Rxf6 34. Ne5) 30. f8=Q+ {Nagesh,Havanur: 'is refuted by Timman.'} Qxf8 $1 31. Qc7+ Kg8 32. Bxg6 Nd5 $18 {Timman} (32... Ra6 33. Re8) {Nagesh,Havanur: 'or'} 33. Qb7 Nf6 {Nagesh,Havanur: '+-' '+-' '+-'} 34. Bf4 Rh7 {Nej} 35. Bxh7+ Nxh7 36. Qd5+ Qf7 (36... Kh8 {!} 37. Qxh5) 37. Qxf7+ Kxf7 $18 {!} 38. Rxa1 {?!}) (28... f6 29. Nh4 $18) 29. Bxf5 $1 {Nagesh,Havanur: 'Gligoric,Svetozar: '!''} Qf8 {Nagesh,Havanur: '?' '?' '?' ?! Nagesh,Havanur: 'anxious to defend the second rank and yet the move turns insufficient'} (29... gxf5 {'+-'} 30. Qg3+ Kh7 (30... Kf8 {'' Timman} 31. Qg6 Qe8 $10 {Timman} (31... Nd6 $10 32. Ne5) 32. Bh6+ Rxh6 33. Qxh6+ Kg8 34. Ng5) 31. Ng5+ Bxg5 32. Bxg5 $4 Ra3 $19 {Purdy} (32... Qe8 {!} {Nagesh,Havanur: 'or'} 33. Rad1 $1 {= Purdy Nagesh,Havanur: 'Gligoric,Svetozar: '!'' %03'better is'} Ra7 34. Rd8 {'' Timman} Qxd8 $1 35. Bxd8 Rxd8 36. e7 Re8 {Nagesh,Havanur: 'followed by 45.Rd7 wins.'} 37. Re6 Rexe7 38. Qg6+ Kh8 39. Qf6+ Rg7 40. Qh6+ Kg8 41. Re8+ Kf7 42. Qe6#) (32... Qd3 33. Qc7+ Kg6 34. Qf7+ Kxg5 $18 {Timman} 35. Qg7+ Kf4 $18 {Zugzwang} 36. Rad1) (32... Qb8 $18 33. Qh4 $2 {'with the idea' g4} Kg6 34. Bf6) 33. Qf4 Qf8 34. Rad1 Rd3 35. h4 Nd5 {!} 36. Qc1 Rd4 37. Rxd4 cxd4 $14 {Polugaevsky} 38. Qd1) (29... Bd6 30. e7 Bxf4 $18 (30... Bxe7 31. Qg3 Ra6 32. Ng5) 31. exd8=Q Rxd8 32. Bxf4 gxf5 33. Bc7) 30. Be4 {Nagesh,Havanur: '!' '!' '!'} (30. Nh4 $18 {Purdy ''} Bxh4 $18 31. Qxh4 Qxf5 (31... Qf6 $18 {Timman} 32. Qg3) (31... gxf5 $18 {Nagesh,Havanur: 'not'} 32. Qg5+ $2 {?} Kh7 33. e7 Qe8 $10 {Nagesh,Havanur: '=' '=' '=' Nagesh,Havanur: 'with a theoretical draw.'} 34. Re6) 32. Qe7+ Kg8 $1 33. Qd8+ Kg7 {Nagesh,Havanur: '+-' '+-' '+-' Nagesh,Havanur: 'Soon Black runs out of moves, either falling into a mating net or losing his queenside pawns.'} 34. Qc7+ Kg8 35. e7) 30... Qxf4 {Nagesh,Havanur: 'Forced.'} 31. Bxf4 Re8 (31... Rxa2 {=} 32. Rxa2 {?} (32. Rad1 {= 'with the idea' g4, Kg5} Ra7) 32... Nxa2 $18 {!} 33. Ne5 g5 34. Bg3) (31... Ra6 {= 'with the idea' Re5} {Nagesh,Havanur: 'not'} 32. Rad1 Rxe6 {!} 33. Rd7) 32. Rad1 {Nagesh,Havanur: 'The point. White exploits the weak second rank.'} Ra6 (32... Rxa2 {!} 33. Rd7 Ra6 34. Bb1) 33. Rd7 (33. Bb7 $19 Ra7 34. Rd7) 33... Rxe6 34. Ng5 {''} Rf6 (34... Ra6 35. Bb1 Kf6 $18 36. Ne4+ {??} Kf7 37. Nxc5) 35. Bf3 Rxf4 {Nagesh,Havanur: '?!' '?!' '?!' Nagesh,Havanur: 'Gligoric,Svetozar: '?'' Nagesh,Havanur: 'By now Spassky was in time trouble. Here he tries to activate his rook & bishop and at the same time keep away the White king from his advancing pawns. Unfortunately, it falls short of expectations.'} (35... Kf8 {= Kasparov} 36. Nh7+ {?}) 36. Ne6+ Kf6 37. Nxf4 Ne5 38. Rb7 Bd6 {?!} 39. Kf1 Nc2 (39... Nxf3 40. Rxe8 Nd2+ 41. Ke2 Bxf4 42. Rf8+ Kg5 43. Rxf4 Kxf4 44. Kxd2) 40. Re4 $1 {Nagesh,Havanur: 'Gligoric,Svetozar: '?''} Nd4 $6 {Nagesh,Havanur: 'Gligoric,Svetozar: '?'' ? %04Time} 41. Rb6 {Sealed move Nagesh,Havanur: 'The sealed move. During the adjournment Spassky and his seconds could find no way of saving the game.'} Rd8 42. Nd5+ $1 { 43.b5 Nagesh,Havanur: 'Gligoric,Svetozar: '+-!'' '+-'} Kf5 43. Ne3+ $1 Ke6 (43... Kf6 44. Be2 {?} b4 45. f4) 44. Be2 Kd7 {Nagesh,Havanur: 'This attempt to prevent g4-g5 does not alter the outcome of the game.'} 45. Bxb5+ Nxb5 46. Rxb5 {Nagesh,Havanur: '!' '!' '!' Nagesh,Havanur: 'Pinning the c-pawn so that its companion can be captured.'} Kc6 47. a4 Bc7 48. Ke2 g5 49. g3 $1 { 50.e6# ! Nagesh,Havanur: 'A little joke.'} Ra8 50. Rb2 Rf8 51. f4 gxf4 52. gxf4 Nf7 53. Re6+ Nd6 (53... Bd6 $18 {If} 54. Rf6 $4) 54. f5 Ra8 55. Rd2 { 56.e8} Rxa4 56. f6 $1 {Nagesh,Havanur: '...and Spassky resigned.'} Rf4 $1 57. Nd5 Re4+ {Nagesh,Havanur: 'Gligoric,Svetozar: '+-''} 58. Rxe4 Nxe4 {'+-'} 59. f7 1-0

