{R.Scherbakov: 'Black was accurate in the opening and White was unable to obtain any serious pressure. At some point he could even have faced some problems but Black was rather peaceful and after some manoeuvres the game ended with a most likely result.'} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Ba4 Nf6 5. O-O Be7 6. Re1 b5 7. Bb3 O-O 8. c3 d6 9. h3 h6 10. d4 Re8 {R.Scherbakov: '!?'} 11. Nbd2 Bf8 12. Nf1 {Gligoric,Svetozar: '!' R.Scherbakov: 'ChessBase: 'Gligoric,Svetozar: '!'''} Bd7 {Gligoric,Svetozar: '!' R.Scherbakov: 'ChessBase: 'Gligoric,Svetozar: '!'''} 13. Ng3 Na5 14. Bc2 c5 15. b3 (15. d5 {and so on.} Nc4) 15... cxd4 (15... Nc6 16. d5 {'' 'pair of bishops' Tal} (16. Be3 exd4 17. cxd4 cxd4 18. Nxd4 d5)) 16. cxd4 Nc6 17. Bb2 g6 18. Qd2 Bg7 19. Rad1 $1 {Timman Gligoric,Svetozar: '!' R.Scherbakov: 'ChessBase: '!' ChessBase: 'Timman Gligoric,Svetozar: '!'''} Qb6 $8 {Gligoric,Svetozar: '!' R.Scherbakov: 'ChessBase: '' ChessBase: 'Gligoric,Svetozar: '!'''} 20. Nf1 {?!} Rad8 21. Ne3 $1 {R.Scherbakov: 'ChessBase: '!''} Qb8 22. Bb1 {R.Scherbakov: 'White has a pair of bishops but the ending is not yet on the board. Besides, a pair of Q-side pawns might be exchanged.'} Qb7 { 23... c5 Timman R.Scherbakov: 'ChessBase: ' 23... c5 Timman''} 23. Rc1 {R.Scherbakov: 'Otherwise Black was fine after ...Nd7-c5, when he had slightly more active rooks and minor pieces.'} Kh7 24. a3 Bc8 $1 {Timman R.Scherbakov: 'Securing a solid position - it is very difficult for White to give his opponent any problems. ChessBase: '!' ChessBase: 'Timman'' ! =} 25. Bc3 {R.Scherbakov: 'This is harmless for Black.'} Bd7 26. Qb2 Qb8 {Gligoric,Svetozar: '' R.Scherbakov: 'ChessBase: 'Gligoric,Svetozar: ''''} 27. b4 Kg8 {Gligoric,Svetozar: '!' R.Scherbakov: 'ChessBase: 'Gligoric,Svetozar: '!'''} 28. Rcd1 Nh7 29. Ba2 {=} Ng5 30. Nxg5 hxg5 {R.Scherbakov: 'Black is just fine - he has no problems and White's bishops are rather passive.'} 31. dxe5 {R.Scherbakov: 'White avoids the repetition but he has no real chances to get an advantage and may only bring problems.' ?!} dxe5 {!} 32. Nd5 Ne7 33. Nxe7+ Rxe7 34. Qd2 Bf6 {Gligoric,Svetozar: '!' R.Scherbakov: 'ChessBase: 'Gligoric,Svetozar: '!'''} 35. Qd6 {Gligoric,Svetozar: '!' R.Scherbakov: '?!' R.Scherbakov: 'ChessBase: 'Gligoric,Svetozar: '!'''} Kg7 {R.Scherbakov: '?!' R.Scherbakov: 'Missing a chance to get the advantage.'} 36. Qxa6 (36. Bxe5 {??} Rxe5 $19 37. Qxb8 $5 {was more promising, trying to get the bishop to d4. However, Black kept good control over the position: ! 'with the idea' Bd4} Rxb8 38. Rxd7) 36... Rc8 37. Rd6 {R.Scherbakov: 'Now White is OK.'} Rxc3 38. Rxf6 Be6 39. Rxe6 fxe6 40. Rd1 Qb7 41. Qxb7 {Abgabezug  42.e4, 43.e5 Gligoric,Svetozar: '[ e4]' R.Scherbakov: 'ChessBase: 'Abgabezug  42.e4, 43.e5 Gligoric,Svetozar: '[ e4]''' Sealed move 'with the idea' e4} Rxb7 {R.Scherbakov: 'Preventing White's e-pawn advance.' !} 42. Bxe6 Rxa3 {!} 43. Kh2 Ra4 44. Rb1 Rc7 45. f3 {R.Scherbakov: 'White has managed to weaken his opponent's king but he has no chances to exploit it.'} Ra6 {Gligoric,Svetozar: '=' R.Scherbakov: 'ChessBase: 'Gligoric,Svetozar: '='''} 46. Bb3 Ra3 47. Rb2 Ra1 {Gligoric,Svetozar: '!' R.Scherbakov: 'ChessBase: 'Gligoric,Svetozar: '!'''} 48. Kg3 Kf6 49. Kg4 Rc3 50. Bd5 Raa3 { 51... h4 Purdy Gligoric,Svetozar: '!' R.Scherbakov: 'ChessBase: ' 51... h4 Purdy Gligoric,Svetozar: '!'''} 51. h4 gxh4 52. Kxh4 {R.Scherbakov: 'Giving his opponent a chance to get an extra pawn, which cannot change the outcome.'} Ra1 {!} 53. Rd2 Raa3 54. Kg4 Rd3 55. Rc2 (55. Re2 Rac3) 55... Rac3 {R.Scherbakov: 'Draw agreed.'} 56. Ra2 Ra3 {Purdy} 57. Rc2 $2 {?} (57. Rb2) 1/2-1/2

