1. e4 c6 2. d4 d5 3. exd5 cxd5 4. Nf3 Nf6 5. c3 Bf5 6. Bb5+ Nbd7 7. Nh4 Bg6 8. Bf4 e6 {In "Schach Archiv" 1971, Euwe remarks that the maneuver g8-g6 seems to entail more drawbacks than advantages for Black.} 9. Nd2 {"From here the white  brings pressure to bear on Black's e-pawn; on the other hand, the position of the white  gives Black the additional possibility of f6-g4 with tactical threats." (Zeuthen/Jarlnaes 71)} Nh5 10. Nxg6 hxg6 11. Be3 Bd6 12. g3 a6 (12... O-O) (12... Nhf6) 13. Bd3 Rc8 (13... Nhf6) 14. O-O Nb6 15. a4 Rc7 16. Qb3 Nc8 17. c4 $14 {(Zeuthen/Jarlnaes 71)} dxc4 18. Nxc4 Nf6 19. Rac1 (19. Na5 $10 {(eco 74/81) Strelakovsky-Petrov USSR 1955 If 13 0-0-0, game transposes to main variation.} b6 20. Nc4 Nd5 21. Nxd6+ Nxd6 22. Bxa6) 19... O-O 20. Bd2 Nd5 21. Be4 Be7 22. Na5 Ncb6 23. Bxd5 Nxd5 24. Nxb7 Qb8 25. Rxc7 Qxc7 26. Rc1 Qb8 27. Rc4 Rd8 28. Bc3 Rd7 29. Na5 Qxb3 30. Rc8+ Kh7 31. Nxb3 Nb6 32. Rc6 Nxa4 33. Rxa6 Nxc3 34. bxc3 Rc7 35. Nd2 Rxc3 36. Ra7 Rd3 37. Nf1 Bf6 38. Rxf7 Rxd4 39. Kg2 g5 40. h3 Kg6 41. Rc7 Ra4 42. Nd2 Rd4 43. Nb3 Rd6 44. Nc5 Kf5 45. Kf3 Rb6 46. Rd7 Rc6 47. Ne4 Ra6 48. Rd3 Be7 49. Rb3 Ra3 50. Rxa3 Bxa3 51. g4+ Kg6 52. Ke3 Bc1+ 53. Kd4 Bf4 54. Kc5 {Fischer's Chess Games p150#284 (Wade/O'Connell)} Kf7 55. Kb6 Ke8 56. Kc6 Ke7 1-0

