{Bobby Fischer: 'GAME N. 17 A very near miss. This is one of the four games that Fischer lost to Tal who, in winning this tournament, earned the right to meet and trounce Botvinnik for the world championship. In jest the whimsical Tal signed Fischer's name, in addition to his own, when asked for an autograph. "Why not?" he quipped; "I've beaten Bobby so often ... that gives me the right to sign for him!" A careful reading of Fischer's notes will reveal a clear echo of the strong emotions that engulfed him during this tense encounter. He misses a win in the opening and several draws along the way, demonstrating dramatically how a continuously advantageous position can abruptly be turned into defeat by seemingly insignificant miscalculations. '} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 e6 6. g4 Nc6 ({Bobby Fischer: 'not'} 6... a6 $2) 7. g5 Nd7 $1 8. Ndb5 $5 Nb6 $1 (8... Nc5 9. Bf4 e5 $16 {Bobby Fischer: 'Such a surprise that I didn't dare believe my eyes! 1 had expected'} 10. Be3 a6 11. Bxc5 dxc5 12. Qxd8+ Kxd8 $14 {Bobby Fischer: 'l and White has a slight edge after a3 because of Black's disconnected Pawns.'} {Bobby Fischer: 'The right move is simply'} 13. O-O-O+ $1 Bd7 14. Nd5 $16) 9. Bf4 Ne5 10. Qh5 Ng6 $2 (10... g6 {Bobby Fischer: 'Many annotators believed that'} 11. Qh3 {Bobby Fischer: 'was the winning move. Tal himself confessed he thought Black was lost after that. But 22 .'} Nec4 $1 12. Bxc4 Nxc4 $1 13. Qd3 Nxb2 14. Qd4 e5 15. Bxe5 dxe5 16. Qxe5+ Be6 $1 17. O-O Rc8 18. Rfd1 Nxd1 $10 {Bobby Fischer: '='} 19. Rxd1 Qxd1+ $1 20. Nxd1 $2 Rg8 $18 {Bobby Fischer: 'wins'} {Bobby Fischer: 'holds all lines'} 21. Ne3 $2 a6 22. Nd6+ Bxd6 $1 23. Qxd6 Rf8 24. f4 Rd8 $18 {Bobby Fischer: 'wins. I've studied this position for ages, it seems, and the best I can find is'} {Bobby Fischer: 'White remains a clear Pawn ahead after 20 ..'} 25. Qb6) 11. Be3 $1 a6 12. Nd4 Ne5 (12... d5 13. O-O-O $17 {Bobby Fischer: 'preserves drawing chances.'} Bb4 {Bobby Fischer: 'is met, as always, by ..'} 14. Nde2 $1 {Bobby Fischer: 'Once White can eliminate Black's b-Pawn it's a theoretical draw.'} Nc4 $2 15. Kb1 $10 {Bobby Fischer: '='} {Bobby Fischer: 'I overlooked this. Now Black has winning chances. I had planned on a draw after'} Nxe3 $2 16. fxe3 {Bobby Fischer: 'dissolving Black's b-Pawn'} Qb6 {Bobby Fischer: 'is answered by'} 17. exd5 {Bobby Fischer: 'followed by'} Qxe3 18. Qg4 {Bobby Fischer: 'Creating losing chances. I don't see how Black can make any progress after'} Qb6 $142 19. Qe4 O-O 20. h4 Ne7 21. Na4 Qa5 $10 {Bobby Fischer: '=' Bobby Fischer: 'etc'} {Bobby Fischer: 'on'} 22. Nf4 Qxa4 $10 {Bobby Fischer: '=' Bobby Fischer: 'White should draw with best play.'} {Bobby Fischer: 'On the wrong track. Right is'} 23. Bd3 $1 g6 24. d6 Nd5 25. a3 $146 {Bobby Fischer: 'draws, since Black can't possibly build up a winning K-side attack and his own King is too exposed.'} {Bobby Fischer: 'if'} Nxf4 26. Qxf4 $1 a5 27. h5) (12... Qc7 $10 {Bobby Fischer: '=' Bobby Fischer: 'draws'} {Bobby Fischer: 'on'} 13. O-O-O Bd7 14. f4 e5 $10 {Bobby Fischer: '='} {Bobby Fischer: 'not'} 15. Nf5 Nxf4 16. Qf3 g6 17. Qf2 Na4 18. Nxa4 Bxa4 $19 {Bobby Fischer: 'wins.'} 19. Ng3 Rc8 $18 {Bobby Fischer: 'Finally Tal "develops" his Bishop. Not'} 20. Rd2 h6 $1 21. gxh6 Bxh6 22. c3 Bc6 $18 {Bobby Fischer: 'wins.'} {Bobby Fischer: 'Black holds after'} 23. h4 Qe7 24. h5 Nxh5 {Bobby Fischer: 'etc.'} {Bobby Fischer: 'if'} 25. Rxh5 gxh5 26. Nf5 $2 Bxe3 $1 {Bobby Fischer: 'and on'} 27. Qxe3) 13. Rd1 $1 g6 14. Qe2 $2 Bd7 15. h4 h6 $1 ({Bobby Fischer: 'Too passive. I wanted to avoid ilnmobilizing my Q-side Pawns with'} 15... h5 $142 {Bobby Fischer: 'but it's the best hope now. On'}) 16. Bg2 hxg5 17. Bxg5 $2 Be7 $1 18. f4 Nc6 $1 19. Bxe7 Qxe7 $1 20. Qf2 Nc8 21. Nf3 Qd8 22. b3 Qa5 23. Qe3 N8a7 24. O-O Qc5 25. Qxc5 dxc5 $1 26. Na4 Nd4 27. Nxc5 Nxf3+ 28. Rxf3 $1 Bc6 29. Rh3 Rc8 30. c4 Ke7 31. Kf2 b5 32. Bf1 $2 bxc4 33. bxc4 a5 34. e5 Rb8 $1 35. Rd2 Rb4 36. Be2 Nc8 37. Nb3 a4 38. Nd4 Be8 39. a3 Rb1 40. Bd3 $2 Ra1 41. Be4 Rc1 42. Rc2 Rxc2+ 43. Nxc2 f6 44. exf6+ Kxf6 $1 45. Ne3 Nd6 46. Bd3 Nb7 47. Ng4+ Kg7 48. Ne5 Nc5 49. Bc2 Bf7 50. Ke3 Rd8 (50... Be8 $19 {Bobby Fischer: 'wins.'}) 51. Rg3 Kf6 (51... Nd7 52. Nxf7 Kxf7 $19 {Bobby Fischer: 'on'} 53. Bxg6+ (53. Bxa4 Nb6 54. Bb3 Nc8) 53... Kf6 54. h5) 52. Bxg6 Bxg6 $1 (52... Rg8 53. Nxf7 $1 {[%emt 0:00:31] If 53 Kxc3 b1=Q+! The discovered-check theme is strangely reminiscent of the finale of game} {Bobby Fischer: 'Equally hopeless is'} Rxg6 54. Rxg6+ Kxg6 55. Ne5+ $19 {Bobby Fischer: 'etc'} Kf6) 53. Rxg6+ $1 Kf5 54. Rg5+ $1 Kf6 55. Ng4+ Ke7 $1 {0-1 (51) Fischer,R-Tal,M Bled/Zagreb/Belgrade 1959 My 60 Memorable Games [Bobby Fischer]} 56. Rxc5 $1 0-1

