1. e4 {Ivkov,Borislav Ivkov,Borislav} c5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 g6 4. Bxc6 bxc6 5. O-O Bg7 6. Re1 f6 (6... Nh6 7. c3 O-O 8. d4 $36 {Murrey,J (2450)-Balashov,Y (2590)/Moskva (open) 1991 (0-1, 45)} cxd4 $16 {Balashov} 9. cxd4 d5 $1 10. e5 Bg4 $44 {The weakness of the e4-square and of the whole white kingside offers Black excellent compensation for the sacrificed exchange.} 11. Nbd2 $5 {may be a try. In any case, the opening of the centre does not favour Black anymore:} (11. h3 Bxf3 12. Qxf3 Nf5) 11... Qb6 12. b3 (12. h3 Bxf3 13. Nxf3 $36 c5 {Ivkov,Borislav} 14. dxc5 Qxc5 15. Be3 Qb5) 12... c5 13. Ba3 cxd4 14. Bxe7 Rfe8 15. Bg5 Bd7) 7. c3 (7. e5 { c5}) 7... Nh6 8. d4 cxd4 9. cxd4 O-O 10. Nc3 (10. Qa4 Qb6 11. Na3) 10... d6 11. Qa4 Qb6 12. Nd2 (12. e5 fxe5 13. dxe5 Ng4) 12... Nf7 13. Nc4 Qa6 {With the bishop on b7, this regrouping is too slow and allows White to consolidate his space advantage.} (13... Qxd4 14. Be3) 14. Be3 {Ivkov,Borislav: 'N!' 'N!'} Qxa4 15. Nxa4 f5 16. exf5 {Ivkov,Borislav: '' ''} (16. f3 fxe4 17. fxe4 d5 18. Na5 $1 {The main idea of the move 13...d7 is revealed. The connection of the rooks is possible at once.}) 16... Bxf5 (16... gxf5) 17. Rac1 Rfc8 18. Na5 (18. b4 $5 Rab8 19. a3) 18... Bd7 19. b3 $14 {A dream position for Fischer. Black has absolutely no counterplay and has to wait for the execution.} (19. Rc4 e5 20. dxe5 (20. Rec1 exd4 $16 {Balashov,Y (2570)-Nikolaevsky,Y (2490)/Leningrad 1971/URS-ch (1-0, 61)} 21. Bxd4 $5 {may be a worthy try to prepare d6-d5, but further practice is needed.} Be6 {White clearly needs an improvement over this standard continuation. Things do not look too good if White answers a developing move with a modest pawn advance.}) 20... Nxe5 21. Rc2 Bf5) 19... Rab8 20. Nc3 Kf8 {Ivkov,Borislav: '?' '?'} 21. a3 (21. f3 h5 (21... Nd8) 22. h3 h4 23. Bf2 g5 24. Ne4) 21... Nh6 22. b4 {Ivkov,Borislav: '' ''} Nf5 23. Red1 Ke8 {Ivkov,Borislav: '!' '!'} (23... Nxe3 24. fxe3 Bh6 25. Rd3 Bf5 26. Rf1 Ke8 27. e4) 24. Ne4 Rb5 25. h3 h5 {Ivkov,Borislav: '??' '??'} 26. Rd2 {Ivkov,Borislav: '!' '!'} a6 (26... Be6 27. Rxc6 Rxc6 28. Nxc6 Bd5 29. Nxa7 $14 {Despite simplifications, Black cannot easily neutralise White's pressure.} Rb7 30. Nc3) 27. Kf1 Rd5 28. Rcd1 (28. Nc3 Rxd4 29. Bxd4 Nxd4 30. Rdd1 Bf5) 28... Rb5 {Ivkov,Borislav: '?' '?'} 29. Ke2 {Ivkov,Borislav: '+-!' '+-!'} (29. Rc1 Rd5) 29... Be6 30. Rc1 Kd7 31. Nc3 {Ivkov,Borislav: '!' '!'} Rbb8 (31... Rxa5 {[%cal Gd2f3]} 32. bxa5 Bc4+ $36 33. Ke1 Nh4 $1 $44 34. f3) 32. Kf1 h4 {Ivkov,Borislav: '?' '?'} (32... Bd5 33. Nxd5 cxd5 34. Rxc8 Rxc8 35. Rd3 Rc2) (32... Bf7) 33. Ke2 Bf6 34. Ne4 Bd5 {Ivkov,Borislav: '?!' '?!'} 35. Kd3 (35. Nxf6+ exf6 $6 {This gives up the exchange for nothing.}) (35. f3 Bxe4 36. fxe4 $14 {Spassky,B-Medina Garcia,A/Palma de Mallorca 1969/MCD (1-0, 30)} Nxe3 {would have required from White the taking of some risks in order to maintain the initiative.} 37. Kxe3 Bg5+) 35... Bg7 36. Rdc2 Rc7 (36... e5 $6 {Ivkov,Borislav: '!?' '!?' has been tried a couple of times, but is unsound.} 37. dxe5 Nxe3 38. fxe3 Bxe5) 37. Re1 Rf8 38. f3 Rb8 (38... Nxe3 39. Rxe3 $16 Rf5 {(Ivkov,Borislav) Ü 7/272}) 39. Nc3 {Ivkov,Borislav: '!' '!'} Bg8 40. Ne2 Bf7 (40... g5 41. Bxg5 $18 Bh7 {Ivkov,Borislav}) 41. Bd2 Bf6 42. Rec1 {Ivkov,Borislav: '!' '!'} Rbc8 43. Nc4 Rb7 44. Na5 Rbc7 {Ivkov,Borislav} 45. Nc4 {Ivkov,Borislav} Rb7 1-0

