{GM Mihail Marin: 'In this game we will see a completely different Fischer. He was more mature than in the previous game, of course, but had not played any single tournament game over the previous 20 years! Still, he could produce perfect games, at least once in 3-4 games.'} 1. e4 {GM Mihail Marin} e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Ba4 Nf6 5. O-O Be7 6. Re1 b5 7. Bb3 d6 8. c3 O-O 9. h3 Nb8 10. d4 Nbd7 11. Nbd2 Bb7 12. Bc2 Re8 13. Nf1 Bf8 14. Ng3 {GM Mihail Marin: 'Black has almost completed his development and enjoys a space advantage. A familiar situation after all. However, all the space he has gained so far implies certain obligations. Should he play only neutral moves, White could prepare either d3-d4 or b2-b4.'} g6 {GM Mihail Marin: 'By far the most popular continuation.'} 15. Bg5 {GM Mihail Marin: '!?' GM Mihail Marin: 'Inducing the slight weakening of the kingside.'} h6 16. Bd2 {GM Mihail Marin: 'One should pay attention to White's regrouping. Both his bishops and his knights are perfectly coordinated, controlling a series of complementary squares and yielding White's position hidden dynamic resources.'} exd4 $6 (16... c5 {GM Mihail Marin: 'may run into'} 17. d5 {GM Mihail Marin: ', which is not entirely clear, though.'} c4 18. b4 cxb3 19. axb3 Qc7 20. Bd3 Nc5 $15 {Illescas-Ivanchuk Linares 1992} 21. Bf1 $2 Reb8 22. c4 bxc4 $17 {Kamsky-Timman Tilburg 1990 (inf. 50/387)} 23. Ba5 {GM Mihail Marin} Qe7 24. Bxc4 Bc8 25. Ra3 Bd7 26. Qe2 {with certain initiatives. We can notice that the square on c5 is weak.} Bb5 $2 27. Rc1 Bxc4 28. Qxc4 $1 Rc8 29. Qe2 Qb7 30. Rc3 Qb5 31. Qc2) 17. cxd4 {GM Mihail Marin: 'A fierce tactical battle starts now.'} c5 $1 18. d5 $1 (18. Bf4 cxd4 19. Nxd4 Ne5 20. b3 d5 $14 {Tseshkovsky-Lukacs Trnava 1986} 21. Qd2 dxe4 {½-½ Matulovic-Tringov Vrnjacka Banja 1990} 22. Nxe4 {GM Mihail Marin} Nd5 {had been played in Teichmann,R-Przepiorka,D Munich 1909 (1-0, 26), examined later.} 23. Bg3 Rc8 24. Re2 f5 25. Bxe5 Rxe5 {½-½ Parma-Geller Kapfenberg EUchT 1970} 26. Ng3 Rxe2 27. Ngxe2 Nb4 28. Rd1 Nxc2 29. Nxc2 Qxd2 30. Rxd2 Rc7 31. Ne3 Kf7 $14 {Kuzmin,G-Kruppa URS sf 1989} 32. h4 $1 {GM Mihail Marin: '!?'} Bc8) 18... Nb6 (18... Bg7 19. Bf4 $18 {GM Mihail Marin: 'Seirawan. Actually '} (19. a4 Nb6 20. Ba5 $1 Nfd7 21. Rb1 b4 22. Nd2 Bd4 23. Nf3 Bg7 24. Nf1 $14 {[%csl Rd5,Rh6][%cal Gh2g4,Gg4e3] The black kingside is a bit exposed to Ng4 and the square on d5 is weak.} Qb8 $6 25. N1d2 $16 Nc8 26. Nc4 $16 Na7 $2 27. Qd2 Nb5 28. Bd3 $18 Bc8 29. Ra1 $16 Nd4 30. Nxd4 {[%cal Gf3d5] attacking f7 and threatening Qxd5 wins.} Bxd4 31. Kh1 Ne5 32. f4 {offers Black a lot of space, Campora,D (2485)-Hazai,L (2480) Nis 1985 (1-0, 40)} Nxc4 33. Bxc4 Bb7) 19... Nb6 20. Rc1 Nfd7 21. b3 Qe7 22. Qd2 $18 {GM Mihail Marin: 'Seirawan'} h5 {GM Mihail Marin} 23. Bg5 Qf8 24. Nh4 {GM Mihail Marin} Bb2 25. Re3 Re5 26. Ngf5 $18 {Marin} Nxd5 $1 {GM Mihail Marin} 27. exd5 Bxc1 28. Qxc1 Rxe3 29. Qxe3 Re8 30. Be7 gxf5 31. Nxf5 Kh8 $16 {Marin Suddenly, WHite has excellent attacking chances.} 32. Qc3+ {(GM Mihail Marin) followed by ...d6-d5 was recommended by Seirawan, who apparently did not know that it had been played.}) 19. Ba5 (19. h4 Bc8 20. h5 g5 21. Ba5 Rb8) (19. Qc1 $18 Kh7 {GM Mihail Marin: '?'} 20. h4) 19... Nfd7 {GM Mihail Marin: '?' GM Mihail Marin: 'Missing or under-evaluating White's answer.'} 20. b3 $18 (20. Nd2 Bg7 21. Rb1 Qh4) (20. a3 Bg7 21. Rb1 Qe7 22. b3 Rac8 23. Nf1 (23. a4 bxa4 24. bxa4 Nc4 25. Rxb7 Nxa5 26. Rb1 $14 c4 27. Ne2 Nc5) 23... c4 24. N1d2 cxb3 25. Bxb3 Ba8 (25... Qf8 26. a4 f5 27. axb5 $18 {GM Mihail Marin: 'Hansen'} axb5 28. Bc2 $132 (28. Ba2 {GM Mihail Marin} Ba6 29. Bb4 Kh7 $19 {Marin} 30. exf5 $5 {(GM Mihail Marin) Marin} Qxf5)) 26. a4 bxa4 27. Bxa4 Nxa4 28. Qxa4 Nc5 {1-0 Conterno,D-Beckett,P (2139) ICCF email 2006} 29. Qa3 f5 30. exf5 Qf6 31. fxg6 Bxd5) 20... Bg7 21. Rc1 {22.f6+/22.bxa5 GM Mihail Marin: '22.Nf6+/ 22.bxa5 White wins a piece and Black will not have enough compensation for it.'} Qf6 22. Rb1 (22. h4 h5 