1. e4 {ChessBase ChessBase 1) Uhlmann,Wofgang: Meine besten Partien. St.Ingbert. 2015. S.6-10.} e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Ba4 Nf6 5. O-O Be7 6. Re1 b5 7. Bb3 d6 8. c3 O-O 9. d3 (9. h3 Nb8) 9... Na5 10. Bc2 c5 11. Nbd2 Re8 12. h3 Bf8 $6 13. Nf1 $1 Bb7 14. Ng3 g6 $1 {"Uhlmann gruppeirt um, weil seine Chancen auf dem Konigsflugel liegen." (Schwarz 67)} (14... h6 15. Nh2 d5 16. Ng4 Re6 17. Nf5) (14... Qc7 15. Bg5 Nd7 16. Bd2 d5 17. b4 cxb4 18. cxb4 Nc6 19. a3 Nb6 20. Bb3) (14... d5 15. exd5 Qxd5 16. Bg5 Qc6 (16... Nd7 17. Qe2 (17. Bd2 b4) 17... h6 18. Bd2 Qd6 19. Ne4 Qc7 20. Nh4 Re6 21. Rac1 Qd8 22. Nf5 Nf6) 17. a4 (17. Nf5 h6 18. Bd2 e4) (17. a3 Rac8 18. Bxf6 (18. b4 cxb4 19. axb4 Qxc3) 18... Qxf6 19. Ne4 Qd8 20. b4) 17... h6 18. axb5 axb5 19. Bd2 c4) 15. Bg5 $1 {ChessBase: '"With this and the following series of fine moves, White ensures an excellent diagonal for his QB and paralyzes any hopes Black may have for meaningful counterplay." (Mednis 74)' "With this and the following series of fine moves, White ensures an excellent diagonal for his QB and paralyzes any hopes Black may have for meaningful counterplay." (Mednis 74) ! Uhlmann: Weiss verhindert Sf5 und kann so seinen Läufer auf der Diagonalen b8-h2 behaupten.} (15. a3 Bg7 16. Bg5 h6 17. Be3 Nc6 18. Qd2 Kh7 19. Rad1) (15. d4 Bg7) (15. a4 d5) 15... h6 16. Bd2 $1 d5 (16... Nc6 17. Nh2 d5 18. exd5 (18. Ng4 Nxg4 19. hxg4 d4) 18... Qxd5 (18... Nxd5 19. Ng4 h5 (19... Kh7 20. Qf3) 20. Nh6+ Kg7 (20... Bxh6 21. Bxh6) 21. Nxh5+ gxh5 22. Qxh5) 19. Ne4 Nxe4 20. dxe4 Qd6 21. Qe2 Rad8 22. Rad1) 17. exd5 $1 {"Weiss will auf den dunklen Feldern zu eimem Ubergewicht kommen, daher die Linienoffnung fur den Th8." (Schwarz 67)} c4 (17... Qxd5 18. c4 (18. Qc1 Kh7 19. c4 Qd8 20. Nxe5 Qc7 21. Bxa5 Qxa5 22. d4 cxd4 23. Qf4) 18... Qd8 (18... bxc4 19. Bxa5 cxd3 20. Bxd3 (20. Qxd3 Qxd3 21. Bxd3 e4 22. Bc3) 20... e4 21. Bc3 exf3 22. Rxe8 Nxe8) 19. Nxe5) 18. b4 $1 {"Fischers Plan sieht gut aus: er will den Laufer auf der Diagonale h2-b8 wirken lassen." (Schwarz 67)} (18. Nxe5 Qxd5 19. Nf3 cxd3 20. Bb3 Nc4) (18. d4 exd4 19. Rxe8 Nxe8 (19... Qxe8 20. cxd4 b4 (20... Qd8 21. Bxg6 fxg6 22. Qc2) 21. d6 Bxd6 22. Bxh6) 20. Nxd4 Nf6 21. Ne4 Nxd5 22. Qg4) 18... cxd3 (18... cxb3 19. axb3 Bxd5 20. c4 Bxf3 21. Qxf3 b4 22. Rxa5 Qxa5 23. Qxf6) 19. Bxd3 Qxd5 {[#]} (19... Nc4 20. Bxc4 bxc4 21. Nxe5 Qxd5 22. Nf3 a5 23. Rxe8 Rxe8 24. a3 Bg7 25. Qf1 Kh7 26. Rd1 Qb5 27. Nd4 Qa4 28. Ra1 Ba6 29. Qb1 Qd7 30. b5 Bb7 31. Qf1 Rd8 32. Qxc4 Rc8 33. Qd3 a4 34. Re1 Qd5 35. Qf3 Qd7 36. Qe2 Rc7 37. Nc2 Qd5 38. Ne3 Qc5 39. c4 Qxa3 40. Ba5 Rc8 41. Qd2 Ra8 42. Bc3 Kg8 43. Be5 Re8 44. Ra1 Qe7 45. Bd6 Qe6 46. Rxa4 Rd8 47. c5 Ne8 48. Nc4 Bf8 49. Qa5 Nxd6 50. Qxd8 Nxc4 51. c6 Bxc6 52. bxc6 Qxc6 53. Ra8 Qd6 54. Qe8 Kg7 55. Ne4 Qe7 56. Qc6 Ne5 57. Qc3 f6 58. Rc8 Nf7 59. Nxf6 Qxf6 60. Qxf6+) 20. Be4 $2 {"But this brute force attempt at an immediate win spoils everything." (Mednis 74) Sperrt den Lh1 ein, und Schwarz will ihn blockiert lassen.} (20. Ne4 Nh5 (20... Nd7 21. Bxh6 Bxh6 22. bxa5) 21. Bxh6 Bxh6 22. bxa5 (22. g4 Red8) 22... Rad8) 20... Nxe4 $6 {ChessBase: '!' '!'} (20... Qc4 $1 $16 {(Schwarz 67, Mednis 74)} 21. Qb1 (21. Qc2 Nc6 $5 {(Ivkov)} 22. Bxg6 Rad8 23. Ne4 {ChessBase: '' ''} Nxe4 $14 {(Keres 69)} 24. Bxe4 Nxb4 25. cxb4 Qxc2 26. Bxc2 Bxf3) 21... Nc6 $1 22. Bxg6 fxg6 (22... Rad8 23. Ne4 $142) 23. Qxg6+ Bg7 $16 {(Schwarz 67)} 24. Nf5 $4) 21. Nxe4 Bg7 $3 {"Black sacrifices a pawn and allows a protected passed pawn to boot, for the strategic objective of locking in White's QB. The damage done by White's 20 f4? is now very obvious." (Mednis 74) Uhlmann: Mit dem Bauernopfer wird der Läufer auf h2 endgültig bis zum Partienende aus dem Verkehr gezogen.} (21... Be7 22. bxa5 f5 23. c4 bxc4 24. Nc3) (21... Re6 $13 {(eco 74/81)} 22. bxa5 $6 f5 23. Ng3 e4 24. Nd4 e3 $1 $16 {(Schwarz 67)} 25. f3) 22. bxa5 f5 $1 23. Ng3 (23. c4 bxc4 {hätten wir mit Zugumstellung die Partiestellung auf dem Brett.} (23... Qd8 {Klavin-Fuchs 1961} 24. Nc5 Bxf3 25. gxf3) 24. Nc3 Qc6 (24... Qxa5 25. Rb1) (24... Qf7 25. Be3 (25. Nh2 Rad8 26. Rb1 Rd3 27. Qc1 Kh7 28. Rb6 Red8 29. Nf1) 25... Rad8 26. Qc1 e4 $1 {Gligoric-Sokolov 1956} 27. Nh2 Rd3) 25. Rb1 $1 {"... White has a marvelous position: pressure on Black's somewhat shaky center, open diagonals for both Bishops, while Black's King can find himself uncomfortably open soon." (Mednis 74)} Rad8 26. Qc1) 23... e4 24. Nh4 ({Nach} 24. Nh2 e3) 24... Bf6 (24... Rad8 $5 25. Be3 (25. Re2 Bxc3 26. Nxg6 $17 {(Schwarz 67)} Bxd2 $5 {Befreit den Lh2.}) (25. Bxh6 Bxh6 26. Nxg6 f4) 25... Qf7 26. Qc1 $142 $1 Rd3 27. Bxh6 {(Schwarz 67)} (27. Ne2 g5 $5) (27. Bd4 $2 f4 28. Ngf5 gxf5 29. Qxf4)) (24... Kh7 25. Nxg6 (25. Be3 $1 {Lässt f4xg5 nicht zu.}) 25... Kxg6 26. Qh5+ $11 {(Schwarz 67, Mednis 74) ChessBase: 'N' 'N'} Kh7 $2 27. Bxh6 Bxh6 28. Nxf5 $1 {(Schwarz 67)} Qe6 29. Rad1 $1) 25. Nxg6 e3 26. Nf4 $8 Qxd2 27. Rxe3 {"Fischer evaluates this position much too optimistically and plans to husband the extra Pawn to victory. The blocked nature of the position makes winning attempts for either side less than fruitful." (Mednis 74)} Qxd1+ 28. Rxd1 Rxe3 $1 {"Now we have a rather full blockade and the game could well be called a draw here." (Mednis 74)} 29. fxe3 $2 Rd8 $1 {[#]} (29... Bxc3 30. Nxf5 Bxa5 31. Rd7 Be4 $15 {(Mednis 74)} 32. Nxh6+ $10) 30. Rxd8+ $4 Bxd8 $1 31. Nxf5 Bxa5 32. Nd5 (32. Nxh6+ Kh7 {(Wade/O'Connell)} 33. Nf5 $8 Bxc3) (32. Ne7+ Kf7 33. Ned5) 32... Kf8 $1 (32... Bxd5 $19 {(Mednis 74)} 33. Ne7+ Kf7 34. Nxd5 Ke6 35. Nb4 Bxb4 36. cxb4 {(Schwarz 67)} Kd5 $2 37. Kf2 Kc4 38. a3 $19 Kb3 $2 39. e4) 33. e4 $5 {"Bobby finally realized that he must be lost and thus characteristically goes for active counterplay. It is not good enough, but is as good a try as any." (Mednis 74)} Bxd5 34. exd5 h5 $1 35. Kf2 Bxc3 36. Ke3 Kf7 $1 37. Kd3 Bb2 38. g4 hxg4 39. hxg4 Kf6 40. d6 Ke6 41. g5 a5 (41... Kxf5 42. d7) 42. g6 Bf6 43. g7 Kf7 44. d7 (44. d7 Bd8 (44... a4 $10 {(Mednis 74)} 45. Nd6+ Kg8 $19 (45... 