{Bobby Fischer: 'GAME N. 6 A small oversight. Fischer's openini repertoire has been less extensive than most practicing Grandmasters', yet his contributions to theory have been numerous. 20 g5!? is one of his innovations. However. it is not responsible for Shocron's defeat. Neither Is Shocron's response; In retrospect. his system of defense seems sutprlslllfly adequate. Neventheless. after defending sensibly. Shocron outfoxes himself. Thinking he has seen one move further than his adversary; he provokes a combination. but his vision is one move short. In consequence, though otherwise it had withstood all of Fischer's assaults, his game crumbles. '} 1. e4 {Shipov,Sergei Shipov,Sergei Bobby Fischer Shipov,Sergei: 'Shipov'} c5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 g6 4. Bxc6 bxc6 5. O-O Bg7 6. Re1 e5 7. b4 cxb4 8. a3 c5 (8... b3) 9. axb4 cxb4 10. d4 exd4 11. Bb2 d6 12. Nxd4 Qd7 (12... Qb6 13. Nd2 $14 {Bobby Fischer: '!' Bobby Fischer: 'with drawing chances.'} {on} Bxd4 {Bobby Fischer} 14. Nc4 {followed by Bd5 should win.} {not} Bxf2+ $2 {Bobby Fischer} 15. Kh1 $1 {Bobby Fischer: 'if'} Qc5 16. Nxd6+ Ke7 17. Rf1 Qxd6 18. Qf3 $1) 13. Nd2 Bb7 (13... Ne7 {Bobby Fischer: '!'}) 14. Nc4 Nh6 (14... Ne7 15. Nb5) 15. Nf5 (15. Nb5) 15... Bxb2 16. Ncxd6+ Kf8 17. Nxh6 f6 (17... Bxa1 18. Qxa1 $18 {Bobby Fischer: 'is crushing.'} {Bobby Fischer: 'Correct is'} Qxd6 $3 {Bobby Fischer: '!' Bobby Fischer: 'and it is not clear how white can improve his position any further. If'} 19. Qxh8+ Ke7 $1 20. Qxh7 Qe6) 18. Ndf7 Qxd1 19. Raxd1 Ke7 $6 20. Nxh8 Rxh8 21. Nf5+ gxf5 $8 22. exf5+ Be5 $1 23. f4 Rc8 24. fxe5 (24. Rd2 $18 {Bobby Fischer: 'wins his queen.'} {Bobby Fischer: 'having seen that'} Rc5 {Bobby Fischer: '?'} 25. Rde2) 24... Rxc2 $10 25. e6 Bc6 26. Rc1 $1 Rxc1 27. Rxc1 Kd6 $1 28. Rd1+ Ke5 29. e7 a5 30. Rc1 Bd7 31. Rc5+ Kd4 32. Rxa5 b3 33. Ra7 $1 Be8 34. Rb7 Kc3 35. Kf2 $14 {× c4/} b2 36. Ke3 Bf7 37. g4 Kc2 38. Kd4 b1=Q $2 39. Rxb1 $1 Kxb1 40. Kc5 $1 $18 Kc2 $1 {Bobby Fischer: 'On'} 41. Kd6 1-0

