{Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'GAME N. 35 A brilliant cadenza. Called upon to face his favorite defense, Fischer quickly obtains the advantage against Block's rather passive opening strategy. Bolbochan, burdened with a bad Bishop against a good Knight, defends with extreme care but is gradually forced to retreat behind his lines. Disdaining several opportunities to enter a favorable ending, Fischer presses for a quick decision in the mid-game. His judgment is rewarded when the pressure which he painstakingly has accumulated erupts in a violent attack, beginning with 34.hxg6. Fischer 's invasion on the weakened squares is a model of accuracy. It culminates in a keen combination which, appropriately, earned a tie for the first brilliancy prize. ''} 1. e4 {Ftacnik Ftacnik,L Ftacnik,L Ftacnik,L Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer'} c6 2. d4 d5 3. exd5 cxd5 4. Bd3 Nc6 5. c3 Nf6 (5... Qc7) 6. Bf4 {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: ', Black's loss of time with ...a6 may possibly justify this loss of time. ''} (6. h3 e5) (6. Bg5 Ne4 7. Bxe4 dxe4 8. d5 Ne5 9. Qa4+ Qd7 10. Qxe4 Qf5) 6... Bg4 (6... g6) 7. Qb3 Na5 (7... Qc8) (7... b6) (7... Qb6) 8. Qa4+ Bd7 9. Qc2 e6 (9... a6) 10. Nf3 $1 Qb6 {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: '; Now the Knight interferes with the normal development of the QB.''} (10... b5) 11. a4 (11. O-O $19 {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'and Black wins.''} {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'After''} Bb5 12. Nbd2 Bxd3 13. Qxd3 Rc8 14. Rab1 Be7 15. h3 {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'etc.''} {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'not''} O-O $2 16. Rfe1 {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'On''} Nc4 17. Nxc4 Rxc4 18. Ne5 $16 { Ftacnik,L: ' Bobby Fischer: 'with a tremendous bind. Black has to reckon with the possible breakthrough on g6.''} {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'The best chance is''} Rcc8 $142 19. Bg5 Qd8 20. Bxf6 gxf6 21. Ng4 Kh8 22. f4 f5 23. Ne5 Bd6 $14 {Kotov,A Ftacnik,L: 'Kotov,A Bobby Fischer: '(KOTOV) holding White to a minimal endgame edge.''} {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Sharper is''} 24. Qf3 Bxe5 25. Rxe5 $13 {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'But on''} Rg8 26. Re2 $16 { e2 Ftacnik,L: ' e2 Bobby Fischer: 'followed by an eventual Be2 will cause trouble.''} {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Weak is''} Qh4 {Gereben,E-Geller,E Budapest 1952 Ftacnik,L: 'Gereben,E-Geller,E Budapest 1952 Bobby Fischer: 'as played in Gereben,E-Geller,E.; Budapest, 1952.''} {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'More accurate is''} 27. Kh2 $142 {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'immediately.''} {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'The variation is specifically directed against the characteristic ...e5 of the Najdorf System. Thus if''} Rg6 28. g3 Qf6 29. Rg1 Kg7 30. Qd3 $1 a6 31. Rc1 h5 32. h4 $40 {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'with a powerful attack: e.g.,''} Kh6 $2 33. c4 dxc4 34. Rxc4 Rxg3 35. Qxg3 Rxc4 36. Rd2 $1 {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'or''} Qg6 37. Qg5+ Qxg5 38. hxg5+ Kg6 39. Kg3 $16 {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'with a comfortable edge.''} {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'For''} Rc6 {Fischer,R-Reshevsky,S ch-USA 1962 Ftacnik,L: 'Fischer,R-Reshevsky,S ch-USA 1962 Bobby Fischer: 'see game 43: Fischer,R-Reshevsky,S; ch-USA, 1962.''} {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'For''} 40. Kf3 {Fischer,R-Najdorf,M Varna ol 1962 Ftacnik,L: 'Fischer,R-Najdorf,M Varna ol 1962 Bobby Fischer: 'see game 40: Fischer,R-Najdorf,M; Varna ol, 1962.''} Rd6) 11... Rc8 $2 (11... Nb3 12. Ra2 Rc8 13. O-O $1 {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Insufficient is''} Be7 $2) (11... Qb3 12. Qe2 Bxa4 $18 (12... Nc4 13. Bc1 $4) {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'or''} 13. Rxa4 $2 Qxa4 {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'But White can't! Not''} 14. Bb5+ $2) 12. Nbd2 Nc6 13. Qb1 Nh5 ({Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Objectively best is''} 13... g6 $142) 14. Be3 h6 (14... f5 15. g4 $18 {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'wins.''} {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Tempting is''} fxg4 $5 16. Ng5 Bd6 17. Bxh7) (14... g6) (14... Qc7 $16 {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'and White has no forced win in sight.''} {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'if''} 15. O-O $2 (15. Bxh7 Nf4 16. Bxf4 Qxf4 $1) 15... Nf4) 15. Ne5 {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: ', Amateurs are often puzzled by this apparent loss of time. Actually it is a handy defensive move, getting out of the pin on the c-file which could become annoying after ...b5-b4. One never knows when lightning will strike! ''} Nf6 {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: '; The knight has no future on c5, so Bolbochan tries to bring it into play via b6. ''} (15... Nxe5 16. dxe5 {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'On''} Bc5 $2 17. a5 $18 {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'wins.''} {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'On''} Qc7 $2 18. Nf3 $1 (18. g4 Bxe3 19. fxe3 Qxe5 20. gxh5 Qxe3+ 21. Be2 (21. Kd1) 21... Bb5 $1 $18 {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: '!' Bobby Fischer: 'forces mate.''} 22. Qd1)) 16. h3 Bd6 17. O-O Kf8 (17... O-O 18. f4 Be8 (18... Nxe5 19. fxe5 {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Not''} Bxe5 $2 20. a5)) 18. f4 Be8 (18... Nxe5 $18 {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'wins.''} {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'And after''} 19. fxe5 Bxe5 {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Black has hardly any moves.''} 20. a5 {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'is answered by''}) 19. Bf2 Qc7 (19... g6 $1 20. f5 gxf5 21. Bxf5 exf5 22. Qxf5 Qd8 $18 {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'wins.''} {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'On''} 23. Bh4) 20. Bh4 $18 {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: ', White has a strategically won game; his Knight cannot be dislodged. ''} Ng8 21. f5 {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: ', Threatening f5. An example of some of the nonsense that has been written about my games, both by admirers and detractors, is the following (by Lublinsky) in the 1962 Russian Yearbook: "Brilliant intuition! Fischer refuses to enter into the Rook and Pawn endgame and plays to continue his attack."''} Nxe5 22. dxe5 Bxe5 23. fxe6 Bf6 24. exf7 $1 {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: ', Shows how ideal the position is - White can afford the luxury of probing weaknesses on both wings. ''} Bxf7 25. Nf3 {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'But I was hoping to win in the middle game. Ironically, I wouldn't have been awarded the brilliancy prize had I chosen the best line here. They don't give medals for endgame technique! ''} Bxh4 $1 (25... g5 26. Bf2 Kg7 27. Bd4) 26. Nxh4 Nf6 27. Ng6+ (27. Qc2) 27... Bxg6 28. Bxg6 Ke7 29. Qf5 Kd8 (29... Rhd8 {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: '!''}) 30. Rae1 Qc5+ (30... Qd6 $1 31. Re6 Qc5+ {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'is decisive.''} 32. Kh1 Rc6 $18 {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'On''} 33. Rfe1) 31. Kh1 Rf8 {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: '; A bid for freedom - otherwise Ra7 mops up the Q-side Pawns.''} (31... Rc6 {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'On''} 32. b4) (31... Kc7 32. Qf4+ Qd6 33. Re7+ Nd7 $1 $18 {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: '!' Bobby Fischer: 'wins.''} {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'After''} 34. Bf5 Rhd8 $18 { e2-g3-f5; a7 Ftacnik,L: ' e2-g3-f5; a7 Bobby Fischer: 'foIlowed by Nd4(or g3)-f5 maintains a winning bind.''} {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'On''} 35. Rxg7 $2) 32. Qe5 Rc7 (32... Qc7 33. Qxd5+ $18 {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'forces mate.''} ({Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'or''} 33. Rxf6)) 33. b4 Qc6 (33... Qxc3 34. Qd6+ $18 {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'leads to a win.''}) {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Black also has to contend with the threat of Ra7. ''} 34. c4 $1 dxc4 35. Bf5 $1 {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: ', The coup de grace. ''} Rff7 36. Rd1+ Rfd7 37. Bxd7 {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: ', Black resigns.''} Rxd7 {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'After''} (37... Nxd7 38. Rfe1) 38. Qb8+ Ke7 (38... Qc8 39. Rxd7+ Nxd7 40. Qd6) 39. Rde1+ (39. Rde1+ $18 {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'mates.''} {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'On''} Kf7 40. Qe8#) 1-0

