{Nigel Davies: 'As Fischer played this opening with Black, his treatment with White is especially noteworthy. In this game Black plays 7...Nxb3 so as to avoid 7...f6 8.Bxg8, but it could be that the medicine is worse than the disease.'} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 a6 6. h3 $1 Nc6 (6... e5 7. Nde2 Be7 (7... Be6 {when Ernst - Tisdall, Gausdal 1993 resulted in a nice win for Black after} 8. g4 d5 9. exd5 Nxd5 10. Bg2) 8. g4 O-O 9. Ng3 g6 10. g5 {left Black with no problems in King - Gausel, Gausdal 1990} {This runs into Fischer's 9.c4, but Black was worried about} Ne8 11. h4 {. Was he right to do so? After} f6 {Ernst's} 12. Bc4+ $5 {can be answered by} Kg7 13. h5 fxg5 14. hxg6 hxg6 15. Nh5+) (6... g6) (6... b5) 7. g4 Nxd4 8. Qxd4 e5 9. Qd3 Be7 (9... Be6) 10. g5 {Nigel Davies: 'The most natural move, but not his only possibility.'} (10. b3) 10... Nd7 (10... Nh5 11. h4) 11. Be3 (11. h4 Nc5 12. Qf3 {was rather equal in Timman - Agdestein, Belgrade 1989}) 11... Nc5 (11... Bxg5 12. Bxg5 {was fine for Black in Ernst - Agdestein, Gausdal 1987} Qxg5 13. Qxd6 Qe7 14. Qxe7+ Kxe7 15. Nd5+ Kf8 16. O-O-O g6) 12. Qd2 Be6 13. O-O-O $14 O-O 14. f3 Rc8 15. Kb1 Nd7 16. h4 b5 17. Bh3 Bxh3 (17... Nb6 18. Bxb6 Qxb6 19. Nd5 Qd8 (19... Bxd5 20. Bxc8) 20. Nxe7+ Qxe7 21. Qxd6) (17... Re8 18. Nd5 Bf8 19. h5) 18. Rxh3 $1 Nb6 19. Bxb6 Qxb6 20. Nd5 Qd8 21. f4 ({Black also seems OK after other moves, for example} 21. Nxe7+ Qxe7 22. Qxd6 Rfd8) 21... exf4 22. Qxf4 Qd7 23. Qf5 Rcd8 (23... Rfd8 24. Qxd7 Rxd7 25. Nb6) (23... Qxf5 24. Nxe7+ {left Black at least equal in Murey - Agdestein, Jerusalem 1986}) 24. Ra3 {Nigel Davies: '!'} Qa7 25. Rc3 (25. Nf6+ Bxf6 (25... gxf6 26. gxf6 Kh8 {gave Black the initiative in Topalov - Agdestein, Biel 1993} 27. Qg5 Rg8 28. fxe7) 26. gxf6 g6 27. Qg5 $1 Kh8) (25. Nxe7+ Qxe7 26. Rxa6 Rfe8 27. a4) 25... g6 $1 (25... Qd7 26. Rc7) (25... Rd7 26. Nf6+ Bxf6 (26... gxf6 27. gxf6 Kh8 {was OK for Black in Wahlbom - Zwaig, Dresden 1969} 28. fxe7) 27. gxf6 g6 28. Qg5 Kh8 {and White had the initiative in Timman - Agdestein, Brussels 1992} {After} 29. Qh6 {Timman might have been intending} Rg8 $5 30. Rc8) 26. Qg4 Qd7 27. Qf3 Qe6 {Nigel Davies: '?'} (27... Rc8 28. Rxc8 Rxc8 29. Nb6) 28. Rc7 Rde8 (28... Rd7 29. Nf4) (28... Rfe8 29. Rf1) (28... Rc8 29. Ra7 Ra8 30. Rxa8 Rxa8 31. Nc7) 29. Nf4 Qe5 30. Rd5 $18 Qh8 31. a3 h6 (31... f6 32. Qb3 Rf7 33. Rxd6 fxg5 {had a slight advantage.} {Black can improve on this with} 34. hxg5 {so as to stop White's knight on b1 from coming to c3.} Qe5 35. Rf6 Ref8 36. Rxf7 Rxf7 37. Rc8+ Bf8 38. Ne6) 32. gxh6 Qxh6 (32... Bxh4 33. Nxg6 fxg6 34. Qb3 Rf7 35. Rf5) 33. h5 Bg5 (33... g5 34. Ne2) 34. hxg6 fxg6 (34... Bxf4 {in this position would be answered by} 35. gxf7+ {In Ivkov - Hoen, Havana (ol) 1966 White played} Rxf7 {and after} 36. Rxf7 Kxf7 37. Rh5) 35. Qb3 Rxf4 (35... Kh8 36. Nxg6+ Qxg6 37. Rxg5 Rf1+ (37... Qxg5 38. Qh3+) 38. Ka2 Qxg5 39. Qh3+ Kg8 40. Qxf1) (35... Bxf4 36. Rh5+ {left Black under serious pressure in Medina Garcia - Zwaig, Havana (ol) 1966}) 36. Re5+ {Nigel Davies: 'Black should play'} Kf8 $1 $14 {Nigel Davies: 'with a reasonable game.'} {Nigel Davies: 'Or if'} 37. Rxe8+ {Nigel Davies: 'there is'} (37. Rxe8+ $1 Kxe8 38. Qe6+ $16 {Nigel Davies: 'and Black is in serious trouble.'} Kf8 39. Qc8+) 1-0

