{Nigel Davies: 'As Fischer played this opening with Black, his treatment with White is especially noteworthy. In this game Black plays 7...Nxb3 so as to avoid 7...f6 8.Bxg8, but it could be that the medicine is worse than the disease.'} 1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. e5 c5 5. a3 Ba5 6. b4 $1 (6. dxc5 Bxc3+ (6... d4 7. b4 dxc3 8. bxa5 Qxa5) 7. bxc3 Qa5) 6... cxd4 7. Qg4 Kf8 8. bxa5 dxc3 9. a4 f5 (9... Ne7) 10. Qg3 {Nigel Davies: 'The most natural move, but not his only possibility.'} Nc6 11. Nf3 Nge7 12. h4 Bd7 13. h5 $14 {Nigel Davies: 'Bulletin: '''} Rc8 14. h6 g6 15. a6 Nb4 16. Qh4 Nec6 17. Ba3 (17. Bg5 Qb6 18. Bd3 Nxd3+ {had a slight advantage.} {Black can improve on this with} 19. cxd3 {so as to stop White's knight on b1 from coming to c3.} Qxa6 20. O-O) 17... d4 (17... Qxh4 18. Rxh4 d4 19. Rb1) 18. axb7 $1 (18. Qxd8+ Rxd8 19. Rb1) 18... Rb8 19. Bb5 Qxh4 20. Rxh4 Ke8 21. Bxc6 Nxc2+ 22. Kd1 Nxa1 23. Bd6 Bxc6 24. Bxb8 $1 Bxa4+ 25. Ke1 (25. Kc1 d3 26. Rb4 Nb3+ 27. Rxb3 Bxb3 28. Bxa7 Kd7 29. b8=Q {left Black under serious pressure in Medina Garcia - Zwaig, Havana (ol) 1966} Rxb8 {in this position would be answered by} 30. Bxb8 {In Ivkov - Hoen, Havana (ol) 1966 White played} g5 {and after} 31. Ba7 g4 32. Nd2 cxd2+ 33. Kxd2) 25... Bc6 $1 26. Nxd4 Bxb7 27. Bd6 (27. Bxa7) 27... Kd7 {Nigel Davies: '?' '?'} 28. f3 (28. Nb5 Rc8 $16 {Nigel Davies: 'and Black is in serious trouble.' Nigel Davies: 'and Black is in serious trouble. Bulletin: '''} 29. Nc7 Be4 30. f3 c2 31. Kd2 Nb3+) 28... Rc8 29. Ne2 Nb3 30. Ba3 $18 {Nigel Davies: 'Bulletin: '+-''} Bd5 31. Ra4 a5 32. Nc1 Nxc1 33. Bxc1 Rc5 34. Ra3 Kc6 35. Be3 c2 36. Ra1 {Nigel Davies: 'Black should play'} Rb5 $1 $14 {Nigel Davies: 'with a reasonable game.' Nigel Davies: 'with a reasonable game. Bulletin: '!''} {Nigel Davies: 'Or if'} 37. Rc1 {Nigel Davies: 'there is'} Bb3 $1 1-0

