{Inf.2/235} {Postny,Evgeny: 'This was an encounter on first board in one of the key matches between the USA and Hungary. '} 1. e4 {Postny,Evgeny} c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 a6 {Postny,Evgeny: 'The Ruy Lopez is one of my main openings and when studying theory of the Exchange Variation from some old Soviet opening encyclopedia, I noticed this game. This was about thirty years ago. Later on I studied a large number of games of Bobby Fischer and he still remains one of my favorite players. '} 6. Bg5 (6. Bc4 {Postny,Evgeny}) 6... e6 7. Qf3 (7. f4 $5 $16 {Postny,Evgeny: ''!?''}) 7... Be7 (7... Nbd7 {Postny,Evgeny was also good enough.}) 8. O-O-O Qc7 9. Qg3 (9. g4 {White should win anyway.}) 9... Nbd7 {Postny,Evgeny: '?!' Postny,Evgeny: 'This natural move is an inaccuracy.'} 10. Nb3 $1 {Postny,Evgeny: 'This was not a novelty at that time, but it does not make this move less effective. The b7 is under pressure and the knight is ready to go to c4.'} b5 {Postny,Evgeny: 'Covering the c4 square, but Black's queenside is now seriously weakened.'} 11. a3 $1 {Postny,Evgeny: '?!' Postny,Evgeny: ''!'' Postny,Evgeny: 'Not the best way to attack Black's queenside.'} Bb7 12. f3 $16 {Postny,Evgeny: 'The c5 is White's main target.'} (12. Bd3) 12... O-O-O $5 {Postny,Evgeny: ''!?''} (12... O-O $1) 13. Bxb5 (13. Kb1 {Postny,Evgeny was a bit more stubborn, but after}) 13... Ne5 (13... axb5 14. Nxb5 Qb6 {mating.} 15. Nxd6+ {Postny,Evgeny} Bxd6 16. Rxd6 Nh5 $18) 14. Be2 $1 {Postny,Evgeny: '!?' Postny,Evgeny: ''!''} h5 $6 {Postny,Evgeny: ''?!''} 15. h4 Nc4 (15... d5) 16. Rd4 Na5 17. Nxa5 {Postny,Evgeny: 'Black's main problem is that his king is stuck in the centre and therefore the rooks are disconnected.'} Qxa5 $6 18. Ra4 Qb6 19. Rb4 $16 {Postny,Evgeny: '!' Postny,Evgeny: ''''} Qa5 20. Be3 {Postny,Evgeny: 'Black can not save the b5.'} (20. Na4) 20... Nd7 21. Ra4 (21. Na4) 21... Qe5 22. Bf4 Qf6 23. Bxd6 Nb6 {Postny,Evgeny: 'Keeping all the rooks on the board actually makes things tougher for Black, as his king is more vulnerable.'} 24. Bxe7 $1 Qxe7 25. Rb4 Qc5 $6 26. Kb1 $18 {Postny,Evgeny: ''+-''} Rd2 27. Bd3 {Postny,Evgeny: '+-' Postny,Evgeny: 'Glorious career for this knight!'} Qc7 28. Qg5 Rxd3 29. cxd3 f6 {Postny,Evgeny: 'The king will come under fire in the centre.'} 30. Qe3 Nd7 31. Rc4 Bc6 32. Rc1 Kd8 33. Ne2 Ne5 34. Nd4 Nxc4 {Postny,Evgeny} 35. Rxc4 1-0

