{Bobby Fischer: 'GAME N. 1 Too little, too late. Although Sherwin makes no serious errors in the opening, he misses several equalizing opportunities. Demonstrating the technical virtuosity that is to become his hallmark, Fischer, with astonishing maturity, gradually strengthens his grip by accumulating small advantages: the better center and the two Bishops. Sherwin, meanwhile, attempts to consolidate his position - only to see his 14-year-old opponent shatter it with a thunderbolt (18 xh7). It brings to mind Alekhine's combinations, which also seemed to spring from nowhere. Sherwin, lashing back, refuses to fall. However, his defense finally disintegrates under a series of acute blows to his wobbly King. ''GAME N. 1 Too little, too late. Although Sherwin makes no serious errors in the opening, he misses several equalizing opportunities. Demonstrating the technical virtuosity that is to become his hallmark, Fischer, with astonishing maturity, gradually strengthens his grip by accumulating small advantages: the better center and the two Bishops. Sherwin, meanwhile, attempts to consolidate his position - only to see his 14-year-old opponent shatter it with a thunderbolt (18 xh7). It brings to mind Alekhine's combinations, which also seemed to spring from nowhere. Sherwin, lashing back, refuses to fall. However, his defense finally disintegrates under a series of acute blows to his wobbly King.  ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'GAME N. 1 Too little, too late. Although Sherwin makes no serious errors in the opening, he misses several equalizing opportunities. Demonstrating the technical virtuosity that is to become his hallmark, Fischer, with astonishing maturity, gradually strengthens his grip by accumulating small advantages: the better center and the two Bishops. Sherwin, meanwhile, attempts to consolidate his position - only to see his 14-year-old opponent shatter it with a thunderbolt (18 xh7). It brings to mind Alekhine's combinations, which also seemed to spring from nowhere. Sherwin, lashing back, refuses to fall. However, his defense finally disintegrates under a series of acute blows to his wobbly King. ''' Quintiliano,Renato: 'This is the first game of Fischer's book, "My 60 Memorable Games", and I think it is a perfect prelude for a great work. I remember when I first studied this game it made a strong impression on me, because even as young as age 14, we can already see many qualities that would bring great successes for Fischer later: excellent opening knowledge, accurate calculation and very strong logical reasoning behind any move, always supported by energetic, concrete play. '} 1. e4 {Quintiliano,Renato Bobby Fischer Bobby Fischer Bobby Fischer: 'ChessBase ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer''} e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 {Bobby Fischer: ''Maddox, ChessBase: 'This is the move Fischer was waiting for.'' ' Bobby Fischer: ''Maddox, ChessBase: 'Dies ist der Zug, auf den Fischer wartete.'' '} 3. Bb5 {Bobby Fischer: ', This used to be my favorite. I thought it led to a favorable variation of the King's Indian reversed, particularly after Black has committed himself with ...e6. ', This used to be my favorite. I thought it led to a favorable variation of the King's Indian reversed, particularly after Black has committed himself with ...e6. 'Bobby Fischer: ', This used to be my favorite. I thought it led to a favorable variation of the King's Indian reversed, particularly after Black has committed himself with ...e6. ' Maddox, ChessBase: 'KIA.'' ' ' Quintiliano,Renato: '!' Quintiliano,Renato: 'The KIA was one of Fischer's weapons for many years against 2...e6 in the Sicilian. In his own words, he was convinced that White gets a good KID (also one of Fischer's main lines as Black) with reversed colours, since Black has already "committed" his position with 2...e6.'} a6 4. Bxc6 dxc6 5. O-O f6 6. d4 exd4 {Bobby Fischer: 'but Black has purposely delayed placing his center Pawns. Has he a new idea in mind? ''but Black has purposely delayed placing his center Pawns. Has he a new idea in mind?  ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'but Black has purposely delayed placing his center Pawns. Has he a new idea in mind? '''} 7. Nxd4 c5 {Bobby Fischer: '; Sherwin slid the Rook here with his pinky, as if to emphasize the cunning of this mysterious move.''; Sherwin slid the Rook here with his pinky, as if to emphasize the cunning of this mysterious move. ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: '; Sherwin slid the Rook here with his pinky, as if to emphasize the cunning of this mysterious move.''' Quintiliano,Renato: '?!' Quintiliano,Renato: 'This seems too odd for me, but Black can justify that after either ...b7-b6 or ...b7-b5 the rook is better placed out of the diagonal, and he has a point.'} 8. Nb3 Qxd1 {Bobby Fischer: ''Maddox, ChessBase: 'By refraining from ...d6-d5, black hopes to neutralize white's e4-e5.'' ' Bobby Fischer: ''Maddox, ChessBase: 'Indem er von ...d6-d5 Abstand nimmt, hofft Schwarz, das weiße e4-e5 zu neutralisieren.'' '} 9. Rxd1 {Bobby Fischer: ''Maddox, ChessBase: 'Supporting d2-d4. If black gives away space in the center, white shouldn't be afraid to take it.'' ' Quintiliano,Renato: 'As Black is not intending to fight for the centre, Fischer proceeds to place another pawn there.' Bobby Fischer: ''Maddox, ChessBase: 'Unterstützt d2-d4. Wenn Schwarz im Zentrum Raum abtritt, sollte Weiß nicht davor scheuen, diesen zu besetzen.'' '} Bd6 {Bobby Fischer: '; Not bad.'; Not bad.'Bobby Fischer: '; Not bad.' Maddox, ChessBase: '?!'' ' ' Quintiliano,Renato: 'Not a bad move, according to Fischer.'} (9... Bd7 $18 {Bobby Fischer: 'is devastating''is devastating ChessBase: '+-' ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'is devastating''' Quintiliano,Renato: 'with huge material losses for Black.'} 10. Bf4 $2 O-O-O 11. Nc3) 10. Na5 b5 $2 {Bobby Fischer: '; This leads to trouble.''; This leads to trouble. ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: '; This leads to trouble.''' Quintiliano,Renato: 'This mistake is the start of Black's problems.'} 11. c4 $1 {Bobby Fischer: ''Maddox, ChessBase: 'Fischer gets e4-e5 in anyway. Now black has no time for ...d6-d5.'' ' Quintiliano,Renato: 'Fischer finds an energetic way to exploit Black's imprecise play.' Bobby Fischer: ''Maddox, ChessBase: 'Fischer kommt trotzdem zu e4-e5. Nun hat Schwarz keine Zeit für ...d6-d5.'' '} Ne7 {Bobby Fischer: ''Maddox, ChessBase: '?!'' '} 12. Be3 f5 13. Nc3 $1 {Quintiliano,Renato: 'The point: White wins the bishop pair.'} f4 {Bobby Fischer: '; An unpleasant choice, since it releases the pressure in the center and gives White a free hand to start operations on the K-side.''; An unpleasant choice, since it releases the pressure in the center and gives White a free hand to start operations on the K-side. ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: '; An unpleasant choice, since it releases the pressure in the center and gives White a free hand to start operations on the K-side.''' Quintiliano,Renato: 'Fischer points out that this was a sad choice, as it releases the central tension, thus leaving White's comfortable to look for operations on the kingside.'} 14. e5 Bxe5 {Quintiliano,Renato: 'The second important moment in the game. One could expect a technical game, with Fischer making use of his bishops to squeeze Black in a positional torture, but... '} 15. Bxc5 $1 {Quintiliano,Renato: 'The young Bobby has different plans! Some defenders are missed on Black's kingside, and White plays for an attack in the KIA, after all.'} Bxc3 $2 {Bobby Fischer: '; A bad mistake.''; A bad mistake. ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: '; A bad mistake.''' Quintiliano,Renato: 'Sherwin is planning a defensive regroupment, but this plan is too slow.'} 16. bxc3 $1 {Quintiliano,Renato: 'As we will see, the queen is surprisingly aggressive from here.'} Ng6 17. Nc6 {Quintiliano,Renato: '!' Quintiliano,Renato: 'Sherwin was probably looking for something like f6-b7. Unfortunately for him, Fischer is not disposed to give him the time needed to accomplish his goal.'} Be6 {Bobby Fischer: '; Apparently everything's defended now.''; Apparently everything's defended now. ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: '; Apparently everything's defended now.''' Quintiliano,Renato: 'Apparently, Black has everything defended.'} 18. cxb5 $1 {Bobby Fischer: ', Throwing a monkey wrench into Black's carefully contrived setup! As usual, tactics flow from a positionally superior game. '', Throwing a monkey wrench into Black's carefully contrived setup! As usual, tactics flow from a positionally superior game.  ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: ', Throwing a monkey wrench into Black's carefully contrived setup! As usual, tactics flow from a positionally superior game. ''' Quintiliano,Renato: 'A cold shower for Black. White has advantage in all lines, proving Fischer's point when he says: tactical ideas always arise from better positions.'} axb5 19. Na7 Rb8 $1 {Bobby Fischer: '; The best fighting chance.''; The best fighting chance. ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: '; The best fighting chance.''' Quintiliano,Renato: 'Sherwin finds the most fighting continuation.'} 20. Rdb1 Kf7 21. Nxb5 Rhd8 $1 {Quintiliano,Renato: 'A creative resource.'} 22. Rb4 $1 {Bobby Fischer: ''Maddox, ChessBase: 'Sacrificing a pawn to open black's king.'' ' Quintiliano,Renato: 'Another important and instructive moment. The young Fischer was already aware that initiative matters more than material in such positions.' Bobby Fischer: ''Maddox, ChessBase: 'Öffnet einen Bauern, um Linien gegen den schwarzen König zu öffnen.'' '} Bxa2 {Bobby Fischer: '; Once again, time-pressure had Sherwin burying his thumbs in his ears.''; Once again, time-pressure had Sherwin burying his thumbs in his ears. ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: '; Once again, time-pressure had Sherwin burying his thumbs in his ears.''' Quintiliano,Renato: '' Quintiliano,Renato: 'Accepting the risks.'} 23. Nxc7 Rbc8 $2 {Bobby Fischer: '; Suicidal.''; Suicidal. ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: '; Suicidal.''' Quintiliano,Renato: 'After this, Black can't avoid the attack.'} ({Bobby Fischer: 'On''On ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'On''' Quintiliano,Renato: 'In the event of'} 23... Rxb4 {Quintiliano,Renato: 'only now does Black accept the rook'} 24. cxb4 $18 {Bobby Fischer: 'nets a whole rook''nets a whole rook ChessBase: '+-' ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'nets a whole rook''' Quintiliano,Renato: 'indeed, the best moment to take it.'} Rd2 $5 {(Bobby Fischer) ChessBase} {Bobby Fischer: 'On''On ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'On'''} 25. b5) 24. h4 $1 {Bobby Fischer: ', Threatening 25 Be5+. '', Threatening 25 Be5+.  ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: ', Threatening 25 Be5+. ''' Quintiliano,Renato: 'With the obvious deadly threat e5+.'} Rd2 25. Bb6 $1 {Bobby Fischer: ', Now the Rook joins the King hunt - and it's murder.' Bobby Fisc', Now the Rook joins the King hunt - and it's murder. ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: ', Now the Rook joins the King hunt - and it's murder.' Bobby Fischer: 'The immediate threat is''' her: 'The immediate threat is' Quintiliano,Renato: 'The smart manoeuvre e4-e3 is very instructive, as well as the precise conducting of the attack by Fischer.'} f3 (25... h5 $18 {Bobby Fischer: 'ChessBase: '+-''}) 26. Be3 Re2 27. Nb5 {Bobby Fischer: 'But by now I felt there was more in the offing. ''But by now I felt there was more in the offing.  ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'But by now I felt there was more in the offing. '''} Ra8 28. h5 $1 {Bobby Fischer: ''Maddox, ChessBase: 'Infiltrating the dark squares.'' ' Quintiliano,Renato: 'Don't think about exchanges, look to the king!' Bobby Fischer: ''Maddox, ChessBase: 'Infiltiert die dunklen Felder.'' '} Ne5 29. Rf4+ Ke7 30. Rd1 Re8 31. Re4 Kf6 32. Rd6+ Kf5 33. Rf4+ {Bobby Fischer: ', Black resigns.'', Black resigns. ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: ', Black resigns.''' Quintiliano,Renato: 'A very instructive game, that really let me excited to read the rest of the book! Also a clear example of Fischer's impressive strength at just 14, showing excellent tactical awareness to grab advantages and handle the initiative.'} Kg5 {Bobby Fischer: 'If''If ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'If'''} 34. Rxf3+ 1-0

