{Fischer dropped out of this world championship qualifier over a scheduling dispute when he was leading and delayed his prospects for several years, but he created a number of beautiful games. Here the Mongolian champion is so intent on breaking through on the queenside that he forgets about his king. Fischer's concluding queen sacrifice is captivating and perfectly timed.} {Matanovic,A: 'Chess Informant'} 1. e4 {Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s)} c6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 {The purpose of this move order is to avert an exchange of queens after 3...dxe4 4. dxe4.} g6 (3... dxe4) 4. e5 (4. h3) 4... Bg7 5. f4 h5 6. Nf3 Bg4 (6... Nh6 7. Bd3 Bf5) 7. h3 Bxf3 {White's quiet buildup postpones sharp hand-to-hand battle until the middle game where operations will take place behind closed lines.} 8. Qxf3 e6 (8... h4 9. f5) 9. g3 (9. Be3 {"Believe it or not, I actually spent more time on this innocuous push (15 minutes) than on any other move in the game! I didn't want to allow Black to get in ...a3 thereby creating holes (weak squares) on c3 and a3. On the other hand, by stopping to meet his positional threat I am forced to postpone my own schemes for at least two moves. Chess is a matter of delicate judgment, knowing when to punch and how to duck" -- Fischer.} Nh6 (9... h4) 10. g3 Nd7 {This decentralization is inadvisable. Black should try 14...Nd4 or Ba6 right away.} 11. O-O-O Nf5 12. Bf2 {Permanently discouraging the f6 freeing maneuver.} Nb6 13. g4 {Fischer is a law unto himself. He abstains from the natural 17. Ng4 because this knight is headed instead for e4. Meanwhile Black has secured d5 for his knight.} Nh4 14. Bxh4 Qxh4 {It's remarkable that such an obvious move is inferior. 18...h6! 19. Ne4 c4 offers reasonable counterplay.} 15. g5 O-O {19...c4 was still a better try. But not 19...h6? 20. Nxe6 fxe6 21. Bxe6+ Kh8 22. Bxa5 Qxa5 23. Bxd5 gaining two buttons.} 16. Bd3 Rfc8 {1-0 (31) Fischer,R-Miagmarsuren,L Sousse 1967 [Matanovic,Aleksandar]} 17. Qe3 Bf8 18. Ne2 c5 19. Qg1 c4 20. Qh2 cxd3 21. Rxd3 Rc6 22. Kb1 Rac8 23. Rc1 Bb4 24. c3 Na4 25. cxb4 Rxc1+ 26. Nxc1 Qe1 27. Qd2 Qf1 28. Qd1 Qxf4 29. Ne2 Qf5 30. Qd2 Nb6 31. a4 Nc4 32. Qc3 Qf1+ 33. Nc1 Na3+ 34. bxa3 Rxc3 35. Rxc3 Qf5+ 36. Nd3 Qxh3) (9. Be2 h4) 9... Qb6 10. Qf2 Ne7 11. Bd3 Nd7 12. Ne2 (12. Bd2 Nf5 13. Bxf5 exf5 14. O-O-O) 12... O-O-O 13. c3 $1 f6 14. b3 {Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s): 'LiveBook: 46 Games'} Nf5 $6 {Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s): ' C00: French: Unusual White 2nd moves'} (14... Rdf8 $5 15. Ba3) 15. Rg1 (15. O-O $11 {(Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s)) deserves consideration.}) 15... c5 16. Bxf5 (16. g4 $11 {(Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s)) remains equal.} hxg4 17. hxg4 Ne7 $1 $14 {Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s)}) 16... gxf5 {Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s): 'Black has an edge.'} 17. Be3 Qa6 18. Kf1 (18. Qf3 fxe5 19. fxe5 $17 Bxe5 $2 20. dxe5 Nxe5 21. Qf1 $19) 18... cxd4 (18... Kb8 $16 {Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s)} 19. Qe1 {Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s)}) 19. cxd4 {Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s): ' And now Nxe6! would win.'} Nb8 20. Kg2 $16 Nc6 {1-0 (31) Fischer,R-Myagmarsuren,L Sousse (izt) 4/17 1967 CI1-130 [Matanovic,Aleksandar]} 21. Nc1 Rd7 (21... Kb8 $16) 22. Qd2 (22. Rd1 $6 {Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s)}) 22... Qa5 23. Qxa5 $1 {Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s): '!' Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s): ' White threatens Qg5 and mate.'} (23. Qb2 {Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s)} Qa6 (23... Bf8)) (23. Qe2 $16 fxe5 24. fxe5 $16 (24. dxe5 $19 d4 $16 {(Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s)) was necessary.}) 24... Qc3 $2) 23... Nxa5 {Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s): '!'} 24. Nd3 {Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s): '!' Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s): ' Bxg7! is the strong threat.'} Nc6 (24... b6) 25. Rac1 {Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s): '+-!'} (25. Nc5 $11 Re7 $18 {Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s)} 26. Rac1) 25... Rc7 26. Rc3 {Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s): '' Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s): ' White attacks with force.'} b6 {Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s): '?'} 27. Rgc1 $1 Kb7 {Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s): '?' Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s): '[#]'} 28. Nb4 {Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s): '!' Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s): ' Intending hxg6 and mate.'} (28. b4 a6 29. a4 {Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s): '+-'} Rhc8 {Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s)} 30. b5 (30. a5 Nd8 31. Rxc7+ $18 {Stronger than} Rxc7 {Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s)} 32. Rxc7+ $11 {Weaker is} Kxc7 {Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s)}) (30. Kf3 Nxe5+) (30. Kf2 $16 Bh8) 30... axb5 31. axb5 Na7) 28... Rhc8 29. Rxc6 $3 {Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s): ' Qh6 would kill now.'} Rxc6 $2 30. Rxc6 $18 Rxc6 {Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s): '[#]'} 31. Nxc6 {Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s): '!' Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s): ' Remove Defender Accuracy: White = 82%, Black =  7%. . Loss on time!?'} Kxc6 32. Kf3 1-0

