{Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Chris Ward: 'Sac, Sac, Mate!:- It's probably fair to say that America's (and many believe the World's) greatest ever player didn't have a particularly high opinion of the Dragon. His recipe for extinguishing the fire was rather unsubtle!'' Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'GAME N. 2 Slaying the dragon. Although the Sicilian, as a whole, is still the best fighting defense at Black's disposal, much of the steam has been taken out of the time-honored Dragon Variation. This is one of the key games which helped to batter its reputation. In a laudable attempt to create complications, Larsen deviates from the book on move 15. That proves to be disastrous, since his counterattack never gets started. Mechanically, routinely, Fischer pries open the h-file, sacrificing first a Pawn and then the exchange. There is an aura of the inevitable about the outcome. Here the notes are as instructive and lucid as the text, which is an object lesson in how to mount an assault against the fianchettoed King. ''} 1. e4 {Ftacnik,Lubomir Ftacnik,Lubomir Ftacnik,Lubomir Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Ftacnik,L Chris Ward Ftacnik,L: 'Ftacnik'' Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer'} c5 2. Nf3 Nc6 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Chris Ward: 'As far as I'm concerned, the Danish Grandmaster Bent Larsen has been the World's leading Accelerated Dragon expert for many a year. In the old days he regularly wheeled out the normal Dragon, but significantly I have noted that such outings were extremely few and far between after this particular encounter.''} (2... d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 g6 6. f3 Nc6 7. Bc4 Bd7 8. Bb3 Na5) 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 d6 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: '; Larsen was one of the diehards who refused to abandon the Dragon until recently. White's attack almost plays itself ... weak players even beat Grandmasters with it. I once thumbed through several issues of Shakhmatny Bulletin, when the Yugoslav Attack was making its debut, and found the ratio was something like nine wins out of ten in White's favor. Will Black succeed in reinforcing the variation? Time will tell. ''} 6. Bc4 (6. Bg5 g6 7. Bxf6 exf6) 6... Bd7 (6... g6 7. Nxc6 bxc6 8. e5 dxe5 (8... Nh5 9. Qf3 e6 (9... d5 10. Nxd5) 10. g4 Ng7 11. Ne4 Qa5+ (11... d5 12. Nf6+ Ke7 13. Qa3+) 12. Bd2 Qxe5 13. Bc3) (8... Ng4) 9. Bxf7+) (6... e6) (6... Qb6) 7. Bb3 (7. f3 e6 8. Ndb5 Qb8) (7. Be3 Ng4) (7. Bg5 e6 8. Bxf6 Qxf6 9. Ndb5 O-O-O 10. Nxd6+ Kb8) (7. O-O g6 8. Nxc6 Bxc6 (8... bxc6 9. f4) 9. Bg5 Bg7 10. Nd5) 7... g6 8. f3 (8. Be3 Ng4 9. Nxc6 bxc6 (9... Nxe3 10. Bxf7+) 10. Qf3 (10. Bxa7 c5) 10... Ne5 11. Qg3) 8... Na5 (8... Nxd4 9. Qxd4 Bg7 10. Bg5 O-O 11. Qd2 b5 12. Bh6 a5 13. Bxg7 Kxg7 14. a4 b4 15. Nd5 Nxd5 16. exd5 Rc8) (8... Rc8 9. Nxc6 bxc6 10. Be3 Bg7 11. Qd2 O-O 12. O-O-O Qa5 13. Bh6 c5 14. Bxg7 Kxg7 15. Qe2) 9. Bg5 Bg7 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Chris Ward: 'A once popular variation that is virtually extinct today. There are known alternatives, but nowadays very rarely is anything other than 9...Bd7 seen.'' Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: '; Just how Black can attempt to thread bis way to equality is not clear.''} 10. Qd2 h6 (10... O-O $1 $18 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: '!' Bobby Fischer: 'wins a pawn.''} {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Chris Ward: 'It's worth noting that an attempt to hassle the bishop immediately with''} 11. Bh6 $2 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Chris Ward: '??' Chris Ward: 'loses to'' Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'still loses to''} Bxh6 $18 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Chris Ward: 'i.e.''} 12. Qxh6 {(Ftacnik,Lubomir) Chris Ward} e5 13. Nde2 b5) 11. Be3 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Chris Ward: '!' Chris Ward: 'Capturing on e6 may double Black's pawns, but it opens up the f-file and more importantly hands over control of d5.''} Rc8 12. O-O-O Nc4 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Chris Ward: 'In contrast to Black, White hasn't pushed any pawns around his king. Hence an attack with pawns (intended to grant access for the rooks to the enemy king) is always likely to be slower. Note that trading bishops on b3 isn't good for as this time it would be White given control of the c4-square as well as extra cover (after 12 cxb3) for his king. This is an excellent illustrative point. So often White loves to get a knight to d5 and likewise, Black one to c4.''} {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'White is lost in the King and Pawn ending, it's true, but Black usually gets mated long before then. As Tarrasch put it: "Before the endgame the gods have placed the middle game." ''} 13. Qe2 (13. Bxc4 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'and if''} Rxc4 14. Kb1 (14. g4 $2)) 13... Nxe3 (13... Qc7 $1 $40 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: '!' Bobby Fischer: 'Black cannot make any attacking headway against this particular Pawn configuration.''} {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Interesting is Donald Byrne's''} 14. Ndb5 $5 {Byrne,D Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Byrne,D Bobby Fischer: 'The strongest reply is''}) 14. Qxe3 O-O (14... Qb6 15. Qd2 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Chris Ward: '!''} Qc5 16. f4 $1 h5 (16... b5) (16... O-O $1 $16 {Tal,M-Larsen,B Zürich 1959 Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Tal,M-Larsen,B Zürich 1959 Chris Ward: '!' Chris Ward: 'is considered to be a better theoretical variation for White and now Black misses his chance.'' Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Tal,M-Larsen,B Zürich 1959 Bobby Fischer: '!' Bobby Fischer: '(Tal-Larsen, Zurich 1959) where White abandons the attack and plays for pressure along the e-file instead.''}) 17. Nf3 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: '!''} Bh6 18. e5 Ng4 (18... dxe5 19. Nxe5 Qxe5 20. fxe5 $10 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'renders white extra pawn useless''} {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'After 15...Nxd5, however, I intended simply''} Bxd2+ 21. Rxd2 Ng4 $13 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'keeping the game alive.''} {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Chris Ward: 'In fact'' Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Stronger is''} 22. Bxf7+ $1 Kxf7 23. Rxd7) 19. Rhe1 $10 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Chris Ward: 'both likely drawn double rook endings.'' Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'etc.''} {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Chris Ward: 'or''} O-O 20. Ne4) ({Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Bad judgement is''} 14... Qa5 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: '?''} 15. Kb1 (15. g4 $16 {Suetin,A-Kortschnoj,V/URS-ch/1953/ Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Suetin,A-Kortschnoj,V/URS-ch/1953/ Bobby Fischer: 'with a crushing bind. (Suetin-Korchnoi, USSR Championship prelims, 1953.)''} {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Weaker is''} Qg5 $2) (15. f4 O-O 16. h3 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'After''} e6) 15... Qc5 16. Qd3 a6 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Chris Ward: 'is better for White because of the pressure he can exert on the e7-pawn.''}) 15. g4 (15. h4 Qb6 $18 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: '!' Bobby Fischer: 'wins.''} ({Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'After the game Larsen explained he was playing for a win, and therefore rejected the forced draw with''} 15... h5 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Chris Ward: '!' Chris Ward: 'was it, with''}) {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Chris Ward: 'Throughout it is clear that the best way to hassle White's light-squared bishop is with ...a5-a4. However this has not been easy to arrange and even now after''} 16. h5 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Chris Ward: ', White can knock this plan on the head with the greedy'' Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: '?' Bobby Fischer: 'is refuted by''} g5 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Chris Ward: '!''}) 15... Qa5 $2 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: '; Losing move.''} (15... Qb6 16. Qd2 (16. h4 e5) 16... a5) 16. h4 $1 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: ', He won't get a second chance to snap off the Bishop! Now I felt the game was in the bag if I didn't botch it. I'd won dozens of skittles games in analogous positions and had it down to a science: pry open the h-file, sac, sac ... mate! ''} e6 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: '; This loss of time is unfortunately necessary if Black is ever to advance his a-Pawn.''} (16... h5 17. g5 Ne8 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: '!''} 18. f4 e5 $18 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'leads to mate.''} {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'on''} 19. fxe5 Qxe5 20. Nd5 Nc7 21. Nf6+ Bxf6 $18 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'mates.''} 22. gxf6 Qxf6 23. Rhf1 Qe5 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: '!''} (23... Qxh4 24. Qh6) 24. Nf3 Qe7 25. Qh6) 17. Nde2 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Chris Ward: '!' Chris Ward: 'Consistent with Fischer's assessment that beating the Dragon was essentially down to prising open the h-file and then sac, sac mate!''} (17. g5 $18 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'wins.''} hxg5 18. hxg5 Nh5 19. f4 $18 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'on''} e5 ({Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'or''} 19... Qc5) 20. Nd5 exd4 21. Ne7+ Kh7 22. Qf3 $18) 17... Rc6 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: '; There's no satisfactory way to impede White's attack.''} (17... Ne8) {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Now Black is threatening to get some counterplay with ...a5-a4. ''} 18. g5 $1 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: ', There's no need to lose a tempo with tho old-fashioned g4. ''} hxg5 (18... Nh5 19. gxh6 Bf6 20. f4) 19. hxg5 Nh5 20. f4 Rfc8 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: '; Now Black needs just one more move to get his counterattack moving. But for the want of a nail the battle was lost... ''} 21. Kb1 (21. e5 $1) (21. f5 exf5 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: '!''} 22. Nd5 Qxa2) 21... Qb6 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Chris Ward: 'Often this succeeds in blocking the h-file and halting White's attack. Alas because Black never got around to exchanging off White's light-squared bishop with the usual ... Ne5-c4 plan, he has lined himself up for some trouble.''} (21... Bxc3 22. Nxc3 Rxc3 23. bxc3 Rxc3 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'If''} 24. Qd4) 22. Qf3 $1 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: ', Fine wrote: "In such positions, combinations are as natural as a baby's smile." ''} Rc5 23. Qd3 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Chris Ward: 'The f-pawn is pinned.''} (23. Rxh5 gxh5 $1 24. Qxh5) (23. f5 $1 exf5 24. Rxh5 $18 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'wins.''} (24. Nd5 Qd8 25. exf5 Bxf5 26. Rxh5 Rxc2) {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Not the impatient''} 24... gxh5 $2 25. Nf4 Rxc3 26. bxc3 $1 $10 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: '!' Bobby Fischer: '(threatening ...Qe5) and Black holds overything.''} {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'On''} Rxc3 27. Qxh5 $1 Rxb3+ 28. cxb3 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: '!''} Qe3) 23... Bxc3 (23... R5c6 24. f5 exf5 25. Rxh5 fxe4 (25... gxh5 26. exf5 $1) 26. Qxe4 gxh5 27. Bxf7+ $18 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'wins.''} {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'if''} Kxf7 28. g6+ {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Vasiukov suggests''} Kg8 {Vasiukov,E Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Vasiukov,E Bobby Fischer: 'as a possible defense; but White crashes through with''} 29. Qd5+) (23... R8c6 24. Na4) (23... Bf8 24. f5 $1 exf5 25. Nd5 Qd8 (25... fxe4 $2 26. Qxe4 $18 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'not''} Bf5 $2 27. Qxf5) 26. Rxh5 $18 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'etc.''} gxh5 ({Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'if''} 26... Rxd5 27. Bxd5 gxh5 28. exf5 $18) 27. Nf6+ $1 Kg7 28. Qh3 $18 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'threatening Rg1.''}) 24. Nxc3 ({Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'if''} 24. bxc3 Bb5) 24... Nxf4 25. Qf3 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Chris Ward: 'Now the b3-bishop is a monster and if it was required, it has the safe d5 square as a resting place.''} Nh5 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Chris Ward: '26 Bh6 was threatened and'' Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: '!' Bobby Fischer: '; A desperate bid for freedom.''} (25... e5 26. Ne2 $18 { f3-f4 Ftacnik,Lubomir: ' f3-f4 Bobby Fischer: '!' Bobby Fischer: '(intending f4) should be decisive.''}) 26. Rxh5 gxh5 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Chris Ward: 'Alas on 26. ..a4, White had 27 d6 anyway.''} 27. Qxh5 Be8 (27... Kf8 28. Qh8+ Ke7 29. Qf6+ Ke8 30. Rh1 Bb5 31. Bxe6 fxe6 32. Qxe6+ $18 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'wins.''} {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'if''} Kd8 (32... Kf8 33. Rh8+ Kg7 34. Qf6#) 33. Rh8+ {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'No better is''} Kc7 34. Rxc8#) 28. Qh6 (28. Rh1 $1 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'On''} Kf8 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Chris Ward: 'fell foul of''} 29. Bxe6 fxe6 (29... Rxc3 30. Qh8+ Ke7 31. Qf6+ Kf8 32. Rh8#) 30. Qh8+ $1 Ke7 31. Rh7+ Bf7 (31... Kd8 32. Qf6#) 32. Qf6+ $18 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Chris Ward: 'with mate next go.'' Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'mates.''} {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'if''} Kd7 33. Qxf7+ $18 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'On''} Kc6 34. Qd7#) 28... Rxc3 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Chris Ward: '28...Qd7 29 Qd5, threatening 30 Qg8 mate was hopeless.''} 29. bxc3 (29. Rh1 $18 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'wins.''} {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Not''} Qd4) 29... Rxc3 ({Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'or try for more with''} 29... Qe3 $40 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'And on''} 30. Rh1 Qxc3 $18 { d6+ Ftacnik,Lubomir: ' d6+ Bobby Fischer: 'threatening Qd6 mate.''} {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'On''} 31. g6 Qg7 $1 32. Qh2) 30. g6 fxg6 (30... Rg3 31. Qh7+ $18 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'wins material.''} {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'if''} Kf8 32. Qh8+ $1 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'On''} Ke7 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'White can either regain the exchange with''} 33. Qh4+ $18) 31. Rh1 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: ', A mistake! Black resigns.''} {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Chris Ward: 'Leading to checkmate although it must be said that''} Qd4 $1 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'forces mate in three.''} 32. Qh7+ {(Ftacnik,Lubomir) Chris Ward} (32. Bxe6+ Bf7 33. Qh7+ {would have been quicker!} {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'On''} Kf8 34. Qxf7# $1) 1-0

