{Bobby Fischer: 'GAME N. 24 Asking for trouble. The Winawer Variation has given Fischer consistent trouble. He has had the utmost difficulty cracking Black's tortoise-like shell; even his successes are unconvincing. Maintaining the same line of attack year after year has provided his opponents with ample opportunity to sharpen their defences. Darga's 12 ... f6 obliges Fischer, in order to get something out of the opening, to speculate on a pawn sacrifice (13 Ba3!?). Though Darga's reaction may not be ideal, he proceeds sensibly and equalises. Underestimating Fischer's chances, however, he falls prey to a scintillating middlegame attack. And so, once again, by virtue of his native ability, Fischer avoids the retribution that is the usual price for failing to secure an advantage in the opening. '} 1. e4 {Bobby Fischer} e6 2. d3 d5 3. Nd2 Nf6 4. g3 c5 5. Bg2 Nc6 6. Ngf3 Be7 7. O-O {Smyslov,V Smyslov,V Smyslov,V Smyslov,V Bobby Fischer: 'Diagram [#] Smyslov's favourite, largely responsible for Botvinnik's giving up the Winawer Variation.'} O-O {Bobby Fischer: 'I may yet be forced to admit that the Winawer is sound. But I doubt it! The defence is anti-positional and weakens the kingside.'} 8. e5 (8. Re1) 8... Nd7 { a6  a6  a6  a6 Bobby Fischer: 'The idea is to eliminate the bad bishop with ... Ba6.'} 9. Re1 $1 b5 10. Nf1 b4 {Bobby Fischer: 'Diagram [#] Black has gained a tempo, but whether his pawn belongs on b6 is a moot point.'} 11. h4 a5 12. Bf4 a4 13. a3 $5 {Bobby Fischer: 'Keeping tension in the centre at the cost of a pawn.'} bxa3 14. bxa3 Na5 15. Ne3 {Bobby Fischer: 'Diagram [#]'} Ba6 {Bobby Fischer: 'Black has a seeming multiplicity of defences:'} 16. Bh3 (16. Ng5) 16... d4 {Bobby Fischer: 'is just a transposition to the game.'} 17. Nf1 {Bobby Fischer: '?'} (17. Ng4) 17... Nb6 {Bobby Fischer: 'Diagram [#]'} 18. Ng5 Nd5 19. Bd2 (19. Qh5) 19... Bxg5 20. Bxg5 Qd7 21. Qh5 { f5-f6  f5-f6  f5-f6  f5-f6 Bobby Fischer: 'To continue with f6, which gets a grip on the f-file.'} Rfc8 $1 {Bobby Fischer: 'Driving the rook from its command outpost on the sixth rank.'} 22. Nd2 (22. Nh2) 22... Nc3 {Bobby Fischer: 'Darga is defending with vigour!' '!'} 23. Bf6 Qe8 (23... gxf6 $18 {Bobby Fischer: 'Correct was'} 24. exf6 $10 {Bobby Fischer: 'with an equal game.'} {Bobby Fischer: 'On'} Kh8 25. Nf3 Nd5 26. Ne5 $10 Nxf6 $2 {Bobby Fischer: 'Better is the finesse'} 27. Qh6 {} Qe7 28. Bxe6 {'' (Fischer)}) 24. Ne4 $1 {Bobby Fischer: 'Commencing operations against the castled king while Black's queen is temporarily cut off from the queens ide.'} g6 $2 (24... Bb7 25. Bxg7 Kxg7 26. Qg5+) 25. Qg5 Nxe4 26. Rxe4 $1 c4 {Bobby Fischer: 'Diagram [#] The opening of the a-file is already decisive.'} 27. h5 $1 {'+-!'} cxd3 {Bobby Fischer: 'There's no satisfactory defence to the threat of Bf4+.'} 28. Rh4 Ra7 29. Bg2 dxc2 30. Qh6 $1 Qf8 31. Qxh7+ (31. Qxh7+ Kxh7 $18 {Bobby Fischer: 'penetrates decisively.'} {Bobby Fischer: 'On'} 32. hxg6+ Kxg6 $18 {Bobby Fischer: 'Or'} 33. Be4#) 1-0

