e had an alternative in'} 21... Bxd4 22. Qxe4 Bg7 23. Rxh5) 22. gxh5 e5 23. h6 $40 {Nigel Davies: 'gives Black a dangerous attack, ChessBase: '''}) 18. h5 Rfc8 ({Nigel Davies: 'After'} 18... gxh5 $2 19. g4 hxg4 20. fxg4 Nxe4 {Nigel Davies: 'White defends himself with'} 21. Qh2 Ng5 22. Bxg7 $1 Kxg7 23. Rd5 $1 Rc5 24. Qh6+ Kg8 25. Rxg5+ Rxg5 26. Qxh7#) 19. hxg6 hxg6 20. g4 $1 {Nigel Davies: 'Preventing c5-c4 and preparing f2-f4.'} ({Nigel Davies: 'And here'} 20. Bxf6 $2 {Nigel Davies: 'is met by'} Bxf6 21. Qh6 e6 {Nigel Davies: 'hitting both a5 and e5.'}) 20... a5 21. g5 Nh5 (21... Ne8 22. Bxg7 Nxg7 (22... Kxg7 23. Qh2) 23. Rh6 e6 (23... a4 24. Qh2 Nh5 25. Rxg6+) 24. Qh2 $1 Nh5 25. Bxe6 fxe6 (25... Qxg5 26. Rxg6+ Qxg6 27. Bxc8 $1 $36) 26. Rxg6+ Ng7 27. Rh1 $36) (21... a4 $5 $14 22. gxf6 {;  a5-...-h4  Nigel Davies: 'was better, preventing f2-f4 and preparing to transfer the knight on a5 to h4 via b7, d6 and f5. ChessBase: ';  a5-...-h4 ''} {Nigel Davies: 'Another strong line was'} axb3 23. fxg7 bxc2+ {Nigel Davies: 'after which'} 24. Qxc2 e5 {wins the knight on b7.} 25. Qh2) 22. Rxh5 $1 gxh5 { h5; f5 Nigel Davies: 'ChessBase: ' h5; f5''} ({Nigel Davies: 'Stronger than'} 22... Bxd4 23. Qxd4 gxh5 {Nigel Davies: 'when Black has'} 24. g6 {Nigel Davies: 'After'} Qe5 $2 {Nigel Davies: 'White can play'} (24... e6 25. Qxd6) 25. gxf7+ $1 {Nigel Davies: 'anyway'} Kh7 {Gegen c4 gerichtet. c3 verhindert c6-d4, e3, g1, e4 g-Linie} (25... Kf8 26. Qxe5 $1 dxe5 27. Rg1 $36 {Agur} e6 $4 28. Bxe6 Ke7 29. Bxc8 $19 Rxc8 30. Rg5) 26. Qd3) 23. g6 e5 ({Nigel Davies: 'After'} 23... e6 {Nigel Davies: 'White consolidates his position with'} 24. gxf7+ Kxf7 (24... Rxf7 25. Bxe6 $1) 25. Bxg7 Kxg7 26. Rg1+ {Nigel Davies: 'which leaves him with a bind.'} Kh7 $2 27. Qg2 $1 Qe5 28. Qg6+ Kh8 29. Rg5 Rg7 30. Rxh5+ $1 Kg8 31. Bxe6+ Kf8 $2 32. Rf5+ Ke7 33. Rf7+) 24. gxf7+ Kf8 25. Be3 d5 (25... a4 26. Qxd6+ Re7 $10 {Nigel Davies: 'ChessBase: '=''} 27. Qd8+ Rxd8 28. Rxd8+ $1 Re8 29. Bc5+ $1) (25... Rd8 26. Bh6 $13) 26. exd5 (26. Bxd5 Rxc2 $10 { Nigel Davies: 'with approximate equality. ChessBase: '=' ChessBase: '''}) 26... Rxf7 $2 {Nigel Davies: 'Losing on the spot.'} (26... a4 $19 27. d6 axb3 $19 28. dxc7 { Nigel Davies: 'ChessBase: '''}) 27. d6 $1 $18 {Nigel Davies: '!' '!' Nigel Davies: 'ChessBase: '+-!''} Rf6 (27... Rd7 28. Be6 (28. Bh6)) (27... Rxf3 28. d7) 28. Bg5 Qb7 (28... Qd7 29. Qd5 Qf7 (29... Rf7 30. Be7+) 30. Bxf6) 29. Bxf6 {Nigel Davies: 'Black should play'} Bxf6 $1 {;  8xe4 Nigel Davies: 'which threaten s to capture the bishop on e4 and then mate on g2. White's best reply is ChessBase: ';  8xe4''} 30. d7 Rd8 31. Qd6+ (31. Qh6+ $1 Ke7 32. Qh7+ Kf8 33. Qf7#) 1-0

