2. Qf4 Qxf4 23. Bxf4 Ne6 24. Bd2 c5) (22. Qe2) 22... Rad8 23. Bxg5 Qxg5 24. Qc6 Re6 25. Qxc7 Rd2) 21... Nc5 22. g3 (22. Bxf5 gxf5 23. Be3 Ne6 24. f4 c6 25. a4) 22... Qc4 23. Qg2 (23. Qxc4 dxc4) (23. b3 Qxf1+ 24. Kxf1 Ng7) 23... Nd3 24. Bxd3 Qxd3 25. Bg5 (25. Rad1 c6 26. Bg5 Rxe5) 25... c6 26. g4 (26. Rad1 Rxe5) 26... Ng7 27. Re3 (27. Rad1 Rxe5) 27... Qd2 28. b3 $1 (28. Bf6 Qxb2 29. Rd1 (29. Rf1 d4) 29... Qxa2 30. Qh3 Qc2 31. Rf1 g5) (28. f3 Qxg2+ 29. Kxg2 Ne6 30. Bf6) (28. Qh3 Qxb2 29. Rae1 Qxa2 (29... d4 30. Rf3 (30. cxd4 Qxd4 31. Bf6) 30... Ne6 31. Bf6 g5 32. Qh6 Qd2 33. Kf1 dxc3 34. Rf5) 30. Qh6 Ne6 31. Bf6 g5 (31... Qd2 32. g5 Z0 33. Qxh7+ Kxh7 34. Rh3+) 32. Rf3) {This move loses on the spot. After} 28... b4 {White is clearly better although far away from win.} (28... a5 29. Qh3 (29. f3) 29... a4 30. b4 d4 31. cxd4 Qxd4 32. Rae1 Qxb4 33. Bf6 Qf4) (28... c5) {At the time this game was played, Bobby wasn't able to find a more subtle} 29. Qh3 (29. f3 {is interesting.} {More common are either} bxc3 (29... Qxg2+ 30. Kxg2 a5) {or} 30. Qxd2 cxd2 31. Rd1 (31. Bf6 a5 32. Re2 Reb8 33. Rxd2 a4 34. Rc1 axb3 35. axb3 Rxb3 36. Rxc6 Rxf3 37. Rxd5)) (29. cxb4 d4) {Better was} 29... bxc3 {although after} 30. Qh6 Ne6 (30... Ne6 $16 {White is clearly better.} 31. Bf6 $5 $16 d4 $5 {Bishop on d7 is not well placed. Better was} 32. Qxh7+ Kxh7 33. Rh3+ $14 {Preferable is} Qh6 $14) 1-0

