{Bobby Fischer: 'GAME N. 50 Tour de force. As one of ten simultaneous clock games played on tour. at Davis College, this is a perfect example of the precept that if White makes a slip in the opening he is punished by loss of the initiative, while if Black makes a slip (since he is skating on thin ice from the very start) it is likely to be fatal. 6 ... d6 is the offender. With 9 Qh5 Fischer assumes a commanding control of space, but faces a strong defense which compels him to offer a piece in order to maintain pressure. Continuing with restraint and circumspection, he builds up the attack with a series of quiet developing moves - reminiscent of Morphy 's famous victory over the Duke of Brunswick at the Paris opera. When the time is ripe, Fischer throws everything at Black's King, including the proverbial kitchen sink. His show of brute force is handsomely rewarded. '} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bc4 Nf6 4. Ng5 $5 {Evans,W Bobby Fischer: 'The Evans was already analyzed to death by the 'nineties. But it still makes for enterprising chess. Evans,W'} (4. d3) (4. O-O Nxe4 5. Nc3 Nxc3 6. dxc3 Qe7) (4. d4) 4... d5 5. exd5 Na5 (5... Nd4) (5... b5) (5... Nxd5 6. d4 (6. Nxf7)) 6. Bb5+ c6 $2 7. dxc6 bxc6 8. Be2 h6 9. Nh3 $1 Bc5 (9... Bd6 10. d4 e4) (9... Bf5 10. O-O Qd7 11. Re1 Bxh3 12. gxh3 Qxh3 13. Bf1 Qg4+ 14. Qxg4 Nxg4 15. h3) (9... g5 10. d3 g4 11. Ng1 Bc5 12. Nc3 Qb6 13. Na4) 10. O-O (10. d3 O-O 11. Nc3 Re8 12. O-O Bxh3 13. gxh3 Qd7 14. Bg4 Nxg4 15. hxg4) 10... O-O {Bobby Fischer: 'Position after'} (10... g5 11. Kh1 g4 12. Ng1 Ne4 13. Bxg4 (13. b4 Nxf2+ (13... Bxf2 14. d3 Qh4 15. dxe4 Bg3 16. Nh3 (16. h3 gxh3 17. gxh3 Rg8) 16... Bxh2 17. Kxh2 g3+ 18. Kg1 Bxh3) 14. Rxf2 Bxf2 15. bxa5 Qh4 16. Qf1 Bg3 17. h3 Rg8) (13. Qe1 Qd4 14. Bd1 Nxf2+ 15. Rxf2 Qxf2 16. Qxe5+ Be6) 13... Nxf2+ 14. Rxf2 Bxf2) 11. d3 $1 {Bobby Fischer: 'Incredible how Black is so completely immobilized by this one move!'} Bxh3 $8 {Bobby Fischer: ''} ({Bobby Fischer: 'Must be the trend. At least, on tour most players answered this way. For'} 11... Nd5 {Fischer,R-Fine,R New York 1963 Bobby Fischer: 'see game 44.Fischer,R-Fine,R New York 1963'} 12. c4 Ne7 13. Kh1 Bxh3 14. gxh3 Nf5 15. f4 exf4 16. Bxf4 Ne3 17. Bxe3 Bxe3 18. Nc3) (11... Nh7) 12. gxh3 Qd7 13. Bf3 ({Bobby Fischer: 'A mistake is usually much more serious in these open games. Black must return the Pawn with'} 13. Bg4 $1 { Bobby Fischer: '>='} Nxg4 14. hxg4 f5) (13. Kg2 $1) 13... Qxh3 14. Nd2 (14. Bg2 Qh4 15. Qe1 $5 Rfe8 $1 {Bobby Fischer: 'IF'} 16. Qxa5 Ng4 $10 {Bobby Fischer: '='} {Bobby Fischer: 'ON'} 17. h3 $2 Bxf2+ $1 18. Rxf2 (18. Kh1 Qg3 $16 {Bobby Fischer: 'IS STRONG.'}) 18... Qxf2+ 19. Kh1 e4 $18 {Bobby Fischer: 'WINS A PAWN.'} 20. hxg4 (20. dxe4 Rxe4) 20... exd3) 14... Rad8 $1 (14... e4 $2 15. Nxe4 Nxe4 16. Bxe4 $1 $18 {Bobby Fischer: 'WINS.'} {Bobby Fischer: 'In an earlier exhibition game I played'} Bd6 {Bobby Fischer: 'but got nothing after'} 17. f4 $1) 15. Bg2 $1 $36 {Bobby Fischer: 'That's how. This forces Black to weaken himself on d6, although White must sacrifice a piece to exploit it. Position after'} Qf5 ({Bobby Fischer: 'The only way to get relief.'} 15... Qh4 $2 {Bobby Fischer: 'works in all lines except'} 16. Nf3 $1 $18 {Bobby Fischer: 'ON'} Qh5 17. Qe1 $1) 16. Qe1 $1 (16. Qf3 { b6;  (?) Bobby Fischer: 'FOLLOWED BY....Nb6 might be better, but this certainly looked good at the time.'}) 16... Rfe8 $1 17. Ne4 Bb6 18. Nxf6+ (18. b4 {Bobby Fischer: 'virtually forces an exchange of Queens'} Nb7 {Bobby Fischer: 'is rendered hannless by'} 19. b5 {Bobby Fischer: 'How's White to sustain the initiative?'}) 18... Qxf6 {Bobby Fischer: 'FORCED'} 19. Kh1 c5 {Bobby Fischer: 'Position after'} ({Bobby Fischer: 'Apparently Black has freed his game. If now'} 19... g5) 20. Qc3 $1 (20. Qe2 c4 21. dxc4 e4 22. Rb1 (22. Bxe4 Qe5 23. f3 $1 f5) 22... Bc7) (20. Bd2 Nc6 21. Qe4 $18 {[%cal Rc5e7] Bobby Fischer: 'ETC....Black may not have seen the mate, but he suspected the worst!'} {Bobby Fischer: 'IF'} Nd4 22. c3 {Bobby Fischer: 'MATE'} {Bobby Fischer: 'OR'} Nf5 23. Qc4 {Bobby Fischer: 'IF'} Nd6 (23... Nh4 {Bobby Fischer: 'NOT'} 24. Be4 g5 $1) 24. Qg4 {Bobby Fischer: 'ANYWAY'} {Bobby Fischer: 'AFTER'} c4 (24... e4 {Bobby Fischer: 'MATE'} {Bobby Fischer: 'IF'} 25. dxe4 Nxe4 $1 $18 {Bobby Fischer: 'WINS.'} {Bobby Fischer: 'ON'} 26. Be3) 25. dxc4 $18 {Bobby Fischer: 'SMASHES BLACK)'} {Bobby Fischer: 'IF'} e4 26. Be3 Nxc4 27. Bxb6 $1 (27. Rab1 Bxe3 28. fxe3 $1 Qg5) 27... axb6) 20... Nc6 (20... g5 21. f4) 21. f4 Nd4 22. Qc4 $1 (22. fxe5 Qxe5 23. Bf4 $1 Qe2) 22... Qg6 (22... Qe6 $10 {Bobby Fischer: '=' Bobby Fischer: 'etc., and the advantage has evaporated.'} {Bobby Fischer: 'Some fascinating possibilities appear after'} 23. Qa4 Qd7 24. Qxd7 Rxd7 25. c3 Nc2 26. Bc6) 23. c3 $1 (23. Be4 $1 {Bobby Fischer: 'FORCING HIM TO SIMPLIFY BY'} Qh5 24. f5 Qe2 25. Rg1 Nf3) 23... Nf5 {Bobby Fischer: 'Position after'} (23... Ne2 24. f5 Qf6 $1 $18 {Bobby Fischer: 'WINS OUTRIGHT.'} (24... Qh5 $18 {Bobby Fischer: 'White wins a Pawn without any risk.'} {Bobby Fischer: 'Piling on the pressure. White mustn't amateurishly rush in with'} 25. Bf3) {Bobby Fischer: 'He might as well take it since after'} 25. Be3 Nf4 26. Be4) 24. fxe5 {Bobby Fischer: 'Note the amusing piece configuration. All Black's pieces are stepping on each other's toes.'} (24. Be4 $18 {Bobby Fischer: 'AND'} Qh5) 24... Rxe5 $8 {Bobby Fischer: '' Bobby Fischer: 'The only legal move!'} 25. Bf4 (25. Qf4 Bc7 26. Be4 {Bobby Fischer: 'MATE'} {Bobby Fischer: 'The attack needs fresh fuel. Material is not what counts now, but open lines. Black is forced to capture against his will'} Qh5 {Bobby Fischer: 'is out because of'}) 25... Re2 (25... Ne3 26. Bxe3 $18 {Bobby Fischer: 'WINS.'} Rxe3) 26. Be4 Rxb2 (26... Re8 27. Rg1 (27. Bf3 Rxb2 28. Rae1) 27... Qh5 28. Raf1 Ne3 29. Qb5 Rxe4 30. dxe4 Nxf1 {Bobby Fischer: 'NOT'} 31. Qe8+ $2 (31. Rxf1 $18 {Bobby Fischer: 'with a won ending. But then I remembered Emanuel Lasker's maxim: "When you see a good move - wait - don't play ityou might find a better one."'} {Bobby Fischer: 'ON'} Qg4) 31... Kh7 32. Rxg7+ Kxg7 {Bobby Fischer: 'MATE'} 33. Be5+ Qxe5 {Bobby Fischer: 'Originally I intended'} 34. Qxe5+ f6 35. Qe7+ Kg6 36. Qe8+ Kg5) 27. Be5 {Bobby Fischer: 'Here I forgot Lasker's maxim.'} Re8 { Bobby Fischer: 'would have forced mate in four.'} 28. Rxf5 {Bobby Fischer: 'Black resigns'} Rxe5 29. Rxe5 1-0

