{Chess Informant Ivkov,Borislav: 'Ivkov,B: 'Chess Informant''} 1. e4 {Ivkov,Borislav Ivkov,Borislav Ivkov,Borislav} e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bc4 Bc5 4. b4 Bxb4 5. c3 Be7 (5... Ba5) 6. d4 {Ivkov,Borislav: 'Nick Conticello: 'Fischer's pet line which now bears his name. ''} d6 (6... Na5 7. Nxe5 Nxc4 8. Nxc4 d5) 7. dxe5 Nxe5 (7... Na5 8. Bxf7+ Kxf7 9. Qd5+ Be6 10. Qxa5) (7... dxe5 8. Qb3 Na5 9. Bxf7+ Kf8 10. Qa4) 8. Nxe5 dxe5 {Ivkov,Borislav: 'Nick Conticello: '?!''} 9. Qh5 {Ivkov,Borislav: 'Nick Conticello: '!' Nick Conticello: 'Fischer was not the first to play this move, but he was the first to demonstrate its full power. ''} (9. Qb3 Be6 10. Bxe6 fxe6 11. Ba3 (11. Qxe6 Qd6) 11... Qd3) 9... g6 {Ivkov,Borislav: 'Nick Conticello: 'After''} 10. Qxe5 $1 {Ivkov,Borislav: 'Nick Conticello: 'Black is in a quandary.''} Nf6 (10... f6 11. Qb5+ c6 12. Qb3 Kf8 13. Bxg8) 11. Ba3 $5 Rf8 $2 {Ivkov,Borislav: 'Nick Conticello: 'Walking right into the trap. ''} (11... Kf8 12. Qxf6) {Ivkov,Borislav: 'Nick Conticello: 'but White might transpose to Fischer-Rubinetti with ''} 12. O-O $3 {Ivkov,Borislav: 'Nick Conticello: '!''} Ng4 (12... Nd7) 13. Qg3 Bxa3 14. Nxa3 $1 Qe7 15. Bb5+ (15. Nc2 Qe5) (15. Nb5 Ne5) 15... c6 (15... Bd7 16. Qxc7 (16. Qxg4 c6)) 16. Nc4 {Ivkov,Borislav: 'Nick Conticello: 'Fischer is following earlier analysis by Maric. White has two pawns and a massive initiative for his piece. ''} Qe6 (16... cxb5 17. Nd6+ {Ivkov,Borislav: 'Nick Conticello: 'rather than Honfi's ''} Kd8 {Ivkov,Borislav: 'Nick Conticello: ',''} 18. Rfd1 Bd7 19. Nxb7+ Kc8 20. Nd6+ Kd8 $5 21. Rd4 Ne5 22. Rad1 Kc7 $13 (22... g5 23. Nf5 Qe8 24. Qxe5 Qxe5 25. Rxd7+ Ke8 (25... Kc8 26. Ne7+) 26. Re7+ Qxe7 27. Ng7#) 23. f4 $1 {Ivkov,Borislav} Ng4 24. h3 $1 Nf6 25. f5 $1 {White should be doing pretty well.} Kb6 {Ivkov,Borislav} {. He cannot play} 26. Qe3 {(Ivkov,Borislav) because of} Kc7 $1 {.} (26... Ka6 27. a4 $1) 27. Rc4+ $2 bxc4 $1 (27... Kd8 28. Qc5) {Ivkov,Borislav: 'Nick Conticello: 'Chiefly as a result of this game, ''} 28. Qc5+ {Ivkov,Borislav: 'Nick Conticello: '!' Nick Conticello: 'is now generally accepted as the best defence. You can find discussion of that move elsewhere in this text, including in Nikolenko-Nagy in Chapter Two.''} Bc6 (28... Kd8 29. Qa5#) (28... Kb8 29. Rb1+) 29. Nb5+) 17. Rad1 $18 (17. Qc7 {(Ivkov,Borislav) as promising for White,} Qd7 18. Nd6+ Ke7 19. Nxc8+ Raxc8 20. Qxd7+ $16 Kxd7) 17... cxb5 (17... Bd7 18. Nd6+ Ke7 19. Bc4 $3 $16) 18. Qc7 Bd7 19. Nd6+ Ke7 20. Nf5+ {Ivkov,Borislav: 'Nick Conticello: '!' Nick Conticello: 'Here they come!''} gxf5 (20... Ke8 {Ivkov,Borislav: 'Nick Conticello: 'while Ivkov in 'Informator' suggests''} 21. Ng7+ $1) (20... Kf6 21. Rd6 gxf5 22. Qxd7 {Ivkov,Borislav: 'Nick Conticello: '.''}) 21. exf5 Rac8 {Ivkov,Borislav: 'Nick Conticello: '?' Nick Conticello: 'I find it amazing that the final moves of this game are glossed over in every published commentary I have yet read.''} ({Instead} 21... Qxf5 {(Ivkov,Borislav) is Tal-Mukhin from Chapter One.} {Ivkov,Borislav: 'Nick Conticello: 'Kavalek gives''} 22. Qd6+ {Ivkov,Borislav: 'Nick Conticello: '!''} Kd8 (22... Ke8 23. Rfe1+ Be6 {which he likes for White.} {Ivkov,Borislav: 'Nick Conticello: 'Fischer is content to lie in wait, but objectively''} 24. Qd7# $1 {Ivkov,Borislav: 'Nick Conticello: 'is probably stronger. King gives''}) 23. Qxf8+ {Ivkov,Borislav: 'Nick Conticello: 'as playable. King continues here with''} Kc7 $5 {Ivkov,Borislav} 24. Qxa8) 22. Rxd7+ Qxd7 23. f6+ (23. Re1+ Ne5 24. Rxe5+ Kf6 {and wins.} 25. Qxd7 {White wins after} Kxe5 $2 {Ivkov,Borislav} 26. Qxb5+ {.}) 23... Nxf6 (23... Ke8 24. Re1+ $1 Qe6 25. Qxc8#) (23... Kxf6 24. Qxd7 $1) 24. Re1+ {No one has yet asked the obvious question: "Why not} Ne4 {(Ivkov,Borislav) - ?"} 25. Rxe4+ {. Clearly the answer is not} Kf6 $2 26. Qxd7 Rfd8 27. Qg4 (27. Qe7+ Kg6 {which trades too many pieces. Surely Mikhail Tal would not have repeated this line if that was all he could achieve!} (27... Kf5 28. Qe5+ $1 Kg6 29. Rg4+ Kh6 30. Qg5#) {. I believe Fischer would have played} 28. Rg4+ $1 {when I don't see a good defence for Black. The main line runs} Kf5 29. Rg5+ Kf4 30. Qe3#) 1-0

