{Bobby Fischer: 'GAME N. 58 Flawed masterpiece.  After Fischer dropped this miniature (his third loss in a row to Geller) Kurajica concluded: "He just cannot play against Geller ... Another Yugoslav, trIfunovich, opined at greater length:   Geller is one of the best-prepared players in the world as to opening theory. and Fischer cannot be superior in that respect ... Fischer [as White1 chose a very sharp and modern variation ... playing to win in the early stage of the game, as he usually does, and successfully, against weaker opponents, Fischer played better and attained a superior position, but it was very difficult to find the right solution over-the-board ... There was his mistake ... He has to impose a hard positional game, playing without pretensions for a win in the very opening.   Nowhere but in the notes that follow have the above errors been answered. Were it not for a momentary lapse (a3?), Fischer would have won this little gem on move twenty - despite his critics. '} 1. e4 {Bobby Fischer} c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 a6 6. Bg5 {Bobby Fischer: 'Position after'} e6 7. f4 Qb6 8. Qd2 Qxb2 {Bobby Fischer: 'Position after'} 9. Rb1 Qa3 10. f5 (10. e5) 10... Nc6 11. fxe6 fxe6 {Bobby Fischer: 'Position after'} 12. Nxc6 { xf6 Bobby Fischer: 'A critical position. White's immediate threat is 13. Bxf6'} bxc6 {? Geller} 13. e5 (13. Be2) 13... Nd5 (13... dxe5 14. Bxf6) 14. Nxd5 cxd5 15. Be2 $3 {+- Geller} (15. Bd3 $1 dxe5 16. O-O) 15... dxe5 16. O-O $1 Bc5+ (16... Ra7) 17. Kh1 Rf8 18. c4 $1 Rxf1+ 19. Rxf1 $1 {Bobby Fischer: 'A hard move to find - it took around 45 minutes. The threat of Rxf6 must be attended to.'} (19. Bxf1 h6 20. Bh4 Qe3 $18) 19... Bb7 {[#]} 20. Bg4 $2 (20. Qc2 e4 (20... Be7 21. Bxe7 Kxe7 22. Qxh7 Rb8 23. Qxg7+ $18 {Bobby Fischer: 'Mates.'} Kd6) 21. Bg4 $3) (20. Bd1 $1) 20... dxc4 21. Bxe6 Qd3 $3 {Bobby Fischer: 'I didn't see it! Moreover, the strength of this resource didn't become fully apparent to me for another two moves.'} 22. Qe1 (22. Bf7+ Kd7 23. Bxc4 $1 {Bobby Fischer: 'B.)'} Qxd2) 22... Be4 $1 23. Bg4 {Bobby Fischer: 'Position after'} ({Bobby Fischer: 'Losing! A couple of hours after the game it occurred to me that White has a problem-like win after'} 23. Bf5 $3 $18 { h5 Bobby Fischer: '(with the threat of Rh5) Black has no adequate defense. A.)'} Bxf5 24. Qxe5+ Kd7) 23... Rb8 $1 {Bobby Fischer: 'At long last I saw the point of Geller's clever defense. As I was studying 24 Rf4, it suddenly dawned on me that 24..Ba2+ was curtains so White resigns'} 24. Bd1 {Bobby Fischer} Kd7 $19 {After..} 25. Rf7+ {Bobby Fischer} Ke6 $1 $19 {is the quietus. It is not enough to be a good player, observed Dr Tarrasch; you must also play well.} {Bobby Fischer: 'Also futile is'} 26. Rf1 (26. Rxg7 Bxg2+ $1 $19 {Geller} 27. Kxg2 Rb2+ 28. Kh1 Qd5+ { 26... d4 -+}) 26... Rb2 27. Bg4+ Kd5 $19 0-1

