{[%evp 0,52,40,31,31,5,8,8,8,8,18,13,13,5,26,8,-23,-23,-19,-1,5,3,8,0,20,17,18,11,38,0,60,58,65,65,98,105,99,116,101,86,86,87,116,106,210,210,74,62,62,62,67,-273,-345,-403,-431]} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 g6 4. O-O Bg7 5. Re1 (5. c3 e6 ({Fischer's move is too violent. Stronger was either} 5... d5 {or} 6. Qa4 {with even play.}) 6. d4 cxd4 7. cxd4 Qb6 $16 {We can see that Fischer was an aggressive player in his youth. Stronger was} 8. Na3 $14 {Dubious move. After a better} Nxd4 9. Nc4 Nxf3+ 10. Qxf3 Qc7 11. Bf4 e5 $16 {White is clearly better.} 12. Nxe5 {was slightly preferable.} {In the case of} Bxe5 13. Rac1 Qb8 {after} 14. Rxc8+ $1 {White has a clear edge.} {Stronger was} Qxc8 $14 {After a stronger} 15. Bxe5 $16 {White has a clear edge.}) 5... e6 6. c3 Nge7 7. d4 $6 cxd4 8. cxd4 Qb6 9. Bxc6 dxc6 10. Na3 O-O 11. Nc4 Qd8 $6 12. Bf4 b6 $11 {The position is even.} 13. Rc1 Bd7 14. Qd2 Be8 $2 15. Bh6 Rc8 16. Qf4 f6 $6 (16... Qc7 17. Nd6 {White has a clear advantage:} Rd8 18. Bxg7 Kxg7 19. Nxe8+) 17. Bxg7 $1 $16 Kxg7 18. Qh4 c5 19. Red1 Qc7 20. Qh3 $6 Bf7 21. e5 Bg8 $6 (21... f5 22. Nd6 Rcd8 23. Nxf7 Rxf7 $11 {After a better} 24. Ng5) 22. Nd6 $6 Rcd8 {[#]} 23. dxc5 $5 fxe5 24. Qg3 h6 {[#]} 25. Qxe5+ $4 Kh7 $19 26. cxb6 Qxb6 {Glarring error which loses the game. After a better} 27. Rd3 {the position is even:} Nd5 (27... Nf5 28. Nxf5 Rxf5 $11 {The game move leads to an even position. Interesting is} 29. Rc7+ {although by precise play Black can attain an even position:} Bf7 30. Ng5+) (27... h5 28. Ng5+ Kh6 29. Qh8+ Kxg5 30. Rg3+ Kf4 31. Rc4+) 28. Ng5+ 0-1

