{Bobby Fischer: 'GAME N. 12 Castling into it.  Although not perfect. this is perhaps the most bitterly contested game in this book. Fischer chooses a difficult variation which requires Olympian judgment. He submits his King to an attack which. on the face of it. can only be described as irresistible. Why did he do it? Because. we are told. it was strategically justified. Gligorich. too. must be given equal credit for his courage and restraint. His continuation. despite intensive post-mortem analysis, has yet to be improved upon. The complexity of each phase of this tumultuous struggle must be studied to be believed. Curiously, in the "barren" Rook and Pawn ending, Gligorich somehow missed a win - a fact which he is probably unaware of to this day. ''GAME N. 12 Castling into it.  Although not perfect. this is perhaps the most bitterly contested game in this book. Fischer chooses a difficult variation which requires Olympian judgment. He submits his King to an attack which. on the face of it. can only be described as irresistible. Why did he do it? Because. we are told. it was strategically justified. Gligorich. too. must be given equal credit for his courage and restraint. His continuation. despite intensive post-mortem analysis, has yet to be improved upon. The complexity of each phase of this tumultuous struggle must be studied to be believed. Curiously, in the "barren" Rook and Pawn ending, Gligorich somehow missed a win - a fact which he is probably unaware of to this day.  Bulletin: 'Bobby Fischer: 'GAME N. 12 Castling into it.  Although not perfect. this is perhaps the most bitterly contested game in this book. Fischer chooses a difficult variation which requires Olympian judgment. He submits his King to an attack which. on the face of it. can only be described as irresistible. Why did he do it? Because. we are told. it was strategically justified. Gligorich. too. must be given equal credit for his courage and restraint. His continuation. despite intensive post-mortem analysis, has yet to be improved upon. The complexity of each phase of this tumultuous struggle must be studied to be believed. Curiously, in the "barren" Rook and Pawn ending, Gligorich somehow missed a win - a fact which he is probably unaware of to this day. '''} 1. e4 {Bobby Fischer Bobby Fischer Bobby Fischer: 'Bulletin Bulletin: 'Bobby Fischer''} c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 a6 6. Bg5 e6 7. f4 Be7 8. Qf3 Qc7 9. O-O-O Nbd7 10. g4 b5 {Bobby Fischer: 'Gligorich and I have a standing feud with this position, which we've reached no less than three times. I've lost twice and drawn once (this one).''Gligorich and I have a standing feud with this position, which we've reached no less than three times. I've lost twice and drawn once (this one). Bulletin: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Gligorich and I have a standing feud with this position, which we've reached no less than three times. I've lost twice and drawn once (this one).'''} 11. Bxf6 ({Bobby Fischer: 'Interesting is''Interesting is Bulletin: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Interesting is'''} 11. Bg2 Bb7 12. Rhe1 b4 13. Nd5 $5 exd5 14. exd5 Kf8 15. Nf5 Re8 {Bernstein,S-Fischer,R ch-USA 1957 0-1 Bobby Fischer: 'and Black won. Bernstein,S-Fischer,R ch-USA 1957 0-1''and Black won. Bernstein,S-Fischer,R ch-USA 1957 0-1 Bulletin: 'Bernstein,S-Fischer,R ch-USA 1957 0-1 Bobby Fischer: 'and Black won. Bernstein,S-Fischer,R ch-USA 1957 0-1'''}) 11... gxf6 $5 {[%emt 0:00:09] Bobby Fischer: 'see game''see game Bulletin: 'Bobby Fischer: 'see game'''} (11... Nxf6 {Walther,E-Fischer,R Zürich 1959 Bobby Fischer: 'Walther, E-Fischer,R Zürich 1959''Walther, E-Fischer,R Zürich 1959 Bulletin: 'Walther,E-Fischer,R Zürich 1959 Bobby Fischer: 'Walther, E-Fischer,R Zürich 1959'''}) 12. f5 {Bobby Fischer: 'Giving up e5 in order to exert pressure on e6. Our game at Zurich 1959 continued''Giving up e5 in order to exert pressure on e6. Our game at Zurich 1959 continued Bulletin: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Giving up e5 in order to exert pressure on e6. Our game at Zurich 1959 continued'''} (12. Bg2 Bb7 13. Rhe1 O-O-O 14. a3 Nb6 $10 {Gligoric,S-Fischer,R Zürich 1959 Bobby Fischer: '=' '=' Bobby Fischer: 'In the US Championship 1959-60, Mednis played''In the US Championship 1959-60, Mednis played Bulletin: '=' Bulletin: 'Gligoric,S-Fischer,R Zürich 1959 Bobby Fischer: '=' Bobby Fischer: 'In the US Championship 1959-60, Mednis played'''}) (12. a3 {Bobby Fischer: 'a3 against me. The game went''a3 against me. The game went Bulletin: 'Bobby Fischer: 'a3 against me. The game went'''} Bb7 (12... Rb8 $13 {Bobby Fischer: 'is sharper''is sharper Bulletin: 'Bobby Fischer: 'is sharper'''}) 13. f5 e5 14. Nde2 Nb6 15. Nd5 Bxd5 16. exd5 Rc8 17. Nc3 Nc4 18. Bxc4 bxc4 19. Kb1 Rb8 20. Ka2 $16 {Mednis,E-Fischer,R/USA-ch/1959/ Bobby Fischer: 'with a better game for White Mednis, E-Fischer,R ch-USA 1959''with a better game for White Mednis, E-Fischer,R ch-USA 1959 Bulletin: 'Mednis,E-Fischer,R/USA-ch/1959/ Bobby Fischer: 'with a better game for White Mednis, E-Fischer,R ch-USA 1959'''}) (12. Bd3 Bb7 13. Kb1 Nc5 14. f5 b4 15. Nce2 d5 16. fxe6 dxe4 17. exf7+ Kf8 18. Bxe4 Bxe4 19. Qxe4 Nxe4 20. Ne6+ Kxf7 21. Nxc7 Ra7 $10 {Padevsky,N-Evans,L Habana ol 1966 Bobby Fischer: '=' '=' Bobby Fischer: 'is exciting but equal. (Padevsky,N-Evans, L Habana ol 1966''is exciting but equal. (Padevsky,N-Evans, L Habana ol 1966 Bulletin: '=' Bulletin: 'Padevsky,N-Evans,L Habana ol 1966 Bobby Fischer: '=' Bobby Fischer: 'is exciting but equal. (Padevsky,N-Evans, L Habana ol 1966'''}) 12... Ne5 {Bobby Fischer: 'Simagin gave this a "?" and proceeded to analyze the alternative''Simagin gave this a "?" and proceeded to analyze the alternative Bulletin: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Simagin gave this a "?" and proceeded to analyze the alternative'''} (12... b4 13. fxe6 bxc3 (13... Ne5 14. Nd5 $1) 14. exd7+ Bxd7 15. e5 $16 {Smagin,V Bobby Fischer: 'etc. By this logic, the whole variation is unsound for Black. We shall see . Smagin,V''etc. By this logic, the whole variation is unsound for Black. We shall see . Smagin,V Bulletin: 'Smagin,V Bobby Fischer: 'etc. By this logic, the whole variation is unsound for Black. We shall see . Smagin,V'''}) 13. Qh3 {Bobby Fischer: 'Position after''Position after Bulletin: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Position after'''} O-O $1 {Bobby Fischer: 'Petrosian and Tal both happened to stroll by the board at this instant. Petrosian made a wry face which looked to me like "Can Black do this and live?" Black's"ugly" defense is based on sound positional considerations: once he can consolidate, there is a strong potential in the two Bishops coupled with his beautifully posted Knight and COlnpact Pawn lnass. These assets, in the long run, hopefully, should outweigh the telnporary weakness of his King and the imrnobile target on e6.''Petrosian and Tal both happened to stroll by the board at this instant. Petrosian made a wry face which looked to me like "Can Black do this and live?" Black's"ugly" defense is based on sound positional considerations: once he can consolidate, there is a strong potential in the two Bishops coupled with his beautifully posted Knight and COlnpact Pawn lnass. These assets, in the long run, hopefully, should outweigh the telnporary weakness of his King and the imrnobile target on e6. Bulletin: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Petrosian and Tal both happened to stroll by the board at this instant. Petrosian made a wry face which looked to me like "Can Black do this and live?" Black's"ugly" defense is based on sound positional considerations: once he can consolidate, there is a strong potential in the two Bishops coupled with his beautifully posted Knight and COlnpact Pawn lnass. These assets, in the long run, hopefully, should outweigh the telnporary weakness of his King and the imrnobile target on e6.'''} ({Bobby Fischer: 'Not''Not Bulletin: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Not'''} 13... Bd7 14. g5 $1 fxg5 {Bobby Fischer: '(if''(if Bulletin: 'Bobby Fischer: '(if'''} (14... exf5 15. Nd5) 15. fxe6 fxe6 16. Nxe6 $18 {Bobby Fischer: 'and Bla