1. d4 {Gligoric: In preparation for his 1992 match with Spassky], Bobby asked if I could play a training match with him.  At first I didn't want to, but I had to give in to his wishes. He was panicking about how theory had developed during his twenty-year absence from chess. That was why he came up with his own version of chess, where the starting position would be determined by the drawing of lots. And he began to torment me with persistent requests to write a book about it.} Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 Bg7 4. e4 d6 5. Nf3 O-O 6. Be2 e5 7. O-O Nc6 8. d5 Ne7 9. Nd2 a5 10. a3 Bd7 (10... Nd7) 11. b3 (11. Rb1) (11. Ra2) 11... c5 {[%csl Rb4]} 12. Bb2 $146 (12. Rb1 b6 (12... Ne8 13. b4 b6 {1-0 Gurevich,M (2630)-Ivanchuk,V (2625) Reggio Emilia-A 8889 31st 1988}) 13. b4 Nc8 14. bxa5 Rxa5 15. a4 Ne8 16. Nb3 Ra8 17. Bd2 f5 18. f3 Nf6 19. Ra1 f4 20. a5 bxa5 21. Nb5 a4 22. Qe1 Bxb5 23. cxb5 Nb6 24. Na5 Nfd7 25. Bd1 Qc7 26. Bxa4 Nxa4 {Danielian,O-Brenjo,S (2320)/Leningrad 1991/CBM 023 ext/½-½ (50)}) 12... Bh6 13. Qc2 b6 14. Nd1 $5 {Les Blancs auront des compensations pour le  sacrifié} Bxd2 15. Qxd2 Nxe4 16. Qd3 f5 17. f4 $1 $44 {[%csl Gb2,Rg7,Rg8]} exf4 18. Rxf4 (18. Nc3 $5 Nf6 (18... Nxc3 $2 19. Qxc3) 19. h4 h6 20. Rae1 g5 21. hxg5 hxg5 22. Bd1 Ng6 23. Nb5 Ne4 24. Rxe4 fxe4 25. Qc3 Qe7 26. Nxd6 $40) 18... Nf6 19. h4 Rf7 20. Nf2 Qf8 21. Nh3 {[%csl Ge6][%cal Gh3g5,Gg5e6]} (21. Rf1 {[%cal Gf4f7,Gg2g4]} Re8 22. g4 fxg4 23. Ne4 Nf5 {[%cal Gf5d6]} 24. Bxf6 Rxf6 25. Nxf6+ Qxf6 26. Bxg4 Qxh4 27. Bxf5 Bxf5 28. Rxh4 Bxd3 29. Rf6 Re1+ 30. Kg2 Rb1 $13) 21... h6 22. Raf1 $1 {[%csl Rf6,Rf7][%cal Gg2g4,Gh3f2]} Re8 23. Bd1 (23. g4 $5) 23... Nc8 24. Qg3 (24. g4) 24... Rg7 25. Qc3 Re5 26. Qc1 (26. g4 Rf7 (26... fxg4 27. Rxf6) (26... Nxg4 27. Rxg4) 27. gxf5 Bxf5) (26. Nf2 {[%cal Gg2g4]}) 26... Qe7 27. R4f2 Kh7 28. Nf4 Ne4 29. h5 gxh5 30. Rf3 Qg5 31. Qc2 {[%csl Rg2]} Ne7 32. Bc1 (32. Bxe5 $6 dxe5 33. Nh3 Qh4) 32... h4 (32... Ng6 33. Ne6 Qf6 34. Nxg7 Qxg7) 33. Ne6 Qf6 34. Nxg7 Kxg7 35. Bb2 {Menace de gagner une seconde qualité mais les Noirs vont trouver des ressources tactiques} Ng3 $132 36. Qf2 Qg5 (36... Nxf1 37. Qxf1 Qg5 38. Bxe5+ dxe5) 37. Re1 Ng6 38. Bc2 f4 39. Bxg6 (39. Bxe5+ dxe5 40. Bxg6 Kxg6 $44) 39... Kxg6 40. Bc1 Qe7 41. Rxe5 dxe5 42. Qe1 Qg5 43. Kh2 Bg4 $1 44. Bxf4 exf4 45. Qe8+ Kg7 46. d6 Bxf3 (46... Bh5 47. Qe7+ Qxe7 48. dxe7 Nf5 49. Rxf4 Nxe7 50. Rxh4 Bf7 $15) 47. Qd7+ Kf8 48. Qc8+ Kf7 49. Qd7+ Kg6 50. Qe8+ Kf5 51. gxf3 Nf1+ 52. Kh1 Ng3+ 53. Kh2 1/2-1/2

