1. d4 {Fischer,R'As Larry Evans described it in Fischer's incomparable Sixty Memorable Games 'This draw has the charm of perfection' Bulletin: 'Andrew Martin: 'As Larry Evans described it in Fischer's incomparable Sixty Memorable Games 'This draw has the charm of perfection''''} Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 Bg7 4. e4 d6 5. Nf3 O-O 6. Be2 e5 7. O-O Nc6 8. d5 Ne7 9. Ne1 Nd7 (9... Ne8 10. Nd3 f5 11. f4 exf4 12. Bxf4 fxe4 13. Nxe4 Nf5 14. Bg5 Nf6 15. g4 Nd4 16. Ndf2 Qe7 $10 {Petrosian,T-Tal,M/Bled/1961/ Fischer,R: '=' Fischer,R: 'Petrosian,T-Tal,M Bled 1961'}) 10. Nd3 (10. f3 f5 11. Be3 f4 12. Bf2 g5 $40) 10... f5 11. exf5 {'A variation which today has been discarded but which might prove useful as an occasional surprise weapon. Perhaps Gligoric wanted to avoid the young man's monstrous theoretical knowledge. Bulletin: 'Andrew Martin: 'A variation which today has been discarded but which might prove useful as an occasional surprise weapon. Perhaps Gligoric wanted to avoid the young man's monstrous theoretical knowledge.'''} Nxf5 {×e4 ; ×d4''×e4 ; ×d4 Andrew Martin: 'Bulletin: '×e4 ; ×d4''' '} ({'If Bulletin: 'Andrew Martin: 'If'''} 11... gxf5 12. f4 {'then Bulletin: 'Andrew Martin: 'then'''} e4 (12... Ng6 $1 13. Be3 exf4 14. Nxf4 Nxf4 15. Bxf4 a6 16. Qd2 Qf6 17. Rae1 Ne5 {Idea ...Bd7 and ...Rae8. This is a solid and reliable way to treat the position as Black}) 13. Nf2 {g2-g4}) 12. f3 Nf6 (12... Nd4 $10 {Reshevsky,S-Fischer,R (11)/Los Angeles m/1961/ Fischer,R: '=' Fischer,R: 'Reshevsky,S-Fischer,R (11) Los Angeles 1961'}) 13. Nf2 Nd4 14. Nfe4 Nh5 $6 {Fischer,R: '=' Andrew Martin: '=!''The Knight dance has left the position equal. White looks for the right moment to play c4-c5 and Black can play his Knight to f4, following up with ...g5-g4! Bulletin: '?!''Andrew Martin: '=!' '=!' Andrew Martin: 'The Knight dance has left the position equal. White looks for the right moment to play c4-c5 and Black can play his Knight to f4, following up with ...g5-g4!' Andrew Martin: 'The Knight dance has left the position equal. White looks for the right moment to play c4-c5 and Black can play his Knight to f4, following up with ...g5-g4! Bulletin: '?!''' '} (14... c5 $1) 15. Bg5 Qd7 {× d6,  c7-c5'One of those strange-looking moves which is the same time absolutely forced. Black wants to play ...c7-c5 to reinforce his Knight , but must keep the d pawn protected.'× d6,  c7-c5 Andrew Martin: 'One of those strange-looking moves which is the same time absolutely forced. Black wants to play ...c7-c5 to reinforce his Knight , but must keep the d pawn protected.' Andrew Martin: 'One of those strange-looking moves which is the same time absolutely forced. Black wants to play ...c7-c5 to reinforce his Knight , but must keep the d pawn protected. Bulletin: '× d6,  c7-c5''' '} 16. g3 h6 {Andrew Martin: '!''Bulletin: 'Andrew Martin: '!' '!'''} ({'Fischer mentions a game Gligoric-Tal where Black played Bulletin: 'Andrew Martin: 'Fischer mentions a game Gligoric-Tal where Black played'''} 16... c5 $2 {'but after Bulletin: '?''Andrew Martin: 'but after' Andrew Martin: 'but after Bulletin: '?''' '} 17. Nb5 $1 {'Bulletin: '!''Andrew Martin: 'Bulletin: '!''' '} Nxb5 18. cxb5 $16 {Tal,M-Gligoric,S/Bled/1961/ Fischer,R: 'Tal,M-Gligoric,S Bled 1961' Andrew Marti'White retained a bind Bulletin: '''Tal,M-Gligoric,S/Bled/1961/ Andrew Martin: '' '' Andrew Martin: 'White retained a bind' Andrew Martin: 'White retained a bind Bulletin: '' Bulletin: 'Tal,M-Gligoric,S/Bled/1961/''' ' n: ''}) 17. Be3 c5 $1 (17... Nxe2+ 18. Qxe2 g5 19. c5 $16) 18. Bxd4 (18. Nb5 Nf5 19. Bd2 a6) 18... exd4 19. Nb5 a6 (19... Be5 $2 20. f4) 20. Nbxd6 {'It looks as though Bobby has blundered a pawn but it was deliberate. After his next move, Black's position comes to life. Bulletin: 'Andrew Martin: 'It looks as though Bobby has blundered a pawn but it was deliberate. After his next move, Black's position comes to life.'''} d3 $1 21. Qxd3 {'Gligoric recognises the danger and plays the line which will keep his King safe. Or so it seems. Bulletin: 'Andrew Martin: 'Gligoric recognises the danger and plays the line which will keep his King safe. Or so it seems.'''} ({'If Bulletin: 'Andrew Martin: 'If'''} 21. Bxd3 Bd4+ 22. Kh1 Nxg3+ 23. Nxg3 Qxd6 24. Qc2 Bh3 $13 {'Fischer Bulletin: 'Andrew Martin: 'Fischer'''}) 21... Bd4+ (21... Bxb2 22. Nxc8 Bxa1 23. Nb6 $19 Bd4+ $2 24. Qxd4 {Fischer,R: '+-'}) 22. Kg2 (22. Kh1 Nxg3+ 23. Nxg3 Qxd6 $44) 22... Nxg3 $1 {Andrew Martin: '!!''A super resource which Fischer recounts that he had visualised back at move 17. Now , as Larry Evans puts it, 'Gligoric rises to the occasion, returning material in an attempt to wrest the advantage' Bulletin: '!''Andrew Martin: '!!' '!!' Andrew Martin: 'A super resource which Fischer recounts that he had visualised back at move 17. Now , as Larry Evans puts it, 'Gligoric rises to the occasion, returning material in an attempt to wrest the advantage'' Andrew Martin: 'A super resource which Fischer recounts that he had visualised back at move 17. Now , as Larry Evans puts it, 'Gligoric rises to the occasion, returning material in an attempt to wrest the advantage' Bulletin: '!''' '} 23. Nxc8 $1 (23. hxg3 $2 Qh3#) (23. Kxg3 $2 Qh3#) (23. Nxg3 Qxd6 $44) 23... Nxf1 24. Nb6 $1 Qc7 $1 25. Rxf1 (25. Nxa8 $2 Qxh2+ 26. Kxf1 Qg1#) 25... Qxb6 26. b4 $1 {Andrew Martin: '!!''A great move! Fischer gives the following variations: Bulletin: '!''Andrew Martin: '!!' '!!' Andrew Martin: 'A great move! Fischer gives the following variations:' Andrew Martin: 'A great move! Fischer gives the following variations: Bulletin: '!''' '} Qxb4 (26... cxb4 27. c5 $1 {'Bulletin: '!''Andrew Martin: 'Bulletin: '!''' '} Bxc5 28. Nxc5 Qxc5 29. Qxg6+ Kh8 30. Qxh6+ Kg8 31. Kh1 $18 {Andrew Martin: '+-!''Bulletin: '+-''Andrew Martin: '+-!' '+-!' Andrew Martin: 'Bulletin: '+-''' '}) (26... Rf7 27. bxc5 Bxc5 28. Rb1 $36 { d5-d6 Andrew Martin: '!''idea d5-d6, with counterplay Bulletin: ''' d5-d6 Andrew Martin: '!' '!' Andrew Martin: 'idea