{Bobby Fischer: 'GAME N. 19 A long voyage home. Illustrating, rather subtly, how a weaker player may be lured to his own destruction, Fischer entices his opponent to abandon his passive though solid attempts to settle for a draw. Wrongly convinced that he holds an advantage, Gudmundsson. with 16 e4, gives Fischer the opportunity to launch a long. unclear sacrifidal combination. Gudmundsson makes matters unexpectedly easy with 24 Rb I, but the analysis accompanying the text shows the sacrifice to be sound in all variations. Fischer's performance from here on is typical in its clarity and forcefulness. '} 1. d4 {Bobby Fischer} Nf6 2. Nf3 {Bobby Fischer: 'Solid but passive.'} d5 3. e3 {Bobby Fischer: 'Voluntarily locking in the Bishop lacks energy and reduces White's options.'} g6 4. c4 (4. c3 {Colle,E Bobby Fischer: '4 c3 would lead to the Colle System. Colle,E'}) 4... Bg7 5. Nc3 O-O 6. Qb3 ({Bobby Fischer: 'AFTER'} 6. Be2 c5 $1 {Bobby Fischer: 'it's difficult for White to equalize: A.)'} 7. O-O $2 ({Bobby Fischer: 'B.)'} 7. cxd5 Nxd5 8. Qb3 Nxc3 9. bxc3 Qc7 10. O-O b6 11. a4 Nc6 $17 {Goglidze,n-Botvinnik,M Moscow 1935 Bobby Fischer: 'Black's better. Goglidze,n-Botvinnik,M Moscow 1935'}) (7. dxc5 Qa5 8. cxd5 (8. O-O dxc4 9. Bxc4 Qxc5) 8... Nxd5 9. Qxd5 Bxc3+ 10. Bd2 (10. Kf1 Bg7 11. Bd2 Qc7 $40 {Bobby Fischer: 'Black regains his Pawn at will, with a strong attack)'}) 10... Rd8 $1 11. Bxc3 Qxc3+ 12. bxc3 Rxd5 $17 {Bobby Fischer: 'with the superior ending IF'} 13. Rd1 Rxc5 14. Rd8+ Kg7 15. O-O Nc6 16. Re8 b6) 7... cxd4 8. Nxd4 Nc6 9. cxd5 Nxd5 10. Nxd5 Qxd5 11. Bf3 Qc4 12. Nxc6 bxc6 $17 {Aaron,M-Gligoric,S Stockholm izt 1962 Bobby Fischer: 'Aaron,M-Gligoric,S Stockholm izt 1962'}) 6... e6 {Bobby Fischer: 'Another good build-up is 6 ... c6 followed by ... e6, ... b6, ...Bb7, Nbd7, .. . c5, etc.'} (6... c6 { b7-b6, b7, bd7, c6-c5 Bobby Fischer: '/\ b7-b6, Bb7, Nbd7, c6-c5'}) 7. Be2 Nc6 8. Qc2 {Bobby Fischer: 'Probably best (Black threatened ...Na5 winning the two Bishops). As Evans pointed out in Trophy Chess (in an analogous position): "8 cxd5 exd5 pennits Black to solve the problem of his QB. He has the semiopen e~file and good squares for his pieces. It is now White who must fight for equality!"'} (8. cxd5 exd5 $17 {Evans,L}) 8... dxc4 9. Bxc4 e5 10. dxe5 {Bobby Fischer: 'Position after'} ({Bobby Fischer: 'ALSO GOOD IS'} 10. Nxe5 Nxe5 11. dxe5 Ng4 12. e6 $1 ({Bobby Fischer: 'NOT'} 12. f4 $2 Nxe5 $1 13. fxe5 Qh4+ 14. g3 Qxc4 $17 {Bobby Fischer: 'ETC'}) 12... Bxe6 13. Bxe6 fxe6 14. O-O $10 {Bobby Fischer: '='}) ({Bobby Fischer: 'IF'} 10. d5 $2 Na5) 10... Ng4 11. O-O ({Bobby Fischer: 'STRONGER IS'} 11. e6 $1 { Bobby Fischer: '>='} Bxe6 12. Bxe6 fxe6 13. O-O (13. Qe4 $2 Nce5 $1 14. Nxe5 $2 Nxf2 $1 15. Qc4 Bxe5 16. Qxe6+ Rf7 17. Qxe5 Nd3+ $19 {Bobby Fischer: 'wins), and Black seems to have nothing better than a draw by perpetual after'}) 13... Rxf3 14. gxf3 Qh4 15. fxg4 Qxg4+ 16. Kh1 Qf3+ $10 {Bobby Fischer: '=' Bobby Fischer: 'ETC'}) 11... Ncxe5 12. Nxe5 Nxe5 13. Be2 c6 $10 {Bobby Fischer: '=' Bobby Fischer: 'The chances are now equal.'} 14. f4 ({Bobby Fischer: 'Apparently stronger is'} 14. e4 { Bobby Fischer: 'BUT AFTER'} Qh4 $1 15. h3 ({Bobby Fischer: 'IF'} 15. f4 Ng4) 15... g5 $1 16. f4 (16. Nd1 f5 17. f4 Ng6 18. fxg5 f4 $1) 16... gxf4 17. Bxf4 (17. Rxf4 Qg3) 17... Kh8 $40 {Bobby Fischer: 'gives Black good prospects along the ventilated g-file.'}) 14... Ng4 $1 15. h3 {Bobby Fischer: 'Position after'} Bf5 $1 {Bobby Fischer: 'White was doubtlessly expecting 15 ... Nf6'} 16. e4 $2 {Bobby Fischer: 'with an ideal center.'} ({Bobby Fischer: 'Provoking a powerful combination. White should abandon his hopes in the center and settle for'} 16. Qb3 { Bobby Fischer: '>='} Nf6 17. Qxb7 Ne4 $1 18. Qxc6 Rc8 19. Qa6 Nxc3 20. bxc3 Bxc3 21. Ba3 Bxa1 22. Bxf8 Bd4 $1 23. exd4 Qxd4+ 24. Kh1 Kxf8 $15 {Bobby Fischer: 'Black is better, but White has excellent drawing chances.'}) 16... Qd4+ 17. Kh1 Nf2+ 18. Rxf2 $8 {Bobby Fischer: ''} ({Bobby Fischer: 'All forced. NOT'} 18. Kh2 Nxe4) 18... Qxf2 19. exf5 Bxc3 $1 ({Bobby Fischer: 'This clean-cut line reduces White's options. Inexact would be'} 19... Rfe8 20. Ne4 $1 Qe1+ 21. Kh2 gxf5 (21... Bd4 22. Be3 $1 Qxa1 23. Bxd4) 22. Ng3 {Bobby Fischer: 'and if'} Bd4 $2 23. Be3 $1) 20. bxc3 Rae8 21. Bd3 Re1+ 22. Kh2 Qg1+ 23. Kg3 {Bobby Fischer: 'Position after'} Rfe8 {Bobby Fischer: 'Just as complicated is 23...gxf5 24 Bxf5 Rfe8 25 Bxh7+ Kg7 26 Qf5 etc'} 24. Rb1 $2 ({Bobby Fischer: 'Also bad is'} 24. Qf2 R8e3+ $1 25. Bxe3 Rxe3+ 26. Qxe3 Qxe3+ $19) ({Bobby Fischer: 'The toughest defense is'} 24. fxg6 $1 hxg6 {Bobby Fischer: 'and now a.)'} 25. Bxg6 $2 ({Bobby Fischer: 'b.)'} 25. Rb1 R8e3+ $1 {Bobby Fischer: 'if'} 26. Bxe3 {Bobby Fischer: 'leads to the same)'} (26. Kg4 Qh2 27. Bxe3 Rxe3) 26... Rxe3+ 27. Kg4 ({Bobby Fischer: 'not'} 27. Kh4 $2 Qh2 28. Qf2 Rxh3+ $1) 27... Qh2 28. Qf2 ({Bobby Fischer: 'if'} 28. Bxg6 Qg3+ 29. Kh5 Qxf4 $1 30. Bf5 Rg3 $1 31. Bg4 Kg7 32. Qc1 ({Bobby Fischer: 'if'} 32. Kh4 Rxg4+ 33. hxg4 Qh2+ $19 {Bobby Fischer: 'mates'}) 32... Re3 $19 {Bobby Fischer: 'wins.'}) 28... Rxd3 (28... Rxh3 $5 29. Bxg6 $1 fxg6 30. Rh1 $1 $10 {Bobby Fischer: '=!' Bobby Fischer: 'holds'}) 29. Rb2 $1 (29. Rxb7 Rxh3 30. Rb8+ Kh7 31. f5 Rh6 $1 $19) 29... Rxc3 30. Rd2 $17 {Bobby Fischer: 'and White has drawing chances even though a Pawn behind.'}) 25... R1e2 $1 ({Bobby Fischer: 'not'} 25... R8e2 26. Bxf7+ Kh8 27. Qf5 Rxg2+ 28. Kh4 Qf2+ 29. Kh5 Qf3+ 30. Kh6 $1 $18 {Bobby Fischer: 'and White wins.'}) 26. Bxf7+ Kh8 27. Qf5 Rxg2+ 28. Kh4 Qe1+ 29. Kh5 Kg7 $1 {Bobby Fischer: '(threatening 30 .. Rh8+)'} 30. Bxe8 Qxe8+ 31. Kh4 Qd8+ 32. Qg5+ Rxg5 33. fxg5 Qd1 $19 {Bobby Fischer: 'with an easy win'}) 24... gxf5 { h8; 8e6  Bobby Fischer: 'Threatening either Kh8; R8e6 with a devastating check to follow on the g-file.'} 25. Bd2 ({Bobby Fischer: 'no better is'} 25. Bxf5 R1e2 26. Bxh7+ Kh8 27. Qf5 Rxg2+ 28. Kh4 Rg7 $19 {Bobby Fischer: '(among others) wins'}) 25... Rxb1 26. Qxb1 Qxb1 27. Bxb1 {Bobby Fischer: 'Final Position after'} Re2 {Bobby Fischer: 'This is what Gudmundsson overlooked. Ifnow 28 i.el l:el picks off one of the Bishops. So ... White resigns'} (27... Re2 28. Bc1 Re1 $19) 0-1

