{[%evp 0,18,32,16,25,-16,36,35,41,26,45,37,46,38,43,27,32,17,24,20,18]} 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 Bg7 4. Nf3 O-O 5. e4 d6 {The King Indian Defence was Fischer's favorite opening from his youth.} 6. h3 {At the time when this game was played, this old continuation was considered to be dubious. However, it is popular again lately. It has two ideas: prophylactics - it limits the scope of c8 and prepares for a potential g4.} Nbd7 ({Nowadays, most often played is} 6... e5) 7. Be3 e5 8. d5 a5 ({The alternative is} 8... Nc5) 9. Be2 ({Interesting is} 9. g4 $5 {which is a modern approach.}) 9... b6 (9... Nc5 {was preferable.}) 10. O-O $6 ({Stronger is} 10. g4 $16) 10... Ne8 $6 ({After a better} 10... Nc5 11. Nd2 Nfd7 {the position is even.}) 11. Qc2 Nc5 12. Nh2 (12. a3 $14 {is preferable.}) 12... f5 13. f3 $6 ({Too passive. Preferable was} 13. exf5 gxf5 14. f4 $13) 13... f4 $1 14. Bf2 Qg5 (14... Bf6 $5 $17) 15. Kh1 Bd7 16. Rg1 (16. b3 $13) 16... Nf6 17. g4 $2 ({Mistake which leads to a lost position. After a better} 17. b3 {the position is unclear.}) 17... fxg3 $19 18. Rxg3 Qh6 19. Nd1 Nh5 20. Rg1 Bxh3 21. Be3 Nf4 22. Nf2 Bf6 (22... Bd7 $5) 23. Rg3 Bd7 24. Nfg4 Bxg4 (24... Qh5 $5 $19) 25. Rxg4 Qg7 26. Rag1 Be7 27. Qd2 Rf7 28. R1g3 Raf8 29. Bxf4 Rxf4 30. Rh3 Qf7 31. Rgg3 Bh4 32. Rg4 Bf2 33. Bd1 $19 1/2-1/2

