{Bobby Fischer: 'GAME N. 37 Only a draw. This contest brings to mind Emanuel Lasker's axiom: "When evenly matched opponents play 'correctly' the games seldom have any content and frequently end in draws." Here a little incorrect play provokes a series of brilliant moves leading to a most unusual draw. Employing a slow, closed system against the Sicilian, Keres is strategically outplayed. By adjournment, however, he manages to achieve equality. Fischer refuses a draw, and the struggle flares anew. Working with a Rook against two minor pieces, he makes steady inroads. Each serpentine twist in the endgame, including the double error on move 56, is a joy, a revelation, and a study in itself. Keres' saving resources smack of sheer wizardry. '} 1. e4 {Bobby Fischer} c5 2. Ne2 d6 3. g3 g6 ({Bobby Fischer: 'Sharper is'} 3... d5 $5 {Bobby Fischer: '!'} 4. Bg2 dxe4 5. Bxe4 ({on Lombardy's} 5. Nbc3 {Bobby Fischer} Nf6 {equalizes.} ({but not} 5... f5 6. d3 exd3 7. cxd3 Nf6 8. O-O {and White's attack is worth more than a Pawn.})) 5... Nf6 6. Bg2 Nc6 7. O-O e6 $10 {Bobby Fischer: '='}) 4. Bg2 Bg7 5. O-O {Bobby Fischer: ', Harmless.'} ({Bobby Fischer: 'Correct is'} 5. c3 $142 Nc6 6. d4 {Bobby Fischer: 'with a powerful center. If Black goes Pawn hunting now he gets shattered:'} cxd4 ({Bobby Fischer: 'The sober'} 6... e5 7. dxc5 dxc5 8. Qxd8+ Nxd8 9. Na3 $14 {Bobby Fischer: 'allows White only a slightly better ending.'}) 7. cxd4 Qb6 $2 8. Nbc3 Nxd4 $2 9. Nd5 Qc5 10. Nxd4 Bxd4 11. Be3 $1 Bxe3 12. fxe3 Qa5+ 13. b4 Qd8 14. Rc1 Rb8 15. O-O Bd7 16. Qd4 f6 17. Nc7+ Kf7 18. e5 $1 $40 {Samarian,S-Wesen/corr/1958/ Bobby Fischer: '!' Bobby Fischer: 'with a strong attack. (Samarian-Wesen, corres. 1958.)'}) 5... Nc6 6. c3 e5 $1 7. d3 {Bobby Fischer: ', Now White has to regroup in order to get in d4. '} Nge7 8. a3 {Bobby Fischer: ', A lemon, but already White must fight for equality.'} ({Bobby Fischer: 'On'} 8. Be3 $142 O-O 9. d4 exd4 10. cxd4 {Bobby Fischer: '(Pachman-Tal, Amsterdam, 1964).'} cxd4 ({Bobby Fischer: 'also good is'} 10... d5 11. Nbc3 Bg4 $1) 11. Nxd4 Ne5 $36 {Pachmann,L-Tal,M Amsterdam 1964 Bobby Fischer: 'Black captures the initiative.'}) 8... O-O {Bobby Fischer: '; Deciding to ignore the Q-side.'} ({Bobby Fischer: 'Keres hoped for'} 8... a5 9. a4 $1 {× b5 Bobby Fischer: 'and White has tricked Black into weakening his b5 square.'}) 9. b4 {Bobby Fischer: ', Probably played against Keres' better judgment, but I guess he wanted to justify his last move. One lemon leads to another. '} b6 10. f4 exf4 $1 {Bobby Fischer: '; Abandoning the center to play against White's shaky Pawn structure. '} 11. gxf4 ({Bobby Fischer: 'Not'} 11. Nxf4 $2 cxb4 12. axb4 Nxb4 $1) ({Bobby Fischer: 'or'} 11. Bxf4 d5) 11... d5 $1 ({Bobby Fischer: 'Wrong is'} 11... cxb4 12. axb4 Nxb4 $2 13. f5 $1 Nec6 14. e5 {Bobby Fischer: 'etc.'}) 12. e5 {Bobby Fischer: ', Poker-faced, as always, Keres made this move as though it were the most natural one on the board. But it was the last thing he wanted to do, since it exposes the poverty of White's strategy. '} Bg4 {Bobby Fischer: '; Not bad,'} ({Bobby Fischer: 'but'} 12... Nf5 $142 {Bobby Fischer: 'a la Nimzovich is even better. After'} 13. Ng3 Nce7 { f7-f6 Bobby Fischer: 'maintains a solid blockade, and Black can break with ... f6 at his leisure.'}) 13. h3 Bxe2 ({Bobby Fischer: 'Even stronger is'} 13... Be6 $142 14. Ng3 Qd7 15. Kh2 f6 {Bobby Fischer: 'The absence of Black's QB makes it difficult to exploit the white square weaknesses.'}) 14. Qxe2 f6 15. b5 {Bobby Fischer: ', The only way to keep the center from crumbling.'} ({Bobby Fischer: 'After'} 15. e6 f5 {× e6 Bobby Fischer: 'the advanced e-pawn becomes a target.'}) 15... Na5 16. Nd2 ({Bobby Fischer: 'Better is'} 16. Ra2 $142 {Bobby Fischer: 'If then'} fxe5 17. fxe5 Rxf1+ 18. Qxf1 Bxe5 19. Bg5 $1 {Bobby Fischer: 'is strong.'}) 16... fxe5 17. fxe5 Rxf1+ 18. Nxf1 {Bobby Fischer: ', Any recapture proves to be awkward.'} ({Bobby Fischer: 'Also'} 18. Bxf1 Qc7 $1 19. Nf3 ({Bobby Fischer: 'not'} 19. d4 cxd4 20. cxd4 Qc3) 19... Nb3 {Bobby Fischer: 'is similar to the game.'}) 18... Nb3 19. Rb1 Nxc1 20. Rxc1 Qc7 $1 21. Re1 ({Bobby Fischer: 'Still impossible is'} 21. d4 $2 cxd4 {Bobby Fischer: 'and White can't recapture because of the pin.'}) {Bobby Fischer: 'Despite the drawing tendency of the opposite colored Bishops, White has a difficult game: he's weak on all the squares and his King is somewhat exposed. '} 21... Rd8 22. Nh2 ({Bobby Fischer: 'Black gets an iron grip after'} 22. d4 cxd4 23. cxd4 Nf5 $36 { h6 Bobby Fischer: 'followed by'} 24. Z0 {Bobby Fischer} Bh6 {etc.}) 22... d4 23. cxd4 cxd4 24. Nf3 $2 {Bobby Fischer: '; A terrible boner,'} ({Bobby Fischer: 'just when White could equalize with'} 24. Ng4 $1 Rf8 25. Rf1 $10) 24... Bh6 $1 {Bobby Fischer: '; Keres probably underestimated the strength of this reply. '} 25. Qa2+ Kh8 26. Qe6 Nd5 $2 {Bobby Fischer: '; Tempting but wrong.'} ({Bobby Fischer: 'Correct is'} 26... Nf5 $1 27. Qf6+ ({Bobby Fischer: 'if'} 27. Nh2 $2 Be3+ $19 {Bobby Fischer: 'wins.'}) 27... Bg7 28. Qe6 Rf8 { h6 Bobby Fischer: 'followed by ...Bh6 again, and it's just a matter of time before Black invades on the weak dark squares. For example,'} 29. Ng5 ({Bobby Fischer: 'not'} 29. Nh2 Qc3 $1) 29... Bh6 30. Ne4 Be3+ 31. Kh1 Bf4 32. Nf6 Qc3 33. Rd1 Qc2 $36 {Bobby Fischer: 'etc.'}) 27. Nh2 $1 {Bobby Fischer: ', The saving clause.'} ({Bobby Fischer: 'Not'} 27. Nxd4 $2 Qc5) 27... Ne3 ({Bobby Fischer: 'After'} 27... Nf4 $2 28. Qf6+ Kg8 29. Ng4 $18 {Bobby Fischer: 'White wins!'}) 28. Bc6 $1 {Bobby Fischer: ', Now the Queen is hemmed in and Black has nothing. The Knight on e3 must coordinate with the heavy artillery to be really meaningful. '} Rf8 29. Nf3 $10 {Bobby Fischer: '='} Bf4 ({Bobby Fischer: 'On'} 29... Qd8 30. Qd6 {Bobby Fischer: 'holds.'}) {Bobby Fischer: 'The chances are now even. '} 30. Nxd4 Bxe5 31. Nf3 Bd4 $1 32. Rxe3 ({Bobby Fischer: 'Not'} 32. Nxd4 $4 Qg3+) 32... Bxe3+ ({Bobby Fischer: 'On'} 32... Qf4 33. Kf2 $1 {Bobby Fischer: 'holds.'}) 33. Qxe3 Qg3+ 34. Kf1 Qxh3+ 35. Ke1 Qf5 36. d4 Kg7 (36... h5 $2 37. Qh6+ Kg8 38. Bd5+ Qxd5 39. Qxg6+ $10 {Bobby Fischer: 'draws.'}) 37. Kf2 $1 {Bobby Fischer: ', The right plan - the King must stay on the K-side to blockade Black's Pawns. Eventually Black, to make progress, must advance; but in so doing he will expose his King to perpetual check.'} ({Bobby Fischer: 'Worse is'} 37. Qe5+ Qxe5+ 38. dxe5 Rf4 { a4 Bobby Fischer: '(intending Ra4).'}) {Bobby Fischer: 'White's e-Pawn can always be stopped by the King. '} 37... h5 38. Kg3 Qg4+ 39. Kh2 Rf4 ({Bobby Fischer: 'On'} 39... Qf4+ 40. Qxf4 Rxf4 41. Kg3 $15 {Bobby Fischer: 'holds.'}) ({Bobby Fischer: 'And not'} 39... h4 $2 40. Qe7+ Rf7 41. Qxf7+ $1) 40. Qe7+ Kh6 {Bobby Fischer: '; The game was adjourned and Keres sealed his move. Upon resuming the next day, he offered me a draw, which I rejected. I knew Black no longer had a winning advantage, but felt no harm could come from continuing since there was little danger of losing. Besides, winning this game would still have put me in contention for first place even as late as round 14, the halfway mark. '} 41. Qe2 Qf5 42. Qe3 g5 43. Kg2 Rg4+ 44. Kf2 Rf4 45. Kg2 Qc2+ {Bobby Fischer: ', Beginning a series of exploratory checks to see if White goes to the wrong square.' Bobby Fischer: 'For instance,'} {Bobby Fischer: 'Hope springs eternal! '} 46. Kh1 (46. Kg3 $2 Rg4+ 47. Kh3 Qg2#) 46... Qb1+ 47. Kh2 Qa2+ 48. Kh3 Qf7 49. Kh2 Qf6 50. Kg2 Kg7 {Bobby Fischer: '; Getting out of the potential pin.'} ({Bobby Fischer: 'Not'} 50... g4 $2 51. Kg3) {Bobby Fischer: 'Black must strive to advance the Pawns so that they retain maximum mobility. '} 51. Kg3 h4+ 52. Kg2 (52. Kh2 $2 {Bobby Fischer: 'loses to'} g4 $19) 52... Rg4+ (52... g4 {Bobby Fischer: 'is refuted by'} 53. Nxh4 $1) 53. Kh1 Rg3 54. Qe4 g4 55. Nh2 Qg5 56. Nf1 $2 {Bobby Fischer: ', A blunder on the last move of the second time-control. Perhaps Keres has allowed me to get a little too much out of the position,'} ({Bobby Fischer: 'but he can still hold a draw with'} 56. Qe5+ $1 Qxe5 57. dxe5 {Bobby Fischer: '(threatening Bd7)'} Rxa3 58. Nxg4 $10 {Bobby Fischer: 'etc.'}) 56... Rh3+ $2 {Bobby Fischer: '; I had a feeling this might be a mistake, but time was short and I had to make a move - any move. "Patzer sees a check, gives a check." But now the game can no longer be won.'} ({Bobby Fischer: 'Correct is'} 56... Rxa3 $1 57. d5 g3 58. d6 ({Bobby Fischer: 'if'} 58. Bd7 Ra1 59. Kg2 Ra2+ 60. Kg1 Qf6 61. Bf5 Rf2) 58... Ra1 59. Qe7+ ({Bobby Fischer: 'if'} 59. Kg1 Qc5+ $19 {Bobby Fischer: 'wins.'}) 59... Qxe7 60. dxe7 h3 $1 61. e8=N+ Kf8 $19 {Bobby Fischer: 'wins.'}) 57. Kg1 Rxa3 58. d5 g3 59. Bd7 $1 Ra1 {Bobby Fischer: '; No longer gains a tempo, as in the last note. '} 60. Bf5 $1 {Bobby Fischer: ', The idea is to advance the Pawn to d6 without allowing ...Qc5+. I must confess that I still expected to win. But now Keres really starts to find moves! '} Qf6 61. Qf4 Re1 62. d6 Re5 63. Qg4+ $1 ({Bobby Fischer: 'No'} 63. d7 $2 Rxf5 64. Qxf5 Qxf5 65. d8=Q Qf2+ {Bobby Fischer: 'and mate next.'} 66. Kh1 Qxf1#) 63... Kf8 64. d7 Rd5 ({Bobby Fischer: 'Now'} 64... Rxf5 65. d8=Q+ $1 Qxd8 66. Qxf5+ $10 {Bobby Fischer: 'draws.'}) 65. Kg2 $1 Rxd7 $1 ({Bobby Fischer: 'On'} 65... Qb2+ 66. Kh3 Qf2 67. Be4 $1 Qxf1+ 68. Bg2 Qf2 69. Qb4+ $10 {Bobby Fischer: 'holds.'}) 66. Bxd7 $1 {Bobby Fischer: ', I thought this was a mistake at the time, but that he was lost anyway. Keres, however, has seen just one move further '} Qf2+ 67. Kh3 Qxf1+ 68. Kxh4 g2 69. Qb4+ Kf7 $1 70. Qb3+ Kg7 71. Qg3+ Kh7 $1 {Bobby Fischer: '; Haven - at last. Now I was sure I had him.' Bobby Fischer: 'Surely he would go in for'} 72. Qe5 $3 {Bobby Fischer: ', What's this? He makes no attempt to stop me from queening!? Gradually my excitement subsided. The more I studied the situation, the more I realized Black had no win. '} (72. Bf5+ Qxf5 73. Qxg2 Qf4+ $1 74. Qg4 ({Bobby Fischer: 'On'} 74. Kh3 Qh6+ $1 $19 {Bobby Fischer: '!' Bobby Fischer: 'wins.'}) 74... Qxg4+ 75. Kxg4 Kg6 $1 $19 {Bobby Fischer: '!' Bobby Fischer: 'gaining the opposition and winning White's last Pawn by force.'}) 72... Qh1+ ({Bobby Fischer: 'The main line also draws - by a miracle:'} 72... Qf2+ 73. Kh3 g1=Q {Bobby Fischer: '(making a Knight with check also doesn't win)'} (73... g1=N+ 74. Kg4 $10) 74. Bf5+ Kh6 (74... Qxf5+ 75. Qxf5+ Qg6 76. Qxg6+ Kxg6 77. Kg4 $10 {Bobby Fischer: '!' Bobby Fischer: 'is similar to the final note.'}) 75. Qf6+ Kh5 76. Bg6+ $1 Qxg6 77. Qg5+ $3 Kxg5 $10 {Bobby Fischer: 'Stalemate!'}) 73. Bh3 Qxh3+ (73... g1=Q 74. Qh5+ Kg7 75. Qg6+ $1 $10 {Bobby Fischer: '!' Bobby Fischer: 'forces stalemate or a perpetual.'}) 74. Kxh3 g1=Q 75. Qe7+ Kh8 76. Qf8+ Kh7 77. Qf7+ {Bobby Fischer: ', Drawn.'} (77. Qf7+ {Bobby Fischer: 'A last try might have been'} Qg7 78. Qxg7+ $1 Kxg7 79. Kg3 $1 {Bobby Fischer: 'holding the "distant opposition": e.g"'} Kf6 80. Kf4 Ke6 81. Ke4 Kd6 82. Kd4 Kc7 83. Kd5 Kb7 84. Kc4 Kc7 85. Kd5 Kd7 86. Ke5 $10 {Bobby Fischer: 'and Black can't penetrate.'}) 1/2-1/2

