{Bobby Fischer: 'GAME N. 57 Change of pace. Larsen, uncharacteristically, forces an early exchange of Queens so that he can spring a surprise in the resulting endgame. Fischer beats him to it (13 ... b6) and proceeds to defend with meticulous care. It looks as if a draw must ensue, but Larsen presses. He is rebuffed, and again a draw seems imminent. Larsen senses no danger and, as if by inertia, continues to play for a win. As the game simplifies, the self-inflicted dark square weaknesses in the Dane's position gradually reveal themselves. By move thirty it becomes Fischer's turn to assume the initiative, and he probes these flaws judiciously. Thrown on the defensive, Larsen makes one or two reckless moves out of which Fischer constructs elegant combinations. Thus, what begins as a barren endgame is transformed into an exhibition of chess sensibility and virtuosity. '} 1. d4 {ChessBase ChessBase ChessBase Bobby Fischer ChessBase: 'Matanovic,Aleksandar'} Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 Bg7 4. e4 d6 5. Be2 ({Larsen had won some good games with} 5. Nf3 {Bobby Fischer} O-O 6. Be3 {but after} e5 $1 {(which no one seems to have played) White gets no advantage.} 7. Be2 ({And} 7. d5 Ng4 8. Bg5 f6 9. Bh4 Qe8 $36 {gives Black dynamic play. Now} 10. h3 Nh6 11. g4 $5 f5 {is too risky for White.}) ({Finally on} 7. dxe5 dxe5 8. Qxd8 Rxd8 9. Nd5 $2 Na6 $1 $17 {gives Black the better ending.}) 7... Nc6 {transposes into well-known modem lines.}) 5... O-O 6. Nf3 e5 7. O-O {Bobby Fischer: 'Position after'} Nc6 8. Be3 ({A bit of a surprise. I had expected} 8. d5 {Bobby Fischer} Ne7 9. Ne1 Nd7 10. Nd3 f5 11. Bd2 {Now I had in mind} c5 $1 ({Larsen-Najdorf, Santa Monica 1966, had continued} 11... Nf6 $2 12. f3 f4 13. c5 $1 g5 14. Rc1 Ng6 15. cxd6 cxd6 16. Nb5 Rf7 17. Qc2 $1 Ne8 18. a4 $16 {and White came first on the Q-side since Black's attack never got off the ground. Larsen, B-Najdorf,M Santa Monica II. Piatigorsky Cup 1966 ChessBase: 'Larsen,B-Najdorf,M Santa Monica II. Piatigorsky Cup 1966'}) 12. f3 f4 $1 $36 ({But not} 12... Nf6 $2 13. g4 $1 f4 14. h4 $1 {and Black's K -side counterplay is completely stymied) with active chances.})) 8... Re8 {Bobby Fischer: '!' ChessBase: '!' '!' '!'} ({The cleanest way to equalize. Najdorf found this move after some painful experiences with 8 ... l} 8... Ng4 {Bobby Fischer}) 9. dxe5 ({in his match vs. Reshevsky. The main point if that} 9. d5 {Bobby Fischer} Nd4 $1 $11 {levels ChessBase: '=!' '=!' '=!'}) 9... dxe5 10. Qxd8 Nxd8 ({A dubious improvement over} 10... Rxd8 $1 {(Bobby Fischer) as played by Reshevsky in his match with Benko. Reshevsky,S after} 11. Bg5 {Black must not play} Rd7 $2 {(after which Benko's} (11... Rf8 $1 $11 {ChessBase: '=!' '=!' '=!'}) 12. Bd1 $3 $16 {followed by Ba4 was very strong) but 11 ... Rf8! solves all his problems.Benko,P ChessBase: ' a4; Benko,P'}) 11. Nb5 Ne6 12. Ng5 Re7 $11 {Bobby Fischer: 'Position after' ChessBase: 'Matanovic,Aleksandar: '=''} 13. Rfd1 ({Larsen is attempting to in1prove on Reshevsky-Fischer, Santa Monica 1966, which continued:} 13. Nxe6 {Bobby Fischer} Bxe6 14. f3 c6 15. Nc3 Rd7 16. Rfd1 Bf8 17. Kf2 b6 18. b3 Rb7 19. Na4 Nd7 20. Nb2 b5 $11 {with an eventual draw. ..Larsen, B-Fischer,R Santa Monica II. Piatigorsky Cup 1966 ChessBase: '=' '=' '=' ChessBase: 'Larsen,B-Fischer,R Santa Monica II. Piatigorsky Cup 1966'}) 13... b6 $1 ({In my 9th match game with Reshevsky, 1961, I tried} 13... c6 $5 {(Bobby Fischer) Instead of} 14. Nxe6 ({Larsen told me he had intcnded} 14. Nxa7 $5 {ChessBase: 'Larsen,B'} Bd7 15. Nxe6 Bxe6 16. f3 {But after} Rd7 $1 $44 {But after (threatening ...Rd4) Black has fair play for the Pawn, considering that the Knight is stranded on a7. The book text was an improvement that 1 had hatched some tinle ago ChessBase: ' d4'}) 14... Bxe6 15. Nc3 Rd7 $11 {Reshevsky,S-Fischer,R (9) Los Angeles 1961 ChessBase: '=' '=' '=' ChessBase: 'Reshevsky,S-Fischer,R (9) Los Angeles 1961'}) 14. c5 $6 {Bobby Fischer: '!?' ChessBase: '!?' '!?' '!?' ChessBase: 'Matanovic,Aleksandar: '?!''} ({Typically, Larsen adopts an enterprising continuation. He should settle for} 14. Nxe6 {(Bobby Fischer) >= ChessBase: ''} Bxe6 15. f3 $11 {with a draw in view. By overestinlating his chances, he gradually drifts into a losing position. ChessBase: '=' '=' '='}) 14... Nxc5 ({Naturally not} 14... bxc5 $2 {Bobby Fischer} 15. Nxe6 Bxe6 16. Bxc5 Rd7 17. f3 $18 {wins.}) 15. Rd8+ Bf8 ({No better is} 15... Re8 {Bobby Fischer} 16. Rxe8+ Nxe8 17. Bxc5 bxc5 18. Bc4 $1) ({Or} 15... Ne8 $2 {Bobby Fischer} 16. Bxc5 bxc5 17. Nxc7 Rxc7 18. Rxe8+ Bf8 19. Nxh7 $1) 16. Nxa7 Rxa7 {Bobby Fischer: 'Position after'} ({On} 16... Bb7 {Bobby Fischer} 17. Rxa8 Bxa8 18. f3 $36 {White has a slight pull despite his misplaced Knight. After} c6 19. Nc8 Rb7 20. Rd1 {maintains some pressure.}) 17. Rxc8 {Bobby Fischer: 'White recovers his pawn with even chances.'} Kg7 ({Black wisely resists the temptation of} 17... Ncxe4 $4 {Bobby Fischer} 18. Nxe4 Nxe4 19. Bh6) ({But even more accurate than the text is} 17... h6 $1 {Bobby Fischer} 18. Nf3 Kg7 19. Bxc5 bxc5 20. Bd3 $11 {completely neutralizing any initiative for either side. ChessBase: '=' '=' '='}) 18. f3 Ne8 19. a3 $2 ({Bobby Fischer: 'Larsen's reluctance to siInplify will soon backfire. Correct is'} 19. Bxc5 $11 {Bobby Fischer: '!' ChessBase: '!' '!' '!' ChessBase: 'Matanovic,Aleksandar: '=''} bxc5 {Bobby Fischer} 20. Rb8 $14 {with theoretical winning chances because of the passed a-Pawn. But it would be difficult to make headway because of the opposite colored Bishops.}) 19... Nd6 $15 {ChessBase: 'Matanovic,Aleksandar: '''} 20. Rd8 ({Optimistic as ever!} 20. Rb8 {Bobby Fischer} Nd7 21. Rd8 Nb7 22. Rc8 Nd6 $11 {would lead to a draw by repetition. ChessBase: '=' '=' '='}) 20... h6 21. Nh3 Ne6 22. Rb8 Re8 23. Rxe8 {Bobby Fischer: 'Position after'} Nxe8 {Bobby Fischer: '=' Bobby Fischer: '"Now White's initiative is over and the position is even but by no means drawish. There is a lot of play. " (KMOCH) White's dark squares, notably his d4, are weak. But it's still not too senous.' ChessBase: '=' '=' '='} 24. Bb5 $2 {ChessBase: 'Matanovic,Aleksandar: '?''} ({Bobby Fischer: 'Pointless. White should start bringing his Knight into the game via'} 24. Nf2 {Bobby Fischer: 'He can't prevent ...' ChessBase: '' '' ''} Bc5 25. Bxc5 {ChessBase: 'Matanovic,Aleksandar'} Nxc5 $15) ({Gaining control of the dark squares. Of course not} 24. b4 $2 {Bobby Fischer} Bxb4) 24... Nd6 25. Bf1 Nb7 {Bobby Fischer: '!' ChessBase: '!' '!' '!'} 26. Nf2 Bc5 {Bobby Fischer: '!' ChessBase: '!' '!' '!'} 27. Bxc5 Nbxc5 28. Rd1 h5 {Bobby Fischer: '!' ChessBase: '!' '!' '!'} ({To keep the Knight out of g4. This "prophylactic" thrust would have gladdened Nimzovich's heart. Noy} 28... Nd4 $2 {Bobby Fischer} 29. Ng4 f6 30. f4 $1) 29. Rd5 $6 {ChessBase: 'Matanovic,Aleksandar: '?!''} ({Larsen still has illusions, but his game is fast deteriorating. More prudent is} 29. Nd3 {Bobby Fischer} Nxd3 30. Bxd3 Nd4 31. Kf2 $17 {White probably should hold the ending despite Black's creeping pressure.}) 29... Kf6 30. h4 Ke7 {Bobby Fischer: '!' ChessBase: '!' '!' '!'} 31. Bc4 ({Bobby Fischer: 'The Pawn is poisoned:'} 31. Rxe5 $6 {Bobby Fischer: '?' ChessBase: '?' '?' '?' ChessBase: 'Matanovic,Aleksandar: '?!''} c6 {Bobby Fischer: '-+' Bobby Fischer: 'followed by Nd7 or f7-f6 The mission of the Rook has failed, but no serious hann has been done.' ChessBase: '-+' '-+' '-+' ChessBase: ' d7; f7-f6'}) 31... c6 32. Rd2 Nd4 $15 {Bobby Fischer: 'Finally the Knight has gained this dominant outpost.' ChessBase: 'Matanovic,Aleksandar: '''} 33. Kf1 ({The more active} 33. Nd3 {(Bobby Fischer) is preft!rable. Now Black's tactical threats begin to proliferate. ChessBase: '' '' ''}) 33... f5 {Bobby Fischer: '!' ChessBase: '!' '!' '!'} 34. b4 $2 {ChessBase: 'Matanovic,Aleksandar: '?''} ({Bobby Fischer: 'Meets with a still sharper counter thrust.'} 34. Nd3 {Bobby Fischer: 'offered a better chance for survival. After the text White's a-Pawn is weakened.' ChessBase: '' '' ''}) ({Not} 34. exf5 {Bobby Fischer} Nxf5 {with the double threat of . ...Ne3+ or Nxh4 And if ChessBase: ' e3+, xh4'} 35. Re2 $2 Ng3+) 34... b5 $1 35. Bg8 {Bobby Fischer: 'Position after'} (35. bxc5 {Bobby Fischer} bxc4 $19 {clearly wins for Black.}) ({And} 35. Bxb5 $2 {(Bobby Fischer) is refuted by} Ncb3 $19) 35... fxe4 {Bobby Fischer: '!' Bobby Fischer: 'Fixing White with another weakness.' ChessBase: '!' '!' '!'} 36. fxe4 ({Not} 36. bxc5 {Bobby Fischer} e3 37. Rxd4 ({If} 37. Rd3 exf2 38. Kxf2 Ra8 39. Ba2 b4) ({Or} 37. Ra2 $2 exf2 38. Kxf2 Kf8 $1) 37... exd4 38. Nd3 Rxa3 39. Ke2 Rc3 {Etc..}) 36... Nd7 $17 {ChessBase: 'Matanovic,Aleksandar: '''} 37. Rd3 Ra6 {Bobby Fischer: '!' Bobby Fischer: '/\ Nc2' ChessBase: '!' '!' '!' ChessBase: ' c2'} ({Threatening} 37... Nc2 {(Bobby Fischer) which, if played immediately, could have been met by} 38. Rc3) 38. Rc3 {Bobby Fischer: 'Position after'} (38. g3 {ChessBase: 'Matanovic,Aleksandar'} Nf6 $17) 38... c5 {Bobby Fischer: '!' Bobby Fischer: 'This surprising combination apparently confused Larsen, who was in time-pressure.' ChessBase: '!' '!' '!'} 39. g4 {Bobby Fischer: '?' ChessBase: '?' '?' '?'} ({The last blunder. On} 39. bxc5 {(Bobby Fischer) >= ChessBase: ''} b4 $1 40. Rc1 $1 {there's still a lot of fight. If} ({Not} 40. axb4 Ra1+) 40... Rxa3 ({Or} 40... bxa3 41. Ba2) 41. c6 Nb6) 39... c4 $19 ({This protected passed Pawn is just too strong. Not} 39... Nf6 {Bobby Fischer} 40. Rxc5 $1) 40. gxh5 gxh5 41. Bd5 Nf6 42. Rg3 Nxd5 43. exd5 Rf6 $1 {ChessBase: 'Matanovic,Aleksandar: '!''} 44. Kg2 ({The sealed lTIOve. White is completely tied up. On} 44. Kg1 {Bobby Fischer} Ne2+ $19 {Wins.}) ({Or if} 44. Ke1 {Bobby Fischer} Rf4 $19 {mops up.}) 44... Nf5 45. Rh3 Rg6+ 46. Kf3 {Bobby Fischer: 'Position after'} Nd4+ 47. Ke3 ({On} 47. Ke4 {Bobby Fischer} Kd6 {White is in zugzwang. If} 48. Rh2 {to prevent Rg2 On} Rg3) 47... Rg2 $1 {ChessBase: 'Matanovic,Aleksandar: '!''} 48. Rh1 Kd6 49. Ne4+ Kxd5 50. Nc3+ Ke6 51. Rc1 (51. Rb1 {(Bobby Fischer) White has to prevent} Rc2 52. Ne4 {as then the Knight cannot move because of ...} Re2# {Mate}) 51... Rh2 52. a4 Rh3+ 53. Kf2 Nb3 54. Kg2 Nxc1 55. Kxh3 bxa4 56. Nxa4 Ne2 57. b5 c3 58. b6 c2 59. Nc5+ {Bobby Fischer: 'Position after'} Kd5 60. Nb3 ({White can choose his own end. If} 60. Nd3 {Bobby Fischer} Nf4+ 61. Nxf4+ exf4 62. b7 c1=Q 63. b8=Q Qh1# {Mate.}) (60. b7 {Bobby Fischer} c1=Q 61. b8=Q Qh1# {Mate.}) 60... Kc6 61. Kg2 Kxb6 {Bobby Fischer: 'White resigns'} 0-1

