{Bobby Fischer: 'GAME N. 7 Pride goeth. Miscalculating, as he explains in his notes, Fischer rapidly gets into trouble and is thrown on the defensive. Olafsson quietly strengthens his attacking prospects and seems well on the road to victory. But he tries, prematurely, to force the issue (21.Nb1) and, as the game opens up, loses the initiative, although he seems to be blissfully unaware of it. He fails to foresee the power of the riposte to his 24.Qd2. Still blind to the danger, while seeking a forced win, he misses several opportunities to equalize. In extreme time pressure, he is compelled to exchange Queens under particularly unfavorable circumstances. The resulting endgame holds no further surprises. '} 1. c4 {Bobby Fischer} Nf6 2. Nc3 g6 3. d4 Bg7 4. e4 d6 5. Nf3 O-O 6. Be2 e5 7. d5 (7. dxe5 dxe5 8. Qxd8 Rxd8 9. Nxe5 Nxe4 $1) 7... Nbd7 8. Bg5 {Bobby Fischer: ', Steinitz automatically gave this pin a question mark. Since there is no real threat involved (because the bishop is worth more than the knight) Black can now gain some time by kicking it around.  Petrosian has had some success with this treatment. The idea is to restrain ... Ne8 and the subsequent ...f5. '} h6 9. Bh4 a6 {Bobby Fischer: '; This slow system has never been refuted.'} ({Bobby Fischer: 'But after is'} 9... g5 $142 $1 {Fischer=:F Bobby Fischer: '!'} 10. Bg3 {Bobby Fischer: '(Black's break with f5 has now been blunted, but on the other hand white's bishop on g3 is deadwood)'} Nh5 $1 11. h4 {Bobby Fischer: 'the latest wrinkle.'} (11. Nd2 Nf4 12. O-O Nxe2+ 13. Qxe2 f5 14. exf5 Nf6 15. c5 Bxf5 16. Rac1 Rf7 $1 17. Nc4 Bf8 $17 {Wexler,B-Reshevsky,S/Buenos Aires/1960 Bobby Fischer: 'is better for black. Wexler - Reshevsky, Buenos Aires, 1960),'}) 11... Nxg3 $1 12. fxg3 gxh4 $1 13. Rxh4 ({Bobby Fischer: 'if'} 13. Nxh4 Qg5 14. Nf5 Nf6) (13. gxh4 f5 14. exf5 Nf6 15. O-O Bxf5) 13... f5 14. Qc2 Nc5 15. Bd3 Qf6 $17 {Damjanovic,M-Hort,V/Sarajevo/1964 Bobby Fischer: 'with advantage. (Damyanovich-Hort, Sarajevo, 1964.).'}) (9... Qe8 10. Nb5 {Euwe=:E}) 10. Nd2 Qe8 { h7, f7-f5; (b7-b5  0-0-0) F Bobby Fischer: '; The idea is to free the knight and thus make possible the break with ...f5. In some variations, the queen may help to support ...b5 also, particularly if white elects to castle long. '} 11. g4 $5 { 12.g5 E} ({Bobby Fischer: 'In the Candidates' Tournament, 1959, Tal essayed against me the quieter'} 11. O-O Nh7 12. b4 Ng5 ({Bobby Fischer: 'later I tried'} 12... Bf6 $5 {Bobby Fischer: 'against him.'}) 13. f3 f5 $10 {Tal,M-Fischer,R/Bled ct/1959 Bobby Fischer: 'with chances for both sides.'}) {Bobby Fischer: 'The text is risky and commits white to Q-side castling. '} 11... Nh7 12. Qc2 (12. Bg3 { 13.h4 E}) 12... Ng5 $2 { g5-h3-f4 Bobby Fischer: '; Intending Nh3-f4, but white's simple reply brands it as a mistaken plan.'} ({Bobby Fischer: 'Correct is'} 12... Nc5 {} 13. O-O-O (13. b4 Nd7 $17 {Bobby Fischer: 'leaves white with a shaky game.'}) 13... f5 $10 {F}) 13. h3 $1 Nc5 14. O-O-O Bd7 ({Bobby Fischer: 'Weak is'} 14... f5 15. Bxg5 $1 hxg5 16. gxf5 gxf5 17. Rdg1 $16 {F}) 15. f3 (15. Rdg1 Na4 16. Nxa4 Bxa4 17. Qd3 {E}) 15... Na4 (15... b5 $5 16. b4 Nb7 {F Bobby Fischer: 'may not be too bad.'}) 16. Nxa4 (16. Ncb1 {E}) (16. Bf2 {E}) 16... Bxa4 17. b3 Bd7 18. Bf2 c5 $1 19. h4 ({Bobby Fischer: 'Black's game springs to life after'} 19. dxc6 $2 {Bobby Fischer: 'e.p.'} bxc6 20. Nb1 {E} d5 $1 21. exd5 ({Bobby Fischer: 'or'} 21. Bc5 d4 22. Bxf8 Bxf8 $44 {Bobby Fischer: 'with a juicy position.'}) 21... cxd5 22. Rxd5 Bc6 $36 {F Bobby Fischer: 'etc.'}) 19... Nh7 20. Be3 b5 21. Nb1 $2 { d2 Bobby Fischer: ', Intending Qd2,'} ({Bobby Fischer: 'but correct is'} 21. Bd3 $142 $1 {F Bobby Fischer: '!' Bobby Fischer: 'maintaining the bind by restraining ...f5.'}) ({Bobby Fischer: 'if'} 21. h5 Ng5 {F}) (21. Rdg1 Kh8 22. Bd3 f5 23. exf5 gxf5 24. Bxf5 Bxf5 25. gxf5 Qh5 26. Ne4 {E}) 21... f5 $1 {Bobby Fischer: '; Ready or not - Here we come! Olafsson was sure this break was impossible, or he wouldn't have allowed it. '} 22. gxf5 gxf5 { f4  F/E} 23. exf5 {Bobby Fischer: ',)To prevent f4 which would seal the K-side and neutralize white's attack. '} Bxf5 24. Qd2 {Bobby Fischer: ', This is the position white played for. '} e4 $1 {Bobby Fischer: '; The game turns on this shot.'} (24... Rf6 $143 {F}) ({Bobby Fischer: 'or'} 24... h5 $143 {F Bobby Fischer: 'cedes the initaitive.'}) 25. Rdg1 (25. Bxh6 {Bobby Fischer: 'loses to'} e3 $1 {E} 26. Bxe3 ({Bobby Fischer: 'if'} 26. Qxe3 Bxb1 {Bobby Fischer: '!'} 27. Kxb1 Qg6+ $19 {Bobby Fischer: 'wins a piece.'}) 26... Bxb1 27. Kxb1 Qe5 $19) 25... exf3 $2 (25... Ra7 $1 {} 26. Bxh6 exf3 {F}) 26. Bxh6 $2 (26. Rxg7+ {Stahlberg Bobby Fischer: '!' Bobby Fischer: '(STAHLBERG)'} Kxg7 27. Bxh6+ Kh8 28. Bxf8 Qxf8 29. Bxf3 {Bobby Fischer: 'wins a pawn. (if'} Bxb1 30. Qc3+ $18 {F Bobby Fischer: ').'}) 26... Ra7 $1 {Bobby Fischer: '; Olafsson later told me that he had underestimated the strength of this defensive move. ' Bobby Fischer: 'transposing to the game.'} 27. Bxg7 (27. Bxf3 $2 Bxb1 $19 {E}) (27. Qb2 Qe5 $17 {E}) 27... Rxg7 28. Rxg7+ Kxg7 29. Bd3 {Bobby Fischer: ', An admission of defeat since blacks f-pawn now becomes dangerously potent.'} ({Bobby Fischer: 'But not'} 29. Bxf3 $2 Bxb1 30. Kxb1 Rxf3 31. Qg2+ Qg6+ $19 {F Bobby Fischer: '(the saving resource) and black hangs onto his extra piece. My game hinges on this defense, on the fact that the f-pawn has such divine protection.'}) ({Bobby Fischer: 'or'} 29. Qc3+ Qe5 30. Qxf3 Bxb1 31. Qg4+ Bg6 $19 {F} 32. h5 Qa1+ $19 {E}) 29... bxc4 30. Rg1+ Kh8 31. Qc3+ {Bobby Fischer: ', Now black gets another passed centre pawn, but white's defense is dificult anyway.'} (31. bxc4 { E} f2 (31... Bxd3 32. Qxd3 Qe5 $17 {E}) 32. Rf1 Bxd3 33. Qxd3 Qe1+ 34. Kc2 Nf6 35. Nd2 Ng4 $19 {F Bobby Fischer: 'wins.'}) 31... Qe5 32. Qxe5+ ({Bobby Fischer: 'After'} 32. Bxf5 Rxf5 33. bxc4 Nf6 {Bobby Fischer: 'white has nothing better than to transpose into the actual game with'} 34. Qxe5 {F}) 32... dxe5 33. Bxf5 Rxf5 34. bxc4 (34. d6 Nf6 35. Nd2 $1 {Bobby Fischer: 'offers no better: e.g.,'} cxb3 36. axb3 e4 37. Nc4 {Bobby Fischer: '!'} f2 38. Rf1 Ng4 { e4-e3 -+ Bobby Fischer: '!' Bobby Fischer: '(threatening ...e3)'} 39. Kd1 Nh2 $1 40. d7 Rd5+ $19 {F Bobby Fischer: 'is decisive.'}) 34... Nf6 35. Nd2 (35. Kd2 Ng4 $1 36. Rf1 e4 {E}) (35. Kd1 e4 {E}) 35... f2 36. Rh1 {Bobby Fischer: ', White must keep the f1 square open for his knight. '} (36. Rf1 e4 {E}) 36... e4 37. Kd1 ({Bobby Fischer: 'A better chance is offered by'} 37. Nf1 {} Ng4 $1 38. Kd2 ({Bobby Fischer: 'if'} 38. d6 Rf6 39. d7 Rd6 {F}) {Bobby Fischer: 'but'} 38... Rf3 $1 $19 {F/E Bobby Fischer: '!' Bobby Fischer: 'squelches all counterplay.'}) 37... e3 38. Nf1 Re5 39. Ke2 (39. Ng3 Nh5 40. Ne2 (40. Nxh5 $2 e2+) 40... Kg7 {E}) 39... Nh5 $1 40. Kf3 e2 {Bobby Fischer: '; White resigns. One of the pawns must reincarnate.'} 0-1

