{GAME N. 27 Sheer pyrotechnics. Here, in probably the most exciting game of the match, Fischer, trying to win a pawn, unwittingly triggers a series of 'desperado' combinations which are brilliant and unorthodox. Pure tactics predominate for a period of ten moves (19 to 29). It is almost impossible to determine who is winning until Reshevsky emerges a clear exchange ahead. In the tricky ending that ensues Fischer obviously is fighting for a draw. But, once again, he has the clock as an ally. In time-pressure, trying to preserve his slim advantage, Reshevsky plays an aggressive line in which Fischer finds a hole-enabling him to reverse their roles. Conscious of his newly acquired advantage, Fischer storms down the board with his kingside pawns and overwhelms his opponent.  ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'GAME N. 27 Sheer pyrotechnics. Here, in probably the most exciting game of the match, Fischer, trying to win a pawn, unwittingly triggers a series of 'desperado' combinations which are brilliant and unorthodox. Pure tactics predominate for a period of ten moves (19 to 29). It is almost impossible to determine who is winning until Reshevsky emerges a clear exchange ahead. In the tricky ending that ensues Fischer obviously is fighting for a draw. But, once again, he has the clock as an ally. In time-pressure, trying to preserve his slim advantage, Reshevsky plays an aggressive line in which Fischer finds a hole-enabling him to reverse their roles. Conscious of his newly acquired advantage, Fischer storms down the board with his kingside pawns and overwhelms his opponent. ''} 1. d4 {ChessBase ChessBase ChessBase ChessBase ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer'} Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 d5 4. cxd5 {This exchange variation, though insipid, has always been to Reshevsky's taste. ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'This exchange variation, though insipid, has always been to Reshevsky's taste.''} Nxd5 (4... exd5 {leads to the kind of wood pushing that always bored me. ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'leads to the kind of wood pushing that always bored me.''}) 5. Nf3 ({Prematurely forceful is ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Prematurely forceful is''} 5. e4 Nxc3 6. bxc3 c5 7. Nf3 cxd4 8. cxd4 Bb4+ $11 {ChessBase: '=' '=' '=' '=' ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: '=''}) 5... c5 6. e3 Nc6 7. Bd3 ({Botvinnik and Robert Byrne prefer ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Botvinnik and Robert Byrne prefer''} 7. Bc4 {A possible continuation might be ChessBase: 'Botvinnik,M; Byrne,R Bobby Fischer: 'A possible continuation might be''} cxd4 8. exd4 Be7 9. O-O O-O 10. Re1 a6 $11 {ChessBase: '=' '=' '=' '=' ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: '=''} ({weaker is ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'weaker is''} 10... b6 11. Nxd5 exd5 12. Bb5 $16 {Botvinnik,M-Alekhine,A Amsterdam AVRO 1938 ChessBase: 'Botvinnik,M-Alekhine,A Amsterdam AVRO 1938 Bobby Fischer: 'Botvinnik,M-Alekhine,A Amsterdam AVRO 1938''})) 7... Be7 ({An alternative is ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'An alternative is''} 7... cxd4 8. exd4 g6 9. h4 $5 (9. O-O Bg7 10. Be4 {is the positional approach ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'is the positional approach''}) 9... Bg7 ({better is ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'better is''} 9... h6 {ChessBase: ''}) 10. h5 Ndb4 11. Bg5 Nxd3+ 12. Qxd3 Qa5 13. Kf1 h6 $2 14. hxg6 hxg5 15. Rxh8+ Bxh8 16. gxf7+ Kxf7 17. Qh7+ Bg7 18. d5 $18 {White won shortly. (Balcerovsky-Dunkelblum Varna ol 1962) ChessBase: 'Balcerkovsky,n-Dunkelblum,n Varna ol 1962 Bobby Fischer: 'White won shortly. (Balcerovsky-Dunkelblum Varna ol 1962)''}) 8. O-O O-O 9. a3 cxd4 10. exd4 {Fairly typical of the semi-Tarrasch formation: White has the freer game and attacking prospects, but the drawback of his isolated d-Pawn should not be minimized. Chances are even. ChessBase: '=' '=' '=' '=' ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Fairly typical of the semi-Tarrasch formation: White has the freer game and attacking prospects, but the drawback of his isolated d-Pawn should not be minimized. Chances are even.''} Nf6 ({Also playable is ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Also playable is''} 10... Bd7 11. Qc2 g6 12. Bh6 Re8 13. Ne4 Rc8 14. Qe2 f5 15. Nc3 Bf6 {Byrne,R-Bisguier,A ch-USA 1963 ChessBase: 'Byrne,R-Bisguier,A ch-USA 1963 Bobby Fischer: 'Byrne,R-Bisguier,A ch-USA 1963''}) ({Another possibility is ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Another possibility is''} 10... b6 $5 11. Nxd5 Qxd5 12. Qc2 Bb7 $1 13. Bxh7+ Kh8 14. Be4 Nxd4 15. Bxd5 Nxc2 16. Bxb7 Nxa1 17. Bxa8 Rxa8 18. Bg5 f6 $11 {ChessBase: '=' '=' '=' '=' ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: '=''}) 11. Bc2 ({A more flexible plan is ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'A more flexible plan is''} 11. Be3 {followed by Qe2 and Rad1. ChessBase: ' e2, ad1 Bobby Fischer: 'followed by Qe2 and Rad1.''}) 11... b6 12. Qd3 Bb7 13. Bg5 g6 14. Rfe1 Re8 15. h4 {Evans criticized this "aggressive pass" and Barden extolled it. I don't see how else White can make headway. He has to create some K-side threats before Black consolidates and piles up on his d-Pawn. ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Evans criticized this "aggressive pass" and Barden extolled it. I don't see how else White can make headway. He has to create some K-side threats before Black consolidates and piles up on his d-Pawn.''} Rc8 16. Rac1 Nd5 17. Ne4 f5 $5 {I knew this was an "ugly positional blunder." But I actually thought Black would get the better of it after 18 Nc3 Bxg5 19 hxg5 Nc3 20 bxc3 (not 20 Qxc3? Ne5) 20 ... Na5! (threatening ... Bxf3 and .... Qxg5). ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'I knew this was an "ugly positional blunder." But I actually thought Black would get the better of it after 18 Nc3 Bxg5 19 hxg5 Nc3 20 bxc3 (not 20 Qxc3? Ne5) 20 ... Na5! (threatening ... Bxf3 and .... Qxg5).''} 18. Nc3 Bxg5 19. Nxg5 $1 {Crossing me up! ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: '!' Bobby Fischer: 'Crossing me up!''} (19. hxg5 Nxc3 20. bxc3 (20. Qxc3 $2 Ne5) 20... Na5 $1 $17 {ChessBase: ' xf3, xg5'}) 19... Nf4 20. Qe3 ({Not ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Not''} 20. Qg3 $2 Nh5 21. Qe3 Nxd4) 20... Qxd4 21. Nb5 $1 {Marvelously alert! After the practically forced trade of Queens, White wins the exchange because of the imminent fork on d6. ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Marvelously alert! After the practically forced trade of Queens, White wins the exchange because of the imminent fork on d6.''} Qxe3 {Best. ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Best.''} ({After the game we analysed ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'After the game we analysed''} 21... Qd5 22. Qxf4 Qxb5 ({if ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'if''} 22... Nd4 $2 23. Be4 $1 Rxc1 24. Qxc1 $1 fxe4 25. Qc7) 23. Nxe6 Qxb2 ({if ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'if''} 23... Qd5 24. Nc7 Rxe1+ 25. Rxe1 Qf7 26. Ne6 {keeps the advantage); ChessBase: '' '' '' '' ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'keeps the advantage);''}) 24. Qh6 $1 $18 {(RESHEVSKY) with an irresistible attack. On ChessBase: '; Reshevsky,S Bobby Fischer: '(RESHEVSKY) with an irresistible attack. On''} Na5 {(to stop Bb3) ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: '(to stop Bb3)''} ({if ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'if''} 24... Rxe6 25. Rxe6 Nd4 26. Re7 $18 {wins ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'wins''}) 25. Bxf5 $1 gxf5 ({if ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'if''} 25... Qf6 26. Ng5 $1 $18 {ChessBase: '!' '!' '!' '!' ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: '+-!''}) (25... Rxc1 26. Rxc1 gxf5 27. Rc7 $18 {wins ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'wins''}) 26. Rb1 Qh8 (26... Qc3 27. Re3) 27. Qg5+ Kf7 28. Qxf5+ Kg8 ({not ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'not''} 28... Qf6 29. Qxh7+) 29. Re3 Rc3 30. Ng5 $1 Rf8 31. Re8 $1 $18 {forces mate. ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'forces mate.''}) 22. fxe3 Nxg2 $1 23. Kxg2 Nd4+ 24. Be4 $1 {This game was played at the Beverly Hilton Hotel in Los Angeles, and I can still hear the audience gasping with each blow, thinking each of us had overlooked it in turn. "Fischer is winning!" "Reshevsky is winning!" The true state of affairs will crystallize in a matter of moves. ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'This game was played at the Beverly Hilton Hotel in Los Angeles, and I can still hear the audience gasping with each blow, thinking each of us had overlooked it in turn. "Fischer is winning!" "Reshevsky is winning!" The true state of affairs will crystallize in a matter of moves.''} Bxe4+ 25. Nxe4 Nxb5 26. Nf6+ {So the fork, after all, takes place here instead of d6! ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'So the fork, after all, takes place here instead of d6!''} Kf7 27. Nxe8 Rxe8 28. a4 $1 ({Inaccurate is ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Inaccurate is''} 28. Red1 Re7 $1 {and the Knight can climb back into the game via Nb5-c7-d5. ChessBase: ' b5-c7-d5 Bobby Fischer: 'and the Knight can climb back into the game via Nb5-c7-d5.''}) 28... Nd6 29. Rc7+ Kf6 $1 ({Black can't afford ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Black can't afford''} 29... Re7 30. Rec1 $18 {The Rook is needed to mobilize the K -side Pawns. ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'The Rook is needed to mobilize the K -side Pawns.''}) 30. Rec1 $1 {Keeping control of the open file. ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Keeping control of the open file.''} (30. Rxh7 Rc8) (30. Rxa7 Rc8) 30... h6 31. Rxa7 Ne4 32. Ra6 Rd8 $1 {Now it's clear that Black's fighting for a draw. ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Now it's clear that Black's fighting for a draw.''} (32... Rb8 {is hopeless ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'is hopeless''} 33. Rc6 $18) 33. Rc2 {The only way to preserve winning chances. ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'The only way to preserve winning chances.''} ({After ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'After''} 33. Rxb6 Rd2+ 34. Kg1 g5 35. hxg5+ ({on ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'on''} 35. Rcc6 gxh4 36. Rxe6+ Kg5 37. Rg6+ Kh5 38. Rxh6+ Kg4 {Black has enough play on the K-side to hold the draw ChessBase: '' '' '' '' ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Black has enough play on the K-side to hold the draw''}) (35. a5 $2 gxh4 36. a6 h3 37. a7 h2+ 38. Kh1 Ng3#) 35... hxg5 36. Rcc6 (36. a5 {ChessBase: '?' '?' '?' '?'} g4 37. a6 $2 {ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: '?''} Ng5 38. a7 Nf3+ 39. Kf1 g3 40. a8=Q g2#) 36... g4 37. Rxe6+ Kg5 38. Rh6 f4 $18 {ChessBase: '=' '=' '=' '=' ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: '+-''}) 33... Rd3 34. Rxb6 ({After ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'After''} 34. Kf3 Rb3 {Black is in great shape. ChessBase: '' '' '' '' ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Black is in great shape.''}) 34... Rxe3 35. a5 f4 36. Rf2 $2 {Short of time, Reshevsky probably didn't see how Black's Rook could get back in time to stop the a-Pawn. But now it is doubtful that White can even draw! ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Short of time, Reshevsky probably didn't see how Black's Rook could get back in time to stop the a-Pawn. But now it is doubtful that White can even draw!''} ({White should settle for ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'White should settle for''} 36. a6 {ChessBase: ''} f3+ 37. Kf1 ({not ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'not''} 37. Kh2 $2 Re2+) 37... Rd3 38. Ke1 Re3+ 39. Kf1 Rd3 {with a draw. If ChessBase: '=' '=' '=' '=' ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'with a draw. If''} 40. Kg1 Rd1+ 41. Kh2 f2 42. Rxf2+ Nxf2 43. Rb3 (43. a7 $2 {ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: '?''} Ra1 $19) 43... Rd7 44. Rf3+ Kg7 45. Rxf2 Ra7 $11 {ChessBase: '=' '=' '=' '=' ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: '=''}) 36... Nxf2 37. Kxf2 Re5 $1 38. b4 Re3 $1 {This maneuver permits the Rook to get behind the passed Pawn. ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'This maneuver permits the Rook to get behind the passed Pawn.''} 39. a6 Ra3 {Now White is stymied. In order to mobilize his Q-side Pawns, he must inch forward with b5, Rb7, a7, b6, etc. But a half-dozen moves, in chess, can be a lifetime. ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Now White is stymied. In order to mobilize his Q-side Pawns, he must inch forward with b5, Rb7, a7, b6, etc. But a half-dozen moves, in chess, can be a lifetime.''} 40. Rc6 $2 {The last move of the time-control, and it definitely loses. ChessBase: '-+' '-+' '-+' '-+' ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: '?' Bobby Fischer: 'The last move of the time-control, and it definitely loses.''} ({The best chance is ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'The best chance is''} 40. b5 {with the possibility of Rb8 and b6 (giving up the a-Pawn) followed by b7, in some key variations. ChessBase: ';  b8, b5-b6-b7 Bobby Fischer: 'with the possibility of Rb8 and b6 (giving up the a-Pawn) followed by b7, in some key variations.''}) 40... g5 41. hxg5+ hxg5 42. b5 g4 {The sealed move. Black's Pawns suddenly proliferate from nowhere! ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'The sealed move. Black's Pawns suddenly proliferate from nowhere!''} 43. Rc8 ({The line I had expected was ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'The line I had expected was''} 43. Rc1 {intending to bolster the Pawns from behind with Rb1 ChessBase: ' b1 Bobby Fischer: 'intending to bolster the Pawns from behind with Rb1''} g3+ 44. Kg1 ({on ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'on''} 44. Kg2 Ra2+ 45. Kf3 Kf5 $19 {wins ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'wins''}) 44... Ra2 $1 45. Rb1 f3 46. b6 Rg2+ 47. Kf1 Rh2 $1 48. Ke1 Rh1+ 49. Kd2 Rxb1 50. a7 f2 51. a8=Q f1=Q $19 {and Black wins, since White has no perpetual check. ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'and Black wins, since White has no perpetual check.''}) 43... Kf5 44. b6 g3+ 45. Ke1 ({He decides to let the Pawns through rather than get mated after ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'He decides to let the Pawns through rather than get mated after''} 45. Kg2 Ra2+ 46. Kg1 f3 $19) 45... Ra1+ 46. Ke2 g2 47. Rf8+ ({On ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'On''} 47. Rg8 Rxa6 48. b7 (48. Rxg2 Rxb6 $19) 48... Rb6 $19 {is decisive. ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'is decisive.''}) 47... Ke4 48. Rxf4+ Kxf4 49. b7 g1=Q {A hasty slip which, fortunately, still wins. ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'A hasty slip which, fortunately, still wins.''} ({As Isaac Kashdan pointed out after the game ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'As Isaac Kashdan pointed out after the game''} 49... Ke4 $1 {wins outright: e.g. ChessBase: 'Kashdan,I Bobby Fischer: 'wins outright: e.g.''} 50. b8=Q Ra2+ 51. Ke1 g1=Q# {''What will the Russians say when they see this match?" he inquired, with gentle irony. ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: '''What will the Russians say when they see this match?" he inquired, with gentle irony.''}) 50. b8=Q+ Kf5 51. Qf8+ Ke4 52. Qa8+ ({No better is ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'No better is''} 52. Qf3+ Ke5 53. Qc3+ (53. Qh5+ Kd6) 53... Qd4 54. Qg3+ Kd5 55. Qf3+ Qe4+ $19 {and so on. ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'and so on.''}) 52... Kd4 {Delicate footwork is required to escape the perpetual. ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Delicate footwork is required to escape the perpetual.''} 53. Qd8+ {Better than ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Better than''} (53. Qh8+ Kc4 54. Qc8+ Qc5 55. Qxe6+ Kb4 56. Qe4+ Qc4+ $19) 53... Kc4 54. Qd3+ Kc5 55. Qc3+ Kd6 56. Qd2+ Ke5 57. Qb2+ Kf5 (57... Kf5 {He runs out of checks after ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'He runs out of checks after''} 58. Qb5+ Kf6 59. Qb2+ e5 $19) 0-1

