{[%evp 0,68,25,6,77,42,16,-2,33,5,32,-47,-39,-43,-43,-65,-65,-55,-19,2,5,-32,-22,-118,-127,-204,-193,-205,-199,-196,-196,-318,-293,-284,-284,-489,-498,-589,-595,-784,-668,-789,-795,-766,-865,-963,-947,-1335,-1342,-1347,-1361,-1387,-1419,-1830,-1905,-2052,-1795,-29989,-816,-827,-808,-835,-859,-857,-551,-556,-598,-632,-632,-793,-845]} 1. e4 c5 2. Bc4 {This move leads to a comfortable play for Black.} Nc6 3. Ne2 e6 4. Nbc3 (4. d4 {seems interesting, whith an even play.}) 4... Nge7 ({After a better} 4... a6 {Black has a slight edge.}) 5. Ng3 $2 ({The Knight on g3 is misplaced. Better was} 5. d4 {with an even play.}) 5... d5 $1 $17 6. exd5 exd5 7. Bb3 ({Slightly preferable is} 7. Bb5 {although after} a6 8. Bxc6+ Nxc6 {Black has a clear advantage.}) 7... c4 $1 8. Ba4 g6 $2 ({This move throws away all Black's advantage. After a better} 8... d4 9. Nce4 Ng6 $17 {Black has a clear advantage.}) 9. O-O (9. d3 {is an interesting move.}) 9... Bg7 10. Bxc6+ ({Again,} 10. d3 {is preferable.}) 10... bxc6 (10... Nxc6 $5) 11. Nce2 $2 {[#]} ({Unnecessary move. After} 11. d3 {Black has only a tiny edge.}) 11... h5 $1 {Very nice move. It's one of early proofs of Fischer's great talent.} 12. Rb1 $2 ({Strange move. After a better} 12. Re1 $17 {White has f1 square for his Knight.}) 12... h4 13. Nh1 h3 $19 14. g3 (14. Nf4 {cannot help as well due to} hxg2 15. Nxg2 Bh3 $19) 14... Bg4 15. f3 Qb6+ 16. Nf2 Bxf3 17. c3 Nf5 18. Re1 O-O-O 19. Qc2 Rde8 20. d4 cxd3 21. Qxd3 Be4 {It was time to resign.} 22. Be3 Nxe3 23. Nxe4 dxe4 24. Qd4 Bxd4 25. Nxd4 Nc2 26. Red1 Nxd4 27. Rxd4 e3 28. Rb4 e2+ 29. Rxb6 e1=Q+ 30. Rxe1 Rxe1+ 31. Kf2 axb6 32. Kxe1 Re8+ 33. Kf2 Rd8 34. Ke3 Rd1 0-1

