{[%evp 0,25,24,24,20,17,13,10,10,10,32,12,24,21,25,16,8,-43,-54,-73,-50,-61,-61,-61,-59,-62,-65,-77]} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. Bb5 Nd4 ({Introduced in serious tournament practice by Rubinstein. More often played is} 4... Bb4) 5. Nxd4 ({The alternative is} 5. Bc4) 5... exd4 6. e5 dxc3 7. exf6 Qxf6 ({The move} 7... cxd2+ $2 {would be a mistake due to} 8. Bxd2 Qxf6 9. O-O {and Black is undeveloped.}) 8. bxc3 $6 ({Preferable is} 8. dxc3 {after which the position is even.}) 8... c6 9. Be2 d5 10. Rb1 $6 ({More natural is} 10. O-O $15) 10... Bd6 11. d4 O-O 12. Be3 ({Again,} 12. O-O {was more natural}) 12... b5 13. Qd2 $6 (13. O-O) 13... Qg6 14. Kf1 $6 ({Strange move. After a better} 14. O-O Bh3 15. Bf3 {Black is preferable, but it is much better than the game move.}) 14... Bf5 15. h4 Be4 $5 ({Interesting was} 15... h5) 16. f3 Bxc2 17. Rc1 Rae8 18. h5 Qe6 19. Kf2 Ba4 $6 ({Stronger was} 19... Bf5 $17) 20. Rh3 $2 ({This move loses. After a better} 20. Bd3 $15 {Black is better, but his a4 is not well placed.}) 20... f5 21. Bg5 $2 (21. f4 $17 {was better.}) 21... h6 $19 22. Re1 $6 ({More tenacious was} 22. Bh4) 22... hxg5 23. Qxg5 Qh6 0-1

