{Bobby Fischer: 'GAME N. 15 A whopper. Here is Fischer's first win against Vassi/y Smyslov; and it is hard to recall when the former world champion. conducting White. has been so badly outplayed. On move 13 of a crucial opening variation, Smyslov makes what appears to be a "laps us manus." Rather than fight a prolonged uphill positional battle, he sacrifices a Pawn to try to regain the initiative. This proves to be a piece of bad judgment, since, basically, the loss of this Pawn alone brings about his demise. Defending with deadly precision, Fischer gradually consolidates - the shadow of his Pawn looming larger with each approach to the endgame. Smys/ov thrashes about. striving desperately for complications, avoiding exchanges like the plague. But he is unable to get off the hook. '} 1. e4 {Bobby Fischer} c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 a6 6. Bg5 ({for} 6. Be2 {(Bobby Fischer) see games 4 and 42. For 6 Bc4 see games 17, 55, 58 Pilnik, H-Fischer,R Mar del Plata 1959 Unzicker,W-Fischer,R Varna ol 1962}) (6. Bc4 {(Bobby Fischer) Fischer,R-Tal,M Beograd ct 1959 Fischer,R-Bednarski,J Habana ol 1966 Fischer, R-Geller,E Skopje 1967}) 6... e6 7. f4 Be7 8. Qf3 Qc7 9. O-O-O Nbd7 ({Bobby Fischer: 'Weak is'} 9... h6 10. Bh4 Nbd7 11. Bd3 b5 12. e5 $1 Bb7 13. Nxe6 $1 fxe6 14. Bg6+ Kf8 15. exf6 Bxf3 {Bobby Fischer: 'better is'} (15... Nxf6 {    Bobby Fischer: '>='}) 16. fxe7+ Kg8 17. gxf3 Nf6 18. Bxf6 gxf6 19. e8=Q+ Rxe8 20. Bxe8 d5 {Gligoric,S-Bobotsov,M Hastings 1959 Gligoric,S-Bobotsov,M Hastings 1959 Gligoric,S-Bobotsov,M Hastings 1959 Gligoric,S-Bobotsov,M Hastings 1959 Bobby Fischer: 'Gligoric,S-Bobotsov,M Hastings 1959'} 21. f5 $1 $18 {Bobby Fischer: '(MCO) wins'}) 10. g4 b5 11. Bxf6 Nxf6 ({Bobby Fischer: 'for'} 11... gxf6 {Gligoric,S-Fischer,R Belgrade ct 1959 Gligoric,S-Fischer,R Belgrade ct 1959 Gligoric,S-Fischer,R Belgrade ct 1959 Gligoric,S-Fischer,R Belgrade ct 1959 Bobby Fischer: 'see game 12. Gligoric,S-Fischer,R Beograd ct 1959'}) 12. g5 {Bobby Fischer: 'Position after'} Nd7 13. Bh3 $2 ({Bobby Fischer: 'Innovation or omission? In either case, after this move White throws away his theoretical advantage and even loses the initiative. Necessary is'} 13. a3 $142 {Bobby Fischer: '>='} Bb7 {Bobby Fischer: 'a.)'} (13... Rb8 $1 {Bobby Fischer: 'is in vogue) and now there are two main lines:'}) 14. h4 ({Bobby Fischer: 'b.)'} 14. Bh3 O-O-O 15. f5 $5 {Bobby Fischer: '(interesting is'} (15. Bxe6 $5 fxe6 16. Nxe6 Qc4 $13 {Tal,M-Gligoric,S Moscow 1963 1-0 Tal,M-Gligoric,S Moscow 1963 1-0 Tal,M-Gligoric,S Moscow 1963 1-0 Tal,M-Gligoric,S Moscow 1963 1-0 Bobby Fischer: '[Keres recommends. Tal,M-Gligoric,S Moscow 1963 1-0'} (16... Qb6 {Keres,P})) 15... Bxg5+ 16. Kb1 e5 17. Ndxb5 axb5 18. Nxb5 Qb6 $1 (18... Qc5 {Gligoric,S-Fischer,R Bled ct 1959 1-0 Gligoric,S-Fischer,R Bled ct 1959 1-0 Gligoric,S-Fischer,R Bled ct 1959 1-0 Gligoric,S-Fischer,R Bled ct 1959 1-0 Bobby Fischer: 'Gligoric,S-Fischer,R Bled ct 1959 1-0'}) 19. Nxd6+ Kc7 20. Nxf7 Bf6 $10 {Bobby Fischer: '='}) 14... d5 15. exd5 Nb6 16. f5 Nxd5 17. fxe6 O-O-O 18. Bg2 Nxc3 19. Qxb7+ Qxb7 20. Bxb7+ Kxb7 21. bxc3 Bxa3+ 22. Kb1 fxe6 23. Nxe6 Rc8 24. Rh3 g6 25. c4 Rhe8 $10 {Sherwin,J-Fischer,R ch-USA 1959 Sherwin,J-Fischer,R ch-USA 1959 Sherwin,J-Fischer,R ch-USA 1959 Sherwin,J-Fischer,R ch-USA 1959 Bobby Fischer: '=' Bobby Fischer: 'and shortly drawn.. Sherwin,J-Fischer,R ch-USA 1959'}) 13... b4 $1 {Bobby Fischer: 'My game with Walther (game 9) had taught me this lesson well.'} 14. Nce2 Bb7 15. Kb1 $2 ({Bobby Fischer: 'In this sharp variation, White has no time for such amenities.'} 15. Ng3 $15 {Bobby Fischer: 'avoids incurring any severe disadvantage, while the speculative'}) (15. Bxe6 $5 fxe6 16. Nxe6 Qc4 17. Nxg7+ (17. N2d4 $142 {Bobby Fischer: '>='}) 17... Kf8 $1 $17 {Bobby Fischer: 'favors black'}) 15... Nc5 16. Ng3 {Bobby Fischer: 'Position after'} d5 $1 {Bobby Fischer: 'I could see from the expression on Smyslov's face that he already thought he was busted.'} 17. f5 $5 ({Bobby Fischer: 'on'} 17. e5 g6 $1 18. Rc1 Qb6 $1 19. c3 a5 { 0-0    0-0    0-0    0-0   Bobby Fischer: 'followed by ... 0-0 with a powerful attack in the works. Smyslov's keen positional judgment tells him that such a course for White is lifeless. So he sacs a Pawn instead.'}) 17... dxe4 18. Qg4 exf5 19. Ndxf5 g6 $1 ({Bobby Fischer: 'Perhaps this simple retort escaped him. Was he hoping for'} 19... O-O $2 20. Nh5 $1 g6 21. Qg3 $1 {Bobby Fischer: 'winning material if'} Bd8 22. Rxd8 $1 Qxd8 23. Nf6+ $18 {Bobby Fischer: 'etc.)? The rest of the game is, if one may use that hackneyed phrase, "a matter of technique." Black's a Pawn ahead with the better game to boot.'}) 20. Nxe7 ({Bobby Fischer: 'not'} 20. Nh6 $2 Bc8 21. Qh4 Bxh3 22. Qxh3 Bxg5 $19) 20... Qxe7 21. Qf4 O-O 22. Rd6 Rad8 23. Rf6 {Bobby Fischer: 'Naturally Smyslov avoids swapping.'} Rd5 24. Bg4 Nd7 25. Rf1 ({Bobby Fischer: 'A desperate attempt to complicate. On'} 25. Nxe4 $2 Rd4 26. Bxd7 Qxd7 $19) ({Bobby Fischer: 'wins a piece. Or'} 25. Qxe4 Rd1+ $1 26. Rxd1 Bxe4 27. Rxd7 Qe5 $19) 25... e3 ({Bobby Fischer: 'not'} 25... Nxf6 $2 26. gxf6 Qe5 27. Qh6 $18 {Bobby Fischer: 'wins.'}) 26. b3 {Bobby Fischer: 'Position after'} Rd2 27. Bxd7 $8 {Bobby Fischer: '' Bobby Fischer: 'Forced, but now White's game rapidly deteriorates and the extra Pawn makes its presence felt.'} Rxd7 28. Re1 Re8 29. h4 Qc5 $1 30. Qc4 $8 {Bobby Fischer: '' Bobby Fischer: 'Horrible, but necessary, to meet the main threat of Qc3'} Qxc4 31. bxc4 Rd4 {Bobby Fischer: 'Now Black hacks away unmercifully.'} 32. c5 Rxh4 33. c6 Bc8 34. Rd6 Rc4 35. Kb2 Kg7 36. Kb3 Rg4 37. Ne2 Re6 $1 38. Red1 ({Bobby Fischer: 'or'} 38. Rxe6 Bxe6+ 39. Kb2 Rc4 {Bobby Fischer: 'etc'}) 38... Rg2 39. Nf4 Rxd6 40. Rxd6 Rd2 41. Rd3 $8 {Bobby Fischer: '' Bobby Fischer: 'The only move. Smyslov might have resigned had we adjourned here. But we were both playing fast and, as a consequence, were still well in the first session, carried by sheer momentum.'} Rf2 42. Rd4 $8 {Bobby Fischer: ''} ({Bobby Fischer: 'Again forced. On'} 42. Nd5 e2 43. Re3 Rf3 $19 {Bobby Fischer: 'wins.'}) 42... e2 43. Nd3 Bf5 44. c7 Rf3 ({Bobby Fischer: 'quicker is'} 44... Bxd3 45. c8=Q e1=Q 46. Rxd3 Qb1+ 47. Ka4 Rxc2 $19 {Bobby Fischer: 'etc.'}) 45. c8=Q Bxc8 ({Bobby Fischer: 'again'} 45... e1=Q {Bobby Fischer: 'was quicker, but I wanted to avoid "complications."'}) 46. Re4 Bf5 47. Rxe2 Bxd3 48. cxd3 Rxd3+ 49. Kxb4 Rd5 50. Rg2 h6 51. gxh6+ Kxh6 52. a4 g5 53. Rc2 Rd6 54. Kc5 {Bobby Fischer: 'Final Position after'} Re6 {Bobby Fischer: 'White resigns'} 0-1

