ram [#]} Kf7 $1 $17 {Boychuk,Taras - Poleshchuk,Nikolai, corr 2014 Gligoric,Svetozar: 'Boychuk,Taras - Poleshchuk,Nikolai, corr 2014'}) 19. Rbf2 {Gligoric,Svetozar: '?' '?' '?''Prusikin,Michael: 'Gligoric,Svetozar: '?''' Gligoric,Svetozar: 'Ripperger: '[The dynamics of White's pieces is limited, and the pawn chain is vulnerable.]'' Gligoric,Svetozar: 'Ripperger: '[Die Dynamik der weißen Figuren ist begrenzt und die Bauernkette verwundbar.]''} Qe7 {Gligoric,Svetozar: 'Prusikin,Michael: ''' Gligoric,Svetozar: 'Prusikin,Michael: '' '''} 20. Bc2 g5 {Gligoric,Svetozar: '!' '!' '!''Prusikin,Michael: 'Gligoric,Svetozar: '!''' Gligoric,Svetozar: 'Ripperger: '[Fischer wants to move his knight to f4. It is also worth noticing that he has optimized his light-squared bishop by placing all his pawns on dark squares.]'' Gligoric,Svetozar: 'Ripperger: '[Fischer will seinen Springer nach f4 überführen. Außerdem ist beachtenswert, daß er bei eigenem weißfeldrigen Läufer alle seine Bauern auf schwarzen Feldern postiert hat.]''} (20... Ng4 $5 {Gligoric,Svetozar} 21. Rxf8+ Rxf8 22. Rxf8+ Qxf8 23. Qe2 g5 24. Bc1 Qe8 25. Qd1 Qh5 26. h3 Nf6 27. Qxh5 Nxh5 28. Kf2 Kh7 $17) 21. Bd2 Qe8 {Gligoric,Svetozar: '!' '!' '!''Prusikin,Michael: 'Gligoric,Svetozar: '!'''} 22. Be1 Qg6 23. Qd3 Nh5 {Gligoric,Svetozar: '!' '!' '!''Prusikin,Michael: 'Gligoric,Svetozar: '!''' Gligoric,Svetozar: 'Ripperger: '[The great Jose Capablanca once said: "Pieces that are not needed to carry out a plan should be exchanged!"]'' Gligoric,Svetozar: 'Ripperger: '[Der große José Raul Capablanca hat den Lehrsatz geprägt: "Figuren, die zur Durchführung eines Planes nicht benötigt werden, soll man abtauschen!"]''} 24. Rxf8+ Rxf8 25. Rxf8+ Kxf8 26. Bd1 Nf4 {Gligoric,Svetozar: '!' '!' '!''Prusikin,Michael: 'Gligoric,Svetozar: '!''' Black has the most pleasant position, but the game took end earlier than expected after the famous... Gligoric,Svetozar: 'Edouard, Romain: 'Black has the most pleasant position, but the game took end earlier than expected after the famous...''} (26... Nf6 {(Gligoric,Svetozar) Prusikin,Michael: 'Gligoric,Svetozar'} 27. Bg3 $1) 27. Qc2 {Gligoric,Svetozar: '??' '??' '??''Prusikin,Michael: 'The last mistake in a difficult but still defendable position. Gligoric,Svetozar: '??''' Gligoric,Svetozar: 'Prusikin,Michael: 'The l'Prusikin,Michael: 'The last mistake in a difficult but still defendable position.' Prusikin,Michael: 'The last mistake in a difficult but still defendable position. Gligoric,Svetozar: '??''' ast mistake in a difficult but still defendable position.'' Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s): '?' Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s): '[#]'} (27. Qb1 $17 {(Gligoric,Svetozar) Prusikin,Michael: 'Gligoric,Svetozar' Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s): '=' Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s): 'and White is okay.' Ripperger: 'was the right move, but it would not have changed the result. White's pieces are practically helpless.' Ripperger: 'war hier der richtige Zug, der aber am Ergebnis nichts geändert hätte. Die weißen Figuren sind fast hilflos.'}) (27. Qe3 {Gligoric,Svetozar} Qe8 28. Qf2 Kg8 29. Qc2 g4 $17) {Gligoric,Svetozar: 'Prusikin,Michael: 'Diagram [#]''} 27... Bxa4 $1 {Gligoric,Svetozar: 'Prusikin,Michael: 'A nice tactical blow at the end.'' Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s): 'Accuracy: White = 20%, Black = 89%. ' Extraordinary understanding of chess by Fischer! Gligoric,Svetozar: 'Edouard, Romain: 'Extraordinary understanding of chess by Fischer!''} 28. Qxa4 {Gligoric,Svetozar} Qxe4 $19 0-1

