eeh: 'Cyrus Lakdawala: '!' '!''} 29. Nd6 {Reeh: 'Cyrus Lakdawala: 'EXERCISE (combination alert): How did Fischer end Spassky's dreams of attack? --- ANSWER: Simplification/sham queen sacrifice.''} Qxd6 {Reeh: 'Cyrus Lakdawala: '!' '!''} (29... Reb8 30. Qd2 b5) 30. exd6 Bxc3 {Reeh: 'Cyrus Lakdawala: 'He gets it right back.''} 31. bxc3 {Damit hat der schwarze a-Bauer freie Fahrt.} f6 {Reeh: 'Cyrus Lakdawala: '!' '!' Cyrus Lakdawala: 'Fischer skilfully reclaims the dark squares, his weak colour. Spassky's position is hopeless for the following reasons: 1. White is a full pawn down in the ending. --- 2. White's queenside structure is weak and he is on the verge of overextension. --- 3. Black passed a-pawn is about to sail down the a-file, tying up White. --- 4. White's passed d-pawn is firmly blockaded.''} 32. g5 $1 {ChessBase: 'Gligoric,Svetozar: '!'' Reeh: 'Cyrus Lakdawala: 'Spassky realizes he cannot allow ...g6-g5!.'' Weiß muß unbedingt die dunklen Felder im schwarzen Lager schwächen.} hxg5 {Reeh: 'Cyrus Lakdawala: 'Craig Pritchett: '?!'''} ({Reeh: 'Cyrus Lakdawala: 'As Smyslov and others pointed out, Black could have won most simply by playing''} 32... c4 $1 {ChessBase} 33. Nb4 hxg5 $15 {Purdy} 34. fxg5 f5 35. Nxd5 exd5 {, and if} 36. Rxd5 Rxe1 37. Bxe1 a3 {.}) ({Also strong is} 32... Bf3 33. Rb1 c4 34. Nb4 hxg5 35. fxg5 f5 36. Bg3 Ra5 $1 37. Re3 Be4 {, when White can resign.}) 33. fxg5 f5 {Reeh: 'Cyrus Lakdawala: 'Black now owns three passed pawns!''} 34. Bg3 {Reeh: 'Cyrus Lakdawala: 'Spassky plays for his only prayer: the central dark squares.''} Kf7 {Reeh: 'Cyrus Lakdawala: '?!' '?!' Cyrus Lakdawala: 'He should play on the principle: Passed pawns should be pushed.''} ({Reeh: 'Cyrus Lakdawala: 'Craig Pritchett: 'And here, too, Fischer could have played the simpler'''} 34... a3 $1 {ChessBase} 35. Ne5 Nxe5 36. Bxe5 Red8 {Reeh: 'Cyrus Lakdawala: '!' '!' Cyrus Lakdawala: 'and if''} 37. Rf1 {Reeh: 'Cyrus Lakdawala: ', intending Rf4 and Rh4, then''} Ra4 {Reeh: 'Cyrus L