{Nigel Davies: 'In the early 1960s Bobby Fischer experimented with the Black side of the Ruy Lopez. He played a few games with the Classical defence 3...Bc5 and in the 1963 US championship adopted the so-called 'Norwegian Variation' with 3...a6 4 Ba4 b5 5 Bb3 Na5. Fischer was probably attracted to this line by the fact that it gains the two bishops. But meanwhile he loses time and White gains the ascendancy in the center...'} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Ba4 b5 5. Bb3 Na5 6. d4 ({Nigel Davies: 'The attempt to refute Black's play with'} 6. Bxf7+ $6 {Nigel Davies: 'is refuted by'} Kxf7 7. Nxe5+ Ke7 $1) ({White's best move is probably} 6. O-O) 6... exd4 7. Qxd4 { 8.f7 f7 9.d5 +-  8.f7 f7 9.d5 +- Nigel Davies: 'ChessBase: ' 8.f7 f7 9.d5 +-''} Ne7 $1 {Nigel Davies: 'White was threatening 8.Bxf7+ followed by 9.Qd5+, picking up the rook on a8.'} 8. c3 $2 {Nigel Davies: 'After this Black gets ...d7-d5 in when his two bishops become quite dangerous.'} (8. O-O Nxb3 9. axb3 Bb7 { d5=}) ({White should prefer simply} 8. Nc3 Bb7 9. O-O (9. Bg5 Nxb3 10. axb3 Nc6 11. Qe3 f6 12. Bf4 Bb4 13. O-O Bxc3 14. Qxc3 O-O 15. Rad1 d6 {was fine for Black in Emms - Yuneev, Leningrad 1990}) 9... d6 10. Qd3 Nxb3 {(Lind - Ernst, Karlskrona 1983) and now} 11. axb3 {looks fairly equal.}) 8... Nxb3 9. axb3 Bb7 10. Bf4 ({Nigel Davies: 'Simply'} 10. O-O $142 {Nigel Davies: 'would also have been an improvement on Addison's choice as' Nigel Davies: 'would also have been an improvement on Addison's choice as ChessBase: '''} d5 11. exd5 Nxd5 $2 {Nigel Davies: 'is answered by'} 12. Re1+ $16 {Euwe Euwe Nigel Davies: 'ChessBase: '' ChessBase: 'Euwe''}) ({Nigel Davies: 'Euwe has suggested'} 10. b4 {Nigel Davies: 'so as to meet'} d5 {Nigel Davies: 'with'} 11. e5 $1 $16 {Euwe Euwe Nigel Davies: '!' '!' Nigel Davies: 'when Black is in a bind because of the difficulties he will have contesting the dark squares (notably c5).' Nigel Davies: 'when Black is in a bind because of the difficulties he will have contesting the dark squares (notably c5). ChessBase: '!' ChessBase: 'Euwe''}) 10... d5 $1 11. e5 ({Nigel Davies: 'In this position'} 11. exd5 {Nigel Davies: 'can be answered by'} Nxd5 {Nigel Davies: 'as White is not ready to play Re1+. But now Black takes the initiative on the queenside.'} 12. Qe5+ Qe7 $15 {  ×b2b3}) 11... c5 $1 12. Qd3 (12. Qxc5 {Nigel Davies: '??' '??'} Nf5 $19 {Nigel Davies: 'wins the queen.' Nigel Davies: 'wins the queen. ChessBase: '-+''}) 12... Ng6 13. Bg3 {Nigel Davies: 'The bishop looks badly placed on this square because its activity is inhibited by the pawn on e5.'} ({Nigel Davies: 'But after'} 13. Bg5 Be7 (13... Qc7 14. O-O h6 $15 {Kmoch}) (13... Qd7 $2 14. O-O h6 15. e6 $1 $40 {Kmoch}) 14. Bxe7 Qxe7 15. Qe2 ({Nigel Davies: 'After'} 15. O-O {Nigel Davies: 'Black can just play'} Nxe5 $1) 15... O-O $17 {Kmoch} (15... Nf4 $145 {Nigel Davies: 'ChessBase: 'RR''} 16. Qf1 f6 {Nigel Davies: 'White's game falls apart.'} 17. g3 Ng6 $19)) 13... Be7 14. Nbd2 Nf8 $1 15. O-O Ne6 16. Rad1 g5 $1 17. h3 (17. Rfe1 $2 g4 $19) 17... h5 18. Rfe1 Qb6 19. Nf1 d4 $1 20. N3d2 g4 { 21... h4 22.h2 g3 23.fg c4 nebst 24... d3+ Euwe  21... h4 22.h2 g3 23.fg c4 nebst 24... d3+ Euwe Nigel Davies: 'Threatening 21... h4 22.Bh2 g3 23.fg c4 followed by 24... d3+.' Nigel Davies: 'Threatening 21... h4 22.Bh2 g3 23.fg c4 followed by 24... d3+. ChessBase: ' 21... h4 22.h2 g3 23.fg c4 nebst 24... d3+ Euwe''} 21. h4 (21. Ra1 $4 gxh3 (21... h4 22. Bh2 g3 23. fxg3 c4 24. bxc4 bxc4 25. Qxc4 dxc3+ $18) 22. gxh3 h4 23. Bh2 $19) 21... Qc6 $1 (21... O-O-O 22. c4 { 23.de4, 24.fd2}) 22. Qe4 (22. Ne4 {Nigel Davies: 'is met by'} c4 $1) 22... O-O-O 23. Qxc6+ Bxc6 24. c4 ({Nigel Davies: 'After'} 24. Ra1 dxc3 25. bxc3 Kb7 {Mit einem gewonnenem Endspiel. Euwe Mit einem gewonnenem Endspiel. Euwe Nigel Davies: 'Black has a winning endgame according to Euwe' Nigel Davies: 'Black has a winning endgame according to Euwe ChessBase: 'Mit einem gewonnenem Endspiel. Euwe''}) 24... Kd7 $1 25. Ra1 Ra8 26. Ne4 { 27.fd2  27.fd2 Nigel Davies: 'ChessBase: ' 27.fd2''} Bxe4 $1 {Nigel Davies: 'Before White has time to play 27.Nfd2'} 27. Rxe4 Ng7 $1 { f5  f5 Nigel Davies: 'The winning move. Black is going to play ... Nf5, winning the h4 pawn.' Nigel Davies: 'The winning move. Black is going to play ... Nf5, winning the h4 pawn. ChessBase: ' f5''} 28. Nd2 Nf5 29. Rf4 Ke6 30. Ne4 bxc4 31. bxc4 Rhb8 32. Ra2 Rb4 33. Nd2 Nxh4 34. Bxh4 Bxh4 { 35... g5  35... g5 Nigel Davies: 'ChessBase: ' 35... g5''} 35. Re4 Bg5 36. f4 gxf3 37. Nxf3 Be3+ 38. Kh2 Rxc4 0-1

