{Bobby Fischer: 'GAME N. 34 Hanging pawns unhung. Classical theory expounds the danger of "hanging Pawns," but Fischer demonstrates here, in a revolutionary manner, that they are just as often an asset as a liability. Bertok's errors seem insignificant, yet he drifts into a passive position. On the verge of exploiting Black's loose center, he always lacks just the one tempo needed to do so. Meanwhile, using the open b-file as a base of operations, Fischer manages to force White into a defensive posture. In the midst of this Q-side tension, the winning move (21...g5) comes unexpectedly on the opposite wing. '} 1. d4 {Bobby Fischer Bobby Fischer Konikowski Bobby Fischer} d5 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 Be7 {Charousek,R; Petrosian,T Bobby Fischer: '; A refinement attributed to Petrosian, but actually played by Charousek in the 'nineties - and probably dating back even farther. '} 4. Nf3 {Bobby Fischer: ', White, having no other good waiting move, is obliged to develop, thus restricting his option of playing this Knight to e2.'} (4. cxd5 exd5 5. Bf4 c6 6. e3 Bf5 7. g4 ({Bobby Fischer: 'R.Byrne's'} 7. Nge2 $1 {Byrne,R Bobby Fischer: 'is best)'}) 7... Be6 (7... Bg6 $5 {Bobby Fischer: '!' Bobby Fischer: 'is better.'}) 8. h3 {Botvinnik,M-Petrosian,T Moscow WCH 1963 Bobby Fischer: 'was played frequently in the 1963 title match between Botvinnik and Petrosian. White is slightly better.'}) 4... Nf6 5. Bg5 {Bobby Fischer: ', Back to the main line. The shadow boxing is over. '} O-O 6. e3 h6 {Bobby Fischer: '; Petrosian usually omits this move (see note to Black's 8th). '} 7. Bh4 b6 {Tartakover,S Bobby Fischer: '; Tartakover's Defense. '} 8. cxd5 {Bobby Fischer: ', The best procedure, opening the c-file and preparing Rc1 with pressure on Black's c-pawn.'} ({Bobby Fischer: 'An alternative is'} 8. Bd3 $5 Bb7 9. O-O Nbd7 10. Rc1 c5 11. Qe2 dxc4 12. Bxc4 Ne4 $10 {Petrosian,T-Fischer,R/Belgrade ct1959/ Bobby Fischer: '=' Bobby Fischer: '(Petrosian-Fischer, Candidates' 1959.)'}) 8... Nxd5 ({Bobby Fischer: 'Inferior here is'} 8... exd5 9. Bd3 {Bobby Fischer: 'and'} Bb7 (9... Z0 {Bobby Fischer} 10. Ne5 $1 {followed by f4 with a Pillsbury attacking formation: White has g4-g5 in the air - this line is playable for Black only with his pawn on h7 (instead of h6).}) 10. Ne5 $1 { f2-f4, g2-g4-g5 }) 9. Bxe7 Qxe7 10. Nxd5 exd5 {Bobby Fischer: '; The text is drawish, but I had already clinched first prize. '} 11. Be2 ({Bobby Fischer: 'Sharper is'} 11. Rc1 Be6 $1 12. Qa4 c5 13. Qa3 Rc8 14. Be2 {Bobby Fischer: 'and now'} Kf8 $10 {Bobby Fischer: 'levels;'} ({Bobby Fischer: 'while'} 14... Qb7 $1 {Bobby Fischer: 'is the prescription for maintaining tension. If'} 15. dxc5 bxc5 16. O-O (16. Rxc5 $2 Rxc5 17. Qxc5 Qxb2 $17 {Bobby Fischer: 'is bad for White.'}) 16... Qb6 $13 {Bobby Fischer: 'is double-edged.'})) 11... Be6 $1 {Bobby Fischer: '; The right post. At b7 this Bishop would block the b-file and obstruct later operations there. '} 12. O-O c5 13. dxc5 $2 {Bobby Fischer: ', Producing hanging center Pawns which, in this case, exert a tremendously cramping influence on White's future development.'} ({Bobby Fischer: 'Better is'} 13. Ne5 $142 Nd7 $10 ({Bobby Fischer: 'not'} 13... c4 $2 14. b3 b5 15. a4) {with equality.} 14. Z0 {Bobby Fischer}) 13... bxc5 14. Qa4 Qb7 $1 15. Qa3 (15. b3) 15... Nd7 16. Ne1 {Bobby Fischer: ', What else is there? Black's center is well-prutected, and he is ready to assume the Q-side initiative with ... a5 and ...Qb4. ' Bobby Fischer: ', What else is there? Black's center is well-prutected, and he is ready to assume the Q-side initiative with ... a5 and ...Qb4. ' Bobby Fischer: ', What else is there? Black's center is well-prutected, and he is ready to assume the Q-side initiative with ... a5 and ...Qb4. ' Konikowski: '?!'} (16. Rac1 $5 {Konikowski}) 16... a5 17. Nd3 c4 18. Nf4 Rfb8 19. Rab1 $2 ({Bobby Fischer: 'White's game is already difficult, e.g.,'} 19. Bf3 Nf6 20. Rfd1 Qxb2 21. Qxb2 Rxb2 22. Nxd5 Nxd5 23. Bxd5 Bxd5 24. Rxd5 c3 $1 25. Rdd1 ({Bobby Fischer: 'if'} 25. Rc5 c2 26. Rc1 Rd8 $19 {Bobby Fischer: 'wins.'}) 25... c2 26. Rdc1 Rab8 27. Kf1 Rb1 {Konikowski: '-+'} 28. Ke2 Rxa1 29. Rxa1 Rb1 $19 {Bobby Fischer: 'wins.'}) ({Bobby Fischer: 'Best is'} 19. Nxe6 $142 fxe6 20. Bg4 Ra6 $1 21. b3 $1 ({Bobby Fischer: 'if'} 21. Qe7 $2 Nf8) ({Bobby Fischer: 'or'} 21. Rab1 Qb4 22. Qc3 Qxc3 23. bxc3 Rab6) 21... cxb3 22. axb3 Qxb3 23. Qe7 Nf8 24. Ra3 {Bobby Fischer: 'with good drawing chances.'} {Bobby Fischer: '(if 24'} Qb4 25. Qxb4 Rxb4 26. Be2 Ra7 27. Rfa1 {Konikowski: 'Fischer'} a4 28. Bd1 $10 {Bobby Fischer: 'etc.)'}) 19... Bf5 $1 20. Rbd1 Nf6 21. Rd2 ({Bobby Fischer: 'The following variation gives some insight into the nature of White's problem:'} 21. Bf3 Qxb2 22. Qxb2 Rxb2 23. Nxd5 Nxd5 24. Bxd5 ({Bobby Fischer: 'if'} 24. Rxd5 Be6 25. Rc5 Rc8 $1 26. Rxa5 c3 27. Rc1 c2 28. Be4 Rb1 $1 29. Rxb1 cxb1=Q+ 30. Bxb1 Rc1#) 24... Rc8 25. e4 Be6 $1 26. Bxe6 fxe6 27. a4 c3 28. Rc1 c2 $19 {Bobby Fischer: 'and White, completely tied up, must lose material.'} 29. f3 {Konikowski} Rd8 $19) 21... g5 $1 $19 {Bobby Fischer: '!' Bobby Fischer: '; Practically forcing the win of a piece. ' Bobby Fischer: '!' Bobby Fischer: '; Practically forcing the win of a piece. ' Bobby Fischer: '!' Bobby Fischer: '; Practically forcing the win of a piece. ' Konikowski: '!'} 22. Nxd5 {Bobby Fischer: ', To break the hammer-lock.'} ({Bobby Fischer: 'On'} 22. Nh5 Ne4 23. Rc2 Qb4 $19 {Bobby Fischer: 'is crushing.' Bobby Fischer: 'is crushing.' Bobby Fischer: 'is crushing.' Konikowski: ''}) 22... Nxd5 23. Bxc4 ({Bobby Fischer: 'Not'} 23. Bf3 $2 Bd3) 23... Be6 {Bobby Fischer: '; Black has some temporary discomfort but it's only a matter of time before he consolidates and wins with his extra piece. '} 24. Rfd1 {Bobby Fischer: ', Blundering a Pawn.'} ({Bobby Fischer: 'The lesser evil is'} 24. Bxd5 $142 Bxd5 25. f3 $19 {Bobby Fischer: 'but White is still lost if Black exercises a modicum of caution.'}) 24... Nxe3 $1 {Bobby Fischer: '; Threatening mate. '} 25. Qxe3 (25. Bxe6 Qxg2#) 25... Bxc4 {Konikowski: '-+'} 26. h4 Re8 27. Qg3 Qe7 28. b3 Be6 29. f4 g4 {Bobby Fischer: '; Sealing the g-file and neutralizing all threats. '} 30. h5 Qc5+ 31. Rf2 Bf5 {Bobby Fischer: '; White resigns.'} 0-1

