{ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'GAME N. 39 The confrontation. This dramatic meeting between the generations took place on board I after it was rumored that Botvinnik would be given a "rest day" against the American team. But it was fated that Fischer, at last, albeit with Black, would have a crack at the world champion. Walking into a prepared variation, Fischer promptly refutes it. "The reader can guess that my equanimity was wrecked", confesses Botvinnik, whose notes are incorporated here. Nervously, he proceeds to run his still tenable position downhill. But Fischer, instead of nursing his winning advantage, simplifies too quickly and reaches an adjournment where victory is problematical. After a sleepless night of analysis, Botvinnik finds a stunning defense. Fischer engages in a seemingly harmless transposition of moves (51...b5), and falls into a pit - throwing away the win he maintains was still there. ''} 1. c4 {ChessBase ChessBase ChessBase ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer'} g6 2. d4 ({ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'If White so desires, he can prevent the Gruenfeld by''} 2. Nc3 Nf6 3. e4) 2... Nf6 3. Nc3 d5 {"Die Eingebung des Augenblicks. Ich konnte am Leuchten seiner Augen erkennen, daß er für mein Königsindisch gut gerüstet war", schreibt Fischer in seiner berühmten Partiensammlung "My 60 Memorable Games". ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: '; The spur of the moment. I could see by the glint in his eye that he had come well anned for my King's Indian. ''} 4. Nf3 ({ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'The sharpest try is''} 4. cxd5 Nxd5 5. e4) 4... Bg7 5. Qb3 {ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: ', The main line, but I don't believe this early development of the Queen can give White anything. ''} dxc4 ({ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'A solid alternative is''} 5... c6) 6. Qxc4 O-O 7. e4 Bg4 {Eine deutliche Kampfansage! Die Smyslov-Variante führt in der Regel zu sehr kompliziertem Spiel. Schwarz vermeidet Vereinfachungen und versucht, mit seinen Leichtfiguren Druck auf das weiße Zentrum auszuüben.}