'Bobby Fischer: 'Botvinnik thinks''} 9... Nb6 {als genauer. Geht die weiße Dame dann, wie in der Partie, nach c5, hat Schwarz die zusätzliche Möglichkeit, mit a6 oder 8d7 ein Tempo zu gewinnen. ChessBase: 'Botvinnik,M: ' ChessBase: 'Botvinnik,M:  Bobby Fischer: 'first is more accurate.'' Botvinnik - Smyslov, Moscow (m/4), 1958 Botvinnik,M: }) 10. Rd1 (10. d5 Na5 11. Qa4 c6) 10... Nb6 (10... Bxf3 {ChessBase: ' e7-e5 ' ChessBase: ' e7-e5  Bobby Fischer: 'followed by 11...e5 also gives Black active play.''  e7-e5 }) 11. Qc5 (11. Qd3 Bxf3 12. gxf3 e5 13. d5 Nd4 {= Botvinnik}) 11... Qd6 $1 {!} 12. h3 (12. Qxd6 {ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'is answered by''} cxd6 $1 $10 {ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: '!' Bobby Fischer: 'improving Black's Pawn structure and neutralizing White's center.'' !=}) (12. d5 Ne5 13. Nxe5 Bxe2 14. Kxe2 Bxe5 15. Qxd6 cxd6 16. Bd4 Rfc8 17. Bxe5 dxe5 18. Rc1 Nc4 19. b3 Nd6 {Arencibia - Konguveel, Linares, 1997 =}) (12. e5 {!?} Qxc5 13. dxc5 Nd7 (13... Nc8 14. h3 Bxf3 15. Bxf3 Bxe5 16. Rd7 a6 17. Bxc6 bxc6 18. f4 Bf6 19. Rxc7 $14 {Kaufman - Kudrin, Chicago, 1997}) 14. h3 Be6 15. Ng5 Ndxe5 16. Nxe6 fxe6 17. f4 Bh6 18. O-O Rad8 19. g3 Nb4 20. Bf2 Ned3 21. a3 Nxf2 22. Rxd8 Nxh3+ 23. Kg2 Rxd8 24. axb4 Nxf4+ 25. gxf4 Rd4 26. b5 $14 {Ziegler - Pribyl, Goeteborg, 1997}) 12... Bxf3 13. gxf3 {Weiß ist gezwungen, seine Bauernstellung zu schwächen.} ({Nach} 13. Bxf3 $2 Qxc5 14. dxc5 Nc4 {steht Schwarz prächtig.} 15. Bc1 Nd4 $13) 13... Rfd8 ({ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Wrong is''} 13... Qxc5 14. dxc5 Bxc3+ 15. bxc3 Na4 16. Kd2 $1 {!$16 Furman} e6 $16 {ChessBase: 'Furman,S' Furman,S}) ({Botvinnik is of the opinion that} 13... e6 {(ChessBase) (Bobby Fischer) (FURMAN) gives Black an equal game. But I feel it is not in the hypermodern spirit, which is precisely to tempt White into advancing his center Pawns in the hope they will become overextended.}) 14. d5 {ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: ', Opening the diagonal for Black's KB can't be right, but White is still s