general and of the position on the diagram in particular! Here I reckoned that whether the Black Queen went to h4 or f5, it would be in danger; for example,' Bobby Fischer: 'Or''} ({ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'On''} 17. Qxc7 $2 {?} Qxb2 {ChessBase: ' b4+' ChessBase: ' b4+ Bobby Fischer: 'White can't castle and 18...Qb4+ is threatened.'' 'with the idea'Qb4  b4+}) {ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Alas, my opponent found a third continuation!" (BOTVINNIK.) ''} 17... Qxf4 $1 {Diese einfache Möglichkeit hatte Botvinnik nicht berücksichtigt. Trotzdem besteht für ihn vorerst kein Grund zur Panik. Für den verlorengehenden Bauern erhält er Vorposten auf d6 und c7 sowie ein lebendiges Figuenspiel. ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: '; "A very unpleasant surprise - now White really had to start playing. UP to here I had only had to remember my analysis, though that was not so easy. I had a recollection of the Black Queen being trapped somewhere on the K-side; and following this track I managed to recall the whole variation. At last everything was in order - on the board was the familiar position; then suddenly it was obvious that in my analysis I had missed what Fischer had found with the greatest of ease at the board. The reader can guess that my equanimity was wrecked. However, if you assess 17...Qxf4 from an objective point of view, then although it is the best way out for Black, as you will see from what comes later, his position is still difficult." (BOTVINNIK.) When I made this move, I felt sure he had overlooked it. '' !} (17... Qf5 18. Qb4 a5 19. Qd4 {ChessBase: ' g4' ChessBase: ' g4 Bobby Fischer: 'threatening 20.Bg4'' ('with the idea'Bg4)  g4} c5 20. dxc6 bxc6 21. Bg4 c5 22. Qxd7 $14 {Botvinnik}) (17... Qh4 18. Qc2 g5 19. Rd4 $1) 18. Bxf4 ({ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Black's last is tactically justified after''} 18. Qxb6 {?} Qe4 $1 {!} 19. f3 Qh4+ $1 {!} 20. Bf2 Qb4+ $19 {ChessBase: ' axb6!' ChessBase: ' axb6! Bobby Fischer: 'followed by ...axb6! (toward the center).''  axb6!}) 18... Nxc5 19. Nxc7 Rac8 20. d6 exd6 21. exd6 ({ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Not''} 21. Rxd6 $2 {?} Ncd7 (21... Nbd7)) 21... Bxb2 {ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: '; "So Black has won a Pawn; but the Knight on c7 and the Pawn on d6 confine his Rooks - and also, White has two Bishops. The first thing White must do is complete his development." (BOTVINNIK.) ''} 22. O-O Nbd7 {ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: '; "A bad mistake; evidently, Black overestimated his possibilities. Of course, he had to prepare the move ...Be5;''} ({ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'the only way this could be done was by''} 22... Ncd7 {ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'and after''} 23. Bf3 Be5 24. Bxe5 Nxe5 25. Bxb7 Rb8 $14 {ChessBase: 'Botvinnik,M' ChessBase: 'Botvinnik,M Bobby Fischer: 'White has no more than a minimal advantage.'' Botvinnik,M}) {ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Now White has the two important squares d5 and c5 at his disposal and his spatial advantage becomes crushing." (BOTVINNIK.) Needless to add, I couldn't disagree more. Why should Black return the Pawn? ''} 23. Rd5 ({ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Archives recommends''} 23. Nd5 {ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'but after''} Kg7 {ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'the burden of proof rests with White - he's a Pawn down.''}) 23... b6 {'passed pawn'} 24. Bf3 $2 {Fischer und Botvinnik stimmen darin überein, daß dies der falsche Platz für den Läufer ist, aber bei der Stellungsbeurteilung nach dem richtigen c4 scheiden sich die Geister. ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: ', "Feeble play.'' ?} ({ChessBase: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Actually, White had played quite consistently so far and here he could have deployed his force with maximum efficiency by''} 24. Bc4 $1 {Während sich Botvinnik angesichts der Drohung e1-e7 im Vorteil sieht, kann Schwarz nach Fischer mit ChessBase: ' f1-e1-e7 ' ChessBase: ' f1-e1-e7  Bobby Fischer: 'with the threat of Re1-e7. The bishop is out of it on f3 and merely becomes an object of attack. Black now frees himself, and a Pawn down