1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Ba4 Nf6 5. O-O Be7 6. Re1 b5 7. Bb3 O-O 8. c3 d5 9. exd5 Nxd5 10. Nxe5 Nxe5 11. Rxe5 c6 12. d4 Bd6 13. Re1 Qh4 14. g3 Qh3 15. Be3 h5 $6 {TH: Although it worked in this game as a one-off, it is not to be recommended.} 16. Qf3 h4 17. Bxd5 cxd5 18. Nd2 (18. Qxd5 hxg3 19. hxg3 Bxg3 20. Qg2 Qxg2+ 21. Kxg2 Bd6 $13) 18... Be6 19. Bf4 Bg4 {Diagram #} 20. Qg2 (20. Qe3 {favours White according to Boleslavsky, but} Rae8 21. Qxe8 Bxf4 22. gxf4 Bf3 23. Nxf3 Qg4+ {draws.}) (20. Qxd5 $145 {is critical.} Bxf4 $140 21. gxf4 Qd3 (21... Rae8 22. Qg2 Qd3 23. f3 {is also very bad for Black - Nunn)}) 22. Ne4 {Black has little to show for the two pawns - Nunn.}) 20... Qxg2+ 21. Kxg2 h3+ $1 {After this Black's solid position made it almost imposible for White to play for a win.} 22. Kg1 Bxf4 23. gxf4 Rfd8 24. f3 Be6 25. Nb3 Rab8 26. a3 Rb6 27. Kf2 g6 28. Re5 Kg7 29. Rae1 Kf6 30. Na5 Rh8 31. b4 Rc8 32. R5e3 Rg8 33. Nb3 Ra8 34. Ra1 g5 $1 35. fxg5+ Kxg5 36. Rg1+ Kf6 37. Ree1 Rc6 38. Rc1 Bf5 39. Rge1 Rg8 40. Rg1 Ra8 $2 (40... Rxg1 41. Kxg1 Kg5 {idea ...Kf4 and ...Rg6 maintains equality (Fischer)}) 41. Nc5 a5 42. Ra1 Rcc8 43. Ra2 Rg8 44. Rg3 axb4 45. cxb4 Rh8 46. Rg1 Rhg8 $14 47. Rxg8 {Sealed move} Rxg8 48. Ke3 Re8+ 49. Kf4 Rg8 50. Ke3 Re8+ 51. Kf4 Rg8 52. Re2 Rg2 53. Ke3 Rg1 $1 54. a4 bxa4 55. Nxa4 Rd1 $1 (55... Rb1 56. Nc3 $1 Rb3 57. Kd2 Rb2+ 58. Ke1 $13) 56. Rb2 Rd3+ 57. Kf2 Rxd4 58. Nc3 Rd3 59. Ne2 d4 $14 {Sealed at second adjournment} 60. b5 Bc8 61. Nc1 (61. Ng3 Bb7 62. Ne4+ Ke5 {and the K goes to the queenside drawing (Wade)}) 61... Rd1 62. Nb3 (62. Rc2 Bb7 63. Nb3 Bxf3 $1 $11) 62... Rh1 63. Kg3 Rg1+ 64. Kf4 Rg2 65. Rd2 Bb7 66. b6 Ba8 $1 (66... Bc6 $2 67. Rxd4) 67. Rxd4 Rxh2 68. Rd6+ Ke7 69. Rh6 Rb2 70. Nd4 h2 71. Kg3 (71. Kg3 {Fischer proposed a draw} Kd7 $140 72. Rxh2 Rxh2 73. Kxh2 Bxf3 $1 74. Nxf3 Kc6) 1/2-1/2

