1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 e6 5. Nb5 d6 6. c4 Nf6 7. N5c3 (7. N1c3 {- 55/(209)}) 7... Be7 8. g3 $146 {Matanovic,A: 'N'} (8. Be2 {Ü 49/(219) Matanovic,A: '- 49/(219)' Ü 49/(219) Ü 49/(219) Ü 49/(219) Matanovic,A: '- 49/(219)'}) 8... O-O 9. Bg2 a6 10. O-O Rb8 11. Na3 Qc7 12. Be3 Bd7 13. Rc1 Ne5 14. h3 Rfc8 15. f4 Ng6 16. Qd2 $14 { Matanovic,A: ''    Matanovic,A: ''} Be8 17. Rfd1 b6 18. Qf2 h6 {MIKHALCHISHIN: 'Diagram '} 19. Kh2 $6 {MIKHALCHISHIN: 'useful move , but Whites' main problem in this position is to include into the game Knight on a3. At this moment it was possible to do ,while pawn c4 is poisoned'} (19. Nab1 $1 Bc6 (19... Qxc4 20. b3 $1 (20. Nd5 Qxa2 $13) (20. Bf1 Qb4 21. a3 Qb3 $13) 20... Qb4 (20... Qc7 21. Nd5) 21. Rd4 Qc5 (21... Qa5 22. f5 exf5 (22... Ne5 23. b4 $18) 23. exf5 Nf8 24. b4 Qe5 25. Re1 $18) 22. Rc4 Qh5 23. Bxb6 $16) 20. a4 Qb7 21. Nd2 a5 (21... Nd7 22. b4) 22. Re1 Nd7 23. Nb3 $16) 19... Qa7 20. Qe2 Qc7 21. Bf3 $6 ({MIKHALCHISHIN: 'it was time to start protecting own pawn.'} 21. Re1 $5) 21... Bc6 $1 {MIKHALCHISHIN: 'Diagram '} 22. Nab1 {MIKHALCHISHIN: '?!' '?!' '?!'} ({MIKHALCHISHIN: 'More active and better was'} 22. Nd5 Qb7 23. Nxe7+ Nxe7 24. Rxd6 Bxe4 25. Bxe4 Qxe4 26. Rd4 Qg6 27. Rd3 Ne4 28. Qg4 Qxg4 29. hxg4 b5 30. b3 {with very tense end.}) ({It was possible to start action on the Queens side} 22. b4) 22... Qb7 23. Nd2 b5 $17 24. cxb5 (24. a3 {was another typical option of fighting against b7-b5.}) 24... axb5 25. b4 Qa8 26. Rc2 {MIKHALCHISHIN: 'Diagram '} d5 ({MIKHALCHISHIN: 'More direct attack on the Queens side was preferable'} 26... Qa3 $1 {MIKHALCHISHIN: '!?' '!?' '!?'} 27. Rb1 (27. Rdc1 Bf8 28. Ncb1 Qa8 29. Nc3 Qa3 30. Ncb1 {with repetition.}) 27... Bxe4 $1 28. Ndxe4 (28. Bxe4 Rxc3 29. Rxc3 Qxc3 $17) 28... Nxe4 $17) 27. e5 Ne4 $1 ({MIKHALCHISHIN: 'Of course active approach-Russians never go back!'} 27... Nd7 28. Rb1 Nb6 29. Bd4 $13 (29. Bxb6 Rxb6 30. Qe3 Qb8 31. Ne2 {with mutual chances.})) 28. Bxe4 dxe4 29. Bc5 $8 ({Maybe better strategy would be attack of the e4 pawn.} 29. Rb1 Bd5 30. Bf2) 29... Bxc5 30. bxc5 Rd8 $1 31. Re1 {MIKHALCHISHIN: 'Diagram '} Ne7 $1 {MIKHALCHISHIN: '!?' '!?' '!?'} ({Similar idea could be conducted differently} 31... e3 $5 32. Qxe3 Ne7 33. Qf2 Nf5 34. Nce4 Nd4 35. Rb2 Qa3 {with initiative.}) 32. Ncxe4 Nf5 33. Nb3 Nd4 34. Nxd4 Rxd4 35. Nd6 Qa4 (35... Qa3 $5) ({Two other options were more direct} 35... Ra4) 36. f5 $8 Ra8 $2 ({MIKHALCHISHIN: 'Better was'} 36... Rd5 $1 37. Rb2 (37. Rd2 Ra8 38. Rb2 exf5 39. Nxf5 Rxc5 {with very tense position.}) 37... Qd4 $1 $17) 37. Rb2 $1 (37. f6 {was very unpleasant for Black.}) 37... Qa3 (37... Rb4 {was much better chance,eliminating the defence of pawn a2.}) 38. fxe6 fxe6 39. Nxb5 Bxb5 40. Qxb5 Rd3 41. Rg2 $14 {MIKHALCHISHIN: 'Diagram  White protected everything and their free pawns are ready to run.'} Qc3 42. Ree2 (42. Re4 {was more powerful - young Bobby would play it!}) 42... Ra3 43. Rc2 Qxe5 44. Rce2 (44. Rb2 Kh7 45. Rbe2 Qd5 46. Qb4 Rac3 47. Qe4+ Qxe4 48. Rxe4 Rxc5 49. Rxe6 Ra5 {was close to draw.}) 44... Re3 45. Rxe3 Rxe3 46. a4 Rc3 47. c6 $1 {MIKHALCHISHIN: 'Fischer decides to sacrifice its c pawn and starts to prepare run of another,more dangerous one.'} Qd6 48. c7 Rxc7 49. Qb8+ Kh7 50. a5 h5 $1 51. h4 {MIKHALCHISHIN: 'Diagram '} Qc5 $2 ({MIKHALCHISHIN: 'It was very difficult way to draw'} 51... Rc6 $1 52. Qxd6 (52. Qb1+ Kh6 53. Rc2 (53. Qe1 Rc4) 53... Rxc2+ 54. Qxc2 Qa3 $11) 52... Rxd6 53. Ra2 Ra6 54. Kg2 Kg6 55. Kf3 Kf5 56. Ra3 e5 57. Ra4 e4+ 58. Ke3 Kg4 59. Kxe4 Kxg3 60. Kd5 (60. Kf5 g6+ 61. Ke5 Kf3 62. Kd5 Kg3 63. Kc5 g5 64. hxg5 h4 65. g6 h3 {with draw.}) 60... g5 $11) 52. a6 Rf7 (52... Ra7 53. Qb1+ Kh6 54. Rc2 Qf5 55. Qc1+ Kh7 56. Ra2 {was stiil winning for White.}) 53. Qb1+ Kh6 54. Qa2 Re7 55. Qd2+ $1 Kg6 56. Re2 $1 (56. Rf2 {was not bad.}) 56... Kh7 57. Qc2+ $18 {MIKHALCHISHIN: 'transposition into winning Rook end.'} Qxc2 58. Rxc2 Kg6 59. Ra2 Ra7 60. Ra5 e5 61. Kg2 Kf6 62. Kf2 Ke6 63. Ke3 Kf5 64. Kf3 g6 65. Ra3 $1 g5 66. hxg5 Kxg5 67. Ke4 {MIKHALCHISHIN: '1-0 '} 1-0

