{Bobby Fischer: 'GAME N. 10 Milking the cow The Ruy Lopez has been so extensively analyzed that often both players reel off their first twenty moves in two minutes flat. Nevertheless, it gives rise to situations that call for tact and patience. As Bronstein remarked. "When you play the Ruy, it's like milking a cow." Fischer, here, milks the cow to a fare-thee-well. The first twenty-two moves are identical with game number 6. Unzicker then varies with the dubious ...f6. which undermines his e-Pawn and leaves him with weak squares. Retribution, though not swift, is sure. Creating simultaneous threats on both wings. Fischer finally infiltrates on the a-file. Black is so tied up that he cannot defend one of his Pawns when attacked - making defeat imminent. '} 1. e4 {Bobby Fischer} e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Ba4 Nf6 5. O-O Be7 6. Re1 b5 7. Bb3 d6 8. c3 O-O 9. h3 Na5 10. Bc2 c5 (10... c6 11. d4 Qc7 {Rossolimo,N Bobby Fischer: 'is an interesting alternative. (ROSSOLIMO) - Black avoids weakening his d5.'}) 11. d4 Qc7 12. Nbd2 Bd7 13. Nf1 Rfe8 14. Ne3 ({Bobby Fischer: 'Tal and Geller recommend'} 14. b3 {Bobby Fischer: 'and if'} g6 15. Bg5 {Tal,M; Geller,E}) 14... g6 15. dxe5 dxe5 16. Nh2 Rad8 17. Qf3 Be6 18. Nhg4 Nxg4 19. hxg4 ({Bobby Fischer: 'Against Matanovich, at Portoroz, 1958, I tried the inferior'} 19. Nxg4 Bxg4 20. hxg4 c4 21. g3 Nb7 22. Kg2 Nc5 23. Rh1 f6 $10 {Fischer,R-Matanovic,A Portoroz izt 1958 Bobby Fischer: '=' Bobby Fischer: 'Black's Knight is already prepared to parachute to d3.'}) 19... Qc6 $2 {Gligoric} ({Bobby Fischer: 'White gets an edge after'} 19... Nc4 20. Nd5 Bxd5 21. exd5 $13) 20. g5 $5 {! Gligoric} Nc4 (20... Bxg5 21. Nd5 Be7 (21... Bxc1 22. Nf6+ $16) 22. Nxe7+ Rxe7 23. Bg5 $16 {Gligoric}) 21. Ng4 Bxg4 22. Qxg4 f6 {Bobby Fischer: '?'} ({Bobby Fischer: 'For analysis of this position see game 6.'} 22... Nb6 $1 {Fischer,R-Shocron,G Mar del Plata 1959 Bobby Fischer: 'Fischer,R-Shocron,G; Mar del Plata, 1959.'}) {Bobby Fischer: 'Unzicker prefers active defense. He eliminates the potential pressure along the h-file, it is true, but at the cost of weakening his e-Pawn. '} 23. gxf6 {× e5} Bxf6 24. a4 $1 {Fischer/Gligoric} Nb6 25. axb5 axb5 26. Be3 $16 { Bobby Fischer: ', Because both flanks are fluid, White, with his two Bishops, is better able to penetrate and exploit the "loose" Pawns. '} Ra8 (26... Nc4 {Bobby Fischer: 'is met by'} 27. Bb3 {Bobby Fischer: 'instituting an awkward pin.'}) 27. Red1 {Bobby Fischer: ', If he swaps, White gains the a-file; if he doesn't. White keeps the d-file. '} Kh8 28. b3 Bg7 ({Bobby Fischer: 'Black should ease the pressure by'} 28... Rxa1 $142 29. Rxa1 Ra8 30. Rxa8+ Nxa8 {Bobby Fischer: 'though'} 31. Qd1 $1 $16 { d1-a1-a~ Bobby Fischer: 'followed by Qa1! forces an invasion on the Q-side.'}) 29. Qh4 Bf6 30. Bg5 $1 Bxg5 31. Qxg5 {Bobby Fischer: ', Now White must penetrate on either the a- or d-file. Black's e-Pawn has clearly been exposed as a weakling. '} Rxa1 ({The threat was} 31... Z0 {Bobby Fischer} 32. Rxa8 Nxa8 33. Rd5) 32. Rxa1 Nd7 {Bobby Fischer: '; Apparently defending everything.'} 33. Bd1 $1 {Bobby Fischer: ', Bringing the Bishop into the game puts additional pressure on Black's overburdened pieces. '} (33. Ra7 {Bobby Fischer: 'can be met by'} Qd6) 33... Nf6 ({Bobby Fischer: 'Not'} 33... Qxe4 34. Bf3 Qf4 ({Bobby Fischer: 'if'} 34... Qc2 35. Ra7 $18 { Bobby Fischer: 'with a winning attack.'}) 35. Qxf4 exf4 36. Bc6 Re7 ({Bobby Fischer: 'or'} 36... Rd8 37. Rd1 $18) 37. Ra8+ $1 Kg7 38. Ra7 $18 {Bobby Fischer: 'wins a piece.'}) 34. Ra7 {Bobby Fischer: ', Infiltration! '} Qd6 ({Bobby Fischer: 'On'} 34... Nxe4 {Bobby Fischer: '?'} 35. Qh6 $18 {Bobby Fischer: 'forces mate.'}) 35. Be2 $1 {Bobby Fischer: ', Simply attacking a Pawn. Curiously, Black is in too much of a straitjacket to do much about it. '} Re7 ({Bobby Fischer: 'How can Black defend the Pawn? '} 35... b4 $2 36. Ra6 Nxe4 37. Qh4 Qd5 38. Bf3 Qd3 39. Ra7 $18 {Bobby Fischer: 'wins.'}) (35... Nxe4 $2 36. Qh6 Re7 37. Qf8#) (35... Qc6 36. Rf7 Ng8 37. Qh4 h6 38. Qg4 Rd8 39. Bxb5 $1 $18 {Bobby Fischer: '!' Bobby Fischer: 'wins.'}) (35... Rb8 36. Rf7 Ng8 37. Rd7 $1 Qf6 ({Bobby Fischer: 'if'} 37... Qxd7 38. Qxe5+ Qg7 39. Qxb8 Qxc3 40. Qxb5 $18) 38. Qe3 Qc6 39. Rd5 $18 {Bobby Fischer: 'when one of Black's hanging Pawns must fall.'}) 36. Rxe7 Qxe7 37. Bxb5 Kg7 38. Be2 {Bobby Fischer: ', The win is still far from clear. White's major technical problem is creating a passed Pawn on the Q-side while sheltering his King from a perpetual check. '} Qc7 {Bobby Fischer: '; Threatening ...Nxe4. '} 39. Qe3 Qa5 40. g3 Qa3 ({Bobby Fischer: 'Black should wait around with'} 40... Qc7 $142) 41. Kg2 ({Sharper and possibly immediately decisive is} 41. b4 $1 {Bobby Fischer} cxb4 42. Qc5 $1) 41... Qa5 ({Bobby Fischer: 'On'} 41... Qxb3 42. Qxc5 Nxe4 (42... Qe6 43. Bc4 $18 {Gligoric}) 43. Qxe5+ Nf6 44. c4 $18 {Bobby Fischer: 'should win.'}) 42. Qd3 Qb6 43. Qc4 Qc6 44. Bd3 ({Bobby Fischer: 'It's better to refrain from'} 44. f3 $2 {× e3, a2-g2 Bobby Fischer: 'which weakens the K -field.'}) 44... Qb6 45. b4 cxb4 46. cxb4 {Bobby Fischer: ', Step one is completed: White has a passed b-Pawn. '} Ng4 47. Qc5 Qxc5 $8 {Bobby Fischer: '; Forced.'} (47... Qd8 {Bobby Fischer: '?' Bobby Fischer: 'loses a second Pawn after'} 48. Be2) 48. bxc5 Kf7 49. f4 $1 {Gligoric Bobby Fischer: ', The idea is to create another passed Pawn in the center. '} Ke7 50. Kf3 Nf6 ({Bobby Fischer: 'On'} 50... h5 51. Bc4 {Bobby Fischer: 'maintains the bind (if'} Kd7 $2 52. Bf7 {Bobby Fischer: ').'}) 51. Bb5 ({Bobby Fischer: 'Not'} 51. fxe5 {Bobby Fischer: '?'} Nd7 $10 {Bobby Fischer: 'draws.'}) 51... Ke6 {Bobby Fischer: '; Striving to keep the blockade as long as possible. '} 52. Bc4+ Ke7 53. c6 $1 Ne8 {Bobby Fischer: '; Makes it easy.'} ({Bobby Fischer: 'The best defense was'} 53... exf4 {} 54. gxf4 Ne8 55. e5 Nc7 56. Ke4 Ne8 ({Bobby Fischer: 'if'} 56... h5 57. Kf3 {Bobby Fischer: 'wins.'}) 57. Bg8 Kf8 58. Bxh7 Kg7 59. Bxg6 Kxg6 60. f5+ Kg5 61. f6 Kg6 62. Kd5 Kf7 63. Kc5 Ke6 64. Kb6 $18 {Bobby Fischer: 'wins.'}) ({Bobby Fischer: 'If'} 53... Kd6 $2 54. fxe5+ Kxe5 55. c7 $18) 54. fxe5 h6 55. Ke3 Nc7 56. Kd4 h5 57. Ke3 $1 g5 58. Be2 h4 (58... Ke6 59. Kd4 h4 60. gxh4 gxh4 61. Bg4+ $18 {Gligoric}) 59. gxh4 gxh4 60. Bc4 Ne8 61. Kf4 Kd8 62. Kg4 Kc7 63. Bf7 Ng7 64. Kxh4 Kxc6 65. Kg5 {Bobby Fischer: ', Black resigns.'} (65. Kg5 {Bobby Fischer: 'After'} Kd7 66. Kf6 Ne8+ 67. Bxe8+ $18 {Bobby Fischer: 'leads to an elementary win.'}) 1-0

