{R.Scherbakov: 'Black was accurate in the opening and White was unable to obtain any serious pressure. At some point he could even have faced some problems but Black was rather peaceful and after some manoeuvres the game ended with a most likely result.'} 1. c4 e6 2. Nf3 d5 3. d4 Nf6 4. Nc3 Be7 5. Bg5 h6 6. Bh4 O-O 7. e3 Nbd7 (7... b6 {leads to the Tartakower System.}) 8. Rc1 c6 9. Bd3 dxc4 10. Bxc4 b5 {R.Scherbakov: '!?'} (10... Nd5 11. Bxe7 (11. Bg3 $14) 11... Qxe7 12. Ne4 $14 {Timman} (12. O-O $14)) 11. Bd3 a6 12. a4 {Gligoric,Svetozar: '!' R.Scherbakov: 'ChessBase: 'Gligoric,Svetozar: '!'''} (12. e4 Nxe4 13. Bxe4 Bxh4 14. Bxc6 Ra7 15. O-O Nb6 $15 {Euwe-Aljechin/wm 1935/}) (12. O-O c5 $1 (12... Bb7 $2 13. Bxf6 Nxf6 14. Ne4 $16) 13. a4 b4 14. Ne4 cxd4 $10 {Timman}) (12. Bb1 c5 13. dxc5 Nxc5 14. Qc2 Re8 15. Bxf6 Bxf6 16. Qh7+ Kf8 $10 {Timman}) 12... bxa4 {Gligoric,Svetozar: '!' R.Scherbakov: 'ChessBase: 'Gligoric,Svetozar: '!'''} (12... b4 {Gligoric,Svetozar: '?'} 13. Bxf6 {Gligoric,Svetozar: '!' Gligoric,Svetozar: ' e4!' R.Scherbakov: 'Gligoric,Svetozar: '!' Gligoric,Svetozar: ' Ne4!''} (13. Ne4 Nxe4 14. Bxe7 Nxf2 15. Bxd8 Nxd1 16. Kxd1 Rxd8 {Capablanca-Rossolimo} 17. Be4 $1 $10 {Timman}) 13... gxf6 $1 $10 {Timman}) 13. Nxa4 Qa5+ 14. Nd2 Bb4 (14... Bb7 15. O-O Rac8 $2 16. Ne4 {/+- Taimanov-Jimenez/Palma de Mallorca/1970/}) 15. Nc3 c5 16. Nb3 (16. Nc4 Qc7 17. Bg3 Qb7 18. O-O cxd4 19. exd4 Rd8 20. Na4 Nd5 $14 {Fine-Belawenez/Moskau/1937/}) 16... Qd8 (16... Qb6 17. dxc5 Bxc5 18. Nxc5 Qxc5 19. O-O Bb7 $14 {Timman}) 17. O-O cxd4 (17... Bb7 18. Be4 cxd4 19. Qxd4 {Timman}) 18. Nxd4 Bb7 19. Be4 $1 {Timman Gligoric,Svetozar: '!' R.Scherbakov: 'ChessBase: '!' ChessBase: 'Timman Gligoric,Svetozar: '!'''} Qb8 $8 {Gligoric,Svetozar: '!' R.Scherbakov: 'ChessBase: '' ChessBase: 'Gligoric,Svetozar: '!'''} ({R.Scherbakov: 'The more risky'} 19... Qb6 {Gligoric,Svetozar: '?' R.Scherbakov: '!?' R.Scherbakov: 'is considered in the game Kharitonov - Nenashev/Omsk 1985. ChessBase: 'Gligoric,Svetozar: '?'''} 20. Na4 Qa7 21. Rc7 $18 {Timman}) 20. Bg3 {?!} (20. Nc6 {R.Scherbakov: '!' R.Scherbakov: 'is probably more promising - see the game Kamsky - Salov/Candidates (m/3) 1995.'} Bxc6 21. Bxc6 Ra7 22. Bg3 Qb6 $2 (22... Qd8 23. Bd6 Bxd6 24. Qxd6 $16 {Timman}) (22... Ne5 23. Qd4 {!} (23. Qe2 Bd6 $13 {! G.Agzamov - T.Georgadze, Tashkent 1984}) (23. Ne4 Be7 24. Qd4 (24. Qe2 {!?}) 24... Nxc6 25. Rxc6 Qb5 {!} 26. Qxa7 (26. Rxe6 Rd7) 26... Qxc6 {= G.Agzamov}) 23... Bd6 24. Ne4 {!} (24. Rfd1 {?!} Bc7 {= Pinter - Martin, Linz 1984}) 24... Nxc6 (24... Nxe4 25. Bxe4 Rd8 26. Rcd1 (26. Rfd1 Rad7 27. Bxe5 $16 {Matanovic}) 26... Rad7 27. Qa4 Ng4 28. Bf3 Nf6 29. Bc6 Bxg3 30. Bxd7 Bxh2+ 31. Kh1 Be5 32. Bc6 Rxd1 33. Rxd1 Qxb2 34. Kg1 $16 {Morovic - Illescas Cordoba, Spain (team ch) Mondariz 1995}) 25. Nxf6+ gxf6 26. Rxc6 Be5 27. Qg4+ {! Polugaevsky} (27. Bxe5 fxe5 28. Qh4 Kh7 29. Qe4+ Kg7 30. f4 exf4 31. Rxf4 Qxb2 $14 {T.Georgadze}) 27... Kh7 28. Qe4+ Kg7 29. f4 $16 {Kamsky - V.Salov, Sanghi Nagar (m/3) 1995}) 23. Na4 Qa5 24. Qd4 $1 $18 {Polugajevsky}) 20... Qa7 21. Nc6 $1 {R.Scherbakov: 'ChessBase: '!''} Bxc6 22. Bxc6 {R.Scherbakov: 'White has a pair of bishops but the ending is not yet on the board. Besides, a pair of Q-side pawns might be exchanged.'} Rac8 { 23... c5 Timman R.Scherbakov: 'ChessBase: ' 23... c5 Timman''} 23. Na4 {R.Scherbakov: 'Otherwise Black was fine after ...Nd7-c5, when he had slightly more active rooks and minor pieces.'} (23. Ne4 {Polugaevsky}) 23... Rfd8 (23... Nc5 {?!} 24. Nxc5 Rxc6 {?} 25. Ne4 {!} Rxc1 26. Nxf6+ gxf6 27. Qxc1 $16 {Krogius}) 24. Bf3 (24. Qe2 Nc5 {Timman}) (24. Qf3) 24... a5 $1 {Timman R.Scherbakov: 'Securing a solid position - it is very difficult for White to give his opponent any problems. ChessBase: '!' ChessBase: 'Timman'' ! =} 25. Rc6 {R.Scherbakov: 'This is harmless for Black.'} ({R.Scherbakov: 'White could have chosen between'} 25. Qe2 $142 {Purdy R.Scherbakov: 'ChessBase: '' ChessBase: 'Purdy'' Polugaevsky} Nb6 {/= Timman}) ({or} 25. Qb3 {, keeping a symbolic edge after the possible} Nc5 26. Nxc5 Rxc5 27. Rfd1) (25. Rxc8 Rxc8 26. Qe2 {Smyslov}) 25... Rxc6 26. Bxc6 Rc8 {Gligoric,Svetozar: '' R.Scherbakov: 'ChessBase: 'Gligoric,Svetozar: ''''} (26... Qa6 $5 {was also good.}) 27. Bf3 (27. Bb5 $5 {was worthy of consideration.}) 27... Qa6 {Gligoric,Svetozar: '!' R.Scherbakov: 'ChessBase: 'Gligoric,Svetozar: '!'''} 28. h3 Qb5 29. Be2 {=} Qc6 30. Bf3 Qb5 {R.Scherbakov: 'Black is just fine - he has no problems and White's bishops are rather passive.'} 31. b3 {R.Scherbakov: 'White avoids the repetition but he has no real chances to get an advantage and may only bring problems.' ?!} Be7 {!} 32. Be2 Qb4 33. Ba6 Rc6 34. Bd3 (34. Bc4 {seemed more accurate.}) 34... Nc5 {Gligoric,Svetozar: '!' R.Scherbakov: 'ChessBase: 'Gligoric,Svetozar: '!'''} ({After} 34... Bd6 $1 {it was already Black who would be hoping for a slight edge. !?} 35. Qf3 Rc8 {Smyslov}) 35. Qf3 {Gligoric,Svetozar: '!' R.Scherbakov: '?!' R.Scherbakov: 'ChessBase: 'Gligoric,Svetozar: '!'''} ({It was time to play safe chess:} 35. Nxc5 Rxc5 36. Qf3 $5 {although Black still had some pressure after} Nd5) 35... Rc8 {R.Scherbakov: '?!' R.Scherbakov: 'Missing a chance to get the advantage.'} (35... Nce4 $1 {!? Krogius} 36. Be5 Rc8 {R.Scherbakov: 'was stronger with pressure on White's Q-side.'} 37. Bxf6 Nxf6 38. Rb1 $10 {Timman}) (35... Nd5 {! Polugaevsky}) 36. Nxc5 (36. Rc1 Qd2 $1 37. Rxc5 Rxc5 38. Qa8+ Bf8 39. Nxc5 (39. Bd6 Rc1+ 40. Kh2 Qxd3) 39... Qc1+) 36... Bxc5 (36... Rxc5 {?} 37. Qa8+ Bf8 38. Bd6) (36... Qxc5 {?!} 37. Qb7) 37. Rc1 {R.Scherbakov: 'Now White is OK.'} Rd8 ({R.Scherbakov: 'Surely not'} 37... Qxb3 {R.Scherbakov: '??'} 38. Rxc5 Rxc5 39. Qa8+ $18 {Purdy R.Scherbakov: 'ChessBase: 'Purdy''}) 38. Bc4 Qd2 39. Rf1 Bb4 (39... Qd7 $10 {Polugajevsky = Polugaevsky}) 40. Bc7 Rd7 41. Qc6 {Abgabezug  42.e4, 43.e5 Gligoric,Svetozar: '[ e4]' R.Scherbakov: 'ChessBase: 'Abgabezug  42.e4, 43.e5 Gligoric,Svetozar: '[ e