{Bobby Fischer: 'GAME N. 17 A very near miss. This is one of the four games that Fischer lost to Tal who, in winning this tournament, earned the right to meet and trounce Botvinnik for the world championship. In jest the whimsical Tal signed Fischer's name, in addition to his own, when asked for an autograph. "Why not?" he quipped; "I've beaten Bobby so often ... that gives me the right to sign for him!" A careful reading of Fischer's notes will reveal a clear echo of the strong emotions that engulfed him during this tense encounter. He misses a win in the opening and several draws along the way, demonstrating dramatically how a continuously advantageous position can abruptly be turned into defeat by seemingly insignificant miscalculations. '} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 a6 6. Bc4 e6 7. Bb3 ({Bobby Fischer: 'I had no better luck against Blackstone, in an exhibition game at Davis, California, 1964, with'} 7. O-O Be7 8. Bb3 Qc7 9. f4 b5 10. f5 b4 11. fxe6 $5 (11. Nce2 e5 12. Nf3 Bb7 $19 {Bobby Fischer: 'is bad for White)'}) 11... bxc3 12. exf7+ Kf8 13. Bg5 Ng4 $1 $19 {Fischer,R-Blackstone,J Davis sim 1964 Bobby Fischer: '! and Black should win. Fischer,R-Blackstone,J Davis sim 1964'}) 7... b5 $1 ({Bobby Fischer: 'This reaction must be prompt! In our first lap game here Tal played the weaker'} 7... Be7 $2 8. f4 O-O {Bobby Fischer: '(for 8 ... b5 see the note to Black's 8th move)'} 9. Qf3 Qc7 {Bobby Fischer: 'and now'} 10. f5 $1 ({Bobby Fischer: 'instead of'} 10. O-O $2 b5 11. f5 b4 $1 12. Na4 e5 13. Ne2 Bb7 $17 {Bobby Fischer: 'and Black stands better)'}) 10... e5 ({Bobby Fischer: 'not'} 10... Nc6 11. Be3 {Bobby Fischer: 'with a bind'}) 11. Nde2 b5 12. a3 Bb7 13. g4 $40 {Bobby Fischer: 'with a strong attack.'}) 8. f4 $5 ({Bobby Fischer: 'R.Byme-Evans, US Championship 1967 went'} 8. Qf3 {Bobby Fischer: 'but White got nothing after'} Bb7 9. Bg5 b4 10. Na4 Nbd7 11. O-O Qa5 12. Bxf6 Nxf6 13. Rfe1 Be7 $10 {Byrne,R-Evans,L ch-USA 1967 Bobby Fischer: '=' Bobby Fischer: 'Byrne, R-Evans,L ch-USA 1967'}) ({Against Olafsson, at Buenos Aires 1960, I continued} 8. O-O Be7 ({if} 8... b4 9. Na4 Nxe4 (9... Bd7 10. Re1 Be7 11. a3 (11. f4) 11... a5 12. axb4 axb4 13. Bd2 Na6 14. c3 $146 (14. Qe2) 14... bxc3 15. Bxc3 (15. Nxc3 $5 $11) 15... O-O 16. Qe2 Qb8 $1 17. Bc4 Nb4 $1 {#5E#CDa4} 18. Bb5 (18. b3 d5 $1 $36) 18... Bxb5 19. Nxb5 Nc2 $1 20. Qxc2 (20. e5 Nxa1 $5 (20... dxe5 21. Bxe5 Qb7 22. Qxc2 (22. Bxf6 $2 Nxe1 $1 $19) 22... Qxb5 $11) 21. exf6 Rxa4 22. fxe7 Re8 $17) 20... Qxb5 21. Bd2 Rab8 22. Bc1 Rfc8 23. Nc3 Qb7 $15 {Ardeleanu,A (2420)-Rodriguez,A (2495) Ubeda 71/247 1998 [Rodriguez,Am]}) 10. Re1 Nf6 11. Bg5 $40 {with attack}) 9. Qf3 $5 Qc7 ({NOT} 9... Bb7 $2 10. Bxe6 $1) 10. Qg3 b4 11. Nce2 g6 12. a3 $2 (12. Bh6 $1 {is very strong)}) 12... Nxe4 13. Qe3 Nf6 14. axb4 O-O $13 {with a double-edged position. Fischer,R-Olafsson, F Buenos Aires 1960 Fischer,R-Olafsson,F Buenos Aires 1960}) (8. Bg5 {- 71/(247)}) 8... b4 $1 9. Na4 Nxe4 ({Bobby Fischer: 'is also playable'} 9... Bb7) 10. O-O g6 $2 ({Bobby Fischer: 'Correct is'} 10... Bb7 $142 {Bobby Fischer: '>='}) 11. f5 $1 gxf5 ({Bobby Fischer: 'Not'} 11... exf5 12. Bd5 Ra7 13. Nxf5 $1 gxf5 14. Qd4 $18) 12. Nxf5 Rg8 ({Bobby Fischer: 'Woozy, Tal stumbles into a dubious defense. Better is'} 12... d5 $142 13. Nh6 Bxh6 14. Bxh6) ({Bobby Fischer: 'not'} 12... exf5 $2 13. Qd5 Ra7 14. Qd4 $18 {Bobby Fischer: 'spearing a rook'}) 13. Bd5 $1 Ra7 (13... exd5 14. Qxd5 Bxf5 15. Rxf5 Ra7 16. Qxe4+ Re7 17. Qxb4 Re2 18. Bg5 $1 Rxg5 19. Rxg5 Qxg5 20. Qxb8+ $18 {Panov,V Bobby Fischer: 'wins. Panov,V'}) 14. Bxe4 $2 ({Bobby Fischer: 'correct is'} 14. Be3 $142 $1 {Bobby Fischer: '!' Bobby Fischer: '>='} Nc5 15. Qh5 $1 Rg6 (15... Nxa4 16. Bxa7 exd5 17. Rae1+) 16. Rae1 $1 $40 {Bobby Fischer: 'and White's every piece is bearing down on Black's King (KEVITZ).'}) 14... exf5 15. Bxf5 ({Bobby Fischer: 'Probably it's better to avoid exchanges with'} 15. Bd5) ({Bobby Fischer: 'or'} 15. Bf3) 15... Re7 $1 16. Bxc8 Qxc8 17. Bf4 $2 ({Bobby Fischer: 'The right move is simply'} 17. c3 $1 Qc6 18. Rf2 $16) ({Bobby Fischer: 'not'} 17. Qxd6 $2 Rxg2+ 18. Kxg2 Re2+ 19. Kf3 Bxd6 20. Kxe2 Qxc2+ $19 {Bobby Fischer: 'wins. if 17 ...Qc6 18 Rf2.'}) 17... Qc6 $1 18. Qf3 Qxa4 $1 ({Bobby Fischer: 'Such a surprise that I didn't dare believe my eyes! 1 had expected'} 18... Qxf3 19. Rxf3 Re2 20. Rf2 Rxf2 21. Kxf2 $14 {Bobby Fischer: 'l and White has a slight edge after a3 because of Black's disconnected Pawns.'}) 19. Bxd6 Qc6 $1 20. Bxb8 Qb6+ ({Bobby Fischer: 'White remains a clear Pawn ahead after 20 ..'} 20... Qxf3 21. Rxf3 Bg7 22. c3 $16) 21. Kh1 Qxb8 22. Qc6+ ({Bobby Fischer: 'Many annotators believed that'} 22. Rae1 {Bobby Fischer: 'was the winning move. Tal himself confessed he thought Black was lost after that. But 22 .'} Kd8 $1 ({Bobby Fischer: 'holds all lines'} 22... Rg6 $2 23. Qxf7+ Kd7 24. Rd1+ $1 Rd6 25. Rxd6+ Kxd6 26. Rf6+ $18 {Bobby Fischer: 'wins. I've studied this position for ages, it seems, and the best I can find is'}) 23. Rd1+ Kc7 $1 (23... Kc8 $2 24. Qc6+ $18 {Bobby Fischer: 'wins'}) 24. Qf4+ (24. Rd4 Qb7 $1) 24... Kb7 25. Rd6 Qc7 26. Qxb4+ Kc8 27. Rxa6 Qb7 $1 28. Qxb7+ Kxb7 29. Raf6 Rg7 $10 {Bobby Fischer: '='}) 22... Rd7 23. Rae1+ ({Bobby Fischer: 'Black holds after'} 23. Rad1 Bd6 24. Rxf7 ({Bobby Fischer: 'if'} 24. Rf6 Rg6 25. Rdxd6 $2 Qxd6 $1) 24... Qc7 {Bobby Fischer: 'etc.'}) ({Bobby Fischer: 'and on'} 23. Rxf7 Qd6) 23... Be7 ({Bobby Fischer: 'Finally Tal "develops" his Bishop. Not'} 23... Kd8 24. Rxf7 $1 Be7 25. Rfxe7 Rxe7 26. Rd1+ $18 {Bobby Fischer: 'wins.'}) 24. Rxf7 Kxf7 25. Qe6+ Kf8 $1 (25... Kg7 26. Qxd7 $18) 26. Qxd7 ({Bobby Fischer: 'not'} 26. Rf1+ Kg7 27. Rf7+ Kh8 28. Qxd7 Rd8 29. Qg4 Qe5 $19 {Bobby Fischer: 'wins.'}) 26... Qd6 27. Qb7 Rg6 28. c3 $1 a5 ({Bobby Fischer: 'on'} 28... bxc3 29. Qc8+ Bd8 30. Qxc3 $10 {Bobby Fischer: '='}) 29. Qc8+ ({Bobby Fischer: 'On the wrong track. Right is'} 29. cxb4 $1 Qxb4 ({Bobby Fischer: 'if'} 29... axb4 30. a3 $1 bxa3 31. bxa3 Qxa3 $10 {Bobby Fischer: '=' Bobby Fischer: 'draws'}) 30. Qf3+ Kg7 31. Qe2 $146 {Bobby Fischer: 'draws, since Black can't possibly build up a winning K-side attack and his own King is too exposed.'}) 29... Kg7 30. Qc4 Bd8 31. cxb4 axb4 ({Bobby Fischer: 'on'} 31... Qxb4 32. Qe2 $10 {Bobby Fischer: '=' Bobby Fischer: 'White should draw with best play.'}) 32. g3 $2 ({Bobby Fischer: 'Creating losing chances. I don't see how Black can make any progress after'} 32. Qe4 $142 Bc7 33. Qe7+ Kg8 34. Qe8+ Qf8 35. Qe4 $10 {Bobby Fischer: '=' Bobby Fischer: 'etc'}) 32... Qc6+ 33. Re4 Qxc4 34. Rxc4 Rb6 $1 ({Bobby Fischer: 'I overlooked this. Now Black has winning chances. I had planned on a draw after'} 34... Be7 $2 35. a3 {Bobby Fischer: 'dissolving Black's b-Pawn'} b3 {Bobby Fischer: 'is answered by'} 36. Rc7 {Bobby Fischer: 'followed by'} Re6 37. Rb7) 35. Kg2 Kf6 36. Kf3 Ke5 37. Ke3 (37. a3 {Bobby Fischer: 'is met, as always, by ..'} b3 $1 {Bobby Fischer: 'Once White can eliminate Black's b-Pawn it's a theoretical draw.'} (37... bxa3 $2 38. bxa3 $10 {Bobby Fischer: '='})) 37... Bg5+ 38. Ke2 Kd5 39. Kd3 Bf6 40. Rc2 $2 ({Bobby Fischer: 'Too passive. I wanted to avoid ilnmobilizing my Q-side Pawns with'} 40. b3 $142 {Bobby Fischer: 'but it's the best hope now. On'} Be7 41. Rd4+ $17 {Bobby Fischer: 'preserves drawing chances.'}) 40... Be5 41. Re2 Rf6 42. Rc2 Rf3+ 43. Ke2 Rf7 44. Kd3 Bd4 $1 45. a3 ({Bobby Fischer: 'on'} 45. b3 Rf3+ 46. Ke2 Rf2+ 47. Kd3 Rxc2 48. Kxc2 Ke4 $19 {Bobby Fischer: 'wins.'}) 45... b3 46. Rc8 ({Bobby Fischer: 'Equally hopeless is'} 46. Re2 Rf3+ 47. Kd2 Bxb2 $19 {Bobby Fischer: 'etc'}) (46. Rd2 Rf3+ 47. Ke2 Rf2+ $19) 46... Bxb2 47. Rd8+ Kc6 48. Rb8 Rf3+ 49. Kc4 Rc3+ 50. Kb4 Kc7 (50... Ba1 51. a4 b2 $1 {0-1 (51) Fischer,R-Tal,M Bled/Zagreb/Belgrade 1959 My 60 Memorable Games [Bobby Fischer]} (51... b2 $1 52. Kxc3 b1=Q+ $1 {[%emt 0:00:31] If 53 Kxc3 b1=Q+! The discovered-check theme is strangely reminiscent of the finale of game})) 51. Rb5 Ba1 52. a4 b2 $1 