{GAME N. 16 Four Queens. Fischer extracted a slight minus score from the seven games in which he was called upon to face the Caro-Kann, prompting Botvinnik to note: "Fischer's both strong and weak point lies in that he is always true to himself and plays the same way regardless of his partners or any external factor. " This variation is not only complex and critical - but perilous. After a single slip the edge passes to Black. But Petrosian overestimates his position and, somewhat recklessly, dissipates his advantage. In timepressure he misses a forced draw and Fischer regains the upper hand. From this point on, with four marauding Queens roaming the board, the play becomes "rich and strange" - resulting in a tortuous draw.  Bulletin: 'ChessCalisthenics: 'B11: Caro-Kann: Two Knights Variation''} 1. e4 {Bulletin Bulletin Bulletin Bulletin Bulletin: 'ChessCalisthenics Fischer, Ragozin'} c6 2. Nc3 d5 3. Nf3 Bg4 ({The purpose of this line is to exclude the possibility of ...Bf5. For example,} 3... dxe4 4. Nxe4 Bf5 $2 5. Ng3 Bg6 ({if} 5... Bg4 6. h3) 6. h4 h6 7. Ne5 Bh7 8. Qh5 g6 9. Bc4 $1 e6 10. Qe2 $16 {(threatening Nxf7) and Black has a terrible game.}) (3... Nf6 4. e5 Ne4 5. Ne2 $1 Qb6 6. d4 c5 7. dxc5 Qxc5 8. Ned4 Nc6 9. Bb5 a6 10. Bxc6+ bxc6 11. O-O Qb6 12. e6 $1 fxe6 13. Bf4 $16 {4 is good for White. Fischer,R-Olafsson,F Beograd ct 1959 1-0 Bulletin: 'Fischer,R-Olafsson,F/Belgrade ct/1959/1-0/'}) 4. h3 Bxf3 ({In our first round game here, Smyslov played} 4... Bh5 5. exd5 cxd5 6. Bb5+ Nc6 7. g4 Bg6 8. Ne5 Rc8 9. d4 e6 10. h4 {to prevent ...} ({(correct is} 10. Qe2 $1 {>= Bulletin: '!' '!' '!' '!'}) 10... f6 11. Nxg6 hxg6 12. Qd3 Kf7 13. h5 gxh5 14. gxh5 Nge7 $11 {Fischer,R-Smyslov,V Bled ct 1959 Bulletin: '=' '=' '=' '=' Bulletin: 'Fischer,R-Smyslov,V/Bled ct/1959/'}) 5. Qxf3 {Position after} Nf6 ({the old} 5... e6 6. d4 dxe4 7. Nxe4 Qxd4 8. Bd3 $146 {gives White a good attack for the Pawn. And on}) (5... dxe4 6. Nxe4 Nd7 7. Ng5 $5 ({(better is simply} 7. d4 {>= Bulletin: '' '' '' ''}) 7... Ngf6 8. Qb3 e6 9. Qxb7 Nd5 $1 $17 {Black gets good play. Fischer,R-Cardoso,R Portoroz izt 1958 Bulletin: 'Fischer,R-Cardoso,R Portoroz izt 1958'}) 6. d3 ({Inferior is} 6. d4 dxe4 7. Nxe4 $5 (7. Qe3 Nbd7 8. Nxe4 Nxe4 9. Qxe4 Nf6 10. Qd3 Qd5 $1 $11 {is equal. Fischer,R-Keres,P Bled 1961 Bulletin: '=!' '=!' '=!' '=!' Bulletin: 'Fischer,R-Keres,P Bled 1961'}) 7... Qxd4 8. Bd3 Nbd7 $17 {threatening Ne5}) ({on} 6. e5 Nfd7 7. e6 $2 ({(playable is} 7. Qg3 e6 8. Be2 {Spassky,B-Reshko,n Leningrad 1961 Bulletin: 'Spassky,B-Reshko/Leningrad/1961/'}) 7... fxe6 8. d4 e5 $1 $17) ({finally} 6. g3 dxe4 7. Nxe4 Nxe4 8. Qxe4 Qd5 $1 9. Qxd5 cxd5 10. Bg2 e6 $11 {Suetin,A Bulletin: '=' '=' '=' '='} 11. c4 Nc6 12. cxd5 Nb4 $1 {gives Black an even ending}) 6... e6 7. g3 ({A recent try is} 7. Bd2 {followed by 0-0-0. Against Larsen, at Zurich 1959, I tried}) (7. a3 Bc5 8. Be2 O-O 9. O-O Nbd7 $11 {and black got a satisfactory game. Fischer,R-Larsen,B Zürich 1959 Bulletin: '=' '=' '=' '=' Bulletin: 'Fischer,R-Larsen,B/Zuerich/1959/'}) 7... Bb4 8. Bd2 ({not} 8. Bg2 $2 d4 9. a3 Qa5 $19) 8... d4 ({Inferior is} 8... Qb6 9. O-O-O d4 10. Ne2 $16) 9. Nb1 Bxd2+ ({in this tournament Keres and Benko both tried} 9... Qb6 {forcing White to weaken the Q-side with} 10. b3 {But Black's Queen is slightly misplaced after} (10. Bg2 {(Bulletin) ChessCalisthenics} O-O 11. O-O Nbd7 12. Bc1 a5 13. Qe2 a4 14. a3 Be7 15. f4 e5 16. Nd2 Qc7 17. Nf3 c5 18. f5 Rfc8 19. g4 h6 20. g5 hxg5 21. Bxg5 c4 22. Rf2 Qb6 23. Bc1 c3 24. bxc3 Rxc3 {Paragua,M (2529)-Bologan,V (2665)/Tripolis 2004/CBM 102/0-1 (37)}) 10... Nbd7 (10... a5 {(Bulletin) ChessCalisthenics} 11. a3 Bxd2+ (11... Be7 12. Bg2 a4 13. b4 Nbd7 14. O-O c5 15. Ra2 O-O 16. bxc5 Bxc5 17. Qe2 e5 18. f4 Rfc8 19. h4 Rc6 20. Bh3 Qc7 21. fxe5 Nxe5 22. Bf4 Bd6 23. h5 Ra5 24. h6 Ng6 25. Qf3 Rh5 26. Bg4 {Fischer,R-Keres,P/Bled/ Zagreb/Belgrade 1959/Candidates/0-1}) 12. Nxd2 Qc5 13. Qd1 g5 14. Bg2 Rg8 15. O-O Nbd7 16. Nc4 Ke7 17. Qe1 Nb6 18. f4 Nxc4 19. bxc4 gxf4 20. Rxf4 Nd7 21. Qf2 Raf8 22. Rb1 b6 23. Rf1 f6 24. Rh4 {Morovic Fernandez,I (2590)-Granda Zuniga,J (2610)/Yerevan 1996/EXT 1997/1-0 (43)}) 11. Bg2 a5 12. a3 Bxd2+ ({(the retreat} 12... Be7 $6 {seems illogical- even though Keres beat me with it) Fischer, R-Keres,P Bled ct 1959 0-1 Bulletin: 'Fischer,R-Keres,P Bled ct 1959 0-1'}) 13. Nxd2 Qc5 14. Qd1 h5 15. h4 $1 $16 {with an edge. (Fischer-Benko. ) Petrosian apparently didn't want to get involved with this line despite the fact that his countryman, Tal. accused me of "bad judgment" for preferring White here. Fischer, R-Benko,P Beograd ct 1959 1-0 Bulletin: 'Fischer,R-Benko,P/Belgrade ct/1959/1-0'}) 10. Nxd2 e5 11. Bg2 c5 {Bulletin: 'ChessCalisthenics: 'N''} (11... O-O {(Bulletin) ChessCalisthenics} 12. O-O Nbd7 13. Qe2 Qe7 14. Rae1 c5 15. f4 Rac8 16. Bf3 Qe6 17. Bg4 Nxg4 18. hxg4 b5 19. b3 f6 20. Kg2 Nb6 21. fxe5 fxe5 22. Rxf8+ Rxf8 23. g5 Rc8 24. Rb1 a6 25. Qh5 c4 26. bxc4 {Bolbochan,J-Van Scheltinga,T/Dubrovnik 1950/MCD/1/2-1/2}) 12. O-O Nc6 {Position after} 13. Qe2 Qe7 ({The critical juncture. In our earlier game (round two) Petros ian continued with} 13... g5 14. Nf3 $2 ({(Simagin gives} 14. f4 gxf4 15. gxf4 Qe7 16. Nc4 Nd7 17. Qg4 {+/-; ·'with advantage" but after Smagin,V Bulletin: '; Smagin,V'} O-O-O 18. fxe5 Kb8 $15 {Black succeeds in planting his Knight on e5 where it cannot be dislodged) Bulletin: '× e5'}) ({Fearing a prepared line, Petrosian deviates. On 13 ... g5 I had intended} 14. c3 $1 Qe7 15. Nf3 h6 16. cxd4 $1 exd4 (16... Nxd4 17. Nxd4 cxd4 18. Rac1) (16... cxd4 17. h4 Rg8 18. hxg5 hxg5 19. Rfc1 O-O-O 20. b4 $1 Kb8 21. b5 Na5 22. Qd2 $16 {wins a pawn.}) 17. e5 $1 O-O-O 18. Rfe1 $14 {Now the Bishop diagonal is unblocked and Black can't set up a blockade on his e5, as in our first game.}) 14... h6 15. h4 Rg8 16. a3 Qe7 17. hxg5 hxg5 18. Qd2 Nd7 19. c3 O-O-O 20. cxd4 exd4 $17 {with advantage for black. Fischer, R-Petrosian,T Bled ct 1959 0-1 Bulletin: 'Fischer,R-Petrosian,T Bled ct 1959 0-1'}) ({After} 13... O-O 14. f4 Kh8 15. f5 Ng8 16. g4 $36 f6 {White has a tough nut to crack, but his initiative is permanent. The text indicates Petrosian's intention to castle long without trying to prevent f4.}) 14. f4 O-O-O 15. a3 Ne8 ({Also playable is} 15... Nd7 16. b4 f6 {and if} 17. Nc4 b5) 16. b4 {Position after} cxb4 ({Wide open! Safer is} 16... f6 17. b5 (17. bxc5 Qxc5 18. fxe5 Nxe5) 17... Na5 18. Nb3 Nxb3 19. cxb3 Kb8 20. a4 $11 {Bulletin: '=' '=' '=' '='}) 17. Nc4 $2 ({Now Black has time to consolidate. Correct is} 17. fxe5 $1 {with advantage in all variations:} Qxe5 (17... bxa3 18. Nc4 Rf8 19. Rxa3 $16 b5 20. Qg4+ $1) (17... Nxe5 18. axb4 Kb8 19. Nf3 f6 20. Qf2 $1 Nxf3+ {penetrates)} (20... Qxb4 21. Nxe5 fxe5 22. Qf7) 21. Qxf3 Nd6 (21... Qxb4 22. e5 $1) 22. Ra5 a6 23. Qf4 Rhe8 24. Rd5 $16) (17... Kb8 18. axb4 Nxb4 (18... Nxe5 19. Nf3 {transposes to (c)}) 19. Nc4 Nc6 (19... Nc7 20. Nd6 $1 Rhf8 21. Rfb1 Nca6 22. Qd2 Qxe5 23. Nxb7 $1 Kxb7 24. Rxa6 $1 $18 {wins}) 20. Qf3 Rf8 21. e6 $1 Qxe6 22. e5 $1 $18 {followed by Rfb1 and White has a winning attack. Bulletin: ' fb1 '}) 18. Rxf7 Qxg3 19. e5 $1 Qe3+ 20. Qxe3 dxe3 21. Nc4 $16) 17... f6 $1 ({I had expected} 17... bxa3 18. fxe5 {transposing to "b" above.}) 18. fxe5 fxe5 19. axb4 Nc7 {Black wants to secure a Q-side blockade. The b-Pawn won't run away.} (19... Qxb4 $5 {(Bulletin) Ragozin}) 20. Na5 Nb5 $1 $17 {I already knew I'd been outplayed. Petros ian didn't even consider 20 Nxb4, opening up the lines.} (20... Nxb4 {(Bulletin) Ragozin} 21. Rfb1 Nca6 22. Qd2 b6 23. Nc4 $40) 21. Nxc6 bxc6 22. Rf2 g6 ({on} 22... Qxb4 23. Qg4+ Rd7 24. Rf7 Rhd8 25. Qxg7 {regains the pawn}) (22... Rhf8 $142 {(Bulletin) Ragozin}) 23. h4 Kb7 ({Ordinarily one would expect Petrosian to simplify and simplify in order to reach a winning ending. 23 ... Rhf8! is strong.} 23... Rhf8 $1) 24. h5 Qxb4 ({Really risky! I was amazed he was allowing so much counterplay. 24 ...Rhf8 is still right. On} 24... Rhf8 $1) (24... gxh5 25. Qxh5 Rhf8 26. Rf5 $1) 25. Rf7+ Kb6 ({on} 25... Kb8 26. Qf2 Rhf8 27. c4 $1 Nc7 (27... dxc3 $2 28. Raxa7 Rxf7 29. Qb6+ $18) 28. Qf6 $16 {with good play}) 26. Qf2 $1 a5 ({not} 26... Rhf8 27. c4 $1 Nc3 28. Raxa7 $18 {wins.}) (26... Qc5 {(Bulletin) Ragozin} 27. c4 dxc3 $2 28. Ra6+ $1) (26... Qc3 {(Bulletin) Ragozin} 27. Ra4) 27. c4 {Position after} Nc3 ({Continuing to underestimate the danger. Safer is} 27... Nd6 {>= Bulletin: '' '' '' ''}) 28. Rf1 $2 ({Why didn't I play} 28. Qf6 $1 {immediately? If then} Rdf8 (28... Rhf8 29. Rf1 $1 Rxf7 30. Qxd8+ $1 Rc7 31. Rf7 $18 {wins.}) (28... Qc5 29. Qg7 $1 Ka6 (29... a4 30. Ra7 $1) (29... Ra8 30. Rb7+ Ka6 31. Qc7 Rhc8 32. Rb5 $1 $18) (29... Rdg8 30. Rb7+ Ka6 31. Qc7 Rc8 32. Rxa5+ $1 $18) 30. Ra7+ $1 Qxa7 31. Rxa5+ Kxa5 32. Qxa7+ Kb4 33. Qb6+ Ka3 34. c5 $36 {and White's c-Pawn is dangerous.}) (28... Qd6 {(Bulletin) Ragozin} 29. Qg7 Rdg8 $2 30. Rb7+ Kc5 31. Rxa5+ $18) 29. Qxe5 Rxf7 30. Qxh8 Qc5 31. e5 $16 {- it's difficult for Black in view of his exposed King and White's passed e-Pawn.}) 28... a4 {Still playing with reckless abandon! Safer is 28 ..... Qd6 to prevent Qf6.} (28... Qd6 {/\ Bulletin: '' '' '' ''}) 29. Qf6 Qc5 (29... Qd6 $142 $1 {(Bulletin) Ragozin} 30. Qg7 Rdg8 $1 31. Rb7+ Kc5 32. Qf7 Rf8 33. Qg7 Rhg8 34. Qxh7 Rh8 35. Qxg6 Qxg6 36. hxg6 Ne2#) 30. Rxh7 $1 ({Now I decided to start playing for the win. On} 30. Qg7 Rdg8 $1 31. Rb7+ Ka6 32. Qc7 Rc8 33. Qg7 Rcg8 $11 {draws by a "perpetual check" on the Queen. Bulletin: '=' '=' '=' '='}) (30. hxg6 $143 {(Bulletin) ChessCalisthenics} hxg6 31. Qg7 Rdg8 32. Rb7+ Ka6 $15) 30... Rdf8 $1 {Forcing what looks like a favorable ending} 31. Qxg6 Rxf1+ (31... Rxh7 $1 {(Bulletin) Ragozin} 32. Qxh7 a3 $1 (32... Rxf1+ {game}) 33. Qg7 Ne2+ 34. Kh2 Rxf1 35. Bxf1 a2 36. Qg8 a1=Q 37. Qb8+ $10) 32. Bxf1 Rxh7 33. Qxh7 a3 {Petrosian had been banking on the speed of this Pawn.} 34. h6 a2 35. Qg8 a1=Q 36. h7 {Position after} Qd6 $2 ({In time-pressure, Petrosian overlooks} 36... Ne2+ {Bulletin: '!' '!' '!' '!'} 37. Kf2 Nxg3 $1 {and White has nothing better than to take a perpetual with} 38. Qb8+ $11 {Bulletin: '=' '=' '=' '='}) 37. h8=Q Qa7 (37... Qe1 $5 $11 {(Bulletin) ChessCalisthenics}) 38. g4 Kc5 $1 {A good last-ditch try. Curiously, the King will be safer in White's territory where it obtains shelter from the cluster of Pawns.} 39. Qf8 $2 {wins the e-Pawn. Finally on Forced, to defend against the threat of' Qxe5+. Not} ({right is} 39. Qh2 $1 {immediately, preventing Black's King from reaching safety behind the lines. If then Bulletin: '!' '!' '!' '!'} Qf6 (39... Qa1 40. Qg7) (39... Qa2 $2 40. Qxa2 Nxa2 41. Qa8 $1 $18) (39... Qae7 40. Qa8 $40) 40. g5 {or}) 39... Qae7 $8 {Bulletin: '!' '!' '!' '!'} (39... Qxf8 40. Qxf8+ Kb6 41. Qb4+ Ka6 (41... Kc7 42. Qe7+) 42. Qa3+ Kb7 43. Qxa7+ Kxa7 44. g5 $18 {and queens}) 40. Qa8 {I thought this was it! The two Queens are closing in for the kill.} Kb4 $1 41. Qh2 {Position after} Kb3 $1 {Slippery as an eel!} 42. Qa1 {After the game a kibitzer asked Petrosian if he thought 42 c5 would have won for White. Petrosian, who must have analyzed it for many hours (not knowing, of course, what my sealed move was), simply replied: "I don't know."} ({Now White sealed. It's fantastically complicated! The tournament bulletins suggest} 42. c5 Qxc5 (42... Qg6 43. Be2 $1 Qgg5 44. Bd1+ $1) 43. Qg8+ Ka3 44. Qc2 Qb4 45. Qa8+ Qa4 ({not} 45... Na4 $2 46. Qc1+ Ka2 47. Qg8+ Qb3 48. Qc2+ $1 $19) 46. Qcxa4+ Nxa4 47. Qxc6 {"with good winning chances, " but after Bulletin: '' '' '' '' Bulletin: 'Ragozin'} Nc3 $14 {it's likely Black can draw. Bulletin: '=!' '=!' '=!' '=!' Bulletin: 'Fischer'}) 42... Qa3 {The only move to stop mate on b2.} 43. Qxa3+ Kxa3 44. Qh6 {Now White has to try to make do with the g-Pawn. Bulletin: 'g4-g5-g6-g7-g8'} Qf7 $1 45. Kg2 ({on} 45. Qxc6 Nd1 $1) 45... Kb3 {Bulletin: 'd1'} ({not} 45... Nd1 46. Qc1+ Nb2 {and the Knight is stranded out-of-play. The text renews the threat of ..Nd1. Bulletin: '+-' '+-' '+-' '+-'}) 46. Qd2 Qh7 $1 47. Kg3 {A gross oversight, but probably best anyway! White can't wIn anymore. If 47 g5 Qh4, etc. Position after Bulletin: '"An gross oversight, but probably best anyway." Fischer'} (47. g5 Qh4 $44) (47. Be2 $142 $5 $14 {(Bulletin) ChessCalisthenics}) 47... Qxe4 $1 {Bulletin: 'ChessCalisthenics: '''} 48. Qf2 $2 ({Having overlooked Petrosian's last move, I was somewhat shaken! Not} 48. dxe4 $2 Nxe4+ 49. Kh4 (49. Kh3 {(Bulletin) ChessCalisthenics} Nxd2 $19) 49... Nxd2 50. g5 Nxf1 51. g6 d3 $19 {wins. Also on}) (48. Qd1+ $2 Nxd1 49. dxe4 Ne3 50. Be2 Nxc4 51. g5 Nd6 52. g6 Ne8 $19 {and Black again wins. The right retort, however, is 48 g5! and it's still a hard fight.}) (48. Qxc3+ $2 dxc3 49. dxe4 c2 $19 {wins.}) (48. g5 $1 $13 {Bulletin: '!' '!' '!' '!'}) 48... Qh1 $1 $17 {Bulletin: 'Petrosian accepted the offered draw. "After having fought so hard for the draw, however, Petrosian was obviously unprepared to readjust his frame of mind and start playsing for a win." Fischer'} (48... Qh1 $1 {I offered a draw, afraid that he wouldn't accept. Black certainly has the edge now. If} 49. g5 {e4! OR IF} (49. Bg2 Qh6 $17 {After having fought so hard for the draw, however, Petrosian was obviously unprepared to readjust his frame of mind and start playing for a win. So ...}) 49... e4 $1 $17 {DRAW}) 1/2-1/2

