'} f4 {Fritz 5.00 (5s): ''} (34... Qxc2 $142 $5 35. Bd4+ Ke6 $11) (34... g5 {Knaak,Rainer: '?' Knaak,Rainer: 'The king was forced to sidestep checks (on d4 and d8)' Knaak,Rainer: 'Der König musste den Schachs (auf d4 und d8) ausweichen.'} 35. Bb6 {Knaak,Rainer: '+-'} Qxc2 36. a5 Qb2 (36... Qa2 {Knaak,Rainer} 37. Bd4+ Ke6 38. Ra1 Qd2 39. Bg1 Qb2 40. a6 Qxa1 41. a7 $18) (36... Qd2 {Knaak,Rainer} 37. a6 Qd6 38. Bd8+ $1 Ke6 39. Bb7 $1 Qb4 40. Bxg5 $18) 37. Bd8+ Ke6 38. a6 Qa3 ({A much harder defence would have been .} 38... Qf2 $5 {Knaak,Rainer . ist weitaus zäher.} {But there is a difficult way to win convincingly: Aber es gibt einen schwierigen Pfad, der klar gewinnt:} 39. Rb1 $1 (39. Bxg5 c3 40. Ra1 $1 f4 $1 (40... c2 41. a7 c1=Q+ 42. Rxc1 Qxa7 $18) 41. Bh4 Qc5 42. Bf3 c2 43. a7 Qxa7 44. Rxa7 c1=Q+ 45. Kg2 {To win this position isn't easy at all. Diese Stellung zu gewinnen ist nicht einfach.}) 39... c3 40. Bb6 Qa2 41. Re1+ Kd6 42. Bb7 c2 43. Bg1 $1 (43. a7 $2 Qb1 $1 $11) 43... Kc7 (43... Qb1 44. Rxb1 cxb1=Q 45. Bg2 $18) 44. Re8 $1 $18) 39. Bb7 Qc5 (39... Qb2 40. Re1+ Kd6) (39... c3 40. Bb6 c2 41. a7 c1=Q 42. Rxc1 Qxc1+ 43. Bg1 {Knaak,Rainer: '+-'}) 40. Rb1 c3 41. Bb6 {1-0 (41) Fischer,R (2760)-Larsen,B (2660) Denver 1971 Candidates [ChessBase]} (41. Bb6 {Knaak,Rainer: 'It was not only inthe opening of this French Defence game that Fischer's understanding of the opening was better than Larsen's. In the further course of the game Fischer's only flaw was 21.f3, while Larsen committed several mistakes. At least this game did not suggest that another 6:0 was impossible. ' Knaak,Rainer: 'Fischers Verständnis der Eröffnung war nicht nur in diesem Franzosen dem Larsens überlegen. Im weiteren Verlauf der Partie beging Fischer nur einen Fehler (21.Lf3) während Larsen mehrere Ungenauigkeiten unterliefen. Diese Partie sprach jedenfalls nicht gegen ein weiteres 6:0.'} c2 42. Re1+ Qe5 43. Rxe5+ Kxe5 44. a7 c1=Q+ 45. Bg1)) (34... Ke6 $1 {Knaak,Rainer (34...e5 works too) (auch 34...Ke5 geht)} 35. Bb6 Qxc2 36. a5 Qa2 $11) 35. Bb6 {Fritz 5.00 (5s): '='} (35. Be4 $142 $5 $16) 35... Qxc2 36. a5 Qb2 37. Bd8+ Ke6 38. a6 Qa3 {Fritz 5.00 (5s): ''} (38... Qd4 39. Bc7 Qc5 40. Re1+ Kf7 41. Be8+ Kf8 42. Bxf4 $11) 39. Bb7 (39. Re1+ Kf5 $14) 39... Qc5 {Fritz 5.00 (5s): ''} (39... c3 {Fritz 5.00 (5s): '!?'} 40. Bb6 (40. Re1+ Kd7 41. Rd1+ Ke6 $11) 40... c2 41. a7 c1=Q 42. Rxc1 Qxc1+ 43. Bg1 $18) 40. Rb1 {Fritz 5.00 (5s): 'White threatens.... what?'} c3 {Fritz 5.00 (5s): '+-??'} (40... Qd4 41. Bb6 Qd7 $18) 41. Bb6 {[%tqu "En","","","","c3c2","",10]} c2 42. Re1+ (42. Bxc5 $4 cxb1=Q+ 43. Bg1 Qf1 $19) 42... Qe5 43. Rxe5+ Kxe5 44. a7 c1=Q+ 45. Bg1 $18 1-0

