{Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: 'GAME N. 36 Gaston and Alphonse. "I like to coax my opponents into attacking, to let them taste the joy of the initiative, so that they may get carried away, become careless, and sacrifice material," wrote Korchnoi, whose comments are interwoven in the notes. Fischer needs no coaxing. He improves on a well-known Capablanca line (with 15.d5). Still, the advantage he derives, if any, is microscopic. Korchnoi seems to labor under the delusion that he has the worst of it, though Fischer keeps asserting that White has nothing. Nevertheless, he overreaches himself, giving Korchnoi a chance to assume the initiative. But Black falters and then cracks under the pressure of the clock. ''} 1. e4 {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer'} e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Ba4 Nf6 5. O-O Be7 6. Re1 b5 7. Bb3 O-O 8. c3 d6 9. d4 {Yates,F; Alekhine,A Yates,F; Alekhine,A Ernst: 'Yates,F; Alekhine,A Bobby Fischer: ', An old try, championed by Yates and Alekhine, but discarded in the course of progress. It is still theoretically crucial - on its success (or failure) hinges the necessity of White's losing a tempo here with the customary 9 h3. ''} (9. h3) 9... Bg4 10. Be3 exd4 ({Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Gligorich's''} 10... d5 $142 {Gligoric,S Gligoric,S Ernst: ' Gligoric,S Bobby Fischer: 'is probably best.''}) ({Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: 'On the old''} 10... Nxe4 $5 11. Bd5 Qd7 12. Bxe4 d5 13. Bxh7+ Kxh7 14. dxe5 $16 {Byrne,R Byrne,R Ernst: 'Byrne,R Bobby Fischer: 'White, according to Robert Byrne, can keep his extra Pawn and weather the attack.''}) 11. cxd4 Na5 (11... d5 12. e5 Ne4 13. Nbd2 Nxd2 14. Qxd2 Bxf3 15. gxf3 Bb4 16. Qc2 Bxe1 17. Qxc6 Bb4 18. Bxd5 $16 {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: 'is known to favor White.''}) 12. Bc2 Nc4 (12... c5 {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: 'may be better;''} 13. Nbd2 ({Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Hence''} 13. dxc5 dxc5 14. Nbd2 $14 {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: 'seems the only try for an advantage.''}) 13... cxd4 14. Bxd4 Nc6 15. Be3 d5 16. exd5 Nb4 $10 {Yates,F-Bogoljubow,E New York 1924 Yates,F-Bogoljubow,E New York 1924 Ernst: 'Yates,F-Bogoljubow,E New York 1924 Bobby Fischer: '=' Bobby Fischer: '(Yates,F-Bogoljubow,E; New York, 1924)''}) 13. Bc1 c5 14. b3 ({Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Interesting is''} 14. Nbd2 Nxd2 15. Qxd2 Bxf3 16. gxf3 {Geller,E-Panno,O Amsterdam 1956 Geller,E-Panno,O Amsterdam 1956 Ernst: 'Geller,E-Panno,O Amsterdam 1956 Bobby Fischer: '(Geller,E-Panno,O; Amsterdam, 1956)''}) 14... Na5 ({Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Korchnoi is of a mind that the retreat''} 14... Nb6 {= Kortschnoj = Kortschnoj Ernst: '= Kortschnoj Bobby Fischer: 'completely equalizes. But White can keep a pull after''} 15. Nbd2 cxd4 ({Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: 'maybe better is''} 15... Nfd7 $142 16. h3 {Bobby Fischer} Bh5 17. g4 Bg6 18. d5 Bf6 19. Rb1 h5 $1 {Pietzsch-Szabo, 1962.}) 16. h3 Bh5 17. g4 $1 Bg6 18. Nxd4 $36 {Pietzsch,W-Matanovic,A Habana 1962 Pietzsch,W-Matanovic,A Habana 1962 Ernst: 'Pietzsch,W-Matanovic,A Habana 1962 Bobby Fischer: '(Pietzsch,W-Matanovic,A; Habana, 1962)''}) 15. d5 $1 ({Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: '"A strong continuation which improves on''} 15. Bb2 Nc6 $1 16. d5 Nb4 $15 {Capablanca,J-Bogoljubow,E London 1922 Capablanca,J-Bogoljubow,E London 1922 Ernst: 'Capablanca,J-Bogoljubow,E London 1922 Bobby Fischer: '(Capablanca-Bogolyubow, London 1922) when Black gains the advantage of the pair of Bishops." (KORCHNOr.)''}) 15... Nd7 ({Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: 'On''} 15... Nxe4 16. Rxe4 Bxf3 17. Qxf3 Bf6 18. Nc3 b4 19. Bb2 bxc3 20. Bxc3 Bxc3 21. Qxc3 $16 {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: 'White has a big advantage.''}) 16. Nbd2 Bf6 {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: '; Aiming to strike on the dark squares before White can mobilize a K-side initiative. ''} 17. Rb1 c4 {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: '; Korchnoi considers this overambitious, believing that it creates too many Pawn weaknesses.''} ({Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: 'He thinks Black ought to play''} 17... Ne5 $142 {Kortschnoj} 18. h3 Nxf3+ 19. Nxf3 Bxf3 20. Qxf3 b4 {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: '; but after''} 21. Bf4 Re8 ({Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: 'too passive is''} 21... Nb7 22. Bd3 {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: 'etc.''}) 22. Qg3 Be5 23. Bxe5 Rxe5 ({Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: 'if''} 23... dxe5 24. Bd3) 24. f4 Re7 25. Rbd1 $36 { e4-e5  e4-e5 Ernst: ' e4-e5 Bobby Fischer: '(threatening e5) maintains the pressure.''}) 18. h3 ({Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: '"White does not fall for''} 18. b4 $2 c3 $1 19. bxa5 cxd2 20. Bxd2 Ne5 $44 {Kortschnoj,V Kortschnoj,V Ernst: 'Kortschnoj,V Bobby Fischer: 'when the ensuing break-up of the Pawn protection of White's King more than compensates for his extra doubled Pawn." (KORCHNOI.)''}) 18... Bxf3 ({Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: '"Giving White the two Bishops, but if''} 18... Bh5 19. b4 $1 {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: 'is now strong:''} ({Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: 'On 18 ...Bh5 I intended''} 19. g4 $1 {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: '(deadening Black's Bishop is worth this weakness).''} Bg6 20. Nf1 { g3  g3 Ernst: ' g3 Bobby Fischer: ' g3, etc. RF.''}) 19... c3 ({Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: 'In this line simply''} 19... Nb7 $142 $132 { a6-a5  a6-a5 Ernst: ' a6-a5 Bobby Fischer: 'followed by ...a5 yields good counterplay. RF''}) 20. bxa5 cxd2 21. Bxd2 Ne5 22. g4 {Korchnoi,V}) 19. Nxf3 cxb3 (19... Re8 20. b4 Nb7 21. Nd4 $16 {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: 'is strong.''}) ({Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: 'And''} 19... c3 $2 20. a3 $1 {× c3 × c3 Ernst: '× c3 Bobby Fischer: 'leaves the c-Pawn artificially isolated: White can encircle it by Be3-d4, Re3, etc.''}) {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Black's Knight on as is stranded; should it retreat to b7, then b4 smothers its future. ''} 20. axb3 Qc7 21. Be3 {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: ', "Up to here, White has played in excellent style, but this inaccurate move considerably improves the Black position.''} ({Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: 'White ought to play''} 21. Bd2 $142 {Kortschnoj Kortschnoj Ernst: 'Kortschnoj Bobby Fischer: 'Korchnoi,V: ''} Bc3 $10 {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: '=''}) ({Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: 'or, still better,''} 21. Re2 $142 $1 { d4 Kortschnoj  d4 Kortschnoj Ernst: ' d4 Kortschnoj Bobby Fischer: '!' Bobby Fischer: 'protecting the K.B and preparing the powerful maneuver Nd4." (KORCHNOI.) ''} {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: 'The truth is, White just doesn't have that much. After 21.Nd2 or Re2 Black can still reply with''} Bc3 $10 {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: 'RF''}) 21... Bc3 $1 22. Re2 b4 $132 {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: '; "Now Black has sufficient play on the black squares." (KORCHNOI.) ''} 23. Nd4 Rfe8 {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: '; "Worried by his loose Pawn front and his scattered minor pieces, Black decides that he ought to get another piece into play rather than spend a move protecting his King's side. However, Fischer soon demonstrates that the White Knight obtains splendid prospects on the King's side,''} ({Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: 'hence''} 23... g6 $142 {Kortschnoj Kortschnoj Ernst: 'Kortschnoj Bobby Fischer: 'is much better." (KORCHNOI.) ''} {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: 'On 23...g6''} 24. Bd3 Nc5 25. Rc2 Nab7 26. Ne2 Bg7 $10 {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: 'the Bishop dances away and White has nothing.''}) 24. Nf5 Nb7 25. Bd4 g6 {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: '; The threat was Nxg7. ''} 26. Nh6+ Kf8 27. Rc1 $1 {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: ', "This powerful move is a reminder to Black that he has problems on the c-file as well as in the neighborhood of his King." (KORCHNOI.) ''} Rac8 {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: '; "In the event of White's exchanging Bishops, Black wants to be ready to recapture with a piece (Queen or Rook) rather than be left with a Pawn on c3 which will most likely be fatally weak." (KORCHNOI.)''} ({Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Not''} 27... Bxd4 28. Qxd4 f6 29. Qxb4) 28. Bd3 {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: ', "This inaccuracy grants Black a fresh chance of recovery.''} ({Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: 'A very strong continuation here was''} 28. Re3 $1 {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: 'with the threat of''} a5 (28... Z0 {Bobby Fischer} 29. Bxc3 bxc3 30. Qd4 $1 f6 31. Bb1 {when the c-Pawn would fall" (KORCHNOI.)}) 29. Bxc3 bxc3 30. Qd4 $1 f6 31. Bb1 $18 {Kortschnoj}) 28... Qa5 ({Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: 'On''} 28... Qd8 29. Rec2 {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: 'maintains the pin.''}) 29. Rec2 Ne5 30. Bf1 Nc5 {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: '; "Sacrificing a Pawn for the moment; but the Black pieces obtain excellent activity." (KORCHNOI.) ''} 31. Bxc3 bxc3 32. Rxc3 Kg7 33. Ng4 Nxg4 34. Qxg4 Rb8 {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: '; Breaking the pin and threatening the e-Pawn and/or the b-Pawn.''} ({Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Not''} 34... Rxe4 $4 35. Qxc8) 35. Rf3 {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: ', "White's best chance is to revive his attack on the King's wing." (KORCHNOI.) ''} Nxe4 36. Qf4 f5 ({Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: '"''} 36... Rb7 $5 {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: 'may be safer here." (KORCHNOI.)''}) {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: 'The text weakens the K-side, but White can't exploit it. ''} 37. Re3 Re5 38. Rc6 Rbe8 $5 {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: '; "Short of time, I overlooked White's next move completely.''} ({Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Even so, the text is not bad, but for practical purposes Black ought to choose the simple''} 38... g5 {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: 'maintaining a good position without risk." (KORCHNOT.) ''} {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: 'After 38...g5''} 39. Qf3 Rbe8 40. Rxa6 Qxd5 41. b4 $10 {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: 'the chances are approximately equal.''}) 39. Rxd6 $1 Qa1 $2 {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: '; "A bad error, after which Black is two Pawns behind with no compensation.''} ({Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Correct and necessary is''} 39... g5 $142 $1 {Kortschnoj Kortschnoj Ernst: 'Kortschnoj Bobby Fischer: '!''} 40. Rd7+ Kg6 41. Qf3 Qb6 $1 { xf2!; f6!  xf2!; f6! Ernst: ' xf2!; f6! Bobby Fischer: 'with the threat 42 ...Nxf2!. For instance:''} 42. Bd3 $2 (42. g4 $2 Nxf2 43. Rxe5 Nxg4+) (42. Rxe4 $1 {  Ernst: ' Bobby Fischer: '(best)''} Rxe4 43. g4 Rf4 44. gxf5+ Kh6 45. Qg3 Re5 $10 {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: 'with at least a draw.''}) ({Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: '"Instead, Black panics at the unexpected tum of events, and Fischer efficiently finishes the game in a few moves." (KORCHNOI.) Incidentally, Korchnoi neglects to add that after 41...Qb6! Black has the additional threat of ...Nf6 (as well as ...Nxf2) trapping the Rook. He also neglects to analyze the right defense:''} 42. Qe2 $142 $1 {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: '!''} Nxf2 ({Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: '(What else? If''} 42... f4 43. Rxe4 Rxe4 44. Qc2 Kh6 45. Rc7 $1 $18 {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: '!' Bobby Fischer: 'wins.''}) 43. Rxe5 $1 Ne4+ ({Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: 'it's fascinating that Black has no better discovery; if''} 43... Ng4+ 44. Re3 $1 Rxe3 45. Qxa6 Qxa6 46. Bxa6 Nf6 $1 47. Rd8 Rxb3 $10 {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: '=''}) ({Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: 'But not''} 43... Nxh3+ $2 44. Kh2 Qg1+ 45. Kg3 $1 f4+ 46. Kf3 $1 Rxe5 47. Qxa6+ $1 $18 {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: '!' Bobby Fischer: 'wins.''}) 44. Kh2 Rxe5 45. Qxa6 Qxa6 46. Bxa6 Nf6 $10 {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: 'regaining the d-Pawn with a draw in view.''}) 42... Nxf2 43. Rxe5 Nxd3+) 40. Rxa6 Qd4 41. Rd3 Qb2 42. d6 g5 43. Qe3 f4 44. Qa7+ {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: ', Black resigns.''} (44. Qa7+ {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Black must lose a Rook after''} Kf8 45. d7 Rd8 46. Qb6 Ke7 47. Qxd8+ Kxd8 48. Ra8+ $18 {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: 'followed by 49 d8=Q+.''}) 1-0

