1. e4 {ChessBase ChessBase 1) Uhlmann,Wofgang: Meine besten Partien. St.Ingbert. 2015. S.6-10.} e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. e5 c5 5. a3 Bxc3+ 6. bxc3 Ne7 7. Nf3 Bd7 8. a4 Qa5 9. Qd2 Nbc6 10. Bd3 c4 11. Be2 f6 (11... O-O-O 12. Ba3 f6 {ChessBase: '' ''} 13. O-O $14 {(Keres 69)}) 12. Ba3 (12. O-O O-O $5 {(Ivkov)}) 12... Ng6 $6 (12... O-O-O $142) 13. O-O $1 O-O-O (13... fxe5 $6 14. Nxe5 Ngxe5 15. dxe5 Nxe5 16. Qg5 $1 $16 {(Schwarz 67)} Ng6 (16... Nc6 17. Bh5+ $1 g6 18. Qf6 Rg8 19. Rfe1 $16 {(Schwarz 67)}) (16... Qxc3 $4 17. Qe7#) 17. Bh5 $1 $16 {(Schwarz 67, Mednis 74)}) 14. Bd6 (14. Rfe1 fxe5 15. dxe5 Ngxe5 16. Nxe5 Nxe5 17. Qd4 Nc6 18. Qxg7 Rhg8 $13 {(eco 74/81)}) 14... Nce7 $1 {"Uhlmann gruppeirt um, weil seine Chancen auf dem Konigsflugel liegen." (Schwarz 67)} (14... fxe5 15. dxe5 h6 16. Kh1 Rhe8 17. Rfd1 Nh8 $1 {Gligoric-Sokolov 1956}) (14... Rde8 15. Rfb1 Nd8 16. Bb4 Qc7 17. Bd6 Qa5 18. Qe3 Nf7 19. Bc5 Kb8 20. Rb2 {Klavin-Fuchs 1961}) 15. Nh4 $1 {ChessBase: '"With this and the following series of fine moves, White ensures an excellent diagonal for his QB and paralyzes any hopes Black may have for meaningful counterplay." (Mednis 74)' "With this and the following series of fine moves, White ensures an excellent diagonal for his QB and paralyzes any hopes Black may have for meaningful counterplay." (Mednis 74) ! Uhlmann: Weiss verhindert Sf5 und kann so seinen Läufer auf der Diagonalen b8-h2 behaupten.} Rde8 16. Nxg6 $1 hxg6 17. exf6 $1 {"Weiss will auf den dunklen Feldern zu eimem Ubergewicht kommen, daher die Linienoffnung fur den Th8." (Schwarz 67)} gxf6 18. h3 $1 {"Fischers Plan sieht gut aus: er will den Laufer auf der Diagonale h2-b8 wirken lassen." (Schwarz 67)} Nf5 19. Bh2 g5 {[#]} 20. f4 $2 {"But this brute force attempt at an immediate win spoils everything." (Mednis 74) Sperrt den Lh1 ein, und Schwarz will ihn blockiert lassen.} (20. Rfe1 $1 {"... White has a marvelous position: pressure on Black's somewhat shaky center, open diagonals for both Bishops, while Black's King can find himself uncomfortably open soon." (Mednis 74)}) (20. Rae1) (20. Bg4) 20... Nd6 $6 {ChessBase: '!' '!'} (20... g4 $1 {Lässt f4xg5 nicht zu.} {Nach} 21. hxg4 (21. Bxg4 Reg8) 21... Nd6 22. Bf3 f5 {hätten wir mit Zugumstellung die Partiestellung auf dem Brett.}) 21. Bf3 (21. fxg5 $5 {Befreit den Lh2.} Ne4 22. Qe3 (22. Qf4 e5 $1) 22... Qxc3 23. Qxc3 (23. Bd3 $2 cxd3 24. cxd3 Qd2 $1 {(Schwarz 67)}) 23... Nxc3 24. Bf3 fxg5 25. a5 $11 {(Schwarz 67, Mednis 74) ChessBase: 'N' 'N'}) 21... g4 $3 {"Black sacrifices a pawn and allows a protected passed pawn to boot, for the strategic objective of locking in White's QB. The damage done by White's 20 f4? is now very obvious." (Mednis 74) Uhlmann: Mit dem Bauernopfer wird der Läufer auf h2 endgültig bis zum Partienende aus dem Verkehr gezogen.} 22. hxg4 (22. Bxg4 $2 Ne4 23. Qe3 f5 24. Bf3 Qxc3 25. Qxc3 Nxc3 $17 {(Schwarz 67)}) 22... f5 $1 23. g5 Re7 24. Bg3 Be8 25. Qe3 Ne4 26. Bxe4 $8 dxe4 27. Kf2 {"Fischer evaluates this position much too optimistically and plans to husband the extra Pawn to victory. The blocked nature of the position makes winning attempts for either side less than fruitful." (Mednis 74)} (27. d5 $5) 27... Reh7 (27... Qd5) 28. Rfb1 (28. d5 $142 $1 Qxd5 29. Rfd1 {(Schwarz 67)}) 28... Qd5 $1 {"Now we have a rather full blockade and the game could well be called a draw here." (Mednis 74)} 29. Qe1 $2 (29. a5 $10) (29. Qd2 $5 Rh1 30. Ke3) 29... Rh1 $1 {[#]} 30. Qxh1 $4 (30. Qe3 $8 Rxb1 31. Rxb1 Bxa4 32. Ra1 Bxc2 33. Rxa7 Kb8 34. Ra1 Bd3 $15 {(Mednis 74)}) 30... e3+ $1 31. Kg1 (31. Kxe3 $2 Qe4+ 32. Kf2 (32. Kd2 $2 Rxh1 33. Rxh1 Qxg2+ $19) 32... Rxh1 (32... Qxc2+ 33. Kg1 Rxh1+ 34. Kxh1 Bc6 35. Rg1 Qxc3 {(Schwarz 67)}) 33. Rxh1 Bc6 $1 34. Rh2 Qxc2+ 35. Kg1 Qxc3 $19 {(Mednis 74)}) (31. Ke2 $2 Rxh1 32. Rxh1 Qxg2+ {(Wade/O'Connell)}) 31... Rxh1+ 32. Kxh1 e2 $1 33. Rb5 $5 {"Bobby finally realized that he must be lost and thus characteristically goes for active counterplay. It is not good enough, but is as good a try as any." (Mednis 74)} (33. Re1 Qe4) (33. Rg1 Qe4) 33... Bxb5 34. axb5 Qxb5 $1 35. Re1 a5 36. Rxe2 a4 $1 37. Rxe6 a3 38. g6 (38. Re5 Qxe5 $19) 38... Qd7 (38... a2 $4 39. g7 a1=Q+ 40. Kh2 $10 {(Mednis 74)}) 39. Re5 b6 40. Bh4 a2 41. Re1 Qg7 42. Ra1 Qxg6 (42... Qxg6 43. Rxa2 Qh5 44. g3 Qf3+ 45. Kh2 Qxc3 46. Bf6 b5 $19 {(Mednis 74)}) 0-1

