Analysis 2.10 (10s): ''} 25. Bxe6 (25. Qxe6 {!} Qxe6 26. Bxe6 Rb5 (26... d3 27. Rfd1 $18 {Krogius})) 25... Rab7 {But after} (25... Rc7 $16) 26. Rce1 $16 {White should prevail according to Kasparov.}) 25. b3 a5 26. f5 {Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s): ' Threatens to win with f6.' Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s): ' Threatens to win with f6.' Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s): ' Threatens to win with f6.' Konikowski: '!' '+-'} exf5 (26... Qg5 $16) 27. Rxf5 {Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s): '+-'} Nh7 (27... Ng6 $2 {loses to} 28. Qg3 $1 ({The careless} 28. Rf7 $2 {is met by} Qg5 $1) 28... Qe8 29. Rcf1 {followed by e5-e6.}) (27... Ne6 $2 {is no worse.} 28. Bxe6 Qxe6 29. Rf8+ $18) 28. Rcf1 ({White also has to be vigilant.} 28. Rf7 $2 {ChessBase: '??' '??'} Ng5 {Konikowski: '!'} 29. Rxe7 Nxh3+ 30. gxh3 Rxe7 $19) 28... Qd8 ({If} 28... Rf8 $2 29. Rxf8+ Nxf8 30. Qc8 $18) 29. Qg3 Re7 (29... a4 $142 30. e6 (30. Rf7 Rxf7 31. Rxf7 Ng5 $16) 30... Rba8) 30. h4 $1 {! %04xNh7 After this move neither the Black queen nor the knight can use g5 as a springboard.} (30. Rf7 $2 Rxf7 31. Rxf7 Qg5 {would have given Black a breather.}) 30... Rbb7 31. e6 {ChessBase: '!' '!'} Rbc7 32. Qe5 Qe8 (32... d3 33. R5f3 $18 {Timman} d2 34. Rd3 $18) 33. a4 {!} Qd8 34. R1f2 (34. Bd3 $5) 34... Qe8 {Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s): '?'} ({Or} 34... d3 $2 35. Rd2 $18) 35. R2f3 Qd8 36. Bd3 {Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s): '[#] Strongly threatening Rh5.'} Qe8 {Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s): '?'} (36... Qg8 {only leads to a suffocating end.} 37. Rf7 Rxf7 38. exf7 Rxf7 39. Bc4 $18) 37. Qe4 $1 {Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s): ' Rf8+! would kill now.' ! 'with the idea' Rf8} Nf6 (37... Rxe6 $4 {is worse.} 38. Rf8+ $1 {Konikowski: '+-!'} Nxf8 39. Rxf8+ Qxf8 40. Qh7#) 38. Rxf6 $1 $18 {!} gxf6 39. Rxf6 Kg8 40. Bc4 {ChessBase: ' 41.f7 Timman'} Kh8 41. Qf4 {Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s): 'Accuracy: White = 90%, Black = 15%. '} (41. Rf7 {!}) 1-0

