{Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'GAME N. 35 A brilliant cadenza. Called upon to face his favorite defense, Fischer quickly obtains the advantage against Block's rather passive opening strategy. Bolbochan, burdened with a bad Bishop against a good Knight, defends with extreme care but is gradually forced to retreat behind his lines. Disdaining several opportunities to enter a favorable ending, Fischer presses for a quick decision in the mid-game. His judgment is rewarded when the pressure which he painstakingly has accumulated erupts in a violent attack, beginning with 34.hxg6. Fischer 's invasion on the weakened squares is a model of accuracy. It culminates in a keen combination which, appropriately, earned a tie for the first brilliancy prize. ''} 1. e4 {Ftacnik Ftacnik,L Ftacnik,L Ftacnik,L Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer'} c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 a6 6. h3 {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: ', Black's loss of time with ...a6 may possibly justify this loss of time. ''} Nc6 ({Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'The variation is specifically directed against the characteristic ...e5 of the Najdorf System. Thus if''} 6... e5 7. Nde2 Be7 ({Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'or''} 7... Be6 8. g4 d5 9. exd5 Nxd5 10. Bg2 $16 {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'with a comfortable edge.''}) 8. g4 O-O 9. Ng3 $1 g6 10. g5 Ne8 11. h4 $40 {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'with a powerful attack: e.g.,''} f6 $2 12. Bc4+ Kg7 13. h5 fxg5 14. hxg6 hxg6 15. Nh5+ $1) ({Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'For''} 6... g6 {Fischer,R-Reshevsky,S ch-USA 1962 Ftacnik,L: 'Fischer,R-Reshevsky,S ch-USA 1962 Bobby Fischer: 'see game 43: Fischer,R-Reshevsky,S; ch-USA, 1962.''}) ({Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'For''} 6... b5 {Fischer,R-Najdorf,M Varna ol 1962 Ftacnik,L: 'Fischer,R-Najdorf,M Varna ol 1962 Bobby Fischer: 'see game 40: Fischer,R-Najdorf,M; Varna ol, 1962.''}) 7. g4 Nxd4 8. Qxd4 e5 9. Qd3 Be7 ({Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'More accurate is''} 9... Be6 $142 {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'immediately.''}) 10. g5 $1 ({Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Weak is''} 10. b3 {Gereben,E-Geller,E Budapest 1952 Ftacnik,L: 'Gereben,E-Geller,E Budapest 1952 Bobby Fischer: 'as played in Gereben,E-Geller,E.; Budapest, 1952.''}) 10... Nd7 {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: '; Now the Knight interferes with the normal development of the QB.''} ({Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'But on''} 10... Nh5 11. h4 $16 { e2 Ftacnik,L: ' e2 Bobby Fischer: 'followed by an eventual Be2 will cause trouble.''}) 11. Be3 ({Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Sharper is''} 11. h4 Nc5 12. Qf3 $13) 11... Nc5 $2 ({Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'The best chance is''} 11... Bxg5 $142 12. Bxg5 Qxg5 13. Qxd6 Qe7 14. Qxe7+ Kxe7 15. Nd5+ Kf8 16. O-O-O g6 $14 {Kotov,A Ftacnik,L: 'Kotov,A Bobby Fischer: '(KOTOV) holding White to a minimal endgame edge.''}) 12. Qd2 Be6 13. O-O-O O-O 14. f3 Rc8 15. Kb1 {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: ', Amateurs are often puzzled by this apparent loss of time. Actually it is a handy defensive move, getting out of the pin on the c-file which could become annoying after ...b5-b4. One never knows when lightning will strike! ''} Nd7 {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: '; The knight has no future on c5, so Bolbochan tries to bring it into play via b6. ''} 16. h4 b5 17. Bh3 Bxh3 ({Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'After''} 17... Nb6 18. Bxb6 Qxb6 19. Nd5 Qd8 ({Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'not''} 19... Bxd5 $2 20. Bxc8) 20. Nxe7+ Qxe7 21. Qxd6 {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'etc.''}) ({Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'On''} 17... Re8 18. Nd5 Bf8 19. h5 $16 { Ftacnik,L: ' Bobby Fischer: 'with a tremendous bind. Black has to reckon with the possible breakthrough on g6.''}) 18. Rxh3 Nb6 19. Bxb6 Qxb6 20. Nd5 $18 {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: ', White has a strategically won game; his Knight cannot be dislodged. ''} Qd8 21. f4 {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: ', Threatening f5. An example of some of the nonsense that has been written about my games, both by admirers and detractors, is the following (by Lublinsky) in the 1962 Russian Yearbook: "Brilliant intuition! Fischer refuses to enter into the Rook and Pawn endgame and plays to continue his attack."''} ({Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'But White can't! Not''} 21. Nxe7+ $2 Qxe7 22. Qxd6 $4 Rfd8 $19 {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'and Black wins.''}) 21... exf4 22. Qxf4 Qd7 23. Qf5 Rcd8 ({Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Insufficient is''} 23... Rfd8 $2 24. Qxd7 Rxd7 25. Nb6 $18) ({Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'or''} 23... Qxf5 $2 24. Nxe7+) 24. Ra3 $1 {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: ', Shows how ideal the position is - White can afford the luxury of probing weaknesses on both wings. ''} Qa7 25. Rc3 ({Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Tempting is''} 25. Nf6+ $5 Bxf6 ({Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'if''} 25... gxf6 $2 26. gxf6 Kh8 27. Qg5 Rg8 28. fxe7 $1) 26. gxf6 g6 27. Qg5 Kh8 $16 {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'and White has no forced win in sight.''}) ({Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Objectively best is''} 25. Nxe7+ $142 Qxe7 26. Rxa6 Rfe8 27. a4 $1) {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'But I was hoping to win in the middle game. Ironically, I wouldn't have been awarded the brilliancy prize had I chosen the best line here. They don't give medals for endgame technique! ''} 25... g6 $1 ({Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'On''} 25... Qd7 $2 26. Rc7 $18 {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'wins.''}) ({Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'On''} 25... Rd7 $2 26. Nf6+ $1 Bxf6 (26... gxf6 27. gxf6 Kh8 28. fxe7 $18 {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'wins.''}) 27. gxf6 g6 28. Qg5 Kh8 29. Qh6 Rg8 30. Rc8 $1 $18 {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: '!' Bobby Fischer: 'forces mate.''}) 26. Qg4 Qd7 27. Qf3 Qe6 ({Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Not''} 27... Rc8 $2 28. Rxc8 Rxc8 29. Nb6) 28. Rc7 Rde8 ({Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'On''} 28... Rd7 29. Nf4 $18 {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'wins.''}) ({Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'And after''} 28... Rfe8 29. Rf1 {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Black has hardly any moves.''}) (28... Rc8 {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'is answered by''} 29. Ra7 Ra8 30. Rxa8 Rxa8 31. Nc7) 29. Nf4 Qe5 30. Rd5 Qh8 31. a3 h6 {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: '; A bid for freedom - otherwise Ra7 mops up the Q-side Pawns.''} ({Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'On''} 31... f6 32. Qb3 {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: '!''} Rf7 33. Rxd6 fxg5 34. hxg5 Qe5 35. Rf6 $1 Ref8 36. Rxf7 Rxf7 37. Rc8+ Bf8 38. Ne6 $18 {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'wins.''}) 32. gxh6 Qxh6 ({Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'On''} 32... Bxh4 $2 33. Nxg6 $1 fxg6 34. Qb3 {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'is decisive.''} Rf7 35. Rf5 $18) 33. h5 Bg5 ({Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'After''} 33... g5 34. Ne2 $18 { e2-g3-f5; a7 Ftacnik,L: ' e2-g3-f5; a7 Bobby Fischer: 'foIlowed by Nd4(or g3)-f5 maintains a winning bind.''}) {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Black also has to contend with the threat of Ra7. ''} 34. hxg6 $1 fxg6 ({Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'On''} 34... Bxf4 35. gxf7+ Rxf7 36. Rxf7 Kxf7 37. Rh5 $1 $18 {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: '!' Bobby Fischer: 'wins.''}) 35. Qb3 $1 {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: ', The coup de grace. ''} Rxf4 ({Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'On''} 35... Kh8 36. Nxg6+ Qxg6 37. Rxg5 Rf1+ (37... Qxg5 38. Qh3+ $18 {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'forces mate.''}) 38. Ka2 Qxg5 39. Qh3+ Kg8 40. Qxf1 $18 {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'leads to a win.''}) ({Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'or''} 35... Bxf4 36. Rh5+) 36. Re5+ Kf8 37. Rxe8+ {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: ', Black resigns.''} (37. Rxe8+ {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'After''} Kxe8 38. Qe6+ Kf8 39. Qc8+ $18 {Ftacnik,L: 'Bobby Fischer: 'mates.''}) 1-0

