1. e4 {MIKHALCHISHIN Mikhalchishin,A} c5 2. Nf3 e6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 a6 5. c4 Qc7 6. Nc3 Nf6 7. Bd3 Nc6 8. Be3 Nxd4 9. Bxd4 Bc5 {MIKHALCHISHIN: 'Blacks' idea in such situations,as it was mentioned before, is to fight over the control of Black squares.It is very instructive to follow, how Fischer is destroying the opponents plan.' Blacks' idea in such situations,as it was mentioned before, is to fight over the control of Black squares.It is very instructive to follow, how Fischer is destroying the opponents plan.} 10. Bc2 $1 d6 11. O-O Bd7 12. Na4 ({MIKHALCHISHIN: 'Another interesting option was' Another interesting option was} 12. Bxc5 Qxc5 (12... dxc5 13. f4 e5 14. Nd5 Nxd5 15. exd5 exf4 16. Re1+ Kf8 17. d6 {MIKHALCHISHIN: 'led to very unpleasant position with the King in the center.' led to very unpleasant position with the King in the center.}) 13. Qd3 Ke7 14. Rad1 Rhd8 15. Qg3 {MIKHALCHISHIN: 'which lead to very unclear position,as King in the center is placed not bad at all.' which lead to very unclear position,as King in the center is placed not bad at all.}) 12... Bxd4 13. Qxd4 Rd8 ({MIKHALCHISHIN: 'stronger was' stronger was} 13... e5 14. Qd2 O-O 15. Nc3 Be6 {MIKHALCHISHIN: 'with sufficient control over d5 and Whites efforts to attack pawn d6 are not real.' with sufficient control over d5 and Whites efforts to attack pawn d6 are not real.}) 14. Rfd1 O-O 15. Rac1 ({MIKHALCHISHIN: 'nothig would give' nothig would give} 15. Nb6 Bc6 16. f3 e5 17. Qe3 Nd7 18. Nxd7 Bxd7 19. b3 Be6 {MIKHALCHISHIN: 'preparing f7-f5 later.' preparing f7-f5 later.}) 15... Qa5 {MIKHALCHISHIN: 'Diagram ' Diagram [#]} 16. Qb6 $1 {MIKHALCHISHIN: 'it is Bobbys plan - to try to exploit his own better technique in the endgame.,' it is Bobbys plan - to try to exploit his own better technique in the endgame.,} Qxb6 (16... Qg5 {MIKHALCHISHIN: 'to very sharp play led the piece sacrifice' to very sharp play led the piece sacrifice} 17. Qxb7 Rb8 18. Qxa6 Ra8 19. Qxd6 Bxa4 20. b3 Be8 21. a4 {MIKHALCHISHIN: 'and three pawns will become dangerous sooner or later.' and three pawns will become dangerous sooner or later.}) 17. Nxb6 Bc6 18. f3 Nd7 19. Nd5 $5 ({MIKHALCHISHIN: 'Possible was' Possible was} 19. Nxd7 Rxd7 20. b4 Rc8 21. Bb3 Rdd8 22. Kf2 Kf8 23. Ke3 Ke7 24. f4 {MIKHALCHISHIN: 'but the advantage is minimal.' but the advantage is minimal.}) 19... Bxd5 20. exd5 e5 21. b4 g6 22. Ba4 b6 (22... a5 $1 {MIKHALCHISHIN: 'was the only chance to create own counterplay.' was the only chance to create own counterplay.}) 23. Rd3 f5 24. Ra3 $1 Nb8 {MIKHALCHISHIN: 'Diagram ' Diagram [#]} 25. c5 $1 {MIKHALCHISHIN: 'Destroying the opponents structure in the center and opening the position,while Blacks Knight is out of action.' Destroying the opponents structure in the center and opening the position,while Blacks Knight is out of action.} bxc5 26. bxc5 dxc5 27. Rxc5 Kg7 28. Rb3 Rf7 29. d6 $1 {MIKHALCHISHIN: 'Passed pawns function is to go forward.' Passed pawns function is to go forward.} Nd7 30. Rc7 Nf8 31. Rbb7 Rxc7 32. dxc7 Rc8 33. Bb3 a5 34. a4 h6 35. h3 g5 36. g4 fxg4 37. hxg4 1-0

