{Nigel Davies: 'As Fischer played this opening with Black, his treatment with White is especially noteworthy. In this game Black plays 7...Nxb3 so as to avoid 7...f6 8.Bxg8, but it could be that the medicine is worse than the disease.'} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Ba4 b5 5. Bb3 Na5 6. O-O $1 d6 7. d4 Nxb3 ({This runs into Fischer's 9.c4, but Black was worried about} 7... f6 8. Bxg8 {. Was he right to do so? After} Rxg8 {Ernst's} 9. b4 $5 {can be answered by} Nc4 10. Nbd2 Nxd2 11. Qxd2 Bb7 12. Re1 Qd7 {when Ernst - Tisdall, Gausdal 1993 resulted in a nice win for Black after} (12... a5 $6 13. bxa5 c5 14. dxc5 dxc5 15. Qe2 $1 Qxa5 16. Nxe5 $1 {was good for White in Ernst - Gausel, Norway 1992}) 13. Bb2 Be7 14. a4 f5 15. axb5 fxe4 16. bxa6 Rxa6 17. Ng5 Rxa1 18. Bxa1 Qg4 19. Nh3 Qxg2+ 20. Kxg2 e3+ 21. Kg1 exd2 22. Rd1 g5 23. dxe5 g4 24. Nf4 Bg5 25. Ne2 Be4 26. exd6 Bxc2 27. dxc7 Kd7 {0-1}) 8. axb3 f6 9. c4 Bb7 ({Black can improve on this with} 9... b4 {so as to stop White's knight on b1 from coming to c3.} 10. Be3 ({Black also seems OK after other moves, for example} 10. Nh4 Ne7 11. Be3 g6 12. Qd2 exd4 13. Bxd4 Bg7 14. Be3 a5 15. Bh6 O-O 16. Bxg7 Kxg7 17. Qe3 c5 18. Nd2 g5 19. Nhf3 Ng6 {was fine for Black in Ernst - Agdestein, Gausdal 1987}) (10. Qd3 c5 11. dxc5 dxc5 12. Qxd8+ Kxd8 13. Be3 Kc7 14. Ne1 a5 15. Nd3 Kc6 {was rather equal in Timman - Agdestein, Belgrade 1989}) (10. d5 c5 11. Nh4 g6 12. f4 exf4 13. Bxf4 Nh6 14. Nd2 Nf7 15. Bg3 Bg7 {left Black with no problems in King - Gausel, Gausdal 1990}) 10... Bb7 11. Nbd2 (11. d5 c5 12. dxc6 Bxc6 13. Nbd2 Qd7 14. Ne1 Qb7 15. f3 g6 16. Nc2 Ne7 17. Qe2 a5 {left Black at least equal in Murey - Agdestein, Jerusalem 1986}) 11... c5 12. dxc5 dxc5 13. Qe2 Bd6 14. Nh4 (14. Ne1 Ne7 15. Nd3 Qb6 16. Qg4 f5 $1 17. exf5 O-O 18. f6 Rxf6 {gave Black the initiative in Topalov - Agdestein, Biel 1993}) 14... g6 15. Rad1 (15. Rfd1 Ne7 16. Nf1 Qc7 {was OK for Black in Wahlbom - Zwaig, Dresden 1969}) 15... Qc7 ({After} 15... Ne7 {Timman might have been intending} 16. f4 $5) 16. Qg4 Bc8 17. Qf3 Be6 18. Nf5 Bf8 19. h3 Rd8 20. Ng3 h5 21. Ne2 Kf7 22. Nc1 Kg7 23. Qe2 Bd6 24. Nd3 Ne7 25. f4 {and White had the initiative in Timman - Agdestein, Brussels 1992}) 10. Nc3 {Nigel Davies: 'The most natural move, but not his only possibility.'} ({In Ivkov - Hoen, Havana (ol) 1966 White played} 10. Qe2 {and after} b4 11. Rd1 Qc8 12. Nbd2 c5 13. dxc5 dxc5 14. Nf1 Ne7 15. Nh4 Qe6 16. Qd3 Nc6 17. Ne3 Nd4 18. Nd5 {had a slight advantage.}) 10... Ne7 (10... b4 {in this position would be answered by} 11. Nd5) 11. Qe2 c6 (11... b4 12. Nd5 Nc6 13. dxe5 dxe5 14. Rd1 Qc8 15. Be3 Be7 16. Nh4 O-O 17. Nf5 Rf7 18. h4 Bf8 19. h5 {left Black under serious pressure in Medina Garcia - Zwaig, Havana (ol) 1966}) 12. Rd1 Qc7 13. Be3 $14 Ng6 14. Rac1 b4 15. Na4 c5 16. dxc5 dxc5 17. Qd3 Rb8 18. Nb6 $1 Be7 ({Nigel Davies: 'Or if'} 18... Bxe4 {Nigel Davies: 'there is'} 19. Nd5 $1 Bxd5 20. cxd5 $16 {Nigel Davies: 'and Black is in serious trouble.'}) 19. Nd5 Qc6 20. Qe2 Bd6 21. Rd3 Rc8 22. Rcd1 Bb8 23. Nd2 Qe6 24. Nf1 {Nigel Davies: '!'} O-O 25. Ng3 Nf4 $1 26. Bxf4 exf4 27. Nh5 Rce8 {Nigel Davies: '?'} ({Nigel Davies: 'Black should play'} 27... Rfe8 $1 $14 {Nigel Davies: 'with a reasonable game.'}) 28. Nhxf4 Bxf4 29. Nxf4 Qxe4 30. Re3 $18 Qc6 31. Re6 Qc8 32. h4 g6 33. Re7 Rxe7 34. Qxe7 Rf7 35. Rd8+ Kg7 36. Ne6+ 1-0

