{Inf.2/235} {Postny,Evgeny: 'This was an encounter on first board in one of the key matches between the USA and Hungary. '} 1. e4 {Postny,Evgeny} e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Bxc6 dxc6 5. O-O f6 {Postny,Evgeny: 'The Ruy Lopez is one of my main openings and when studying theory of the Exchange Variation from some old Soviet opening encyclopedia, I noticed this game. This was about thirty years ago. Later on I studied a large number of games of Bobby Fischer and he still remains one of my favorite players. '} 6. d4 exd4 (6... Bg4 {Postny,Evgeny is another important theoretical line.}) 7. Nxd4 c5 8. Nb3 ({Nowadays the main line is} 8. Ne2 {Postny,Evgeny}) 8... Qxd1 9. Rxd1 Bd6 {Postny,Evgeny: '?!' Postny,Evgeny: 'This natural move is an inaccuracy.'} (9... Bd7 10. Bf4 $1 O-O-O 11. Nc3 $16) ({Later on the right approach for Black was found:} 9... Bg4 {Postny,Evgeny} 10. f3 Be6 {Black provokes the white pawn to f3 and only then puts the bishop on e6. The idea is that in some lines after c5-c4 black's dark-squared bishop can come to c5 with check.}) 10. Na5 $1 {Postny,Evgeny: 'This was not a novelty at that time, but it does not make this move less effective. The b7 is under pressure and the knight is ready to go to c4.'} b5 {Postny,Evgeny: 'Covering the c4 square, but Black's queenside is now seriously weakened.'} (10... Bg4 $2 11. f3 O-O-O $4 {Postny,Evgeny: '?' Postny,Evgeny: ''??'' Postny,Evgeny: 'This tactical attempt loses to'} 12. e5 {1-0 Hort-Zheljandinov,Havanna 1967 Postny,Evgeny: '!' Postny,Evgeny: '1-0 (12) Hort,V-Zheliandinov,V Havana 1967 1-0 Hort-Zheljandinov,Havanna 1967'}) (10... b6 {Postny,Evgeny} 11. Nc4 {is also unpleasant for Black.} Be7 12. Bf4 Bd8 13. Nc3 Ne7 14. Rd2 Be6 15. Ne3 {½-½ (49) Firman,N (2517)-Graf,A (2595) Dresden 2007}) 11. c4 $1 {Postny,Evgeny: '?!' Postny,Evgeny: ''!'' Postny,Evgeny: 'Not the best way to attack Black's queenside.'} (11. a4 $1 {Postny,Evgeny is more annoying for Black, opening the a-file.} Ne7 12. Na3 (12. Nc3 $6 Rb8 13. axb5 axb5 $11 {½-½ (36) Perez Perez,F-Spassky,B Havana 1962}) 12... Bd7 13. Nb7 Nc8 14. Be3 Bc6 15. Nxc5 $16 {½-½ (30) Skowronek,J (1786)-Schultheiss,K (2135) GER email 2015}) 11... Ne7 (11... b4 $6 12. Nd2 Kf7 13. Ndb3 {Postny,Evgeny: '' Postny,Evgeny: '1-0 (29) Piesina,G-Romanishin,O Riga 1968'} f5 14. exf5 Nf6 15. Be3 Ng4 16. Bxc5 Bxh2+ 17. Kf1 Be5 18. f3 $16 {Peshina-Romanischin, URS 1968}) 12. Be3 $16 {Postny,Evgeny: 'The c5 is White's main target.'} (12. Nc3 {Postny,Evgeny} Ng6 13. a4 {Postny,Evgeny} b4 14. Ne2 O-O 15. Be3 Re8 $11 {½-½ (63) Sellos,D (2405)-Kupreichik,V (2520) Val Maubuee 1989}) 12... f5 $5 {Postny,Evgeny: ''!?''} (12... Rb8 {Postny,Evgeny: '?!'} 13. Nd2 Be6 14. Rac1 Kf7 15. Ndb3 (15. f4 {Postny,Evgeny is also good for White.}) 15... Rhd8 16. cxb5 axb5 17. Nxc5 $16 {Lukin-Kaminski,URS 1970 Postny,Evgeny: '1-0 (51) Lukin,A-Kaminsky,O Leningrad 1970 Lukin-Kaminski,URS 1970'}) (12... Kf7 13. Nc3 (13. Nd2 {Postny,Evgeny} Re8 14. Ndb3 Ng6 15. f3 {and in order not to lose the c5 right away Black has to make an awkward move:} Re5 $16) 13... Rb8 14. e5 $1 Bxe5 (14... fxe5 15. Ne4 $16) 15. Bxc5 Bxc3 16. bxc3 Ng6 17. Nc6 $16 {Dvoretsky-Ivanov,Moscow 1972}) (12... Ng6 {Postny,Evgeny} 13. Nc3 {will transpose to the correspondence game Peczkowski-Sorensen, mentioned above.} Kf7 {Postny,Evgeny} 14. a4 b4 15. Nd5 Re8 16. f3 Ne5 17. Rac1 {White should be slightly better, but a draw was agreed a couple of moves later.} g5 18. Nb3 Nd7 19. a5 Rb8 {½-½ (19) Peczkowski,M (2283)-Sorensen,K (2321) ICCF email 2011}) 13. Nc3 f4 (13... O-O {Postny,Evgeny} 14. f3 (14. e5 Bxe5 15. Bxc5 Re8 16. Re1 Ng6 17. Bd4 $14) 14... Ng6 15. exf5 Bxf5 16. Nb7 Be5 17. Nxc5 bxc4 18. Bd4 $14) (13... Kf7 $6 {Postny,Evgeny} 14. f4 $1 fxe4 15. Nxe4 $16) 14. e5 $1 {Postny,Evgeny: '!?' Postny,Evgeny: ''!''} ({Simply} 14. Bd2 {Postny,Evgeny was actually a good alternative.} b4 $6 ({Covering the d5-square would be the lesser evil:} 14... c6 15. Ne2 O-O 16. f3 $14) 15. Nd5 Ng6 16. f3 Be6 17. Be1 Ne5 18. Nb7 Nxc4 19. Nxd6+ cxd6 20. Nxf4 $16 {1-0 (54) Guseinov,G (2654)-Davidov,S (2306) Baku 2019}) (14. Rxd6 $5 {Postny,Evgeny was another interesting idea.} fxe3 (14... cxd6 $6 15. Bxf4 Be6 16. Bxd6 $16) 15. Rdd1 exf2+ 16. Kxf2 Be6 $14) 14... Bxe5 $6 {Postny,Evgeny: ''?!''} (14... fxe3 15. exd6 exf2+ 16. Kxf2 O-O+ 17. Kg1 cxd6 18. Rxd6 Bf5 19. Re1 $14 {Postny,Evgeny: '½-½ (54) Teterev,V (2507)-Novitzkij,D (2373) Minsk 2006'}) 15. Bxc5 Bxc3 16. bxc3 Ng6 (16... Kf7 {Postny,Evgeny} 17. Bxe7 (17. a4 $6 {is too soft.} bxa4 18. Rxa4 Re8 19. Raa1 Ng6 {and Black is only slightly worse - ½-½ (31) Habes,J (1704)-Luers,C (1879) LSS email 2013}) 17... Kxe7 18. Rd5 $1 Be6 19. Rc5 {with a serious advantage.}) 17. Nc6 {Postny,Evgeny: 'Black's main problem is that his king is stuck in the centre and therefore the rooks are disconnected.'} Be6 $6 (17... Bd7 18. Re1+ $2 {Postny,Evgeny} (18. Na7 {Postny,Evgeny} bxc4 19. Rd4 $14) (18. cxb5 {Postny,Evgeny} axb5 19. Na7 Rf8 $1 20. Bxf8 Nxf8 {The knight is trapped, so White has to return the exchange.} 21. Rxd7 Kxd7 22. Rd1+ Ke7 23. Nxb5 c6 24. Nd4 c5 {with good chances for a draw.}) 18... Kf7 19. Ne5+ Nxe5 20. Rxe5 Rhe8 $11 {½-½ (26) Stets,D (2436)-Koziak,V (2479) Sautron 2016}) 18. cxb5 axb5 19. Na7 $16 {Postny,Evgeny: '!' Postny,Evgeny: ''''} Rb8 (19... Bc4 {Postny,Evgeny} 20. a4 bxa4 21. Rxa4 Be6 22. Ra6 Kf7 23. Rc6 $16) 20. Rdb1 {Postny,Evgeny: 'Black can not save the b5.'} Kf7 (20... Bd7 {Postny,Evgeny} 21. a4 $16) 21. Nxb5 Rhd8 (21... Ne5 {Postny,Evgeny} 22. Ba7 $1 Rbc8 23. a4 $16) 22. Rb4 ({After} 22. a4 {Postny,Evgeny} Rd5 23. Bd4 Rc8 {the idea ...c7-c5 does not allow the white a-passer to go forward so smoothly.}) 22... Bxa2 23. Nxc7 (23. h4 $1 {Postny,Evgeny was even more precise.}) 23... Rbc8 {Postny,Evgeny: 'Keeping all the rooks on the board actually makes things tougher for Black, as his king is more vulnerable.'} (23... Rxb4 24. cxb4 Rd2 (24... Rd7 {Postny,Evgeny} 25. Nb5 Bb3 {would keep decent hopes for a draw thanks to the presense of opposite colour bishops.}) 25. b5 $18) 24. h4 $1 Rd2 (24... Rxc7 $2 {Postny,Evgeny} 25. Bb6 $18) 25. Bb6 f3 $6 (25... h5 $5 $16 {Postny,Evgeny: ''!?''} 26. Rb5 {Postny,Evgeny} Nxh4 27. Rxh5 Ng6 {would still force White to work hard in order to convert the extra pawn into a full point.}) 26. Be3 $18 {Postny,Evgeny: ''+-''} (26. Nb5 {Postny,Evgeny was also good enough.}) 26... Re2 (26... Rd7 {Postny,Evgeny was a bit more stubborn, but after} 27. Na6 $1 Bd5 28. Rd1 {White should win anyway.}) 27. Nb5 {Postny,Evgeny: '+-' Postny,Evgeny: 'Glorious career for this knight!'} Ra8 28. h5 Ne5 29. Rf4+ Ke7 {Postny,Evgeny: 'The king will come under fire in the centre.'} (29... Kg8 {Postny,Evgeny} 30. Nd4 Rb2 31. Nxf3 $18) 30. Rd1 Rc8 31. Re4 Kf6 32. Rd6+ Kf5 33. Rf4+ Kg5 34. Rxf3+ Kh4 {Postny,Evgeny} 35. Rh3+ Kg4 36. Rg3+ Kxh5 37. Rg5+ Kh4 38. Rd4+ {mating.} 1-0

