{Bobby Fischer: 'GAME N. 52 Peekaboo strategy. The MacCutcheon Variation gives rise to unusual positions where White is frequently obliged to forfeit the privilege of castling in order to try and wrest an advantage. After some slight but instructive opening inexactitudes on both sides, Rossolimo appears to achieve equality. Indeed. he is constantly on the brink of crashing through with a counter-attack against White's vulnerable King, although his own monarch is also stranded in the center. After 13. ... f5. which shores up his fortress, it's not clear just whose attack will come first. In a theoretically important formation - a logical. offshoot of this variation - Fischer unearths two fine moves (17 Bb5 + and 19. Ng 1) to sustain his flagging initiative. Still, he is forced to wage a running battle. no sooner landing a blow than having to duck. Consequently, the outcome is in doubt until the very last punch. '} 1. e4 {Belov Belov Bobby Fischer} e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. Bg5 Bb4 {Bobby Fischer: 'Mac Cutcheon,n'} ({The MacCutcheon Variation, giving rise to immediate complications.} 4... Be7 {Bobby Fischer}) ({or} 4... dxe4 {(Bobby Fischer) are tamer}) 5. e5 h6 6. Bd2 (6. exf6 {Bobby Fischer} hxg5 7. fxg7 Rg8 {leads to nothing.}) 6... Bxc3 7. bxc3 ({Against Petrosian, at Cura9ao 1962, I tried the ridiculous} 7. Bxc3 $2 {Bobby Fischer} Ne4 8. Ba5 $4 ({if} 8. Bb4 c5 9. dxc5 Nxf2 $1 10. Kxf2 Qh4+) 8... O-O ({weaker is..} 8... b6 9. Bb4 c5 10. Ba3 cxd4 11. Qxd4 Nc6 12. Bb5) 9. Bd3 Nc6 10. Bc3 Nxc3 11. bxc3 f6 $36 {and Black already had the initiative. ..Fischer,R-Petrosian,T Curacao ct 1962}) 7... Ne4 8. Qg4 g6 ({Bobby Fischer: 'More risky is'} 8... Kf8 9. Nf3 $6 (9. h4 {Bobby Fischer} c5 10. Rh3) 9... c5 10. Bd3 Nxd2 11. Kxd2 Nc6 12. Qf4 Qe7 $10 {Anand,V-Ivanchuk,V (08)/Linares m/1992/1:0/37/}) 9. Bd3 Nxd2 10. Kxd2 c5 {Bobby Fischer: 'Position after'} ({Bobby Fischer: 'Producing a position well-known to theory, but never completely worked out. Not'} 10... Qg5+ 11. Qxg5 hxg5 12. g4 $1 $16 {Bobby Fischer: '!'}) 11. Nf3 (11. Qf4 cxd4 12. cxd4 Qa5+ 13. Ke3 $5 b6 14. Ne2 Nd7 15. Rhc1 Ba6 $10 {Petrushin,A-Piskov,Y/RUS/1992/1:0/36/}) 11... Nc6 ({According to Modern Chess Openings,} 11... Qc7 {(Bobby Fischer) is more accurate; the point being that} 12. Qf4 {can be met by..} f5 $1) (11... Bd7 {Bobby Fischer} 12. dxc5 {deserves testing.}) 12. Qf4 {Bobby Fischer: 'Position after'} ({Bobby Fischer: 'Possibly better is'} 12. Rab1 $5 {Bobby Fischer: 'restraining the development of Black's Q-side.'}) 12... Qc7 ({Bobby Fischer: 'Better is the natural'} 12... Qa5 $5 {Bobby Fischer: '>='} 13. Rab1 ({if} 13. Rhb1 {Bobby Fischer} b6 14. a4 Ba6 15. Bb5 Rc8 16. dxc5 bxc5 17. Bxc6+ Rxc6 18. Rb8+ Rc8 {holds.}) 13... b6 14. dxc5 Qxc5 15. Nd4 Nxd4 16. cxd4 Qa5+ $10 {Bobby Fischer: '=' Bobby Fischer: 'with eqality.'}) ({if} 12... g5 {Bobby Fischer} 13. Qf6 $1 Qxf6 14. exf6 g4 15. Ne5 cxd4 16. cxd4 Nxd4 17. h3 $16 {with a better ending.}) 13. h4 ({Bobby Fischer: 'Sharper is'} 13. Qf6 $142 {Bobby Fischer: '!'} Rg8 14. h4 $16 {Bobby Fischer: 'and if...'} Qa5 {Bobby Fischer} (14... h5 $8 {(Bobby Fischer) looks practically forced)}) 15. h5 $1 gxh5 16. Rxh5 cxd4 17. Rah1 $40 {yielding good attacking prospects.}) 13... f5 $1 $10 {Bobby Fischer: '=!' Bobby Fischer: 'Re-establishing parity.'} 14. g4 cxd4 15. cxd4 Ne7 $6 {Bobby Fischer: '?'} ({Bobby Fischer: 'After the game Rossolimo suggested'} 15... Bd7 {Bobby Fischer: 'but White keeps the better of it after Rossolimo,N if'} 16. gxf5 gxf5 (16... exf5 {Bobby Fischer} 17. Qg3 Ne7 18. e6 $1 Qa5+ 19. c3 Bxe6 20. Rhe1 $40 {gives a powerful attack)}) 17. Rhg1 $14 O-O-O {Bobby Fischer} 18. Rg6 $16 {At least Black's King reaches safety in this line.}) 16. gxf5 exf5 {Bobby Fischer: 'Position after'} 17. Bb5+ {Bobby Fischer: '!'} Kf8 $6 {Bobby Fischer: '?'} (17... Kd8 $1 {Bobby Fischer: '>='} 18. Bd3 Be6 $13 {Fischer/ Fischer/ Bobby Fischer: '' Bobby Fischer: 'White undoubtedly has the initiative, but it's hard to get at the King'}) ({ON} 17... Nc6 {Bobby Fischer} 18. Bxc6+ bxc6 (18... Qxc6 {IS MET BY..} 19. e6 $1 Bxe6 20. Ne5 Qd6 21. Nxg6 Qxf4+ 22. Nxf4 $18 {and the Knight beats the Bishop in the ending)}) 19. Rhg1 {, etc. Black's best chance, however, is to try and reach sanctuary with}) ({IF...} 17... Bd7 {Bobby Fischer} 18. Bxd7+ Qxd7 19. e6 $1) 18. Bd3 {Bobby Fischer: 'Mission accomplished. Now Black's King is pinioned to the K-side'} Be6 19. Ng1 $1 $16 { h3-f4/  h3-f4/ Bobby Fischer: '!' Bobby Fischer: 'The key move. This Knight is headed for f4 where it can exert maximum pressure on the g-Pawn..'} Kf7 20. Nh3 Rac8 {Bobby Fischer: '!?' Bobby Fischer: 'Quite rightly. Rossolimo prefers active defense. After Position after 21'} (20... Rag8 {(Bobby Fischer) White eventually triples on the g-file (bringing his Knight to f4) with a crushing bind.}) 21. Rhg1 b6 ({Bobby Fischer: 'This takes a5 away from the Queen, eliminating any possible defenses there with check. But Black also loses after'} 21... Qc3+ 22. Ke3 Nc6 23. Rab1 Nb4 24. Rxb4 $1 Qxb4 25. h5 $16 Rcg8 {Bobby Fischer} 26. hxg6+ Rxg6 27. Rxg6 Qe1+ 28. Kf3 Kxg6 29. Qh4 $1 Qd1+ 30. Kg2 Rg8 31. Kh2 $1 $18) 22. h5 $1 Qc3+ 23. Ke2 Nc6 ({Bobby Fischer: 'IF..'} 23... g5 24. Nxg5+ $1 hxg5 25. Qxg5 Ke8 26. Qf6 $18 Kd7 {Bobby Fischer} 27. Bb5+ $1 Rc6 28. Qxh8 Qxc2+ 29. Kf1 $18 {WINS.}) ({Bobby Fischer: 'ON..'} 23... Rcg8 24. hxg6+ Rxg6 ({IF..} 24... Nxg6 {Bobby Fischer} 25. Qf3) 25. Qh4 $16 {Bobby Fischer: '+-' Bobby Fischer: 'IS DECISIVE'}) 24. hxg6+ Kg7 ({Bobby Fischer: 'NO BETTER IS...'} 24... Ke7 25. Qh4+ Kd7 26. Rad1 $1 Qxd4 (26... Nxd4+ $2 {Bobby Fischer} 27. Qxd4 $1) 27. Nf4 $1 $18 {Fischer/ Fischer/ Bobby Fischer: '!'}) 25. Rad1 {Bobby Fischer: '!'} Nxd4+ ({ON..} 25... Qxd4 {Bobby Fischer} 26. Kf1 $1 Qxe5 27. Re1 Qxf4 28. Nxf4 Bd7 29. Nh5+ $18 {WINS.}) 26. Kf1 Rhe8 27. Rg3 ({Bobby Fischer: 'Overprotecting the Bishop. After the hasty'} 27. Qh4 $2 Nf3 $1 28. Qf6+ Kg8 29. Bxf5 Nh2+ 30. Kg2 Qf3+ 31. Kxh2 Qxf5 $10 {Bobby Fischer: 'HOLDS.'}) 27... Nc6 28. Qh4 Nxe5 ({AFTER,} 28... Qxe5 {Bobby Fischer} 29. Nf4 $18 {contains too many threats.}) 29. Nf4 $18 Ng4 30. Nxe6+ $1 Rxe6 31. Bxf5 Qc4+ 32. Kg1 $1 {Bobby Fischer: '' Bobby Fischer: 'No credit for other moves!'} ({Bobby Fischer: 'Final Position after,'} 32. Kg1 {Bobby Fischer: '' Bobby Fischer: 'Black resigns IF'} Nxf2 33. Qxc4 Rxc4 34. Kxf2 Rf4+ 35. Rf3 $18 {Bobby Fischer: 'etc. A hard-fought game!'}) 1-0

