{Fischer dropped out of this world championship qualifier over a scheduling dispute when he was leading and delayed his prospects for several years, but he created a number of beautiful games. Here the Mongolian champion is so intent on breaking through on the queenside that he forgets about his king. Fischer's concluding queen sacrifice is captivating and perfectly timed.} {Matanovic,A: 'Chess Informant'} 1. e4 {Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s)} e6 2. d3 d5 3. Nd2 {The purpose of this move order is to avert an exchange of queens after 3...dxe4 4. dxe4.} Nf6 4. g3 c5 5. Bg2 Nc6 6. Ngf3 Be7 7. O-O O-O {White's quiet buildup postpones sharp hand-to-hand battle until the middle game where operations will take place behind closed lines.} 8. e5 Nd7 9. Re1 b5 10. Nf1 (10. Qe2 b4 11. h4 a5 12. Nf1 a4 13. a3 {"Believe it or not, I actually spent more time on this innocuous push (15 minutes) than on any other move in the game! I didn't want to allow Black to get in ...a3 thereby creating holes (weak squares) on c3 and a3. On the other hand, by stopping to meet his positional threat I am forced to postpone my own schemes for at least two moves. Chess is a matter of delicate judgment, knowing when to punch and how to duck" -- Fischer.} bxa3 14. bxa3 Na5 {This decentralization is inadvisable. Black should try 14...Nd4 or Ba6 right away.} 15. Ne3 Ba6 16. Bh3 {Permanently discouraging the f6 freeing maneuver.} d4 17. Nf1 {Fischer is a law unto himself. He abstains from the natural 17. Ng4 because this knight is headed instead for e4. Meanwhile Black has secured d5 for his knight.} Nb6 18. Ng5 Nd5 {It's remarkable that such an obvious move is inferior. 18...h6! 19. Ne4 c4 offers reasonable counterplay.} 19. Bd2 Bxg5 {19...c4 was still a better try. But not 19...h6? 20. Nxe6 fxe6 21. Bxe6+ Kh8 22. Bxa5 Qxa5 23. Bxd5 gaining two buttons.} 20. Bxg5 Qd7 {1-0 (31) Fischer,R-Miagmarsuren,L Sousse 1967 [Matanovic,Aleksandar]}) 10... b4 11. h4 a5 12. Bf4 a4 13. a3 $1 bxa3 14. bxa3 {Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s): 'LiveBook: 46 Games'} Na5 $6 {Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s): ' C00: French: Unusual White 2nd moves'} (14... Nd4 $5) 15. Ne3 Ba6 16. Bh3 d4 {Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s): 'Black has an edge.'} 17. Nf1 Nb6 18. Ng5 Nd5 19. Bd2 {Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s): ' And now Nxe6! would win.'} Bxg5 20. Bxg5 $16 Qd7 {1-0 (31) Fischer,R-Myagmarsuren,L Sousse (izt) 4/17 1967 CI1-130 [Matanovic,Aleksandar]} 21. Qh5 Rfc8 (21... Bb7 $11 {(Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s)) deserves consideration.}) 22. Nd2 (22. Nh2 $1 $14 {Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s)}) 22... Nc3 (22... c4 $11 {(Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s)) remains equal.} 23. Bg2 cxd3) 23. Bf6 $1 {Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s): '!' Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s): ' White threatens Qg5 and mate.'} Qe8 {Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s): '!'} 24. Ne4 {Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s): '!' Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s): ' Bxg7! is the strong threat.'} (24. Bxg7 {Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s)} Kxg7 25. Qg5+ (25. Ne4 $2 Nxe4 26. Rxe4 Kh8 $19) 25... Kf8 $17) 24... g6 (24... Nb3 $16 {Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s)}) 25. Qg5 {Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s): '+-!'} (25. Qh6 $6 {Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s)} Qf8 $16) 25... Nxe4 26. Rxe4 {Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s): '' Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s): ' White attacks with force.'} c4 {Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s): '?'} (26... Bb7 $16 {(Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s)) was necessary.}) 27. h5 $1 (27. Rxd4 {Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s)} cxd3 28. Rg4 (28. cxd3 Nb3 $16) (28. Qh6 $2 Qf8 $19) 28... Rc7 $16) 27... cxd3 {Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s): '?' Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s): '[#]'} (27... Rc7 $18 {Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s)} 28. Qh6 Qf8) 28. Rh4 {Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s): '!' Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s): ' Intending hxg6 and mate.'} ({Stronger than} 28. Qh6 {Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s)} Qf8 $11) ({Weaker is} 28. hxg6 {Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s)} fxg6 29. Be7 (29. Qh6 Ra7 $11) 29... Rc6 $16) 28... Ra7 (28... dxc2 29. hxg6 $18) 29. Bg2 $3 {Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s): ' Qh6 would kill now.'} dxc2 $2 (29... Qf8 {Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s): '+-'} 30. Be4 {Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s)} dxc2 31. hxg6 fxg6 32. Bxg6 hxg6) 30. Qh6 $18 Qf8 {Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s): '[#]'} (30... c1=Q+ 31. Rxc1 Rxc1+ 32. Kh2) 31. Qxh7+ {Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s): '!' Tactical Analysis 2.10 (10s): ' Remove Defender Accuracy: White = 82%, Black =  7%. . Loss on time!?'} 1-0

