{Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Chris Ward: 'Sac, Sac, Mate!:- It's probably fair to say that America's (and many believe the World's) greatest ever player didn't have a particularly high opinion of the Dragon. His recipe for extinguishing the fire was rather unsubtle!'' Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'GAME N. 2 Slaying the dragon. Although the Sicilian, as a whole, is still the best fighting defense at Black's disposal, much of the steam has been taken out of the time-honored Dragon Variation. This is one of the key games which helped to batter its reputation. In a laudable attempt to create complications, Larsen deviates from the book on move 15. That proves to be disastrous, since his counterattack never gets started. Mechanically, routinely, Fischer pries open the h-file, sacrificing first a Pawn and then the exchange. There is an aura of the inevitable about the outcome. Here the notes are as instructive and lucid as the text, which is an object lesson in how to mount an assault against the fianchettoed King. ''} 1. e4 {Ftacnik,Lubomir Ftacnik,Lubomir Ftacnik,Lubomir Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Ftacnik,L Chris Ward Ftacnik,L: 'Ftacnik'' Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer'} c5 2. Nf3 d6 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Chris Ward: 'As far as I'm concerned, the Danish Grandmaster Bent Larsen has been the World's leading Accelerated Dragon expert for many a year. In the old days he regularly wheeled out the normal Dragon, but significantly I have noted that such outings were extremely few and far between after this particular encounter.''} 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 g6 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: '; Larsen was one of the diehards who refused to abandon the Dragon until recently. White's attack almost plays itself ... weak players even beat Grandmasters with it. I once thumbed through several issues of Shakhmatny Bulletin, when the Yugoslav Attack was making its debut, and found the ratio was something like nine wins out of ten in White's favor. Will Black succeed in reinforcing the variation? Time will tell. ''} 6. Be3 Bg7 ({Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Chris Ward: 'It's worth noting that an attempt to hassle the bishop immediately with''} 6... Ng4 $2 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Chris Ward: '??' Chris Ward: 'loses to'' Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'still loses to''} 7. Bb5+ $18 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Chris Ward: 'i.e.''} Bd7 {(Ftacnik,Lubomir) Chris Ward} 8. Qxg4) 7. f3 O-O 8. Qd2 Nc6 9. Bc4 Nxd4 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Chris Ward: 'A once popular variation that is virtually extinct today. There are known alternatives, but nowadays very rarely is anything other than 9...Bd7 seen.'' Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: '; Just how Black can attempt to thread bis way to equality is not clear.''} ({Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Interesting is Donald Byrne's''} 9... a5 $5 {Byrne,D Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Byrne,D Bobby Fischer: 'The strongest reply is''} 10. g4 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'and if''} Ne5 11. Be2 d5 $2 12. g5 $1 $18 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: '!' Bobby Fischer: 'wins a pawn.''}) 10. Bxd4 Be6 11. Bb3 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Chris Ward: '!' Chris Ward: 'Capturing on e6 may double Black's pawns, but it opens up the f-file and more importantly hands over control of d5.''} Qa5 12. O-O-O b5 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Chris Ward: 'In contrast to Black, White hasn't pushed any pawns around his king. Hence an attack with pawns (intended to grant access for the rooks to the enemy king) is always likely to be slower. Note that trading bishops on b3 isn't good for as this time it would be White given control of the c4-square as well as extra cover (after 12 cxb3) for his king. This is an excellent illustrative point. So often White loves to get a knight to d5 and likewise, Black one to c4.''} ({Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'After''} 12... Bxb3 13. cxb3 $1 $40 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: '!' Bobby Fischer: 'Black cannot make any attacking headway against this particular Pawn configuration.''}) {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'White is lost in the King and Pawn ending, it's true, but Black usually gets mated long before then. As Tarrasch put it: "Before the endgame the gods have placed the middle game." ''} 13. Kb1 b4 14. Nd5 ({Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Weaker is''} 14. Ne2 $2 Bxb3 15. cxb3 Rfd8) 14... Bxd5 ({Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Bad judgement is''} 14... Nxd5 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: '?''} 15. Bxg7 Kxg7 16. exd5 Bd7 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Chris Ward: 'is better for White because of the pressure he can exert on the e7-pawn.''} 17. Rde1 $16 {Suetin,A-Kortschnoj,V/URS-ch/1953/ Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Suetin,A-Kortschnoj,V/URS-ch/1953/ Bobby Fischer: 'with a crushing bind. (Suetin-Korchnoi, USSR Championship prelims, 1953.)''}) 15. Bxd5 ({Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Chris Ward: 'In fact'' Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Stronger is''} 15. exd5 $1 Qb5 16. Rhe1 a5 17. Qe2 $1 $16 {Tal,M-Larsen,B Zürich 1959 Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Tal,M-Larsen,B Zürich 1959 Chris Ward: '!' Chris Ward: 'is considered to be a better theoretical variation for White and now Black misses his chance.'' Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Tal,M-Larsen,B Zürich 1959 Bobby Fischer: '!' Bobby Fischer: '(Tal-Larsen, Zurich 1959) where White abandons the attack and plays for pressure along the e-file instead.''}) 15... Rac8 $2 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: '; Losing move.''} ({Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'After the game Larsen explained he was playing for a win, and therefore rejected the forced draw with''} 15... Nxd5 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Chris Ward: '!' Chris Ward: 'was it, with''} 16. Bxg7 ({Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'After 15...Nxd5, however, I intended simply''} 16. exd5 Qxd5 17. Qxb4 $13 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'keeping the game alive.''}) 16... Nc3+ {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Chris Ward: '!''} 17. bxc3 ({Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Chris Ward: 'or''} 17. Bxc3 bxc3 18. Qxc3 Qxc3 19. bxc3 Rfc8 $10 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'renders white extra pawn useless''}) 17... Rab8 $1 18. cxb4 Qxb4+ {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: '!''} 19. Qxb4 Rxb4+ 20. Bb2 Rfb8 $10 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Chris Ward: 'both likely drawn double rook endings.'' Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'etc.''}) 16. Bb3 $1 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: ', He won't get a second chance to snap off the Bishop! Now I felt the game was in the bag if I didn't botch it. I'd won dozens of skittles games in analogous positions and had it down to a science: pry open the h-file, sac, sac ... mate! ''} Rc7 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: '; This loss of time is unfortunately necessary if Black is ever to advance his a-Pawn.''} ({Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Chris Ward: 'Throughout it is clear that the best way to hassle White's light-squared bishop is with ...a5-a4. However this has not been easy to arrange and even now after''} 16... Qb5 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Chris Ward: ', White can knock this plan on the head with the greedy'' Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: '?' Bobby Fischer: 'is refuted by''} 17. Bxa7 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Chris Ward: '!''}) 17. h4 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Chris Ward: '!' Chris Ward: 'Consistent with Fischer's assessment that beating the Dragon was essentially down to prising open the h-file and then sac, sac mate!''} Qb5 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: '; There's no satisfactory way to impede White's attack.''} ({Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'If''} 17... h5 18. g4 $1 hxg4 (18... Rfc8 19. Rdg1 hxg4 20. h5 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: '!''} gxh5 21. fxg4 Nxe4 22. Qf4 e5 23. Qxe4 exd4 24. gxh5 Kh8 25. h6 Bf6 26. Rg7 $18 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: '!' Bobby Fischer: 'wins.''}) 19. h5 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: '!''} gxh5 ({Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'on''} 19... Nxh5 20. Bxg7 Kxg7 21. fxg4 Nf6 22. Qh6+ $18 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'mates.''}) 20. fxg4 Nxe4 ({Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'on''} 20... hxg4 21. Rdg1 e5 22. Be3 Rd8 23. Bh6 $18) ({Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'or''} 20... Nxg4 21. Rdg1 Bxd4 22. Rxg4+ {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: '!''} hxg4 23. Qh6 $18 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'leads to mate.''}) 21. Qe3 Nf6 (21... Bxd4 22. Qxe4 Bg7 23. Rxh5 $18) 22. gxh5 e5 23. h6 $18 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'wins.''}) {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Now Black is threatening to get some counterplay with ...a5-a4. ''} 18. h5 $1 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: ', There's no need to lose a tempo with tho old-fashioned g4. ''} Rfc8 ({Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'On''} 18... gxh5 19. g4 $1 hxg4 20. fxg4 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: '!''} Nxe4 21. Qh2 Ng5 22. Bxg7 Kxg7 23. Rd5 Rc5 24. Qh6+ Kg8 25. Rxg5+ Rxg5 26. Qxh7#) 19. hxg6 hxg6 20. g4 ({Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Not the impatient''} 20. Bxf6 $2 Bxf6 21. Qh6 e6 $1 $10 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: '!' Bobby Fischer: '(threatening ...Qe5) and Black holds overything.''}) 20... a5 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: '; Now Black needs just one more move to get his counterattack moving. But for the want of a nail the battle was lost... ''} 21. g5 Nh5 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Chris Ward: 'Often this succeeds in blocking the h-file and halting White's attack. Alas because Black never got around to exchanging off White's light-squared bishop with the usual ... Ne5-c4 plan, he has lined himself up for some trouble.''} ({Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Vasiukov suggests''} 21... Ne8 {Vasiukov,E Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Vasiukov,E Bobby Fischer: 'as a possible defense; but White crashes through with''} 22. Bxg7 Nxg7 (22... Kxg7 $2 23. Qh2 $18) 23. Rh6 $1 e6 ({Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'if''} 23... a4 24. Qh2 Nh5 25. Rxg6+ $18) 24. Qh2 Nh5 25. Bxe6 $1 fxe6 (25... Qxg5 26. Rxg6+ $1 Qxg6 27. Bxc8 $18 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'threatening Rg1.''}) 26. Rxg6+ Ng7 27. Rh1 $18 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'etc.''}) ({Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'not''} 21... a4 $2 22. gxf6 axb3 23. fxg7 $1 bxc2+ 24. Qxc2 $1 e5 25. Qh2 $18 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'wins.''}) 22. Rxh5 $1 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: ', Fine wrote: "In such positions, combinations are as natural as a baby's smile." ''} gxh5 ({Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'No better is''} 22... Bxd4 23. Qxd4 gxh5 24. g6 Qe5 ({Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'if''} 24... e6 25. Qxd6) 25. gxf7+ Kh7 ({Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'if''} 25... Kf8 26. Qxe5 dxe5 27. Rg1 e6 28. Bxe6 Ke7 29. Bxc8 Rxc8 30. Rg5 $18 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'wins.''}) 26. Qd3 $18 { f3-f4 Ftacnik,Lubomir: ' f3-f4 Bobby Fischer: '!' Bobby Fischer: '(intending f4) should be decisive.''}) 23. g6 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Chris Ward: 'The f-pawn is pinned.''} e5 ({Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'On''} 23... e6 24. gxf7+ Kxf7 ({Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'if''} 24... Rxf7 25. Bxe6) 25. Bxg7 Kxg7 26. Rg1+ Kh7 27. Qg2 Qe5 28. Qg6+ Kh8 29. Rg5 Rg7 30. Rxh5+ Kg8 31. Bxe6+ Kf8 32. Rf5+ Ke7 33. Rf7+ $18 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'wins.''}) 24. gxf7+ Kf8 25. Be3 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Chris Ward: 'Now the b3-bishop is a monster and if it was required, it has the safe d5 square as a resting place.''} d5 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Chris Ward: '26 Bh6 was threatened and'' Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: '!' Bobby Fischer: '; A desperate bid for freedom.''} ({Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'On''} 25... a4 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Chris Ward: 'fell foul of''} 26. Qxd6+ Re7 27. Qd8+ $1 Rxd8 28. Rxd8+ Re8 29. Bc5+ $18 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Chris Ward: 'with mate next go.'' Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'mates.''}) ({Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'if''} 25... Rd8 26. Bh6 $18) 26. exd5 ({Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Not''} 26. Bxd5 Rxc2 $1) 26... Rxf7 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Chris Ward: 'Alas on 26. ..a4, White had 27 d6 anyway.''} ({Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'On''} 26... a4 27. d6 $1 axb3 28. dxc7 $18 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'wins.''}) 27. d6 Rf6 ({Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'On''} 27... Rd7 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'White can either regain the exchange with''} 28. Be6 $18 ({Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'or try for more with''} 28. Bh6 $40)) ({Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'And on''} 27... Rxf3 28. d7 $18 { d6+ Ftacnik,Lubomir: ' d6+ Bobby Fischer: 'threatening Qd6 mate.''}) 28. Bg5 Qb7 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Chris Ward: '28...Qd7 29 Qd5, threatening 30 Qg8 mate was hopeless.''} ({Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'On''} 28... Qd7 29. Qd5 $1 Qf7 ({Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'if''} 29... Rf7 30. Be7+ $1) 30. Bxf6 $18 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'wins material.''}) 29. Bxf6 Bxf6 30. d7 Rd8 31. Qd6+ {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: ', A mistake! Black resigns.''} ({Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Chris Ward: 'Leading to checkmate although it must be said that''} 31. Qh6+ $1 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Bobby Fischer: 'forces mate in three.''} Ke7 {(Ftacnik,Lubomir) Chris Ward} 32. Qh7+ Kf8 33. Qf7# {would have been quicker!}) 1-0

