{Bobby Fischer: 'GAME N. 24 Asking for trouble. The Winawer Variation has given Fischer consistent trouble. He has had the utmost difficulty cracking Black's tortoise-like shell; even his successes are unconvincing. Maintaining the same line of attack year after year has provided his opponents with ample opportunity to sharpen their defences. Darga's 12 ... f6 obliges Fischer, in order to get something out of the opening, to speculate on a pawn sacrifice (13 Ba3!?). Though Darga's reaction may not be ideal, he proceeds sensibly and equalises. Underestimating Fischer's chances, however, he falls prey to a scintillating middlegame attack. And so, once again, by virtue of his native ability, Fischer avoids the retribution that is the usual price for failing to secure an advantage in the opening. '} 1. e4 {Bobby Fischer} e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. e5 c5 5. a3 Bxc3+ ({Bobby Fischer: 'For'} 5... Ba5 {Fischer,R-Tal,M Leipzig ol 1960 Fischer,R-Tal,M Leipzig ol 1960 Fischer,R-Tal,M Leipzig ol 1960 Fischer,R-Tal,M Leipzig ol 1960 Bobby Fischer: 'see Game 23. Fischer,R-Tal,M Leipzig ol 1960'}) 6. bxc3 Ne7 7. a4 {Smyslov,V Smyslov,V Smyslov,V Smyslov,V Bobby Fischer: 'Diagram [#] Smyslov's favourite, largely responsible for Botvinnik's giving up the Winawer Variation.'} ({Bobby Fischer: 'Sharper is'} 7. Qg4 {Bobby Fischer: '. I felt that Black's carapace could be cracked only by positional means, but my results have been somewhat disheartening.'}) 7... Qc7 {Bobby Fischer: 'I may yet be forced to admit that the Winawer is sound. But I doubt it! The defence is anti-positional and weakens the kingside.'} ({Bobby Fischer: 'More usual is'} 7... Nbc6 8. Nf3 Qa5 9. Qd2 ({Bobby Fischer: 'After'} 9. Bd2 Bd7 10. Be2 c4 11. h4 $5 f6 12. h5 fxe5 13. h6 gxh6 14. Nxe5 Nxe5 15. dxe5 O-O-O 16. Rxh6 Ng6 $17 {Fischer,R-Padevsky,N Varna ol 1962 Fischer,R-Padevsky,N Varna ol 1962 Fischer,R-Padevsky,N Varna ol 1962 Fischer,R-Padevsky,N Varna ol 1962 Bobby Fischer: 'Black has secured an advantage; Fischer, R-Padevsky,N Varna ol 1962'}) 9... Bd7 10. Bd3 {Bobby Fischer: 'and now Black has two main continuations:'} c4 (10... f6 $1 11. O-O fxe5 12. Nxe5 (12. dxe5 $10 {Smyslov,V-Uhlmann,W Habana 1964 Smyslov,V-Uhlmann,W Habana 1964 Smyslov,V-Uhlmann,W Habana 1964 Smyslov,V-Uhlmann,W Habana 1964 Bobby Fischer: '=' Bobby Fischer: 'as Smyslov tried against Uhlmann at Havana, 1964'}) 12... Nxe5 13. dxe5 O-O 14. c4 Qxd2 15. Bxd2 Bc6 $10 {Fischer,R-Uhlmann,W Stockholm izt 1962 Fischer,R-Uhlmann,W Stockholm izt 1962 Fischer,R-Uhlmann,W Stockholm izt 1962 Fischer,R-Uhlmann,W Stockholm izt 1962 Bobby Fischer: '=' Bobby Fischer: 'Fischer,R-Uhlmann,W Stockholm izt 1962'}) 11. Be2 f6 12. Ba3 O-O-O (12... Ng6 13. O-O O-O-O 14. Bd6 $16 {Fischer,R-Uhlmann,W Buenos Aires 1960 Fischer,R-Uhlmann,W Buenos Aires 1960 Fischer,R-Uhlmann,W Buenos Aires 1960 Fischer,R-Uhlmann,W Buenos Aires 1960 Bobby Fischer: 'White keeps the edge; Fischer, R-Uhlmann,W Buenos Aires 1960'}) 13. O-O Nf5 14. Rfe1 Be8 15. g4 $5 Nfe7 16. Bf1 Bd7 $10 {Fischer,R-Weinstein,R ch-USA 1960 Fischer,R-Weinstein,R ch-USA 1960 Fischer,R-Weinstein,R ch-USA 1960 Fischer,R-Weinstein,R ch-USA 1960 Bobby Fischer: '=' Bobby Fischer: 'Fischer,R-Weinstein,R ch-USA 1960'}) 8. Nf3 b6 { a6  a6  a6  a6 Bobby Fischer: 'The idea is to eliminate the bad bishop with ... Ba6.'} ({Bobby Fischer: 'An alternative is'} 8... Bd7 9. Bd3 Nbc6) 9. Bb5+ $1 Bd7 ({Bobby Fischer: 'More radical is'} 9... Kf8 {Bobby Fischer: '!?'} 10. Bd3 Ba6) ({Bobby Fischer: 'On'} 9... Nec6 {Bobby Fischer: '(after 9 ... Nbc6 Black can no longer enforce ... Ba6)'} 10. O-O Ba6 11. Ng5 h6 12. Nh3 $16 {Bobby Fischer: 'is in White's favour.'}) 10. Bd3 ({Bobby Fischer: 'After the continuation'} 10. O-O Bxb5 11. axb5 a5 12. Ng5 h6 13. Nh3 Nd7 14. Nf4 O-O $10 {Ivkov,B-Byrne,R Sousse izt 1967 Ivkov,B-Byrne,R Sousse izt 1967 Ivkov,B-Byrne,R Sousse izt 1967 Ivkov,B-Byrne,R Sousse izt 1967 Bobby Fischer: '=' Bobby Fischer: 'Black has no problems. Ivkov,B-Byrne,R Sousse izt 1967'}) 10... Nbc6 {Bobby Fischer: 'Diagram [#] Black has gained a tempo, but whether his pawn belongs on b6 is a moot point.'} 11. O-O c4 ({Bobby Fischer: 'Not'} 11... O-O $2 12. Bxh7+ $1 Kxh7 13. Ng5+ $40) (11... h6 $1) 12. Be2 f6 13. Ba3 $5 {Bobby Fischer: 'Keeping tension in the centre at the cost of a pawn.'} (13. Re1 {Bobby Fischer: 'is solid but less aggressive. I tried this same pawn sac against Mednis in the 1962/3 US Championship with the slight but significant difference that Black's b-pawn was still on b7. The sac may well have been unsound in that game.'}) 13... fxe5 ({Mednis declined and castled kingside} 13... O-O {(Bobby Fischer) , but after} 14. Re1 $1 {got a cramped game} fxe5 {is met by} 15. Nxe5 {keeping the e-file open.}) 14. dxe5 ({Bobby Fischer: 'White doesn't have anything to show after'} 14. Nxe5 Nxe5 15. dxe5 Qxe5 16. Re1 Qxc3 17. Bh5+ g6 18. Bg4 (18. Bxe7 Kxe7 19. Qxd5 $2 Qxa1 $1 $19) 18... Qf6 $19) 14... Nxe5 ({Bobby Fischer: 'After'} 14... O-O 15. Nd4 $1 { f2-f4  f2-f4  f2-f4  f2-f4 Bobby Fischer: 'is followed by f4 and White has not been inveigled into misplacing his rook on e1.'}) 15. Re1 {Bobby Fischer: 'Diagram [#]'} N7c6 {Bobby Fischer: 'Black has a seeming multiplicity of defences:'} (15... N5c6 16. Ng5 $1 O-O $1 ({Bobby Fischer: 'after'} 16... h6 17. Bh5+ g6 18. Nxe6 Bxe6 19. Rxe6 gxh5 20. Qxd5 $1 Rd8 21. Qxh5+ Kd7 22. Rae1 $18 {Bobby Fischer: 'White regains the piece'}) 17. Bg4 Qf4 $1 (17... e5 18. Be6+ Kh8 19. Bxd5 $1) 18. Bxe6+ $1 (18. Nxe6 Qxf2+ 19. Kh1 Rf7 $1) 18... Bxe6 19. Nxe6 Qxf2+ 20. Kh1 Rf5 $1 21. Re2 $1 Qh4 22. Nd4 $1 Rh5 (22... Nxd4 $2 23. Bxe7) 23. Nf3 Qf6 24. Qe1 Re8 25. Re6 Qf7 26. Qe2 $1 Rh6 27. Re3 $36 { e1  e1  e1  e1 Bobby Fischer: 'followed by ... Re1 and Black's crushed.'} Rf6 28. Re1 $18 {(Gligoric 75)}) (15... N5g6 16. h4 $1 ({Bobby Fischer: 'on'} 16. Ng5 O-O $1 17. Bg4 Qf4 {Bobby Fischer: 'holds'}) 16... Nc6 17. Ng5 {Bobby Fischer: 'and it's difficult for Black's king to escape the criss-cross:'} O-O-O $2 ({Bobby Fischer: 'Or'} 17... h6 $2 18. Nxe6 $1 Bxe6 19. Bg4) ({Bobby Fischer: 'Finally. on'} 17... Nf4 18. Bg4 $36 {Bobby Fischer: 'continues the pressure.'}) 18. Nf7) (15... N7g6 16. Nxe5 Nxe5 17. f4) (15... Z0 {(Bobby Fischer) The threat is} 16. Nxe5 $140 Qxe5 17. Bh5+) 16. Nxe5 Nxe5 {Bobby Fischer: 'is just a transposition to the game.'} 17. f4 {Bobby Fischer: '?'} (17. Qd4) 17... Nc6 {Bobby Fischer: 'Diagram [#]'} ({Bobby Fischer: 'On'} 17... Nf7 18. Bh5 g6 19. f5 $1 O-O-O 20. fxe6 {Bobby Fischer: '!'} Bxe6 21. Rxe6 gxh5 22. Qxh5 $16 {Bobby Fischer: '+-' Bobby Fischer: 'White stands much better.'}) (17... Ng6 $2 18. f5 {Bobby Fischer: '!'}) 18. Bg4 ({Bobby Fischer: 'Better is the finesse'} 18. Bh5+ {} g6 (18... Kd8 {Bobby Fischer: '?'} 19. f5) 19. Bg4 {'' (Fischer)} O-O-O 20. Bxe6 Bxe6 21. Rxe6 Rd7 22. Qf3 Nd8 23. Rf6 $1 Re8 24. Rd1) 18... O-O-O (18... Kf7 $2) 19. Bxe6 Bxe6 20. Rxe6 Rd7 21. f5 { f5-f6  f5-f6  f5-f6  f5-f6 Bobby Fischer: 'To continue with f6, which gets a grip on the f-file.'} ({Bobby Fischer: 'On'} 21. Qf3 Nd8 22. Re5 Qc6 $10) 21... Nd8 $1 {Bobby Fischer: 'Driving the rook from its command outpost on the sixth rank.'} 22. Re3 Qf4 {Bobby Fischer: 'Darga is defending with vigour!' '!'} 23. Rf3 Qe4 24. a5 $1 {Bobby Fischer: 'Commencing operations against the castled king while Black's queen is temporarily cut off from the queens ide.'} Nc6 $2 ({Bobby Fischer: 'Correct was'} 24... b5 $10 {Bobby Fischer: 'with an equal game.'}) 25. axb6 axb6 26. Qb1 $1 Kc7 {Bobby Fischer: 'Diagram [#] The opening of the a-file is already decisive.'} ({Bobby Fischer: 'On'} 26... Kb7 27. Bc5 $18) ({Bobby Fischer: 'Or'} 26... Rb7 27. f6 gxf6 28. Rxf6 d4 29. Qb5 $18) 27. Bc1 $1 {'+-!'} Qe1+ {Bobby Fischer: 'There's no satisfactory defence to the threat of Bf4+.'} (27... Ne5 28. Bf4 Re8 29. Qb5 $18 {Bobby Fischer: 'penetrates decisively.'}) 28. Rf1 Qxc3 29. Bf4+ Kb7 30. Qb5 $1 1-0

