{Demuth,Adrien: 'A few months after starting to play chess, I received a book for my 8th birthday. It was "My 60 best games" by Bobby Fischer. I read it a couple of times, with my father. Of course none of us were able to understand all the subtleties, but we were already sensible to the beauty of most of the games. I am still a huge fan of his play, and I am glad to comment one of his games now! This game of Bobby Fischer, was played during his first Candidates tournament, in 1959. At only 16, Fischer managed to get very nice wins in this super strong tournament. This game against Pal Benko, shows his natural tactical skills. '} {Bobby Fischer: 'GAME N. 11 Unheard melodies.  Paul Morphy is the idol of all the romantics who pine for the swashbuckling chess of yesteryear; but it is rarely possible to succeed with that kind of flamboyance any longer since players now are more evenly matched. A rise in the standard of defense has necessitated a corresponding adjustment in the character of attack. In modern chess most of the beauty resides in the annotations. Brilliancies often exist only as grace notes - because the opposition anticipates and thwarts them with appropriate rejoinders. To the uninitiated, some of the most hard-fought struggles seem devoid of all bravura. That is the situation in this game. Confj-onted with a dozen beautiful outlandish losing variations, Benko chooses what appears to be a prosaic one. Is this "ugliness" not a by-product of skill? Though the reader may feel cheated, and the winner fj-ustrated, does it not argue for the perspicacity of the loser who sidestepped those seductive invitations?'} 1. e4 {Demuth,Adrien Bobby Fischer} c5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 d6 6. Bc4 {Demuth,Adrien: 'Fischer is facing a Classical Sicilian. He always has been fond of the Sozin Attack, that is caracterised by 6.c4 (and can be played against several types of Sicilian. It's not a surprise to see that it was already his favourite here.'} Qb6 {Demuth,Adrien: '!?'} ({Bobby Fischer: 'For'} 6... Bd7 {Fischer,R-Gligoric,S Bled ct 1959 Bobby Fischer: 'see game 13 (Fischer,R-Gligoric,S; Bled ct, 1959). By putting immediate pressure on the center, Black forces the Knight to a passive post.'}) 7. Nde2 ({Bobby Fischer: 'For 7 Nb3 see game 58, note to Black's sixth move. No good is'} 7. Ndb5 a6 8. Be3 Qa5 9. Nd4 Nxe4 $19 {Bobby Fischer: 'Etc..'} (9... e6 {Demuth,Adrien This is now considered to be the best.}) 10. Qf3 $1 {Demuth,Adrien} Nf6 (10... f5 $6 11. Nxc6 bxc6 12. O-O-O $1 $16) 11. Nxc6 Qc7 $8 12. Nxe7 Bxe7 13. Bb3 $16) ({Bobby Fischer: 'And..'} 7. Nxc6 $5 bxc6 {Bobby Fischer: 'only helps Black strengthen his center, but after'} 8. O-O $13 {Bobby Fischer: 'White has promising tactical chances.'}) 7... e6 8. O-O {Demuth,Adrien: 'In the Sozin Attack, White decides to castle to the kingside, and he will try to advance with f2-f4 later.'} Be7 9. Bb3 O-O 10. Kh1 {Demuth,Adrien: 'White can't really do without this move.'} ({Bobby Fischer: 'If..'} 10. Be3 Qc7 11. f4 {Demuth,Adrien: '?!'} Ng4 $1 {Demuth,Adrien: '!' Demuth,Adrien: ''!'' Demuth,Adrien: 'and White more or less has to give up his bishop.'}) 10... Na5 {Demuth,Adrien: '!?' Demuth,Adrien: 'Suppressing this annoying bishop is a very common plan, even if it takes a couple of tempi.'} 11. Bg5 Qc5 $1 {Demuth,Adrien: ''!''} 12. f4 ({Bobby Fischer: 'A finesse aimed at provoking'} 12. Be3 Qc7 $10 {Bobby Fischer: '=' Bobby Fischer: 'after which White's initiative is blunted.'}) 12... b5 {Bobby Fischer: 'Another virtue of Black's last Inove was that it freed this Pawn.'} 13. Ng3 {Demuth,Adrien: 'This is the first really important moment of the game. Black should have gotten rid of the light-squares bishop.'} b4 $2 {Bobby Fischer: 'Position after' Demuth,Adrien: '?!' Demuth,Adrien: ''?''} ({Bobby Fischer: 'Gligorich suggests simply'} 13... Bb7 {Gligoric,S}) ({Bobby Fischer: 'Also satisfactory is'} 13... Nxb3 $1 14. axb3 (14. cxb3 {Demuth,Adrien In these kinds of Sicilian, it's very usual to see White taking with the c-pawn (while the common principles tell us to use the a-pawn). The point is to have some play on the c-file.} b4 15. e5 (15. Bxf6 Bxf6 16. e5 bxc3 17. Ne4 Qb4 18. Nxf6+ gxf6 19. Qg4+ Kh8 20. Qh4 $11 {Forcing a perpetual check, but nothin more.}) 15... dxe5 16. Bxf6 bxc3 $1 17. Ne4 Qb4 18. bxc3 Qxe4 19. Bxe7 Re8 20. Bd6 Bb7 $132 {The battle is very tensed and approximately equal.}) 14... Bb7 ({Bobby Fischer: 'Or..'} 14... b4) 15. Nh5 Kh8 $10 {Bobby Fischer: '=' Bobby Fischer: 'The text exposes Black to a vicious attack.'}) (13... h6 $2 {Demuth,Adrien As often, this is too slow.} 14. Bxf6 Bxf6 15. e5 dxe5 16. Nce4 Qe7 17. Nh5 $18 {White has too many threats, Black can't handle it.}) 14. e5 $1 {Demuth,Adrien: '!?' Demuth,Adrien: ''!''} (14. Bxf6 $5 {Demuth,Adrien This was also a possible move order.} gxf6 15. Na4 Qc7 16. Qh5 $40) 14... dxe5 ({Bobby Fischer: 'A.) It's too late now for'} 14... Nxb3 {Demuth,Adrien: '??'} 15. exf6 gxf6 ({Bobby Fischer: 'If..'} 15... Bxf6 16. Nce4) 16. Bh6 $18 {Bobby Fischer: 'Etc..'}) ({Bobby Fischer: 'B.)'} 14... bxc3 {Demuth,Adrien: '?'} 15. exf6 Bxf6 ({Bobby Fischer: 'If..'} 15... gxf6 16. Bh6 f5 17. Nh5 $40 {Bobby Fischer: 'threatening to bring the Queen to g3)'} (17. Rf3 $18 {Demuth,Adrien})) 16. Bxf6 gxf6 17. Ne4 $1 Qf5 18. Nxd6 Qg6 19. Rf3 $18 {, Judovic,A Bobby Fischer: 'with a decisive attack . Judovic,A'} Kh8 20. Rg3 Qh6 21. Qg4 { g8+! +- Bobby Fischer: '(threatening Qg8+! +-'} Qg6 22. Qh4) 15. Bxf6 {Demuth,Adrien: 'Once again, Black has a vast choice. It wasn't easy, and he couldn't find the best move.'} gxf6 {Demuth,Adrien: '?' Demuth,Adrien: 'After this move, Fischer won't give another chance.'} ({Bobby Fischer: 'A.) On..'} 15... Bxf6 16. Nce4 Qe7 ({Bobby Fischer: 'If..'} 16... Qd4 {Demuth,Adrien: '?' Demuth,Adrien: 'This is losing by force, and the finish is really elegant.'} 17. Nxf6+ gxf6 18. Qg4+ Kh8 19. Rad1 {Demuth,Adrien: '!'} Qxb2 {Demuth,Adrien: '?'} 20. Nh5 Rg8 21. Qxg8+ {Demuth,Adrien: '!'} Kxg8 22. Rd8# {Bobby Fischer: 'Mate.'}) 17. Nh5 $1 Kh8 ({Bobby Fischer: 'If..'} 17... Bh4 18. fxe5 { g4, Gligoric,S Bobby Fischer: 'followed by Qg4, Gligoric,S'}) 18. Nexf6 gxf6 19. fxe5 fxe5 20. Nf6 { h5 +- Bobby Fischer: 'threatening Qh5 +- Wins.' Demuth,Adrien: '+-'}) ({Bobby Fischer: 'B.) The best chance is'} 15... bxc3 $1 16. Ne4 (16. Bxe5 $5 {Demuth,Adrien} cxb2 17. Bxb2 Bb7 18. Qg4 g6 $1 $15 {This may look very dangerous, but White is actually unable to make use of the long dark squared diagonal.}) 16... Qb4 17. Qg4 Bxf6 18. Nxf6+ Kh8 19. Qh4 h6 20. Ng4 $40 { xh6 Bobby Fischer: 'threatening Nxh6 with a strong attack.'} Nxb3 $1 {Demuth,Adrien} (20... cxb2 {Demuth,Adrien} 21. Rad1 $1 Nxb3 22. Nxh6 $1 Nd2 $1 23. a3 $1 {This little move decides the game.} Qb7 (23... Qc5 24. Rxd2 $18) (23... Qc3 $4 24. Nf5+ Kg8 25. Ne7#) 24. fxe5 $1 Nxf1 25. Ng4+ Kg8 26. Nf6+ gxf6 27. exf6 $18 {And Black is defenceless against the coming mate.}) 21. Nxh6 Nxa1 22. a3 Qb7 23. fxe5 f5 $3 24. exf6 Rxf6 25. Ng4+ Kg8 26. Nxf6+ gxf6 27. Qxf6 Qg7 $13 {And this is still a really complicated position, with at least a draw for White.}) 16. Nce4 {Demuth,Adrien: '!'} Qd4 {Bobby Fischer: 'Position after' Demuth,Adrien: '?!'} ({Bobby Fischer: 'Benko gave this move a lot of thought. On the alternative'} 16... Qc7 17. Nh5 $1 ({Bobby Fischer: 'Black holds after..'} 17. Qg4+ Kh8 18. Qh4 Rg8 19. Nxf6 Rg7 20. Qh6 Bb7 $1) 17... f5 (17... Kh8 $1 {Demuth,Adrien The last way to hold, but the position remains bad.} 18. Nexf6 $1 Qd8 19. fxe5 $16) 18. Nhf6+ $1 Kg7 19. Qh5 $1 Bxf6 ({Bobby Fischer: 'Not..'} 19... h6 20. Rf3 {Demuth,Adrien: '+-'} Rh8 (20... exf4 21. Rh3 Rh8 22. Ne8+ $1 $18) 21. Rg3+ Kf8 22. Qxh6+ $18) 20. Nxf6 {Demuth,Adrien: '+-' Demuth,Adrien: 'Black can't take on f6, so it's completely lost.'} h6 ({Bobby Fischer: 'If..'} 20... Rh8 21. Qg5+ Kf8 22. Qh6+ Ke7 23. Qh4 Kf8 24. Nxh7+ $18 {Bobby Fischer: 'Wins the exchange.'}) 21. Rf3 $1 Rh8 ({Bobby Fischer: 'Not..'} 21... Kxf6 22. Qh4+ Kg7 23. Rg3+ Kh7 24. Rh3 $18 {Bobby Fischer: 'Wins.'}) 22. Ne8+ Rxe8 23. Rg3+ Kf8 24. Qxh6+ Ke7 25. Qh4+ Kd6 ({Bobby Fischer: 'If..'} 25... Kf8 26. Rh3 $1 Qd8 27. Qh6+ Ke7 28. Qg5+ $18 {Bobby Fischer: 'Wins the Queen.'}) 26. Rd3+ Kc6 ({Bobby Fischer: 'If..'} 26... Kc5 27. Ba4 $1 { f2+ Bobby Fischer: 'Threatens Qf2+'}) 27. Ba4+ Kb7 28. Bxe8 $18 {Bobby Fischer: 'Wins material.'}) 17. Qh5 $1 $18 {Bobby Fischer: 'Already Black is without a satisfactory defense.' Demuth,Adrien: '!' Demuth,Adrien: ''+-!'' Demuth,Adrien: 'Black is defenceless, but he will try to make Fischer's task as hard as possible.'} Nxb3 ({Bobby Fischer: 'A.) On..'} 17... Kh8 18. Qh6 Rg8 ({Bobby Fischer: 'If..'} 18... exf4 19. Nh5 $18 {Bobby Fischer: 'Wins' Demuth,Adrien: ''+-''} Rg8 {Demuth,Adrien} 20. Nexf6 Bxf6 21. Nxf6 Rg7 22. Rad1 Qb6 23. Nh5 $18) 19. Nxf6 $18 {Bobby Fischer: 'Etc..'}) ({Bobby Fischer: 'B.)'} 17... exf4 18. Nf5 $1 {Demuth,Adrien: 'A very nice blow.'} exf5 {Demuth,Adrien: 'I think I had never seen quadruple pawns before.'} 19. Rxf4 {Demuth,Adrien: 'The point is that Black is unable to properly protect h7.'} Qxe4 (19... fxe4 {Bobby Fischer: 'Otherwise'} 20. Rh4 $18) 20. Rxe4 fxe4 21. Qxa5 $18 {Bobby Fischer: 'Wins. (This key line wouldn't work had Black interpolated 13 ... Nxb3! earlier!)'}) ({Bobby Fischer: 'C.)'} 17... Kg7 {Lombardy,W} 18. Rad1 Qxb2 19. Qh4 Bb7 20. Nxf6 $1 $18) 18. Qh6 $1 exf4 ({Bobby Fischer: 'On..'} 18... f5 19. c3 $1 {Bobby Fischer: 'is devastating: e.g.,'} (19. Ng5 $1 {Demuth,Adrien} Bxg5 20. Qxg5+ Kh8 21. Qf6+ Kg8 22. Rad1 $18 {If the queen moves, 23.h5 will mate.}) 19... bxc3 20. bxc3 Qb6 {Bobby Fischer: 'Any.'} 21. Nh5 $18 {Bobby Fischer: 'forces mate.'}) 19. Nh5 f5 20. Rad1 {Demuth,Adrien: 'The last finesse, White shouldn't leave his opponent have a free lunch on a1.'} (20. Nef6+ {Demuth,Adrien It was still possible to misplay, and to lose most of White's advantage.} Bxf6 21. Nxf6+ Qxf6 22. Qxf6 Nxa1 23. Rxa1 Bb7 $14 {White obviously keeps the better chances, but things are complicated!}) 20... Qe5 21. Nef6+ {Demuth,Adrien: 'Now, this is over.'} Bxf6 22. Nxf6+ Qxf6 23. Qxf6 {Bobby Fischer: 'Now it's skin and bones.'} Nc5 24. Qg5+ Kh8 25. Qe7 $1 Ba6 26. Qxc5 Bxf1 27. Rxf1 {Bobby Fischer: 'Black resigns' Demuth,Adrien: 'A really well organised attack, that made his opponent's position completely fall apart.'} 1-0

