{Bobby Fischer: 'GAME N. 50 Tour de force. As one of ten simultaneous clock games played on tour. at Davis College, this is a perfect example of the precept that if White makes a slip in the opening he is punished by loss of the initiative, while if Black makes a slip (since he is skating on thin ice from the very start) it is likely to be fatal. 6 ... d6 is the offender. With 9 Qh5 Fischer assumes a commanding control of space, but faces a strong defense which compels him to offer a piece in order to maintain pressure. Continuing with restraint and circumspection, he builds up the attack with a series of quiet developing moves - reminiscent of Morphy 's famous victory over the Duke of Brunswick at the Paris opera. When the time is ripe, Fischer throws everything at Black's King, including the proverbial kitchen sink. His show of brute force is handsomely rewarded. '} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bc4 Bc5 4. b4 $5 {Evans,W Bobby Fischer: 'The Evans was already analyzed to death by the 'nineties. But it still makes for enterprising chess. Evans,W'} Bxb4 5. c3 Be7 ({Bobby Fischer: 'Must be the trend. At least, on tour most players answered this way. For'} 5... Ba5 {Fischer,R-Fine,R New York 1963 Bobby Fischer: 'see game 44.Fischer,R-Fine,R New York 1963'}) 6. d4 d6 $2 ({Bobby Fischer: 'A mistake is usually much more serious in these open games. Black must return the Pawn with'} 6... Na5 $1 { Bobby Fischer: '>='} 7. Nxe5 Nxc4 8. Nxc4 d5 $1) 7. dxe5 Nxe5 ({Bobby Fischer: 'ON'} 7... Na5 $2 8. Bxf7+ $1 Kxf7 9. Qd5+ Be6 10. Qxa5 $18 {Bobby Fischer: 'WINS A PAWN.'}) (7... dxe5 8. Qb3 Na5 9. Bxf7+ Kf8 10. Qa4 $16 {Bobby Fischer: 'IS STRONG.'}) 8. Nxe5 dxe5 9. Qh5 $1 ({Bobby Fischer: 'In an earlier exhibition game I played'} 9. Qb3 {Bobby Fischer: 'but got nothing after'} Be6 $1 10. Bxe6 fxe6 11. Ba3 $5 ({Bobby Fischer: 'IF'} 11. Qxe6 Qd6 $10 {Bobby Fischer: '='}) 11... Qd3 $1) 9... g6 10. Qxe5 Nf6 {Bobby Fischer: 'Position after'} ({Bobby Fischer: 'ON'} 10... f6 11. Qb5+ $1 c6 $2 12. Qb3 Kf8 13. Bxg8 $1 $18 {Bobby Fischer: 'WINS.'}) 11. Ba3 $1 {Bobby Fischer: 'Incredible how Black is so completely immobilized by this one move!'} Rf8 $8 {Bobby Fischer: ''} ({Bobby Fischer: 'The only way to get relief.'} 11... Kf8 $2 {Bobby Fischer: 'works in all lines except'} 12. Qxf6 $1 $18) 12. O-O Ng4 (12... Nd7 { b6;  (?) Bobby Fischer: 'FOLLOWED BY....Nb6 might be better, but this certainly looked good at the time.'}) 13. Qg3 Bxa3 14. Nxa3 Qe7 $1 15. Bb5+ $1 $36 {Bobby Fischer: 'That's how. This forces Black to weaken himself on d6, although White must sacrifice a piece to exploit it. Position after'} ({Bobby Fischer: 'Apparently Black has freed his game. If now'} 15. Nc2 Qe5) ({Bobby Fischer: 'virtually forces an exchange of Queens'} 15. Nb5 {Bobby Fischer: 'is rendered hannless by'} Ne5 {Bobby Fischer: 'How's White to sustain the initiative?'}) 15... c6 ({Bobby Fischer: 'ON'} 15... Bd7 16. Qxc7 ({Bobby Fischer: 'NOT'} 16. Qxg4 c6 $1)) 16. Nc4 $1 Qe6 $1 ({Bobby Fischer: 'Some fascinating possibilities appear after'} 16... cxb5 17. Nd6+ Kd8 18. Rfd1 Bd7 19. Nxb7+ Kc8 20. Nd6+ Kd8 21. Rd4 $1 Ne5 22. Rad1 Kc7 ({Bobby Fischer: 'IF'} 22... g5 23. Nf5 Qe8 24. Qxe5 $1 Qxe5 25. Rxd7+ Ke8 ({Bobby Fischer: 'IF'} 25... Kc8 26. Ne7+ $1 $18 {Bobby Fischer: 'WINS.'}) 26. Re7+ $1 Qxe7 27. Ng7# {Bobby Fischer: 'MATE'}) 23. f4 Ng4 24. h3 Nf6 25. f5 Kb6 26. Qe3 Kc7 ({Bobby Fischer: 'AFTER'} 26... Ka6 27. a4 $18 {Bobby Fischer: 'SMASHES BLACK)'}) 27. Rc4+ $1 bxc4 ({Bobby Fischer: 'IF'} 27... Kd8 28. Qc5 {Bobby Fischer: 'ANYWAY'}) 28. Qc5+ Bc6 ({Bobby Fischer: 'IF'} 28... Kd8 29. Qa5# {Bobby Fischer: 'MATE'}) ({Bobby Fischer: 'OR'} 28... Kb8 29. Rb1+) 29. Nb5+ $18 {[%cal Rc5e7] Bobby Fischer: 'ETC....Black may not have seen the mate, but he suspected the worst!'}) 17. Rad1 ({Bobby Fischer: 'Piling on the pressure. White mustn't amateurishly rush in with'} 17. Qc7 Qd7 $1 {Bobby Fischer: 'FORCING HIM TO SIMPLIFY BY'} 18. Nd6+ Ke7 19. Nxc8+ Raxc8 20. Qxd7+ Kxd7 $10 {Bobby Fischer: '=' Bobby Fischer: 'etc., and the advantage has evaporated.'}) 17... cxb5 ({Bobby Fischer: 'He might as well take it since after'} 17... Bd7 18. Nd6+ Ke7 19. Bc4 $18 {Bobby Fischer: 'White wins a Pawn without any risk.'}) 18. Qc7 Bd7 {Bobby Fischer: 'FORCED'} 19. Nd6+ Ke7 {Bobby Fischer: 'Position after'} 20. Nf5+ $1 gxf5 ({Bobby Fischer: 'The attack needs fresh fuel. Material is not what counts now, but open lines. Black is forced to capture against his will'} 20... Ke8 {Bobby Fischer: 'is out because of'} 21. Ng7+ $18) ({Bobby Fischer: 'AND'} 20... Kf6 21. Rd6 gxf5 22. Qxd7 $1 $18 {Bobby Fischer: 'WINS OUTRIGHT.'}) 21. exf5 Rac8 ({Bobby Fischer: 'ON'} 21... Qxf5 22. Qd6+ Kd8 (22... Ke8 23. Rfe1+ Be6 24. Qd7# {Bobby Fischer: 'MATE'}) 23. Qxf8+ Kc7 24. Qxa8 $18 {Bobby Fischer: 'WINS.'}) 22. Rxd7+ $1 Qxd7 23. f6+ $1 ({Bobby Fischer: 'Originally I intended'} 23. Re1+ Ne5 24. Rxe5+ Kf6 25. Qxd7 Kxe5 26. Qxb5+ $18 {Bobby Fischer: 'with a won ending. But then I remembered Emanuel Lasker's maxim: "When you see a good move - wait - don't play ityou might find a better one."'}) 23... Nxf6 {Bobby Fischer: 'Position after'} ({Bobby Fischer: 'NOT'} 23... Ke8 $2 24. Re1+ Qe6 25. Qxc8# {Bobby Fischer: 'MATE'}) (23... Kxf6 24. Qxd7) 24. Re1+ {Bobby Fischer: 'Note the amusing piece configuration. All Black's pieces are stepping on each other's toes.'} Ne4 $8 {Bobby Fischer: '' Bobby Fischer: 'The only legal move!'} 25. Rxe4+ Kf6 26. Qxd7 Rfd8 27. Qg4 ({Bobby Fischer: 'Here I forgot Lasker's maxim.'} 27. Qe7+ { Bobby Fischer: 'would have forced mate in four.'} Kg6 {Bobby Fischer: 'Black resigns'} (27... Kf5 28. Qe5+ Kg6 29. Rg4+ Kh6 30. Qg5#) 28. Rg4+ Kf5 29. Rg5+ Kf4 30. Qe3#) 1-0

