{Chess Informant Ivkov,Borislav: 'Ivkov,B: 'Chess Informant''} 1. e4 {Ivkov,Borislav Ivkov,Borislav Ivkov,Borislav} c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 e6 6. Bc4 {Ivkov,Borislav: 'Nick Conticello: 'Fischer's pet line which now bears his name. ''} a6 7. Bb3 b5 8. O-O Bb7 {Ivkov,Borislav: 'Nick Conticello: '?!''} ({Ivkov,Borislav: 'Nick Conticello: 'Chiefly as a result of this game, ''} 8... Be7 {Ivkov,Borislav: 'Nick Conticello: '!' Nick Conticello: 'is now generally accepted as the best defence. You can find discussion of that move elsewhere in this text, including in Nikolenko-Nagy in Chapter Two.''} 9. f4 O-O 10. e5 (10. f5 b4 $1) 10... dxe5 11. fxe5 Nfd7 12. Bf4 Nc5) 9. Re1 {Ivkov,Borislav: 'Nick Conticello: '!' Nick Conticello: 'Fischer was not the first to play this move, but he was the first to demonstrate its full power. ''} Nbd7 (9... Be7 $2 10. Bxe6 $1) {Ivkov,Borislav: 'Nick Conticello: 'After''} 10. Bg5 $1 {Ivkov,Borislav: 'Nick Conticello: 'Black is in a quandary.''} h6 (10... Nc5 11. Bd5 h6 {Ivkov,Borislav: 'Nick Conticello: 'rather than Honfi's ''} 12. Bxb7 {Ivkov,Borislav: 'Nick Conticello: ',''} (12. Bxf6 $1 {Ivkov,Borislav} Qxf6 13. b4 $1 exd5 14. exd5+ $1 {White should be doing pretty well.}) 12... Nxb7 13. Bh4 Rc8 14. a4 b4 15. Nd5 $5 exd5 16. exd5+ Kd7 17. Nc6 $13) (10... Z0 {Ivkov,Borislav}) ({. He cannot play} 10... Be7 {(Ivkov,Borislav) because of} 11. Bxf6 $1 {.}) 11. Bh4 $5 ({Ivkov,Borislav: 'Nick Conticello: 'Fischer is content to lie in wait, but objectively''} 11. Bxf6 $1 {Ivkov,Borislav: 'Nick Conticello: 'is probably stronger. King gives''} Nxf6 (11... Qxf6 12. a4 b4 13. Na2 a5 14. c3 $16) {Ivkov,Borislav: 'Nick Conticello: 'while Ivkov in 'Informator' suggests''} 12. a4 $1 (12. Qf3 {(Ivkov,Borislav) as promising for White,}) 12... b4 13. Na2 Nxe4 14. Nxb4 {Ivkov,Borislav: 'Nick Conticello: '.''} d5 15. Nbc6 Qb6 16. c4 $3 $16) 11... Nc5 $2 {Ivkov,Borislav: 'Nick Conticello: 'Walking right into the trap. ''} ({Ivkov,Borislav: 'Nick Conticello: 'Kavalek gives''} 11... g5 {Ivkov,Borislav: 'Nick Conticello: '!''} 12. Bg3 Ne5 {Ivkov,Borislav: 'Nick Conticello: 'as playable. King continues here with''} 13. Bxe6 $5 {Ivkov,Borislav} fxe6 14. Nxe6 Qd7 15. Nd5 {which he likes for White.}) {Ivkov,Borislav: 'Nick Conticello: 'but White might transpose to Fischer-Rubinetti with ''} 12. Bd5 $3 {Ivkov,Borislav: 'Nick Conticello: '!''} exd5 ({Instead} 12... b4 {(Ivkov,Borislav) is Tal-Mukhin from Chapter One.}) 13. exd5+ Kd7 ({White wins after} 13... Be7 $2 {Ivkov,Borislav} 14. Nf5 {.}) 14. b4 $1 Na4 15. Nxa4 bxa4 16. c4 {Ivkov,Borislav: 'Nick Conticello: 'Fischer is following earlier analysis by Maric. White has two pawns and a massive initiative for his piece. ''} Kc8 17. Qxa4 $18 Qd7 18. Qb3 g5 19. Bg3 Nh5 20. c5 {Ivkov,Borislav: 'Nick Conticello: '!' Nick Conticello: 'Here they come!''} dxc5 21. bxc5 Qxd5 {Ivkov,Borislav: 'Nick Conticello: '?' Nick Conticello: 'I find it amazing that the final moves of this game are glossed over in every published commentary I have yet read.''} ({No one has yet asked the obvious question: "Why not} 21... Bxd5 {(Ivkov,Borislav) - ?"} 22. Z0 ({. Clearly the answer is not} 22. c6 $2 Bxb3 23. cxd7+ Kxd7 24. Nxb3 Nxg3 {which trades too many pieces. Surely Mikhail Tal would not have repeated this line if that was all he could achieve!}) ({. I believe Fischer would have played} 22. Qc2 $1 {when I don't see a good defence for Black. The main line runs} Nxg3 23. hxg3 Bg7 24. c6 Qg4 25. Nf5 $1 Bxa1 26. Ne7+ Kc7 27. Nxd5+ Kd6 28. Ne3 $1 Qb4 29. Rd1+ Bd4 30. Qe4 $1 Kc5 31. Qd5+ Kb6 32. Nc4+ {and wins.} (32. Z0))) 22. Re8+ Kd7 23. Qa4+ Bc6 24. Nxc6 1-0

