{Bobby Fischer: 'GAME N. 58 Flawed masterpiece.  After Fischer dropped this miniature (his third loss in a row to Geller) Kurajica concluded: "He just cannot play against Geller ... Another Yugoslav, trIfunovich, opined at greater length:   Geller is one of the best-prepared players in the world as to opening theory. and Fischer cannot be superior in that respect ... Fischer [as White1 chose a very sharp and modern variation ... playing to win in the early stage of the game, as he usually does, and successfully, against weaker opponents, Fischer played better and attained a superior position, but it was very difficult to find the right solution over-the-board ... There was his mistake ... He has to impose a hard positional game, playing without pretensions for a win in the very opening.   Nowhere but in the notes that follow have the above errors been answered. Were it not for a momentary lapse (a3?), Fischer would have won this little gem on move twenty - despite his critics. '} 1. e4 {Bobby Fischer} c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 Nc6 6. Bc4 {Bobby Fischer: 'Position after'} e6 ({There is no apparent refutation to Benko's roguish} 6... Qb6 $5 {(Bobby Fischer) Saidy ventured it against me in the 1967 US Championship. ·After Benko,P} 7. Nb3 e6 8. O-O Be7 9. Be3 Qc7 10. f4 O-O 11. Bd3 $13 {3 it's a mutually hard game. Also see game 11. Fischer,R-Saidy, A ch-USA 1966 Fischer,R-Saidy,A ch-USA 1966}) 7. Be3 (7. Bb3 {(Bobby Fischer) cuts down Black's options. Fischer-Dely, Skopje 1967, continued:} a6 8. f4 $1 Qa5 (8... Na5 9. f5 $1 Nxb3 10. axb3 Be7 11. Qf3 O-O 12. Be3 Bd7 13. g4 e5 14. Nde2 $16 {Fischer,R-Bielicki,C Mar del Plata 1960 /+- Fischer,R-Bielicki,C Mar del Plata 1960}) ({with a crush in sight: FischerBielicki, Mar del Plata 1960.} 8... Qc7 9. f5 $1 Nxd4 10. Qxd4 exf5 11. exf5 Bxf5 12. O-O $40 {yields a strong attack)}) 9. O-O $1 Nxd4 $2 ({(a better try is} 9... d5 {>= but after } 10. Nxc6 $1 bxc6 11. f5 $1 {Whites on top If} d4 $2 ({Also on} 11... Be7 12. e5 Nd7 13. fxe6 fxe6 ({Or} 13... Nxe5 14. Bf4 $1) 14. Qg4 $16) ({Finally} 11... Bc5+ 12. Kh1 O-O $13) 12. Ne2 e5 {Either} 13. Ng3 $16 ({Or} 13. Qd3 $16 {retains the advantage.})) 10. Qxd4 d5 ({May be tanable} 10... Qc5 11. Qxc5 dxc5 12. a4 $1 $36 {puts Black in an excruciating bind)}) 11. Be3 $1 Nxe4 ({If} 11... Ng4 12. Kh1 $1 Nxe3 13. Qxe3 dxe4 14. Qxe4 $1 Be7 15. Rae1 {and mate is lurking in the wings: e.g.} g6 16. Nd5 $1 Bd8 17. Qe5 O-O 18. Ne7+ $18) ({wins. Slightly more accurate, but still bad, is} 11... dxe4 12. Nxe4 Be7 13. Nd6+ $16 {Etc..}) 12. Nxe4 dxe4 13. f5 $1 Qb4 ({If} 13... exf5 14. g4 $1 Be6 (14... Qb4 15. Ba4+ $1 b5 16. Qd5 $1 $18 {Wins.}) 15. gxf5 Bxb3 16. axb3 Qb4 17. Ra4 $1 Qxd4 18. Rxd4 $18 {and Black is in a curiously hopeless predicament: e.g.,} Be7 19. Rxe4 Kf8 20. f6 $3 Bxf6 21. Rxf6 $1 gxf6 22. Bh6+ {mates} Kg8 23. Rg4#) 14. fxe6 Bxe6 15. Bxe6 $1 fxe6 16. Rxf8+ $1 Qxf8 17. Qa4+ {resigns. 1-0; Fischer,R-Dely,P Skopje 1967 On 1-0; Fischer,R-Dely,P Skopje 1967} b5 18. Qxe4 Rd8 19. Qc6+ $1 Rd7 20. Rd1 Qe7 21. Bb6 $1 $18 {Dely,P} ({(About the only move that doesn't win is} 21. Bg5 $2 O-O $1)) 7... Be7 ({Bobby Fischer: 'Too routine. Black should start quicker action on the Q-side. More reasonable is'} 7... a6 { Bobby Fischer: '>='} 8. Bb3 Qc7 9. Qe2 ({Bobby Fischer: 'Or'} 9. f4 b5 10. f5 b4 11. fxe6 $5 {Geller}) (9. f4) 9... b5 10. O-O-O Na5 (10... Bb7 {Bobby Fischer: '7 is also possible, whereupon White might reply'} 11. f3)) 8. Bb3 (8. Qe2 a6 (8... Nxd4 9. Bxd4 O-O 10. O-O-O Qa5 11. e5 dxe5 12. Bxe5 {[%cal Gd2d8,Gf2f4,Gg2g4] Velimirovic-Geller/Budapest/1973/}) 9. O-O-O Qc7 10. Bb3 Bd7 11. g4 Nxd4 12. Bxd4 ({Bobby Fischer: '(Fishy. Better is'} 12. Rxd4 { Bobby Fischer: '>='}) 12... e5 13. g5 exd4 14. gxf6 dxc3 15. fxe7 cxb2+ 16. Kb1 Kxe7 $2 (16... Be6 $10 {Bobby Fischer: '=' Bobby Fischer: 'equalizes)'}) 17. Qh5 $1 {1-0 (28); Fischer,R-Pascual,n Davoa sim 1967} g6 {Bobby Fischer} 18. Qh4+ f6 19. e5 $1 dxe5 20. f4 e4 21. Qh6 Rae8 22. Rd4 Kd8 23. Rhd1 Kc8 ({(the beauty part is} 23... Re7 24. Be6 $3 Rxe6 25. Qg7 $18 {mopping up}) 24. Rxd7 Qxd7 25. Rxd7 Kxd7 26. Qg7+ Kd6 27. Qxb7 e3 28. Qb6+ {Resigns..1-0; Fischer,R-Pascual,n Davoa sim 1967 1-0; Fischer,R-Pascual,n Davoa sim 1967}) 8... O-O {Bobby Fischer: 'Position after'} 9. Qe2 ({Preparing Q-side castling and disallowing the reply ...Ng4 which would be the case after} 9. Qd2 {Bobby Fischer} Ng4) 9... Qa5 ({Bobby Fischer: 'Geller's attempt to improve on the customary'} 9... a6 10. O-O-O Qc7 (10... Qa5 11. Rhg1 $1 { g2-g4-g5 Tal-Bolbochan/Havanna ol/1966/}) 11. g4 Nxd4 12. Rxd4 $1 b5 ({Bobby Fischer: '(Tal gives'} 12... e5 {Tal,M} 13. Rc4 $1 Qd8 14. g5 Ne8 15. Rxc8 $1 Rxc8 16. h4 Nc7 17. Qg4 $40 { h4-h5 Bobby Fischer: 'followed by h5 , with a terrific attack)'}) 13. g5 Nd7 14. Qh5 Ne5 15. f4 Nc6 16. Rd3 Nb4 {Bobby Fischer} 17. Rd2 Rd8 18. f5 g6 19. fxg6 hxg6 20. Qh4 Nc6 21. Qg3 Ne5 22. h4 Bb7 23. h5 b4 24. hxg6 Nxg6 25. Rdh2 bxc3 26. Bd4 e5 27. Rh8+ $3 Nxh8 28. g6 $1 Bf6 29. gxf7+ Kf8 30. Rh7 $1 $18 {And White wins.Velimirovic,D-Nikolic,S Beograd 1964 Velimirovic,D-Nikolic,S Beograd 1964}) 10. O-O-O (10. O-O {(Bobby Fischer) also comes into consideration.} Nxd4 11. Bxd4 b6 $13 { 12... a6 Geller}) 10... Nxd4 ({Bobby Fischer: 'Apparently Geller rejected'} 10... Bd7 11. Ndb5 $1 Ne8 12. Bf4 a6 13. Nxd6 Nxd6 14. Bxd6 Bxd6 15. Rxd6 Qg5+ 16. Qd2 Qxg2 17. Rd1 Be8 18. Qf4 $36 {Bobby Fischer: 'with good pressure'}) 11. Bxd4 (11. Rxd4 { 12.d4} Bd7 12. g4 e5 13. Nd5 {Geller} (13. Ra4)) 11... Bd7 {Bobby Fischer: 'Position after'} (11... Qg5+ $2 12. Kb1 Qxg2 $2 ({Bobby Fischer: 'But interesting is'} 12... e5 {Bobby Fischer: 'instead of 12 Qxg2)'} 13. h4 Qxg2 14. Rdg1 Bg4 15. Rxg2 $1 Bxe2 16. Nxe2 exd4 17. Nxd4 $16 {Bobby Fischer: 'with an advantage If'} Nxe4 18. f3 $1 { f5 Bobby Fischer: 'followed by Nf5'}) 13. Rhg1 $1 Qh3 {Bobby Fischer} ({If} 13... Qxh2 {Bobby Fischer} 14. Rh1 Qf4 15. Rdg1 $1 e5 ({Or} 15... g6 16. Be3 Qe5 17. Rg5 $18) 16. Be3 Bg4 17. Qe1 Qf3 18. Rg3 $18 {wins the Queen.}) 14. e5 Ne8 ({On} 14... dxe5 15. Qxe5 $40 {carries to many threats}) 15. exd6 Bxd6 16. Bxg7 $1 Nxg7 17. Rxd6 $18 {and it's not a game any more.}) 12. Kb1 { xf6 Bobby Fischer: 'A critical position. White's immediate threat is 13. Bxf6'} (12. Rhg1 $6 Rfc8 {(!)} (12... Bc6 {! Kholmov} 13. g4 e5 14. Be3 Nxe4 15. Nxe4 (15. Nd5 {Kholmov}) 15... Bxe4 16. Bd2 $18) 13. g4 e5 (13... b5 $132) 14. Be3 Rxc3 15. Bd2 Bb5 $1 16. Qe1 Rxc2+ 17. Kxc2 Qa6 $146 { 18... d3, 18.... e2 Geller}) 12... Bc6 {? Geller} (12... Rfc8 $142 {Geller}) ({In a later round Sofrevsky tried to improve against me with} 12... Rad8 {(Bobby Fischer) , but got into trouble after} 13. Qe3 $1 a6 {Consequently, Sofrevsky chose 13... b6 ? Geller} ({Black now rejected a dangerous Pawn sac which must be examined very carefully:} 13... b5 $5 {But} 14. a3 $1 ({Not} 14. Bxa7 Ra8 $36 {with active play}) 14... b4 15. axb4 Qxb4 16. Bxa7 Qb7 17. Qb6 $1 Qa8 18. f3 {and Black has no good way to prosecute his attack.}) (13... Bc6 14. Bxa7 $6 Nd7 {Geller}) 14. Bxf6 $1 gxf6 ({(Black should reconcile himself to the loss of a Pawn after} 14... Bxf6 {>= } 15. Rxd6 Bc8) 15. Nd5 $3 Rfe8 ({If..} 15... exd5 16. Rxd5 Qb4 17. Rh5 $1 $18 {Wins} Bg4 18. Qg3 {Etc..}) 16. Nxe7+ (16. Qh6 $1 $18 {is a quicker kill)}) 16... Rxe7 17. Rxd6 Rc8 18. Qd4 Be8 $2 19. Qxf6 {Resigns.. 1-0; Fischer,R-Sofrevski,J Skopje 1967 1-0; Fischer,R-Sofrevski,J Skopje 1967}) 13. f4 Rad8 ({Bobby Fischer: 'If..'} 13... e5 14. Be3 $1 Bxe4 (14... Nxe4 $2 15. Nxe4 Bxe4 16. Bd2 $18 {Bobby Fischer: 'Wins'}) 15. Nxe4 Nxe4 16. Qf3 $16 {Bobby Fischer: 'with an advantage'}) 14. Rhf1 ({Bobby Fischer: 'I already had in mind the ensuing sacrifice. Also strong is 14 g4 - not to mention Trifunovich' s post-mortem suggestion'} 14. f5 $1 {Trifunovic,P} exf5 ({Bobby Fischer: 'Not..'} 14... e5 15. Bf2 d5 $2 16. exd5 Nxd5 17. Nxd5 Bxd5 18. Qxe5 $18) 15. exf5 Rfe8 16. Qf2 $36 {Bobby Fischer: 'with positional pressure.'}) (14. g4 {Kholmov} e5 (14... d5 15. exd5 $1 Nxd5 16. Nxd5 Bxd5 17. Bc3 Qc5 18. Bxd5 Rxd5 19. Rxd5 Qxd5 20. Qd1 Qc5 21. f5 exf5 22. gxf5 $16) 15. fxe5 dxe5 16. Bf2 Rxd1+ 17. Rxd1 Rd8 18. Rf1 $16 {Geller}) 14... b5 ({Bobby Fischer: 'On'} 14... d5 15. e5 Ne4 16. f5 $1 $36 {Bobby Fischer: 'maintains the initiative.'}) 15. f5 $3 {+- Geller} ({Bobby Fischer: 'The die is cast. I didn't want to lose a tempo playing it safe with'} 15. a3) 15... b4 16. fxe6 $1 (16. Nd5 exd5 17. exd5 Nxd5 18. Bxd5 Bxd5 19. Qxe7 Qxa2+ 20. Kc1 Rc8 $1 21. Qxa7 (21. Bxg7 Bb3 $1) 21... Qc4 $1 22. Rf2 Be4 23. Rdd2 b3 $40 {Geller}) 16... bxc3 17. exf7+ (17. Rxf6 $1 {Murey/Boleslavsky} gxf6 (17... Bxf6 18. Bxf6 gxf6 19. e7 $16 Qe5 20. exd8=Q Rxd8 21. Qc4 Be8 22. Qxc3 $16) 18. exf7+ (18. Qg4+ Qg5 $1 19. exf7+ Rxf7 20. Qe6 Rdf8 21. Qxe7 Qd2 $3) 18... Kh8 (18... Rxf7 19. Bxf7+ Kxf7 20. Qc4+ {21.c6 }) 19. Qg4 $1 { 20.e6} Rb8 (19... Bd7 20. Qh4 Kg7 21. Rd3 Rxf7 22. Rg3+ Kf8 23. Qxh7 $1) 20. Qe6 Qd8 21. Rf1 { 22.f6} Rb4 22. Bxc3 Rxe4 23. Rxf6 $1 Re1+ 24. Bxe1 Bxf6 25. Ba5 $3 $18 {Geller}) 17... Kh8 ({Bobby Fischer: 'Not..'} 17... Rxf7 18. Bxf7+ Kxf7 19. Qc4+ d5 20. Qxc6 {Bobby Fischer: 'Etc...'}) 18. Rf5 $1 Qb4 ({Not..} 18... Qc7 {(Bobby Fischer) I had intended} 19. Rdf1 {threatening Rxf6 if then  xf6} Nd7 ({Or on..} 19... Nxe4 20. Qg4 $18 {is bitter}) 20. Rh5 $1 $18 {(threatening Rxh7+ is decisive  xh7+}) 19. Qf1 $1 {Bobby Fischer: 'A hard move to find - it took around 45 minutes. The threat of Rxf6 must be attended to.'} (19. bxc3 Qb7 { 20... f7, 20... e4 Geller}) (19. Rxf6 Bxf6 20. Bxf6 gxf6 21. Qf2 Rxf7 $10 {Geller}) (19. Bxc3 Qxe4 {Geller}) 19... Nxe4 {[#]} ({Bobby Fischer: 'A fighting defense.'} 19... Nd7 {Bobby Fischer: 'loses immediately to'} 20. Rh5 Ne5 21. Qf5 h6 22. Qg6 $3 Rxf7 (22... Nxg6 {Bobby Fischer: 'allows'} 23. Rxh6# {Bobby Fischer: 'Mate.'}) 23. Bxe5 $18 {Bobby Fischer: 'Etc..'}) ({Bobby Fischer: 'On..'} 19... Rxf7 20. Bxc3 $18 {Bobby Fischer: 'Wins.'}) ({Bobby Fischer: 'Objectively best is'} 19... Ng4 { Bobby Fischer: 'But after'} 20. Bxc3 (20. Rh5 Bd7 $1 {Bobby Fischer: 'holds.'}) 20... Qb7 ({Bobby Fischer: 'If..'} 20... Qxe4 21. Rd4 $1) 21. Qf4 $40 {Bobby Fischer: 'with three Pawns for the piece and a winning attack in the offing.'} (21. Rh5 Bxe4 (21... Ne5 22. Qf5 h6 23. Qg6 $1 $18) 22. Bd5 Bxd5 (22... Bxc2+ 23. Kxc2 Ne3+ 24. Kd3 Qxd5+ 25. Rxd5 Nxf1 26. Rxf1 Bf6 $2 27. Rxf6 $18) 23. Qf5 h6 24. Rxd5 Nf6 25. Bxf6 Bxf6 26. Rxh6+ gxh6 27. Qxf6+ Kh7 28. Rh5 $18 {Murey})) ({And} 19... Bxe4 {(Bobby Fischer) gives White the pleasant choice of} 20. Rxf6 $18 ({Or..} 20. Rb5 $18)) 20. a3 $2 ({Bobby Fischer: 'Losing! A couple of hours after the game it occurred to me that White has a problem-like win after'} 20. Qf4 $3 $18 { h5 Bobby Fischer: '(with the threat of Rh5) Black has no adequate defense. A.)'} d5 ({Bobby Fischer: 'B.)'} 20... Nd2+ 21. Rxd2 cxd2 22. c3 $3 Qxb3 (22... Qb7 23. Bxg7+ $1 Kxg7 24. Qg4+ Kh8 25. Qd4+ $18) (22... Qc5 23. Kc2 $1 Bd7 (23... Qe5 $5 24. Rxe5 dxe5 25. Qxe5 Bf6 26. Qc5 (26. Qxf6 $2 d1=Q+ $1) 26... Bxd4 27. cxd4 Rc8 28. Kxd2 Ba4 29. Qe7 Bxb3 30. axb3 Rcd8 31. Ke3 $18) 24. Bxc5 Bxf5+ 25. Qxf5 dxc5 26. Kd1 Rd6 27. Qe5 Rd7 28. Qe6 Rb7 29. Bc2 { 30.f5 +- Geller}) 23. Bxg7+ Kxg7 24. Qg4+ Kh8 25. Qd4+ $18 {Bobby Fischer: 'Mates.'}) (20... cxb2 21. Rh5 $1 { xg7+} Nc3+ (21... Bf6 {Bobby Fischer} 22. Qf5 h6 23. Rxh6+ $1 gxh6 24. Qg6 $3 $18 {forces mate}) (21... Nf6 22. Rh6 { 23.f6} d5 23. Rxf6 Rd6 24. Rxd6 Qxd6 25. Qxd6 Bxd6 26. Rf1 $18 { 27.f6! +-} Bxh2 $2 27. Bc5 $18) 22. Kxb2 Nxd1+ (22... Rxf7 23. Qxf7 Nxd1+ 24. Kb1 $3 Qxd4 25. Rxh7+ $3 Kxh7 26. Qh5# {Bobby Fischer: 'Mate.'}) 23. Kc1 Rxf7 $8 $8 {(Bobby Fischer) Forced} 24. Bxf7 $1 {if} (24. Qxf7 $4 Bg5+ {and Black has no satisfactory answer to the threat of 25. Rxh7+ kxh7 26. Qf5+ and mates.}) 24... Bd7 (24... Nc3 25. Rxh7+ Kxh7 26. Qf5+ Kh6 27. Qh5#) 25. Bxg7+ {wins Black's Queen.} Kxg7 26. Qxb4 $18) 21. Qe5 Nf6 22. Rxf6 Bxf6 23. Qxf6 $1) 20... Qb7 21. Qf4 Ba4 $3 {Bobby Fischer: 'I didn't see it! Moreover, the strength of this resource didn't become fully apparent to me for another two moves.'} 22. Qg4 ({Bobby Fischer: 'Also futile is'} 22. Qh6 Bf6 23. Rxf6 Bxb3 $19 24. Rxd6 (24. cxb3 Qxb3 25. Rf2 Qxd1+ { 26... d4 -+}) 24... Ba2+ $1 $19 {Geller}) 22... Bf6 $1 23. Rxf6 {Bobby Fischer: 'Position after'} Bxb3 $1 {Bobby Fischer: 'At long last I saw the point of Geller's clever defense. As I was studying 24 Rf4, it suddenly dawned on me that 24..Ba2+ was curtains so White resigns'} 24. Rf4 {Bobby Fischer} ({After..} 24. cxb3 {Bobby Fischer} Nxf6 $1 $19 {is the quietus. It is not enough to be a good player, observed Dr Tarrasch; you must also play well.}) 24... Ba2+ $19 0-1

