{ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: 'Cuenta Anthony Saidy: "El día antes de que se jugase esta partida, Fischer dijo que derrotaría a su famoso adversario en 25 jugadas. ¿Pura bravata? ¿Colosal egotismo? ¿Guerra psicológica con el impresionante Najdorf? ¿O era fe mística?. Fe, realmente, Fischer la tenía. Y muchos de los que creían en él. Lo queno pudo anunciar de antemano, sin embargo, fue la revelación de una de las gemas más sorprendentemente originales de la tradición creadora del ajedrez". Larry Evans comenta en "Mis 60 memorables partidas": "La perdurable Variante Najdorf sigue siendo la favorita de Fischer, quien cuando se enfrenta a ella efectúa continuos experimentos. Aquí, contra el padre del sistema, emplea una continuación poco ortodoxa. Najdorf replica con energía y pronto se entabla una dura lucha. A fin de conservar la iniciativa, Fischer entrega un peón, con 7.d5. Najdorf rehusa la oferta, sólo para aceptarla tres jugadas más tarde, en circunstancias más desfavorables. El veterano gran maestro pierde pie en las complicaciones, permitiendo un devastador sacrificio que fija su rey en el centro, y si bien se defiende con precisión, se encuentra con que es tarde para compensar su indecisa táctica de la apertura. Así, pronto se ve envuelto en una red de mate, después de 24 jugadas. Antes que prolongar su agonía, opta, finalmente, por rendirse".''' Ris,Robert: 'The following game was shown in a group lesson organised by the Dutch Chess Federation with IM Edwin van Haastert, when I was about 13 years old. At that time Fischer's play made a big impression on me, not particularly because of the sacrifices, but more because of his calm follow-up between moves 16 and 20. Hope you like it too! '} 1. e4 {ChessBase Ris,Robert ChessBase ChessBase ChessBase: 'ChessBase II ChessBase II: 'González,JA''} c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 a6 6. h3 {ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: 'Esta jugada se trata de una idea del maestro norteamericano Weaver W. Adams. El plan blanco es atacar el caballo rey negro mediante el avance g4-g5, a fin de reforzar su control sobre la casilla "d5. Esta partida se hizo popular precisamente después de la partida que comentamos.'''} (6. Bg5 {Walther,E-Fischer,R Zürich 1959 Smyslov,V-Fischer,R Beograd ct 1959 ChessBase: 'Walther,E-Fischer,R Zürich 1959; Smyslov,V-Fischer,R Belgrade ct 195 ChessBase II: 'Walther,E-Fischer,R Zürich 1959 Smyslov,V-Fischer,R Beograd ct 1959''}) ({Ris,Robert: 'In the seventh round of the same event, Fischer played a model game of the Black side of the Najdorf:'} 6. Be2 {Pilnik,H-Fischer,R Mar del Plata 1959 Unzicker,W-Fischer,R Varna ol 1962 ChessBase: 'Pilnik,H-Fischer,R Mar del Plata 1959; Unzicker,W-Fischer,R Varna ol 1962 ChessBase II: 'Pilnik,H-Fischer,R Mar del Plata 1959 Unzicker,W-Fischer,R Varna ol 1962''} e5 {Ris,Robert} 7. Nb3 Be6 8. O-O Nbd7 9. f4 Qc7 10. f5 Bc4 11. a4 Be7 12. Be3 O-O 13. a5 b5 14. axb6 Nxb6 15. Bxb6 Qxb6+ 16. Kh1 Bb5 17. Bxb5 axb5 18. Nd5 Nxd5 19. Qxd5 Ra4 20. c3 Qa6 21. h3 Rc8 22. Rfe1 h6 23. Kh2 Bg5 24. g3 Qa7 25. Kg2 Ra2 26. Kf1 Rxc3 {0-1 Unzicker.W-Fischer,R Varna 1962. It's this game which influenced the further development and assessment of the weakened dark-square on d5 in the Sicilian Najdorf. Another absolute classic every Najdorf player should know!}) (6. Bc4 {Fischer,R-Tal,M Beograd ct 1959 Fischer,R-Bednarski,J Habana ol 1966 Fischer,R-Geller,E Skopje 1967 ChessBase: 'Fischer,R-Tal,M Belgrade ct 1959; Fischer,R-Bednarski,J Havana ol 1966; Fischer,R-Geller,E Skopje 1967 ChessBase II: 'Fischer,R-Tal,M Beograd ct 1959 Fischer,R-Bednarski,J Habana ol 1966 Fischer,R-Geller,E Skopje 1967''}) 6... b5 $5 {ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: 'Según Alberik O'Kelly, en vez de la jugada del texto, el negro tiene tres razonables defensas a su disposición: 6...e6, 6...c6, y 6...g6.'''} ({ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: 'Según Fischer, la réplica más aguda es'''} 6... g6 {Fischer,R-Reshevsky,S ch-USA 1962 ChessBase: 'Fischer,R-Reshevsky,S ch-USA 1962 ChessBase II: 'Fischer,R-Reshevsky,S ch-USA 1962 González,JA: 'y se jugó en Fischer-Reshevsky, USA-ch 1962'''} 7. g4 {Ris,Robert} Bg7 8. g5 $6 ({Nowadays people prefer either} 8. Bg2 {or}) (8. Be3) 8... Nh5 9. Be2 e5 10. Nb3 Nf4 11. Nd5 Nxd5 12. Qxd5 Nc6 13. Bg4 Bxg4 14. hxg4 Qc8 15. Qd1 Nd4 $6 ({A technical mistake, after which Black is left with only a poor bishop on g7. The engine mentions} 15... d5 $5 {as a reasonable try for Black.}) 16. c3 Nxb3 17. axb3 Qe6 18. Ra5 $1 f6 19. Qd5 Qxd5 20. Rxd5 Kd7 21. gxf6 Bxf6 22. g5 $1 {Another great move of Fischer in the 6.h3 Najdorf which always springs to mind. Fixing the weakness on h7 is more relevant than placing the g5 pawn on the colour of your own bishop. Fischer demonstrates great technique, developing pressure on all sides of the board:} Be7 23. Ke2 Raf8 24. Be3 Rc8 25. b4 b5 26. Rdd1 Ke6 27. Ra1 Rc6 28. Rh3 Bf8 29. Rah1 Rc7 30. Rh4 d5 31. Ra1 Rc6 32. exd5+ Kxd5 33. Rd1+ Ke6 34. Rd8 Kf5 35. Ra8 Re6 36. Rh3 Bg7 37. Rxh8 Bxh8 38. Rxh7 Re8 39. Rf7+ Kg4 40. f3+ Kg3 41. Kd3 e4+ 42. fxe4 Rd8+ 43. Bd4 Kg4 44. Rf1 Be5 45. Ke3 Bc7 46. Rg1+ Kh4 47. Kf3 Rd7 48. e5 Rf7+ 49. Ke4 Rf5 50. e6 Bd8 51. Bf6 Bxf6 52. gxf6 Rxf6 53. Kd5 Rf2 54. Re1 {1-0 Fischer-Reshevsky, New York 1962.}) (6... Nc6 {Fischer,R-Bolbochan,J Stockholm izt 1962 ChessBase: 'Fischer,R-Bolbochan,J Stockholm izt 1962 ChessBase II: 'Fischer,R-Bolbochan,J Stockholm izt 1962 González,JA: 'se jugó en Fischer-Bolbochan, Stockholm izt 1962'''} 7. g4 {Ris,Robert} Nxd4 8. Qxd4 e5 9. Qd3 Be7 10. g5 Nd7 11. Be3 Nc5 $6 {This knight isn't fighting for the d5-square.} 12. Qd2 Be6 13. O-O-O O-O 14. f3 Rc8 15. Kb1 Nd7 16. h4 b5 17. Bh3 $16 {Typical strategy for White to go for the exchange of light-squared bishops in order to gain more control over the d5-square.} Bxh3 18. Rxh3 Nb6 19. Bxb6 $1 {These kinds of move weren't so common still at that time, though nowadays most people would play it without spending a second!} Qxb6 20. Nd5 Qd8 21. f4 exf4 22. Qxf4 Qd7 23. Qf5 Rcd8 24. Ra3 Qa7 25. Rc3 g6 26. Qg4 Qd7 27. Qf3 Qe6 28. Rc7 Rde8 29. Nf4 Qe5 30. Rd5 Qh8 31. a3 h6 32. gxh6 Qxh6 33. h5 Bg5 34. hxg6 fxg6 35. Qb3 Rxf4 36. Re5+ Kf8 37. Rxe8+ {1-0 Fischer-Bolbochan, Stockholm 1962.}) ({Unos diez años más tarde, Najdorf prefería Ris,Robert: 'The main moves nowadays are'} 6... e6 {(ChessBase) (ChessBase II) (González,JA) y lograba equilibrar. Veamos: Ris,Robert: 'and'} 7. g4 d5 (7... b5 $5 8. g5 Nfd7 9. a3 Bb7 10. Bd3 Nc6 $13) 8. exd5 Nxd5 9. Nde2 Bb4 10. Bg2 (10. Bd2 Bxc3 11. Nxc3 Bd7 12. Qe2 Bc6 13. Rg1 Qc7 $11 {Gipslis-Geller, Moscow 1967}) 10... O-O 11. Bd2 Nb6 (11... Nxc3 12. Nxc3 Qc7 13. a3 Be7 14. Qf3 $1 $16 {Kurajica-Bukic, YUG 1972}) 12. Ne4 Be7 13. O-O Nc6 14. b3 f5 15. gxf5 exf5 16. N4c3 Bc5 17. a4 a5 $11 {Kurajica-Najdorf, Hastings 1971/72}) (6... e5 {Ris,Robert}) 7. Nd5 $5 {ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: '"La idea es explotar el hole de c6. Najdorf debió subestimar la fuerza de esta excéntrica jugada, que parece violar el principio de apertura de no mover una misma pieza dos veces" (Fischer).'''} ({Según el mismo Fischer, una buena alternativa es} 7. a4 {(ChessBase) (ChessBase II) González,JA}) ({Intending to exploit the weakened c6-square. Another approach is} 7. g4 {Ris,Robert}) 7... Bb7 $2 {ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: '"Los inminentes problemas de las negras tienen su origen en este desafortunado movimiento de alfil" (Fischer).'''} ({ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: 'Es claro que es malo'''} 7... Nbd7 $4 {ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: 'por'''} 8. Nc6 $18 {ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: 'ganando la dama''' Ris,Robert: 'is a funny way to win the queen.'}) ({ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: 'Y si'''} 7... Nfd7 8. Bg5 $1 h6 $2 9. Ne6 $1 {ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: '+-!' González,JA: 'Fischer''' Ris,Robert: 'is another fun trap.'}) ({ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: 'Si''' Ris,Robert: 'A safer option is'} 7... e6 8. Nxf6+ Qxf6 {Ris,Robert: 'when the queen is bit strangely placed on f6. I think a developing move like 9.d3 makes sense. However, Fischer's recommendation'} 9. c4 {Ris,Robert: 'can strongly be met by'} b4 $16 {ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: 'y la dama negras se halla mal situada y su flanco está debilitado (Fischer)'''} (9... d5 $1 {Ris,Robert and Black seizes the initiative in the centre.})) ({ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: '"Confusas eran las complicaciones derivadas de'''} 7... Nxe4 $1 {ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: '!?''' Ris,Robert: ''!'' Ris,Robert: 'is playing with fire, e.g.'} 8. Qf3 Nc5 {ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: 'y las blancas deben afrontar dos líneas principales:'''} 9. Nf6+ $2 (9. b4 $1 e6 (9... Nb7 $2 10. Qc3 $1) (9... Ncd7 10. Qc3 $1 Ra7 11. Bg5 $5 ({ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: 'o incluso'''} 11. Bxb5 {Ris,Robert: '!'})) (9... Na4 {Ris,Robert} 10. c4 $2 (10. Be3 $1 {is a better way to fight for an advantage.}) 10... e6 11. Nc3 {was seen in Short-Sarana, Moscow 2018 and now again} d5 $1 {would have given Black an excellent position.}) 10. bxc5 ({ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: 'si'''} 10. Nf6+ Qxf6 11. Qxa8 Qxd4 12. Qxb8 Qxa1 13. Qxc8+ Ke7) 10... exd5 11. Qxd5 Ra7 $10 {ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: '" Fischer''' Ris,Robert: ''=''} 12. c6 $14 {Ris,Robert}) 9... gxf6 10. Qxa8 Bb7 11. Qa7 Qc7 {Ris,Robert: 'does offer Black fantastic play for the exchange.'} (11... e5 12. b4 exd4 13. bxc5 Qe7+ 14. Be2 (14. Kd1 $1 {(ChessBase) (ChessBase II) González,JA}) 14... Nc6 15. Qb6 dxc5 16. O-O $1 $16 {ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: 'Fischer'''}) 12. b4 Ncd7 $44 {ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: 'y las negras tienen excelente juego por la calidad, según Fischer'''} 13. Bd2 {(ChessBase) (ChessBase II) González,JA} e5 14. Nb3 Nc6 15. Qe3 d5 16. c3 $14) (7... Nxd5 {Ris,Robert} 8. exd5 {is positionally ugly.} Bb7 9. c4 $1 {and the bishop is badly placed on b7.}) 8. Nxf6+ gxf6 {ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: ''''} 9. c4 {ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: '!' González,JA: '"Las blancas deben jugar con energía, ya que de otro modo se disiparía su ventaja" (Fischer).''' Ris,Robert: '!?'} ({ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: '"Después de la tranquila''' Ris,Robert: 'An interesting move, attempting to exploit Black's early ...b7-b5. Equally good is a solid move like'} 9. Bd3 {Ris,Robert: 'which isn't putting Black under pressure right away and probably not seriously considered by Fischer.'} Nd7 $14 {ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: 'sostiene la posición negra" Fischer'''}) 9... bxc4 {Ris,Robert: '?!'} ({ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: '"Si Najdorf hubiera evaluado correctamente las consecuencias de su decisión, habría elegido''' Ris,Robert: 'Opening the position (with your king in the centre and other pieces on the back rank still) simply feels wrong. A safer option is'} 9... b4 { ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: ' González,JA: '" (Fischer) y si''' ChessBase: '' Ris,Robert: 'but then'} 10. Bd3 {(ChessBase) (ChessBase II) González,JA Ris,Robert: 'and the inclusion of the move c2-c4 is in White's favour. White has a nice central grip, can develop his pieces and ideas to play on both sides as Black's kingside has been weakened and with a2-a3 the queenside can be opened as well.'} Nc6) ({ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: '"El anuario soviético de 1962 indica'''} 9... Bxe4 {Ris,Robert: '?!'} 10. cxb5 Bg7 11. Qg4 Bg6 {Ris,Robert: 'and now instead of'} 12. Nf5 {ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: 'con ventja, pero''' Ris,Robert: 'which was mentioned both by Fischer and Kasparov, I think White might also consider'} (12. f4 $5 {Ris,Robert . In both cases Black remains under serious pressure I would say.}) 12... O-O $13 {ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: 'es confuso" Fischer'''}) 10. Bxc4 Bxe4 ({ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: 'Según O'Kelly, es mejor'''} 10... Qa5+ {ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: 'pero esta variante ya había sido considerada por Fischer:'''} 11. Bd2 Qe5 {ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: 'pero ahora sigue'''} 12. Qb3 $1 Qxe4+ 13. Kd1 $40 ({o bien Ris,Robert: 'I love this move, preparing e1 and is clearly more ambitious than'} 13. Be3 $18 {(ChessBase) (ChessBase II) (González,JA) con ataque ganador}) 13... e6 {Ris,Robert} 14. Nxe6 $1 ({Even stronger than} 14. Re1 {which is Kasparov's recommendation.}) 14... fxe6 15. Bxe6 {and because of Black's coordination problems (king in centre, underdevelopment, b7 which requires protection) White quickly brings in his rook to e1 with a crushing attack. You hardly feel have just sacrificed a piece :)}) 11. O-O {Ris,Robert: '!' Ris,Robert: 'Simple chess: just completing your development!'} d5 {ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: '!'''} ({Si Ris,Robert: 'In the event of'} 11... e6 {(ChessBase) (ChessBase II) González,JA Ris,Robert: 'sacrifices on e6 may be considered, though probably many of us would first play'} 12. Re1 {[%csl Ye6][%cal Ye1e6,Yc4e6] con amenaza de sacrificio en e6 (O'Kelly) Ris,Robert: '!?'}) 12. Re1 {ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: '!' González,JA: 'Ahora la amenaza es 13.xe4 dxe4 14.xf7+ (O'Kelly)''' Ris,Robert: '?!'} ({Probably Fischer's only inaccurate decision, but in this complex position with a wealth of options both players overlooked Black's powerful resource on the next move. After} 12. Bb3 $1 {Ris,Robert intending a4 and installing a knight on c6, Black's position will be paralysed.} Bg7 ({Another nice line illustrating the effect of White's 12th move:} 12... e6 13. Re1 Bc5 14. Ba4+ Nd7 15. b4 $1 Bb6 (15... Bxb4 16. Nc6 Qb6 17. Rxe4 $1 dxe4 18. Rb1 {and White is winning.}) 16. Nc6 Qc7 17. Qg4 {and there are no good moves left for Black.}) 13. Ba4+ Nd7 14. Re1 O-O 15. Nc6 Qc7 (15... Qe8 16. f3) 16. Nxe7+ $18 {followed by taking on d5, leading to a position with extra pawn, bishop pair and better structure.}) 12... e5 (12... Rg8 {Ris,Robert: '?' Ris,Robert: 'is met by'} 13. Rxe4 $1 dxe4 14. Qh5 Rg7 ({ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: 'si'''} 14... Rg6 15. Qxh7 Rg7 16. Qxe4 Ra7 17. Nf5 {ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: ''''} ({ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: 'o bien'''} 17. Bf4)) (14... Qxd4 {Ris,Robert} 15. Qxf7+ Kd8 16. Be3 {with a crushing attack.}) 15. Nf5 {ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: ''''}) ({ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: 'Hubiera sido pasiva'''} 12... e6 13. Qh5 ({Again} 13. Bb3 $5 {Ris,Robert makes sense as well.}) 13... Bg6 14. Qxd5 Qxd5 15. Bxd5 Ra7 16. Bf4 Rd7 17. Nxe6 fxe6 18. Bxe6 Nc6 19. Rac1 {ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: '+-' González,JA: 'etc. Fischer'''}) (12... h5 13. Rxe4 $1 dxe4 14. Qb3 $1 Qxd4 15. Be3 $18 {ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: 'con ataque ganador (Fischer)''' Ris,Robert: 'followed by taking on f7 and d1.'}) (12... Nd7 13. Nc6 (13. Rxe4 $1 {Ris,Robert} dxe4 (13... dxc4 14. Nc6 Qc7 15. Rxc4 {with a free attack!}) 14. Bxf7+ $1 Kxf7 15. Qh5+ Kg8 16. Qg4+ Bg7 17. Nf5 {and White wins, as} Qf8 18. Nh6#) 13... Qc7 14. Bxd5 {ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: '' González,JA: 'etc. (Fischer)'''}) ({Ris,Robert: 'The remarkable'} 12... Bxg2 {Ris,Robert: '!' Ris,Robert: 'would have kept Black in the game!'} {Ris,Robert: 'After'} 13. Kxg2 dxc4 14. Qf3 {Ris,Robert: 'various annotators have tried to prove something in vain, as with correct play Black should be able to manage his position.'} Nd7 (14... Ra7 {Ris,Robert} 15. Be3 Rd7 16. Rad1) 15. Nf5 Rg8+ (15... e6 16. Rxe6+ $1 fxe6 17. Qh5#) 16. Kh1 e5 (16... e6 17. Qc6 { xe6+ ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: ' xe6+'' ChessBase: ' xe6+'}) 17. Be3 $18 {ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: '' González,JA: 'con iniciativa ganadora, a pesar del déficit de dos peones (Fischer)'''}) ({ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: 'Lo mejor relativamente es'''} 12... dxc4 { ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: ''' ChessBase: ''} 13. Rxe4 Qd5 14. Qf3 e6 {ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: '(Fischer)'''} 15. Bd2 $44 {(ChessBase) (ChessBase II) (González,JA) } (15. Bf4 $1 {Ris,Robert} Nd7 (15... f5 16. Nxf5 $1 Qxf5 17. Re5 $18) 16. Nxe6 fxe6 17. Rd1 Qc6 18. Rd6 $1 Bxd6 19. Rxe6+ Kf7 20. Qxc6 Kxe6 21. Qxd6+ {and White wins.})) 13. Qa4+ $1 ({ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: 'Es inferior''' Ris,Robert: 'The immediate'} 13. Rxe4 {ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: '!?''' Ris,Robert: 'is also good, though Fischer's idea to start with a check is more logical.'} dxe4 14. Qa4+ Qd7 15. Bb5 axb5 16. Qxa8 exd4 17. Qxb8+ Ke7 {ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: 'etc. (Fischer)'''} 18. Bd2 {[%cal Ga1c1] (ChessBase) (ChessBase II) (González,JA) con la idea de c1}) 13... Nd7 {ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: '?' González,JA: ''''} ({ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: 'Si'''} 13... Qd7 14. Bb5 $1 axb5 15. Qxa8 Bd6 16. Rxe4 $1 dxe4 17. Qxe4 $36 { f5 ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: ' f5 González,JA: '' González,JA: 'con la idea de seguir f5, con esquema dominante (Fischer)''' ChessBase: ' f5'} Bc5 {Ris,Robert} 18. Nb3 $1 (18. Nf5 $6 Qd1+ 19. Kh2 Bxf2 {is less convincing.}) 18... Qd1+ 19. Kh2 Bxf2 20. Bd2 Qh5 21. Bb4 {with a crushing attack.}) (13... Ke7 {(ChessBase) (ChessBase II) González,JA} 14. Rxe4 $1) 14. Rxe4 $1 dxe4 (14... dxc4 15. Nf5 {ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: 'conduce al mismo tipo de posición de la partida, con la particularidad de que las negras no tienen ninguna compensación material (Fischer)''' Ris,Robert: 'is hopeless.'}) 15. Nf5 $1 {ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: '+-!'''} ({ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: '"Quizás las negras esperaban'''} 15. Qb3 Qb6 16. Bxf7+ Kd8 {ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: 'con algunas chances de supervivencia" (Fischer)'''}) 15... Bc5 {Ris,Robert: 'Particularly this position had made a deep impression on me when I saw this game for the first time. I remember we were asked to look for the best continuation and greedy as we all were, only suggested developing ideas to make further sacrifices possible. I still remember the fun we had, until the games continuation was presented to us and we realised that Fischer's choice is more clever. '} 16. Ng7+ $1 Ke7 ({ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: 'O bien'''} 16... Kf8 17. Bh6 Kg8 18. Qb3 $18 {ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: 'con ejecución inmediata'''} Bxf2+ {Ris,Robert} 19. Kxf2 $1 (19. Kh1 {also wins of course.}) 19... Qb6+ 20. Qxb6 Nxb6 21. Nh5 Nd7 22. Rd1 {and mate is inevitable.}) 17. Nf5+ Ke8 {ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: '"El rey negro regresa a su casilla inicial, pero ha perdido el derecho a enrocar" (Fischer).''' Ris,Robert: 'So we are back with the same position, realising that Black is no longer allowed to castle.'} 18. Be3 {ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: '!''' Ris,Robert: '!'} ({ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: '"Tal sugirió''' Ris,Robert: 'Tal later suggested'} 18. Bh6 {Tal,M ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'Tal,M González,JA: 'pero después de''' ChessBase: 'Tal,M' Ris,Robert: 'but the text is much cleaner, depriving Black any hope of counterplay.'} Ra7 19. Rd1 Qb6 {ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: 'las negras siguen con vida. La textual impide todo contrajuego" (Fischer)'''}) 18... Bxe3 19. fxe3 { d6+ ChessBase: ' d6+ ChessBase II: ' d6+ González,JA: '' González,JA: '"El cambio de alfiles no facilitará la defensa negra. Ahora está en cartera la amenaza d6+" (Fischer).''' Ris,Robert: 'd6 becomes a big threat, although I somehow would feel sad moving the knight away from its amazing outpost on f5! :)'} Qb6 ({Si} 19... Qc7 {(ChessBase) (ChessBase II) González,JA} 20. Bb5 $1 ({mejor que} 20. Rd1 {que también es fuerte} Rd8 21. Rd6 $18) (20. Rc1 Kf8 (20... Kd8 21. Rd1) 21. Qb4+ Kg8 22. Qe1 Nf8 23. Bxf7+) 20... axb5 21. Qxa8+ Nb8 22. Rd1 $18 {etc.}) 20. Rd1 {Ris,Robert: 'Including the remaining last piece into the attack.'} ({ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: '"De nuevo, tras'''} 20. Bxf7+ {ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: '?!'''} Kd8 $1 (20... Kxf7 $2 {(ChessBase) (ChessBase II) González,JA} 21. Qxd7+ Kg6 22. Qg7+ Kxf5 23. Qg4#) 21. Rd1 Qb5 {ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: 'las blancas seguirían sin tener una victoria forzada" (Fischer)'''} 22. Qa3 $18 {(ChessBase) (ChessBase II) González,JA} (22. Qxe4 $40 {(ChessBase) (ChessBase II) González,JA})) ({También gana} 20. Bb5 $1 {(ChessBase) (ChessBase II) González,JA} Ra7 21. Qa3 $18) 20... Ra7 {ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: ''''} 21. Rd6 $1 $18 {ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: '"¡Definitivo!" (Fischer).''' Ris,Robert: '!' Ris,Robert: ''+-!''} ({ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: 'Tanto'''} 21. Bxf7+ Kd8 22. Qa3 $18 {(ChessBase) (ChessBase II) González,JA}) ({ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: 'como'''} 21. Nd6+ Ke7 {ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: 'permitían resistencia (Fischer)'''}) 21... Qd8 { ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: ' González,JA: '"Lo mejor, dadas las circunstancias" (Fischer).''' ChessBase: ''} ({ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: 'Si'''} 21... Qc7 22. Rxf6 $18 {ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: 'gana'''} (22. Rc6 {Ris,Robert is convincing, e.g.} Qd8 23. Qb4 {Threatening g7} Rg8 24. Rc8 Qxc8 25. Qe7#)) ({ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: 'Y si'''} 21... Qxb2 22. Bxf7+ $1 {ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: '(¡por fin!)'''} Kxf7 ({ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: 'si'''} 22... Kd8 23. Qa5+ Kc8 (23... Rc7 24. Be6 $18) 24. Ne7+ Kb8 25. Nc6+ Ka8 26. Nxa7 {Ris,Robert: 'and wins.'} (26. Rxd7 $18 {(ChessBase) (ChessBase II) González,JA})) 23. Rxd7+ Rxd7 24. Qxd7+ Kg6 25. Qg7+ Kxf5 26. Qg4#) 22. Qb3 Qc7 ({ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: 'Si'''} 22... Rf8 23. Ng7+ (23. Nh6 {(ChessBase) (ChessBase II) González,JA} Qe7 24. Bxf7+ Rxf7 25. Re6 $18) 23... Ke7 24. Qa3 $1 $18 (24. Qb4 $18 {(ChessBase) (ChessBase II) González,JA}) 24... Qc7 {Ris,Robert} 25. Rd5+ $1 Kd8 (25... Nc5 26. Rxc5 Qd6 27. Nf5+ {and wins.}) 26. Qxf8#) (22... Qc8 {(ChessBase) (ChessBase II) González,JA} 23. Bxf7+ Kd8 24. Qb6+ Qc7 25. Qb3 $18) 23. Bxf7+ Kd8 ({ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: 'Si'''} 23... Kf8 24. Bh5 { f7# ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: ' f7# González,JA: 'y no se puede evitar el mate''' ChessBase: ' f7#'} (24. Qe6 {Ris,Robert} Qd8 25. Bh5 {and mate follows.})) 24. Be6 {ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: '"A Najdorf no le apetecía prolongar la tortura" (Fischer).''' Ris,Robert: '!'} (24. Be6 {Ris,Robert: '!' Ris,Robert: 'and Black had seen enough. For example'} Rb7 25. Qa4 ({O bien} 25. Qd5 $18 {(ChessBase) (ChessBase II) González,JA Ris,Robert: '!' Ris,Robert: 'is absolutely hopeless for Black, as a loss of material can't be avoided. Judging from these analyses, 1962 wasn't such a bad year for Fischer with the Najdorf!'}) 25... Qc8 26. Qa5+ Ke8 27. Qxa6 Kd8 28. Bxd7 Rxd7 29. Rxd7+ Qxd7 (29... Kxd7 30. Qd6+ Ke8 31. Qe7#) 30. Qxf6+ Kc7 31. Qxe5+ Kb6 32. Qxh8 $18 {ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: 'Los análisis de la presente partida se han completado con notas de Robert Fischer, Alberik O'Kelly, Vasily Smyslov, Vladimir Tukmakov, Mikhail Tal.'''}) 1-0

