{Bobby Fischer: 'GAME N. 23 No holds barred. Their first encounter after Tal became world champion proves to be an old-fashioned slugfest. Typically aggressive, Fischer rapidly achieves a winning bind, but unwisely permits Tal to touch off 'a dazzling array of fireworks' with 14 ... Nxe5. The struggle see-saws for seven moves before settling in a perpetual check. The quality of this confrontation left little doubt that, in time, Fischer would yet take Tal's measure. He did just that less than a year later, after Tal had lost his return match with Botvinnik (Game 32). Reading Tal's palm, Fischer predicted: "The next world champion will be ... Bobby Fischer!" ' Obwohl nur 21 Züge lang und dann auch noch mit Remis endend ist die Begegnung zwischen dem frischgebackenen Weltmeister Tal und dem 17jährigen Fischer die zentrale Partie der Schacholympiade in Leipzig gewesen.} 1. e4 {Bobby Fischer Bobby Fischer Huebner,R Bobby Fischer} e6 {Tal soll 12 Minuten für diesen Zug gebraucht haben.} 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. e5 c5 5. a3 Ba5 ({A dubious alternative to the usual} 5... Bxc3+ {(Bobby Fischer) see Game 24. Fischer, R-Darga,K Berlin (W) t-ch FRG-USA}) 6. b4 {Bobby Fischer: '!' Bobby Fischer: 'Alekhine's recommendation.'} cxd4 (6... cxb4 {Bobby Fischer} 7. Nb5 $40 {yields a potent attack.}) 7. Qg4 {Bis heute ist die Güte dieses Zuges ungeklärt. Mit 7.b5 kann es Weiß ruhiger angehen.} Ne7 ({After} 7... Kf8 {Bobby Fischer} 8. bxa5 dxc3 9. a4 $1 {followed by 10 Ba3+ is strong (Lilienthal and Zagoriansky)}) 8. bxa5 ({Also good is} 8. Nb5 {Bobby Fischer}) 8... dxc3 9. Qxg7 Rg8 10. Qxh7 Nbc6 ({On} 10... Nd7 {Bobby Fischer} 11. Nf3 Qc7 12. Bb5 a6 13. Bxd7+ Bxd7 14. O-O d4 $5 {(Archives)} 15. Nxd4 (15. Bg5 {Huebner,R} Bc6 16. Bxe7 Kxe7 17. Qh4+ Ke8 18. Ng5 Qxe5 19. f4 $14 {Euwe ECO 2.Auflage 16/17 Fußnote 80} Qf5 $17) 15... Qxe5 16. Qd3 $16 {is better for White.} Qg7 {Huebner,R} (16... O-O-O {Huebner,R} 17. Qc4+ (17. Qxc3+ $2 Bc6 $19) (17. g3 Nd5 (17... Bb5 $2 18. Qxc3+ Nc6 19. Nxb5 $18) 18. Rb1 Qc7 $15) 17... Kb8 18. Bf4 Rxg2+ 19. Kh1 (19. Kxg2 Qxf4 $40 {-+  20... e5}) 19... Rxh2+ 20. Bxh2 Rh8 21. f4 (21. Nf3 Bc6 22. Qxc6 Rxh2+ $17) 21... Qe4+ 22. Rf3 Nf5 23. Qd3 (23. Qe2 $2 Ng3+ $19) 23... Qxd4 $19) (16... Rd8 {Huebner,R} 17. Qe3 Qg7 (17... Qd5 18. f3 Ba4 19. Ne2 Nf5 20. Qxc3 (20. Qf2 Qc4 $17 21. Bf4 Bxc2 22. Rac1 Rd2) 20... Bb5 21. Nf4 Qd4+ 22. Qxd4 Nxd4 23. Rf2 Nb3 $19) 18. g3 e5 (18... Nd5 19. Qe4 $10) (18... Ba4 19. Ne2 Nd5 (19... Bxc2 20. Qxc3) 20. Qe4 Bb5 21. Re1 $10 (21. a4 $10)) 19. Nf3 $14) 17. g3 e5 18. Ne2 Bb5 19. Qf3 Qh7 20. Re1 Bc6 21. Qe3 O-O-O $17 22. Qxe5 $2 (22. Nxc3 $2 Nf5) 22... Qxh2+) 11. Nf3 {Bobby Fischer: 'Diagram [#]'} (11. f4 {(Bobby Fischer) bolsters the centre but shuts in the queen's bishop and weakens the dark squares.}) 11... Qc7 ({On} 11... Qxa5 {Bobby Fischer} 12. Ng5 $1 Rf8 13. f4 $16 {(followed by the advance of the h-pawn) ties Black up.}) 12. Bb5 {Bobby Fischer: '!' Bobby Fischer: 'Harmoniously pursuing development without losing time.' Aus heutiger Sicht kann höchstens 12.f4 Chancen auf vorteilhaftes Spiel geben} ({Also playable is} 12. Bf4 {Bobby Fischer} Bd7 13. Be2 O-O-O 14. Qd3 Qxa5 15. O-O Rg4 16. Bg3 {Unzicker, W-Dueckstein, A Zürich 1959}) 12... Bd7 ({Not} 12... Rxg2 {Bobby Fischer} 13. Kf1 $1 Rg8 14. Rg1 $1 Rxg1+ 15. Kxg1 $18 {and Black's king remains hemmed in the centre while White merely marches his h-pawn to victory.}) 13. O-O ({Unsound is} 13. Bxc6 $2 {Bobby Fischer} Bxc6 14. O-O d4 $1 15. Ng5 Qxe5 16. Qxf7+ Kd7 $17 {with advantage for Black.}) 13... O-O-O $1 {Bobby Fischer: 'Diagram [#]' Nach} ({Bobby Fischer: 'After the game Petrosian suggested'} 13... Nxe5 {Bobby Fischer: 'but' Bobby Fischer: 'but' Bobby Fischer: 'but' Huebner,R: 'Petrosian,T'} 14. Nxe5 Qxe5 15. Bxd7+ Kxd7 16. Qd3 {Bobby Fischer: '!' Bobby Fischer: 'keeps White on top.' Bobby Fischer: '!' Bobby Fischer: 'keeps White on top.' Bobby Fischer: '!' Bobby Fischer: 'keeps White on top.' Huebner,R: '!' hätte Schwarz einige Probl