{Alexander Volzhin: 'This line was known not to be very good but it has received a certain amount of attention recently and from time to time it occurs even at the very highest level, mainly in Michael Adams' games.'} 1. e4 {ChessBase Alexander Volzhin} d5 2. exd5 Qxd5 (2... Nf6 3. c4 (3. Bb5+ Bd7 4. Bc4 Bg4 5. f3 Bf5 (5... Bc8) 6. g4 $1 Bc8 7. Nc3 Nbd7 8. g5 Nb6 9. Bb5+ Nfd7 10. f4 Nxd5 11. Nxd5 c6 12. Bc4 cxd5 13. Bxd5 $18 {Fischer,R-Bergraser,C Monte Carlo 1967}) (3. d4)) 3. Nc3 Qd8 (3... Qa5 4. d4 Nf6 5. Nf3 Nc6 6. d5 $5 (6. Bb5) 6... Nb4 7. Bb5+ c6 (7... Bd7 8. Bxd7+ Nxd7 9. a3 Nf6 10. axb4 Qxa1 11. O-O Qa6 12. Re1 $40 O-O-O $2 13. Ne5) 8. dxc6 bxc6 9. Ba4 Ba6 $2 (9... Bd7 {}) 10. a3 Rd8 11. Bd2 Qf5 12. axb4 Rd6 13. Bb3 Ne4 14. Rxa6 Rxd2 15. Qc1 Nxc3 16. bxc3 Rd6 17. O-O {Fischer,R-Seidman,H ch-USA 1958}) 4. d4 {Alexander Volzhin: 'The initial position of the variation. Now Black has two different plans. One possibility is the fianchetto of his dark-squared Bishop, and another is to play the light-squared Bishop to f5 and the arising position looks like a typical Caro Kann.'} g6 $5 { g8-h6-f5; × d4} 5. Bf4 $1 {Alexander Volzhin: 'Although this game was played almost 40 years ago Fischer's plan is considered as the best nowadays. The idea of this move (followed by 6 .Qd2) is to prevent Black's Knight manoeuvre to f5-square via h6.'} (5. Nf3 Bg7 6. h3 Nf6 $14 (6... Nh6 7. g4 $1 {Sokolsky,A})) ({Alexander Volzhin: 'Another possible plan is'} 5. Bc4 Bg7 6. Nf3 {Alexander Volzhin: 'aiming for a small but steady advantage, but recent practice proves Black has good chances of equalising:'} Nh6 7. Bxh6 $5 {Alexander Volzhin} ({The alternatives are:} 7. Ne4 {Alexander Volzhin} Nf5 8. c3 O-O 9. O-O Nd7 10. Bf4 Nd6 11. Bd3 {Kaminski-Kiedrowicz, Bielsko-Biala 1991.}) (7. Bg5 {Alexander Volzhin} Nf5 8. O-O O-O 9. Re1 h6 10. Bf4 c6 11. Be5 {Arakhamia-Petrovic, Tuzla 1987, with a tiny edge in both cases.}) 7... Bxh6 8. Ne5 O-O 9. O-O Nd7 10. Qe2 Nb6 11. Rad1 Nxc4 12. Qxc4 Bf5 13. Qb3 Rb8 {and Black has little to worry about, Tiviakov-Galliamova, Elista 1998.}) 5... Bg7 ({Alexander Volzhin: 'the immediate'} 5... Nh6 {Alexander Volzhin: 'is not good in view of'} 6. Be5 $1 f6 7. Bf4 {Alexander Volzhin: ', weakening Black's K-side.'}) 6. Qd2 $1 ({Alexander Volzhin: 'Tempting is'} 6. Nb5 {Alexander Volzhin: 'as was played in Bronstein-Kholmov, Tbilisi 1959 is harmless:'} Na6 { c7-c6; Bronstein,D-Kholmov,R URS 1959} 7. Nf3 {Alexander Volzhin} Nf6 8. c4 c6 9. Nc3 Bg4 10. Be2 O-O 11. O-O Nd7 12. Be3 e5 13. d5 c5 14. Ne1 Bxe2 15. Qxe2 f5 {and in this complicated position Black's chances are by no means bad.}) (6. Nf3 Nh6) 6... Nf6 ({Alexander Volzhin: 'It's not good for Black to take the d4-pawn:'} 6... Qxd4 7. Qxd4 Bxd4 8. Nb5 Bb6 $8 9. Nxc7+ Bxc7 10. Bxc7 $16 { Alexander Volzhin: 'and the endgame clearly favors White'}) (6... Bxd4 $2 7. O-O-O Nc6 8. Bb5 Bd7 9. Nd5 $1 (9. Bxc6 $2 Bxc6 10. Qxd4 $2 Qxd4 11. Rxd4 Bxg2) 9... e5 10. Nf3 $18 {Alexander Volzhin: 'and Black can't avoid gross material losses.'}) 7. O-O-O c6 (7... Nd5 {} 8. Be5 (8. Bh6 $5 Bxh6 9. Qxh6 Nxc3) 8... O-O 9. h4 h5 10. Nge2 $16) 8. Bh6 O-O $2 {Alexander Volzhin: 'This natural looking move is indeed the decisive mistake!'} (8... Bxh6 {} 9. Qxh6 Bf5 { 0-0-0 Alexander Volzhin: 'intending to castle Q-side should be played, although in my opinion White is clearly better here.'}) 9. h4 {Alexander Volzhin: '!' Alexander Volzhin: 'Exploiting Black's mistake White starts a K-side attack without delay.'} Qa5 10. h5 $1 gxh5 {Alexander Volzhin: 'The only move.'} ({Alexander Volzhin: 'Black can't allow the opening of the h-file:'} 10... Rd8 11. hxg6 fxg6 12. Bxg7 Kxg7 13. Qh6+ Kg8 14. Nf3 $18 {[%emt 0:00:15]  g5 Alexander Volzhin: 'and Black can't parry the threat of Ng5'}) (10... Nxh5 {Alexander Volzhin: 'is also insufficient:'} 11. Be2 Nf6 12. Bxg7 Kxg7 13. Qh6+ Kg8 14. g4 $1 {Alexander Volzhin: 'and White wins by force:'} Rd8 15. g5 Nh5 16. Bxh5 gxh5 17. Rxh5 {Alexander Volzhin: 'or'} Bf5 (17... Qf5 18. g6 $1 Qxg6 19. Rg5 {Alexander Volzhin: 'winning the Queen.'}) 18. g6 $1 $18 {Alexander Volzhin: '!'}) 11. Bd3 {Alexander Volzhin: '!'} Nbd7 ({Alexander Volzhin: 'It would be very good for Black to transfer his light-squared Bishop to the g6-square but White's last move made this manoeuvre impossible:'} 11... Bf5 $2 12. Qg5) 12. Nge2 Rd8 13. g4 $1 {Alexander Volzhin: 'The decisive breakthrough. Now White's attack becomes unstoppable.'} Nf8 ({Alexander Volzhin: 'Black can't accept the sacrifice in view of'} 13... Nxg4 14. Rdg1 $1 $18 { f2-f3; xg4 Alexander Volzhin: '!' Alexander Volzhin: 'with decisive threats.'}) 14. gxh5 {Alexander Volzhin: 'Now Black is helpless against threats on the g-file.'} Ne6 15. Rdg1 Kh8 ({Alexander Volzhin: 'Or'} 15... Kf8 16. Bxg7+ Nxg7 17. Qh6 Ng4 18. Qxh7 $18 {Alexander Volzhin: 'and White wins.'}) 16. Bxg7+ Nxg7 17. Qh6 Rg8 (17... Ne6 18. Nf4 $1 $18 {Alexander Volzhin: '!'}) 18. Rg5 Qd8 (18... Nf5 {Alexander Volzhin: 'is also bad:'} 19. Rxg8+ Nxg8 20. Qf8 { g1 Alexander Volzhin: ', Rg1 to follow.'}) 19. Rhg1 Nf5 {Alexander Volzhin: '?' Alexander Volzhin: 'A blunder but Black's position is lost anyway.'} (19... Qf8 20. d5 $1 Bd7 (20... cxd5 21. Nxd5 Nxd5 22. Qxh7#) 21. d6 $1 Nf5 22. Qxf8 Raxf8 (22... Rgxf8 23. Bxf5 h6 24. dxe7 Rfb8 25. Rg7 Bxf5 26. Rxf7) 23. Bxf5 Rxg5 24. Rxg5 h6 25. dxe7 Rb8 26. Rg3 $1 Bxf5 27. Rf3 $18) 20. Bxf5 {Alexander Volzhin: 'Bobby Fischer at his best!'} 1-0

