{[%evp 0,52,40,31,31,5,8,8,8,8,18,13,13,5,26,8,-23,-23,-19,-1,5,3,8,0,20,17,18,11,38,0,60,58,65,65,98,105,99,116,101,86,86,87,116,106,210,210,74,62,62,62,67,-273,-345,-403,-431]} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bc4 Bc5 4. d3 d6 5. Nc3 ({Nowadays, most often played is} 5. c3) 5... Nf6 ({Interesting is} 5... Na5) 6. Bg5 Na5 7. Bb5+ $6 ({Dubious move. Preferable is} 7. Bb3 $11 {with an even play.}) 7... c6 8. Ba4 b5 9. Bb3 Nxb3 10. axb3 h6 11. Be3 Qb6 $6 ({Slightly preferable was} 11... Bxe3 12. fxe3 a5 $15) 12. Bxc5 Qxc5 $11 {The position is even.} 13. O-O Bg4 14. Ra5 (14. d4 {is an alternative.}) 14... g5 $2 ({Fischer's move is too violent. Stronger was either} 14... Qb6) ({or} 14... O-O {with even play.}) 15. Qe2 ({After a stronger} 15. h3 $16 {White has a clear edge.}) 15... Qb6 16. b4 Nh5 $6 ({Stronger was} 16... a6 $14) 17. Qe3 $1 $16 Qb7 ({In the case of} 17... Qxe3 18. fxe3 O-O {after} 19. Ra6 $1 {White has a clear edge.}) 18. Rfa1 (18. d4 {was slightly preferable.}) 18... a6 19. d4 f6 20. d5 $6 ({Dubious move. After a better} 20. dxe5 fxe5 21. h3 Be6 22. Qd3 Ke7 23. Ne2 $16 {White is clearly better.}) 20... Bd7 21. g3 f5 $6 ({We can see that Fischer was an aggressive player in his youth. Stronger was} 21... Ng7 $14) 22. exf5 $6 ({After a better} 22. dxc6 Bxc6 23. Qd3 {White has a clear advantage:} fxe4 24. Qxd6 exf3 25. Qg6+ Kf8 26. Qxh5 Kg7 27. Nd1 Rhf8 28. Ne3 $16) 22... cxd5 {[#]} 23. Nxe5 $5 ({The game move leads to an even position. Interesting is} 23. Qd3 {although by precise play Black can attain an even position:} d4 24. Nxb5 Bxb5 25. Qxb5+ axb5 26. Rxa8+ Kd7 27. R8a7 Kc6 28. R1a6+ Qxa6 29. Rxa6+ Kd5 30. Rb6 Ke4 $11) 23... dxe5 24. Qxe5+ Kf7 {[#]} 25. Nxb5 $4 ({Glarring error which loses the game. After a better} 25. Nxd5 {the position is even:} Rae8 26. Qd4 Ra8 27. c4 Bc6 $11) 25... axb5 $19 26. Rd1 Nf6 0-1

