{Bobby Fischer: 'GAME N. 4 Tact and tactics. The presence in Argentina of Pilnik, Najdorf, and Eliskases, who chose to remain there after participating in the Buenos Aires chess Olympic of 1939, created a chess renaissance, as attested by the annual event at Mar del Plata which, though not lavish with prizes, offers an exotic vacation and attracts the world's best. Fischer tied for 3-4 with Ivkov, a mere half point behind Pachman and Najdorf in a strong field of fifteen. After a lackluster opening by both sides, and a middle game that, with the exception of 26. (come back here), can scarcely be described as more than routine, Fischer pilots the game into an even ending. Both he and Pilnok then prodceed to complicate; but the latter is drawn into making a false lead, which Fischr explots by obtaining a passed center Pawn. From this point on, although Pilnik does all that can be done to stave off the inevitable, Fischer is not gulled into making a single wrong step. ' Neil McDonald: 'Later in Jakovenko-Carlsen, Jakovenko's omission of 49 Kg1 reminds me of a similar incident in one of Fischer's games.' Neil McDonald: 'Later in Jakovenko-Carlsen, Jakovenko's omission of 49 Kg1 reminds me of a similar incident in one of Fischer's games. '} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 a6 6. Be2 ({Bobby Fischer: 'For'} 6. h3 {Fischer,R-Bolbochan,J Stockholm izt 1962 Fischer,R-Najdorf,M Varna ol 1962 Fischer,R-Reshevsky,S ch-USA 1962 Fischer,R-Bolbochan,J Stockholm izt 1962 Fischer,R-Najdorf,M Varna ol 1962 Fischer,R-Reshevsky,S ch-USA 1962 Bobby Fischer: 'see games 35, 40, 43.'}) ({Bobby Fischer: 'For'} 6. Bc4 {Fischer,R-Tal,M Beograd ct 1959 Fischer,R-Bednarski,J Habana ol 1966 Fischer,R-Geller,E Skopje 1967 Fischer,R-Tal,M Beograd ct 1959 Fischer,R-Bednarski,J Habana ol 1966 Fischer,R-Geller,E Skopje 1967 Bobby Fischer: 'see games 17, 55, 58.'}) 6... e5 7. Nb3 Be7 ({Bobby Fischer: 'For'} 7... Be6 {Unzicker,W-Fischer,R Varna ol 1962 Unzicker,W-Fischer,R Varna ol 1962 Bobby Fischer: 'see game 42.'}) 8. O-O ({Bobby Fischer: 'Another try is'} 8. Bg5 O-O $1 (8... Nbd7 {Bobby Fischer: '?'} 9. a4 $1 $16 {Bobby Fischer: '!' Bobby Fischer: 'gives a powerful bind.'}) (8... Be6 $1 9. Bxf6 $6 {Kasparov} Bxf6 10. Qd3 $6 (10. Nd5 Nd7 (10... Bg5 11. h4 Bh6 12. g4 $16 {}) (10... Nc6 11. Nxf6+ Qxf6 12. Qxd6 Rd8 13. Qa3 Bxb3 14. axb3 Nd4 15. Bd1 $1 $16) 11. O-O O-O 12. Bg4 (12. a4 Rc8 13. c3 $14 {Savon}) 12... Bg5 $10 {Abramovic-Savon, Erevan 1982}) 10... Nc6 11. O-O-O Nd4 12. Nxd4 exd4 13. Nd5 Bxd5 14. exd5 O-O $15 {Kasparov} 15. Qf3 Qd7 $5 { a5-a4-a3} 16. Bd3 Rfe8 17. h4 a5 18. g4 a4 19. g5 Bd8 20. Bf5 Qc7 21. Rxd4 a3 22. b4 g6 23. Bg4 Qe7 24. c3 Qe5 25. Rf1 Bb6 26. Rd2 Qe4 $10 {Estevez-Vilela}) 9. Nd2 Nxe4 $1 10. Bxe7 Nxc3 11. Bxd8 Nxd1 12. Be7 Re8 13. Nc4 Nxb2 $1 14. Nb6 Rxe7 15. Nxa8 Na4 16. O-O-O {Bobby Fischer: '(Fischer-Ghitescu, Leipzig, 1960)'} Rd7 $1 $14 {Fischer,R-Ghitescu,T Leipzig ol 1960 Fischer,R-Ghitescu,T Leipzig ol 1960 Bobby Fischer: '!' Bobby Fischer: 'with the better game.'}) 8... O-O 9. Be3 Be6 10. f3 ({Bobby Fischer: 'A sharper alternative is'} 10. a4 Qc7 11. a5 Nbd7 12. Nd5 (12. Qd2 Rac8 (12... Bc4 13. Ra4 Bxe2 14. Qxe2 Rac8 15. Rd1 Qc6 16. Rd3 Nb8 17. Nd2 Qd7 18. b3 Rc6 19. Nc4 $14 {Eichhorn E.-Berbecaru J., corr. 1990}) 13. Rfc1 Bc4 (13... Bxb3 14. cxb3 Nc5 15. Bc4 Qb8 16. f3 Ne6 17. Rd1 h6 18. Qe2 Qc7 19. Na4 Nd7 20. Nb6 Nxb6 21. Bxb6 Qd7 22. g3 Bd8 23. Be3 Bg5 24. Bb6 {- Juutistenaho-Halttunen, corr. 1972}) 14. Bxc4 Qxc4 15. Ra4 Qc7 16. Qe2 Rfd8 17. Nd2 Nc5 18. Bxc5 dxc5 19. Nc4 Rd4 20. Raa1 Rcd8 21. b3 h6 $15 {Hracek Z.-Malisauskas V., Novy Smokovec 1992}) 12... Nxd5 13. exd5 Bf5 14. c4 Bg6 15. Kh1 Rac8 16. Qd2 Qd8 17. Rac1 h6 18. f4 exf4 19. Bxf4 Bg5 $10 {Smyslov,V-Gligoric,S Habana 1962 Smyslov,V-Gligoric,S Habana 1962 Bobby Fischer: '=' Bobby Fischer: '(Smyslov-Gligorich, Havana, 1962).' Fischer/PS: '='}) (10. Qd3 Nbd7 11. Nd5 Bxd5 12. exd5 Ne8 13. Qd2 Qc7 14. c4 a5 15. Rac1 g6 16. Na1 Ng7 17. Bd3 Nc5 18. Nc2 e