anted to build a little more and keep the option of moving the Knight to a4 as well as c4.'} ({Bobby Fischer: 'But Black should pounce on the chance to play'} 14... Nc4 {Bobby Fischer: '!' Fischer/PS: '!'} 15. Bxc4 bxc4 16. Bb6 ({Bobby Fischer: 'if'} 16. Na1 Rab8 17. Rb1 Rb7 $17 {Bobby Fischer: 'is strong.'}) ({Bobby Fischer: 'or'} 16. Nc1 Rab8 17. Na4 c3 $1 18. bxc3 $2 Qc6 19. Nb6 Bd8 $19) 16... Qc8 17. Na5 Nd7 $1 {Bobby Fischer: 'and White's in trouble. e.g.,'} 18. Nd5 (18. Be3 Bd8 19. Nd5 Bxd5 20. Rxd5 Nf6 $19 {Bobby Fischer: '... Wining at least the exchange.'}) 18... Bxd5 19. Rxd5 ({Bobby Fischer: 'if'} 19. exd5 Nxb6 20. Qxb6 Bd8 21. Qb4 Rb8 22. Qa3 Bxa5 23. Qxa5 Rxb2 $19) 19... Rb8 $17 {Bobby Fischer: 'winning at least a Pawn.'}) 15. Bxb6 $1 {Bobby Fischer: ', Pilnik hastens to make amends for his omissino.'} ({Bobby Fischer: 'Not'} 15. Na5 $2 d5 $1 $17 {Stahlberg,G Stahlberg,G Bobby Fischer: '!' Bobby Fischer: 'wins material. (Stahlberg).'}) 15... Rxb6 16. Nd5 Nxd5 17. exd5 Bd7 18. f4 Bf6 (18... f5 19. c3 (19. c4 Bf6 20. fxe5 dxe5 ({if} 20... Bxe5 21. Nd4) 21. Nc5 $11) 19... Bf6 20. fxe5 dxe5 (20... Bxe5 21. Nd4) 21. Nc5 $10 {Fischer/PS: '='}) 19. c3 Rbb8 20. fxe5 Bxe5 ({Bobby Fischer: 'On'} 20... dxe5 21. d6 $36 {Bobby Fischer: 'gives White active play.'}) {Bobby Fischer: ' Black's advantage of the Bishop pair is neutraliazed by the weakness of his c6, which White White can later occupy with his Knight. '} 21. Nd4 g6 22. a3 ({Bobby Fischer: 'More to the point was'} 22. Bf3 { Fischer/PS: ''} b4 23. cxb4 Rxb4 24. Nc6 $10 {Bobby Fischer: '=' Fischer/PS: '='}) 22... a5 23. Kh1 (23. Bf3 {  Bobby Fischer: 'should again be played.' Fischer/PS: ''}) {Bobby Fischer: 'White starts drifting. '} 23... b4 24. cxb4 ({Bobby Fischer: 'On'} 24. axb4 axb4 25. c4 b3 $1 $36 {Bobby Fischer: '!' Bobby Fischer: 'holds the initiative.'}) 24... axb4 25. Rc2 ({Bobby Fischer: 'On'} 25. Bf3 bxa3 26. bxa3 Ra8 $17 {Bobby Fischer: 'presents its problems.'}) 25... Qb6 26. Nc6 {Bobby F