{ChessCalisthenics: 'C99: Closed Ruy Lopez: Chigorin Defence: 11 d4 Qc7 12 Nbd2 cxd4' Bobby Fischer: 'GAME N. 8 Meat and potatoes. Alekhine said, in his prime, that to wrest a point from him it was necessary to win the same rame three times: once at the beginning, once in the middle, once at the end. No less a tribute may be paid to Keres. Each phase of rhis game is fascinating and hard-fought. Even rhe errors. and there are more than a few. contribute to making it an unusually complete exhibition of two master craftsmen using all the tools of rheir trade. While perhaps unglamorous, there is meat here, and potatoes tao. And it is likely rhat as a result of rhls victory Fisd!er came to be regarded as a serious contender by the leading Soviet Grandmasters - thls was the first time he had defeated one. ' Eine Großkampfpartie voller Spannung, hier besiegt Fischer das erste Mal einen Großmeister der Sowjetunion. Tabellenstand: Tal 10, Fischer 9, Gligoric 8.5 Keres 8 PS} 1. e4 {ChessCalisthenics Bobby Fischer} e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Ba4 Nf6 5. O-O Be7 6. Re1 b5 7. Bb3 O-O 8. c3 d6 9. h3 Na5 10. Bc2 c5 11. d4 Qc7 12. Nbd2 cxd4 ({Bobby Fischer: 'Keres has abandoned'} 12... Rd8 13. Nf1 d5 $2 14. dxe5 $1 dxe4 ({Bobby Fischer: 'if'} 14... Nxe4 15. Qe2 Bb7 16. Ne3 { Sxd5 +-  Sxd5 +-  Sxd5 +- Bobby Fischer: 'threatening Nxd5.'}) 15. N1d2 {Bobby Fischer: '!'} exf3 16. exf6 Bxf6 17. Qxf3 Be6 18. Ne4 $40 {+- +- +- Bobby Fischer: 'with a winning attack.' +- Fischer}) 13. cxd4 Bb7 14. Nf1 (14. d5 Bc8 15. Rb1 b4 $1 (15... Bd7 16. Bd3 Rfc8 17. Nf1 Bd8 18. Ng3 Qa7 19. Rf1 Ne8 20. Kh1 Nb7 21. b4 $1 a5 22. a3 axb4 23. axb4 Be7 24. Ne2 $1 {Bronstein-Geller/UdSSR-19.ch/1-0}) (15... Nb7 $2 16. b4 $1) 16. Bd3 Nd7 17. Nf1 Nc5 18. Bc2 Nc4 19. b3 Nb6 20. Be3 f5 $10 {Gligoric-Reshevsky/Match/1952/ Barcza '='}) 14... Rac8 15. Bd3 (15. Bb1 d5 16. exd5 exd4 17. Bg5 Rfe8 (17... h6 $2 18. Bxh6 $3 gxh6 19. Qd2) 18. Nxd4 Nxd5 19. Bxe7 Rxe7 {Niephaus-Trifunovic/Wageningen/1957/Barcza}) (15. Re2 Nd