s no better}) 18. Rd1 ({or} 18. Rg1 $5 g6 19. Rd1) 18... Qc8 19. Rd7 Qxb7 20. Rxb7 {Black would have faced a difficult defence.}) 15. Rb1 $1 $16 {The innovation. Months before the game I had shown this line to Benko and he suggested this innocent-looking move. Upon looking deeper I found that, horrible as White's Pawn structure may be, Black can't exploit it because he'11 be unable to develop his K -side normally. It's the little quirks like this that could nlake life difficult for a chess machine. Benko,P Garry Kasparov: '!' Garry Kasparov: 'An important innovation. "Months before the game I had showed this line to Benko and he suggested this innocent-looking move. Upon looking deeper I found that, horrible as White's pawn structure may be, Black can't exploit it because he'll be unable to develop his kingside normally. It's the little quirks like this that could make life difficult for a chess machine." (Fischer) Karsten Müller: '(Benko)'' Petronijevic,Zoran: 'White wins the open b-file.' Petronijevic,Zoran: 'Weiß gewinnt den Kampf um die offene b-Linie.'} Rd8 $2 {Garry Kasparov: 'An unsuccessful defensive plan involving the manoeuvre of the rook to d7 (it wastes precious time!): Euwe overestimated the danger of an invasion of the seventh rank.'} ({also difficult is Garry Kasparov: '"Also difficult is'} 15... Qxb5 16. Rxb5 Kd6 $1 17. Rb7 f6 18. Ke2 Kc6 19. Rf7 a5 20. Be3 $16 {with an enduring pull Garry Kasparov: 'with an enduring pull" (Fischer), although after the counterattacking'} Rb8 $1 {(Garry Kasparov) Black would have retained possibilities of resisting. Karsten Müller: '' Karsten Müller: '(Kasparov)'}) ({Garry Kasparov: 'If'} 15... Rc8 $5 {Petronijevic,Zoran Garry Kasparov: ', then'} 16. Qa6 {Garry Kasparov} ({or} 16. Qa5 {(Garry Kasparov) is unpleasant.})) 16. Be3 Qxb5 17. Rxb5 Rd7 18. Ke2 {Petronijevic,Zoran: 'Fischer does not hurry: he can take a7 later.' Petronijevic,Zoran: 'Fischer hat keine Eile: den a7 kann er später schlagen.'} ({Garry Kasparov