1. e4 {Uhlmann u.a. Wells ChessBase ChessBase 1) Uhlmann,Wofgang: Meine besten Partien. St.Ingbert. 2015. S.6-10.} e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. e5 c5 (4... Ne7 {Uhlmann u.a.} 5. a3 Bxc3+ 6. bxc3 {0-1 (42) Fischer,R-Uhlmann,W Buenos Aires 1960 Fischer [Uhlmann u.a.]}) 5. a3 Bxc3+ 6. bxc3 Ne7 7. Nf3 (7. a4 {Uhlmann u.a.} Nbc6 8. Nf3 Bd7 9. Qd2 {0-1 (42) Fischer,R-Uhlmann,W Buenos Aires 1960 Fischer [Uhlmann u.a.]}) 7... Bd7 8. a4 Qa5 9. Qd2 Nbc6 10. Bd3 c4 11. Be2 f6 (11... O-O-O 12. Ba3 f6 {ChessBase: '' '' Uhlmann u.a.: ''} 13. O-O $14 {(Keres 69) Uhlmann u.a.: 'Fischer,R-Weinstein,R/ch-USA 1960'}) 12. Ba3 (12. O-O O-O $5 {(Ivkov)}) 12... Ng6 $6 (12... O-O-O $142) 13. O-O $1 O-O-O (13... fxe5 $6 14. Nxe5 Ngxe5 15. dxe5 Nxe5 16. Qg5 $1 $16 {(Schwarz 67)} Ng6 (16... Nc6 17. Bh5+ $1 g6 18. Qf6 Rg8 19. Rfe1 $16 {(Schwarz 67)}) (16... Qxc3 $4 17. Qe7#) 17. Bh5 $1 $16 {(Schwarz 67, Mednis 74) Uhlmann u.a.: 'Schwarz , Mednis'}) 14. Bd6 (14. Rfe1 fxe5 15. dxe5 Ngxe5 16. Nxe5 Nxe5 17. Qd4 Nc6 18. Qxg7 Rhg8 $13 {(eco 74/81) Uhlmann u.a.: 'ECO'}) 14... Nce7 $1 {"Uhlmann gruppeirt um, weil seine Chancen auf dem Konigsflugel liegen." (Schwarz 67)} (14... fxe5 15. dxe5 h6 16. Kh1 Rhe8 17. Rfd1 Nh8 $1 {Gligoric-Sokolov 1956}) (14... Rde8 15. Rfb1 (15. Rfe1 {Uhlmann u.a.} h5 16. h4 Nd8 17. Bf1 Nf7 18. Bb4 Qc7 19. Qe2 a5 20. Ba3 Bxa4 21. Bf8 Rhxf8 22. Rxa4 Nd8 23. g3 b5 24. Ra2 Nc6 25. exf6 $13 {Fischer,R-Sherwin,J/ch-USA 1960}) 15... Nd8 16. Bb4 Qc7 17. Bd6 Qa5 18. Qe3 Nf7 19. Bc5 Kb8 20. Rb2 {Klavin-Fuchs 1961}) 15. Nh4 $1 {ChessBase: '"With this and the following series of fine moves, White ensures an excellent diagonal for his QB and paralyzes any hopes Black may have for meaningful counterplay." (Mednis 74)' "With this and the following series of fine moves, White ensures an excellent diagonal for his QB and paralyzes any hopes Black may have for meaningful counterplay." (Mednis 74) ! Uhlmann: Weiss verhindert Sf5 und kann so seinen Läufer auf der Diagonalen b8-h2 behaupten.} Rde8 16. Nxg6 $1 hxg6 17. exf6 $1 {"Weiss will auf den dunklen Feldern zu eimem Ubergewicht kommen, daher die Linienoffnung fur den Th8." (Schwarz 67)} gxf6 18. h3 $1 {"Fischers Plan sieht gut aus: er will den Laufer auf der Diagonale h2-b8 wirken lassen." (Schwarz 67)} Nf5 19. Bh2 g5 {[#]} 20. f4 $2 {"But this brute force attempt at an immediate win spoils everything." (Mednis 74) Wells: 'The first sign that this is a bad day for the maestro. Fischer would have been horrified of course if he had thought that the f-pawn would still be on f4 in the final position. Such a move can only be made in the 'safe assurance' that fxg5 will follow soon.' Sperrt den Lh1 ein, und Schwarz will ihn blockiert lassen.} (20. Rfe1 $1 {"... White has a marvelous position: pressure on Black's somewhat shaky center, open diagonals for both Bishops, while Black's King can find himself uncomfortably open soon." (Mednis 74) Uhlmann u.a.: '"... White has a marvelous position: pressure on Black's somewhat shaky center, open diagonals for both Bishops, while Black's King can find himself uncomfortably open soon." Mednis'}) (20. Rae1) (20. Bg4) 20... Nd6 $6 {ChessBase: '!' '!' Wells: '!'} (20... g4 $1 {Lässt f4xg5 nicht zu.} {Nach} 21. hxg4 (21. Bxg4 Reg8) 21... Nd6 22. Bf3 f5 {hätten wir mit Zugumstellung die Partiestellung auf dem Brett.}) 21. Bf3 (21. fxg5 $5 {Befreit den Lh2.} Ne4 22. Qe3 (22. Qf4 e5 $1 23. Qf3 {Uhlmann u.a.} fxg5 $1 (23... Qxc3 24. gxf6 Qxd4+ (24... Qxf3 25. Bxf3 exd4 26. f7 Ref8 27. Be5 $1 $16 {Agur} (27. Bxe4 $1 dxe4 28. Bd6 e3 29. Rf4 $1 Be6 (29... d3 30. Rxc4+ Kd8 31. Bxf8 Rxf8 32. cxd3 Rxf7 33. Re4 Re7 34. Rxe7 Kxe7 35. Kf1 $1 $18) 30. Bxf8 Rxf8 31. Rxd4 $18 {PS})) 25. Kh1 Nd2 26. Qa3 Nxf1 27. Rxf1 Reg8 28. f7 Rf8 29. Qd6 $18 {Agur}) (23... Nd2 24. Qxf6 Nxf1 25. Rxf1 Qxc3 26. Bxe5 Qe3+ 27. Qf2 $1 $16 Qxf2+ 28. Kxf2 Rhg8 29. h4 Bxa4 30. Bf3 Bc6 31. Bf6 {[%cal Rh4h8] Agur}) (23... Ref8 24. dxe5 {?? PS} (24. Bxc4 $1 Rfg8 (24... fxg5 25. Qxf8+ Rxf8 26. Rxf8+ Kc7 27. Bxe5+ Nd6 (27... Kc6 28. Bb5+ $18) (27... Kb6 28. Rb1+ Kc6 29. Bb5+ $18) 28. Rf6 $18 {PS}) (24... Nxg5 25. Qxd5 $16 {PS}) (24... dxc4 25. Qxe4 Bc6 (25... Qxc3 26. dxe5 fxg5 27. e6 Bc6 28. e7 Rf6 29. Qg4+ $16 {[%csl Rg5]}) 26. Qf5+ Bd7 27. Qf2 $16 {PS}) 25. gxf6 (25. Rae1 Rxg5 26. Bxd5 Qxd5 27. Rxe4 Rxh3 28. Qe2 Bc6 $19) 25... Bxh3 26. f7 Rxg2+ 27. Qxg2 Bxg2 28. f8=Q+ Rxf8 29. Rxf8+ $16 {PS}) 24... Nxg5 (24... Qc5+ 25. Kh1 fxe5 $19 {PS}) 25. Qe3 Rhg8 26. Kh1 $16 {Agur}) 24. Bxe5 Rxe5 $1 (24... Nd2 25. Qf7 Nxf1 26. Rxf1 Rhg8 27. Rf5 Be6 28. Bg4 $16 {Agur}) (24... g4 $5 25. Qe3 $1 (25. Qf7 {?Agur} gxh3 26. Bxh8 h2+ 27. Kxh2 Rxh8+ 28. Kg1 (28. Bh5 Qxc3 29. Qxd5 Qg3+ 30. Kg1 Qe3+ 31. Kh2 (31. Kh1 Ng3+ 32. Kh2 Rxh5+) 31... Qg5 32. Qxg5 (32. Qxe4 Qxh5+ 33. Kg1 Qh2+ 34. Kf2 Rf8+ 35. Ke3 Re8) 32... Nxg5 33. g4 Bxg4 34. Rf8+ Rxf8 35. Bxg4+ $15 {PS}) 28... Qxc3 $19 {Agur}) (25. hxg4 $2 Rxe5 $1 26. dxe5 Qb6+ $19 {Agur}) 25... Rhg8 (25... Nxc3) 26. Bxg4 Bxg4 27. hxg4 $16 {Agur}) 25. dxe5 Qb6+ 26. Kh2 g4 27. Qf4 (27. a5 $1 Qc5 (27... gxf3 28. axb6 fxe2 29. Rf7 a6 $17) 28. Qf7 g3+ 29. Kh1 Bxh3 30. Qg7 Nf2+ (30... Bxg2+ 31. Kxg2 Rh2+ 32. Kf3 Rf2+ 33. Kg4) 31. Kg1 Ne4+ $11 {PS}) (27. Qf7 g3+ 28. Kh1 Bxh3 29. Qg7 Bxg2+ 30. Kxg2 Rh2+ 31. Kf3 Rf2+ 32. Kg4 Qe6+ 33. Kh5 Rh2#) 27... g3+ (27... gxh3 28. g4 $14 {Agur}) 28. Kh1 Bxh3 $19 {PS}) 22... Qxc3 23. Qxc3 (23. Bd3 $2 cxd3 24. cxd3 Qd2 $1 {(Schwarz 67)}) 23... Nxc3 24. Bf3 fxg5 25. a5 $11 {(Schwarz 67, Mednis 74) ChessBase: 'N' 'N' Uhlmann u.a.: ''}) 21... g4 $3 {"Black sacrifices a pawn and allows a protected passed pawn to boot, for the strategic objective of locking in White's QB. The damage done by White's 20 f4? is now very obvious." (Mednis 74) Wells: '!' Wells: 'An excellent pawn sacrifice which effectively kills the h2 bishop as an offensive force.' Uhlmann: Mit dem Bauernopfer wird der Läufer auf h2 endgültig bis zum Partienende aus dem Verkehr gezogen.} 22. hxg4 (22. Bxg4 $2 Ne4 23. Qe3 f5 24. Bf3 Qxc3 25. Qxc3 Nxc3 $17 {(Schwarz 67) Uhlmann u.a.: 'Uhlmann'}) 22... f5 $1 23. g5 (23. gxf5 $143 {Uhlmann u.a.} exf5 {Uhlmann}) 23... Re7 24. Bg3 Be8 25. Qe3 Ne4 26. Bxe4 $8 dxe4 27. Kf2 {"Fischer evaluates this position much too optimistically and plans to husband the extra Pawn to victory. The blocked nature of the position makes winning attempts for either side less than fruitful." (Mednis 74)} (27. d5 $5 {Uhlmann u.a.: '!?' Uhlmann u.a.: 'Um Raum für die Dame zu schaffen. (Uhlmann)'}) 27... Reh7 (27... Qd5) 28. Rfb1 {Wells: '?' Wells: 'Another uncharacteristic lapse. Fischer's normal feel for the initiative would surely dictate that he should take the chance to increase the scope of his queen, lest he not get another.'} (28. d5 $142 $1 {Wells: '!' Uhlmann u.a.: 'Uhlmann'} Qxd5 29. Rfd1 {(Schwarz 67)}) 28... Qd5 $1 {"Now we have a rather full blockade and the game could well be called a draw here." (Mednis 74)} 29. Qe1 $2 (29. a5 $10) (29. Qd2 $5 {Uhlmann u.a.: '=!?'} Rh1 30. Ke3) 29... Rh1 $1 {[#]} 30. Qxh1 $4 (30. Qe3 $8 Rxb1 31. Rxb1 Bxa4 32. Ra1 Bxc2 33. Rxa7 Kb8 34. Ra1 Bd3 $15 {(Mednis 74) Uhlmann u.a.: 'Uhlmann'}) 30... e3+ $1 {Wells: 'The point. This opening of a key line decisively swings the initiative Uhlmann's way. It is well known that positions with opposite coloured bishops favour 'the attacker', but it many cases who fulfils this happy role is not yet determined. So, seize the initiative! Of course, it is not so hard to see that the queen and the bishop will operate very effectively together.'} 31. Kg1 (31. Kxe3 $2 Qe4+ 32. Kf2 (32. Kd2 $2 Rxh1 33. Rxh1 Qxg2+ $19) 32... Rxh1 (32... Qxc2+ 33. Kg1 Rxh1+ 34. Kxh1 Bc6 35. Rg1 Qxc3 {(Schwarz 67)}) 33. Rxh1 Bc6 $1 34. Rh2 Qxc2+ 35. Kg1 Qxc3 $19 {(Mednis 74) Uhlmann u.a.: 'Uhlmann'}) (31. Ke2 $2 Rxh1 32. Rxh1 Qxg2+ {(Wade/O'Connell)}) 31... Rxh1+ 32. Kxh1 e2 $1 33. Rb5 $5 {"Bobby finally realized that he must be lost and thus characteristically goes for active counterplay. It is not good enough, but is as good a try as any." (Mednis 74) Wells: 'More an admission of how bad things have got than a serious bid for counterplay.'} (33. Re1 Qe4) (33. Rg1 Qe4 34. Rac1 {Uhlmann u.a.} Kd8 $19 {Uhlmann}) 33... Bxb5 34. axb5 Qxb5 $1 35. Re1 a5 36. Rxe2 a4 $1 37. Rxe6 a3 38. g6 (38. Re5 Qxe5 $19 {Uhlmann u.a.: 'Uhlmann'}) (38. Re1 {Uhlmann u.a.} a2 39. g6 Qa6 40. g7 Qh6+ $19 {[%cal Rh6g7] Uhlmann}) 38... Qd7 (38... a2 $4 39. g7 a1=Q+ 40. Kh2 $10 {(Mednis 74) Uhlmann u.a.: '+-'}) 39. Re5 b6 {Wells: '!'} 40. Bh4 a2 41. Re1 Qg7 42. Ra1 Qxg6 (42... Qxg6 43. Rxa2 Qh5 44. g3 Qf3+ 45. Kh2 Qxc3 46. Bf6 b5 $19 {(Mednis 74) Uhlmann u.a.: 'Uhlmann'}) 0-1

