Fischer: 'or, still better,''} 21. Re2 $142 $1 { d4 Kortschnoj  d4 Kortschnoj Ernst: ' d4 Kortschnoj Bobby Fischer: '!' Bobby Fischer: 'protecting the K.B and preparing the powerful maneuver Nd4." (KORCHNOI.) '' '!' Korchnoi,V: ;  d4} {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: 'The truth is, White just doesn't have that much. After 21.Nd2 or Re2 Black can still reply with''} Bc3 $10 {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: 'RF'' '='}) 21... Bc3 $1 22. Re2 b4 $132 {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: '; "Now Black has sufficient play on the black squares." (KORCHNOI.) '' Korchnoi,V} 23. Nd4 Rfe8 {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: '; "Worried by his loose Pawn front and his scattered minor pieces, Black decides that he ought to get another piece into play rather than spend a move protecting his King's side. However, Fischer soon demonstrates that the White Knight obtains splendid prospects on the King's side,''} ({Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: 'hence''} 23... g6 $142 {Kortschnoj Kortschnoj Ernst: 'Kortschnoj Bobby Fischer: 'is much better." (KORCHNOI.) '' Korchnoi,V: } {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: 'On 23...g6''} 24. Bd3 Nc5 25. Rc2 Nab7 26. Ne2 Bg7 $10 {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: 'the Bishop dances away and White has nothing.'' '='}) 24. Nf5 Nb7 25. Bd4 g6 {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: '; The threat was Nxg7. ''} 26. Nh6+ Kf8 27. Rc1 $1 {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: ', "This powerful move is a reminder to Black that he has problems on the c-file as well as in the neighborhood of his King." (KORCHNOI.) ''} Rac8 {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: '; "In the event of White's exchanging Bishops, Black wants to be ready to recapture with a piece (Queen or Rook) rather than be left with a Pawn on c3 which will most likely be fatally weak." (KORCHNOI.)''} ({Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Not''} 27... Bxd4 28. Qxd4 f6 29. Qxb4) 28. Bd3 {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: ', "This inaccuracy grants Black a fresh chance of recovery.''} ({Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: 'A very strong continuation here was''} 28. Re3 $1 {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: 'with the threat of''} a5 (28... Z0 {Bobby Fischer} 29. Bxc3 bxc3 30. Qd4 $1 f6 31. Bb1 {when the c-Pawn would fall" (KORCHNOI.)}) 29. Bxc3 bxc3 30. Qd4 $1 f6 31. Bb1 $18 {Kortschnoj Korchnoi,V}) 28... Qa5 ({Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: 'On''} 28... Qd8 29. Rec2 {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: 'maintains the pin.''}) 29. Rec2 Ne5 30. Bf1 Nc5 {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: '; "Sacrificing a Pawn for the moment; but the Black pieces obtain excellent activity." (KORCHNOI.) ''} 31. Bxc3 bxc3 32. Rxc3 Kg7 33. Ng4 Nxg4 34. Qxg4 Rb8 {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: '; Breaking the pin and threatening the e-Pawn and/or the b-Pawn.''} ({Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Not''} 34... Rxe4 $4 35. Qxc8) 35. Rf3 {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: ', "White's best chance is to revive his attack on the King's wing." (KORCHNOI.) ''} Nxe4 36. Qf4 f5 ({Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: '"''} 36... Rb7 $5 {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: 'may be safer here." (KORCHNOI.)'' Korchnoi,V}) {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: 'The text weakens the K-side, but White can't exploit it. ''} 37. Re3 Re5 38. Rc6 Rbe8 $5 {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: '; "Short of time, I overlooked White's next move completely.''} ({Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Even so, the text is not bad, but for practical purposes Black ought to choose the simple''} 38... g5 {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: 'maintaining a good position without risk." (KORCHNOT.) '' Korchnoi,V} {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: 'After 38...g5''} 39. Qf3 Rbe8 40. Rxa6 Qxd5 41. b4 $10 {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: 'the chances are approximately equal.'' '='}) 39. Rxd6 $1 Qa1 $2 {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: '; "A bad error, after which Black is two Pawns behind with no compensation.''} ({Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Correct and necessary is''} 39... g5 $142 $1 {Kortschnoj Kortschnoj Ernst: 'Kortschnoj Bobby Fischer: '!'' '!' Korchnoi,V: } 40. Rd7+ Kg6 41. Qf3 Qb6 $1 { xf2!; f6!  xf2!; f6! Ernst: ' xf2!; f6! Bobby Fischer: 'with the threat 42 ...Nxf2!. For instance:''} 42. Bd3 $2 (42. g4 $2 Nxf2 43. Rxe5 Nxg4+) (42. Rxe4 $1 {  Ernst: ' Bobby Fischer: '(best)''} Rxe4 43. g4 Rf4 44. gxf5+ Kh6 45. Qg3 Re5 $10 {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: 'with at least a draw.'' '='}) ({Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: '"Instead, Black panics at the unexpected tum of events, and Fischer efficiently finishes the game in a few moves." (KORCHNOI.) Incidentally, Korchnoi neglects to add that after 41...Qb6! Black has the additional threat of ...Nf6 (as well as ...Nxf2) trapping the Rook. He also neglects to analyze the right defense:''} 42. Qe2 $142 $1 {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: '!'' '!' } Nxf2 ({Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: '(What else? If''} 42... f4 43. Rxe4 Rxe4 44. Qc2 Kh6 45. Rc7 $1 $18 {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: '!' Bobby Fischer: 'wins.''}) 43. Rxe5 $1 Ne4+ ({Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: 'it's fascinating that Black has no better discovery; if''} 43... Ng4+ 44. Re3 $1 Rxe3 45. Qxa6 Qxa6 46. Bxa6 Nf6 $1 47. Rd8 Rxb3 $10 {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: '='' '='}) ({Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: 'But not''} 43... Nxh3+ $2 44. Kh2 Qg1+ 45. Kg3 $1 f4+ 46. Kf3 $1 Rxe5 47. Qxa6+ $1 $18 {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: '!' Bobby Fischer: 'wins.''}) 44. Kh2 Rxe5 45. Qxa6 Qxa6 46. Bxa6 Nf6 $10 {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: 'regaining the d-Pawn with a draw in view.'' '='}) 42... Nxf2 43. Rxe5 Nxd3+) 40. Rxa6 Qd4 41. Rd3 Qb2 42. d6 g5 43. Qe3 f4 44. Qa7+ {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: ', Black resigns.''} (44. Qa7+ {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: 'Black must lose a Rook after''} Kf8 45. d7 Rd8 46. Qb6 Ke7 47. Qxd8+ Kxd8 48. Ra8+ $18 {Ernst: 'Bobby Fischer: 'followed by 49 d8=Q+.''}) 1-0

