 Najdorf hubiera evaluado correctamente las consecuencias de su decisión, habría elegido''' Andrew Soltis: 'This gets Black into major trouble. Betterw as the ugly' Ris,Robert: 'Opening the position (with your king in the centre and other pieces on the back rank still) simply feels wrong. A safer option is'} 9... b4 { ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: ' González,JA: '" (Fischer) y si''' Andrew Soltis: 'Fischer: ''' ChessBase: '' Ris,Robert: 'but then'} 10. Bd3 {(ChessBase) (ChessBase II) González,JA Ris,Robert: 'and the inclusion of the move c2-c4 is in White's favour. White has a nice central grip, can develop his pieces and ideas to play on both sides as Black's kingside has been weakened and with a2-a3 the queenside can be opened as well.'} (10. Qa4+ {Andrew Soltis} Qd7) ({Popov suggested White "stands excellently" after} 10. Be2 {Andrew Soltis} Bxe4 11. Bf3 {but after} Bxf3 12. Qxf3 Ra7 {is unclear}) 10... Nc6) ({ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: '"El anuario soviético de 1962 indica''' Andrew Soltis: 'Or even'} 9... Bxe4 {Ris,Robert: '?!'} 10. cxb5 Bg7 (10... e5 {Andrew Soltis} 11. Ne2 Bb7 12. Nc3 d5 13. Qf3 Ra7 (13... Be7 14. bxa6 Bxa6 15. Nxd5 Bxf1 16. Kxf1) 14. bxa6 Bc6 15. a4 d4 16. Ne4 Bb4+ 17. Kd1 (17. Bd2 $2 Bxd2+ 18. Kxd2 Qa5+ 19. Ke2 Rxa6 20. b3 Rb6 21. Kd1 Bxe4 22. Qxe4 Rxb3 $19) 17... Bxe4 18. Qxe4 Qd6 19. Bb5+ Ke7 20. f4 Nxa6 21. fxe5 Qxe5 22. Qf3 Nc7 23. Bf4 Qd5 24. Qxd5 Nxd5 25. Bd2 Ne3+ 26. Ke2 Bxd2 27. Kxd2 Nxg2 $16) 11. Qg4 Bg6 {Ris,Robert: 'and now instead of'} 12. Nf5 {ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: 'con ventja, pero''' Ris,Robert: 'which was mentioned both by Fischer and Kasparov, I think White might also consider'} (12. f4 $5 {Ris,Robert . In both cases Black remains under serious pressure I would say.}) 12... O-O $13 {ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: 'es confuso" Fischer''' Andrew Soltis: 'Fischer: '''}) (9... e5 $1 {Andrew Soltis} 10. Ne2 f5 11. cxb5 fxe4 12. Nc3 d5 13. bxa6 Bc6 14. Qb3 Bg7 $11) 10. Bxc4 Bxe4 {Gauthier: 'Najdorf wins a center Pawn. This is a worthy goal to strive for you in your own games.' Gauthier: 'Najdorf gewinnt einen Zentralbauern- immer ein lohnendes Ziel, auch in Ihren Partien.'} ({ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: 'Según O'Kelly, es mejor''' Andrew Soltis: 'Also bad is'} 10... Qa5+ {ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: 'pero esta variante ya había sido considerada por Fischer:'''} 11. Bd2 Qe5 {ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: 'pero ahora sigue''' Andrew Soltis: 'because of'} 12. Qb3 $1 {Andrew Soltis: 'Fischer: '!''} Qxe4+ {Andrew Soltis: '!' '!'} 13. Kd1 $40 {Andrew Soltis: 'Fischer: '''} ({o bien Ris,Robert: 'I love this move, preparing e1 and is clearly more ambitious than'} 13. Be3 $18 {(ChessBase) (ChessBase II) (González,JA) con ataque ganador}) 13... e6 {Ris,Robert} 14. Nxe6 $1 ({Even stronger than} 14. Re1 {Andrew Soltis: '!' '!' which is Kasparov's recommendation.} Qxd4 {Andrew Soltis} 15. Qxb7 Qa7 16. Qc8+ {and Bxe6} Ke7 17. Bxe6) 14... fxe6 15. Bxe6 {and because of Black's coordination problems (king in centre, underdevelopment, b7 which requires protection) White quickly brings in his rook to e1 with a crushing attack. You hardly feel have just sacrificed a piece :)}) 11. O-O {Ris,Robert: '!' Andrew Soltis: '!' '!' Ris,Robert: 'Simple chess: just completing your development!'} d5 {ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: '!''' Andrew Soltis: '!' '!'} ({Si Andrew Soltis: 'The game wouldn't have reached move 20, let alone Fischer's prediction of 25, if Black had played' Ris,Robert: 'In the event of'} 11... e6 {(ChessBase) (ChessBase II) González,JA Ris,Robert: 'sacrifices on e6 may be considered, though probably many of us would first play'} 12. Re1 {[%csl Ye6][%cal Ye1e6,Yc4e6] con amenaza de sacrificio en e6 (O'Kelly) Ris,Robert: '!?' Andrew Soltis: 'and allowed a sacrifice on e6'}) 12. Re1 {ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: '!' González,JA: 'Ahora la amenaza es 13.xe4 dxe4 14.xf7+ (O'Kelly)''' Ris,Robert: '?!' Gauthier: '?!' Gauthier: 'If Najdorf takes the c4-Bishop, White returns the favor and takes the e4-Bishop with his Rook.' Gauthier: 'Schlägt Najdorf nun den Läufer, hält Weiß sich an seinem Kollegen auf e4 schadlos.'} ({Probably Fischer's only inaccurate decision, but in this complex position with a wealth of options both players overlooked Black's powerful resource on the next move. After} 12. Bb3 $1 {Ris,Robert intending a4 and installing a knight on c6, Black's position will be paralysed.} Bg7 ({Another nice line illustrating the effect of White's 12th move:} 12... e6 13. Re1 Bc5 14. Ba4+ Nd7 15. b4 $1 Bb6 (15... Bxb4 16. Nc6 Qb6 17. Rxe4 $1 dxe4 18. Rb1 {and White is winning.}) 16. Nc6 Qc7 17. Qg4 {and there are no good moves left for Black.}) 13. Ba4+ Nd7 14. Re1 O-O 15. Nc6 Qc7 (15... Qe8 16. f3) 16. Nxe7+ $18 {followed by taking on d5, leading to a position with extra pawn, bishop pair and better structure.}) 12... e5 {Andrew Soltis: '?' '?' Andrew Soltis: 'This was the last major choice Black made.' Gauthier: 'Fischer now has two pieces hanging.' Gauthier: 'Nun hängen bei Fischer zwei Figuren.'} (12... Rg8 {Ris,Robert: '?' Ris,Robert: 'is met by'} 13. Rxe4 $1 dxe4 14. Qh5 Rg7 {Andrew Soltis: 'Fischer'} ({ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: 'si'''} 14... Rg6 15. Qxh7 Rg7 16. Qxe4 Ra7 17. Nf5 {ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: '''' Andrew Soltis: 'with a winning attack in either case.'} ({ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: 'o bien'''} 17. Bf4 {Andrew Soltis: 'Fischer'})) (14... Qxd4 {Ris,Robert} 15. Qxf7+ Kd8 16. Be3 {with a crushing attack.}) 15. Nf5 {ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: ''''}) ({ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: 'Hubiera sido pasiva''' Andrew Soltis: 'or'} 12... e6 13. Qh5 ({Again} 13. Bb3 $5 {Ris,Robert makes sense as well.}) 13... Bg6 14. Qxd5 Qxd5 {Andrew Soltis: 'Fischer'} 15. Bxd5 Ra7 16. Bf4 Rd7 17. Nxe6 fxe6 18. Bxe6 Nc6 19. Rac1 {ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: '+-' González,JA: 'etc. Fischer'''}) ({Andrew Soltis: 'From now on both players have to consider the possibility of Rxe4, and if ...dxe4 then either Bxf7+ or a queen to b3 or h5. This can't be stopped by artificial means'} 12... h5 13. Rxe4 $1 dxe4 14. Qb3 $1 Qxd4 15. Be3 $18 {ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: 'con ataque ganador (Fischer)''' Andrew Soltis: 'Fischer: '+-'' Ris,Robert: 'followed by taking on f7 and d1.'}) ({Andrew Soltis: 'His move was superior to'} 12... Nd7 13. Nc6 (13. Rxe4 $1 {Ris,Robert} dxe4 (13... dxc4 14. Nc6 Qc7 15. Rxc4 {with a free attack!}) 14. Bxf7+ $1 Kxf7 15. Qh5+ Kg8 16. Qg4+ Bg7 17. Nf5 {and White wins, as} Qf8 18. Nh6#) 13... Qc7 14. Bxd5 {ChessBase: 'ChessBase II: 'González,JA: '' González,JA: 'etc. (Fischer)'''}) ({Andrew Soltis: 'But two captures come into consideration. Fischer felt White had a winning position even though two pawns down after' Ris,Robert: 'The remarkable'} 12... Bxg2 {Ris,Robert: '!' Gauthier: '!' Ris,Robert: 'would have kept Black in the game!'} {Ris,Robert: 'After'} 13. Kxg2 (13. Qa4+ {[%csl Yc4,Ye8,Yg2]} Nd7 {[%csl Yc4,Yg2]} 14. Kxg2 {[%csl Yc4]} Rg8+ {[%csl Yc4,Yg2]} 15. Kh1 {[%csl Yc4]} dxc4 {[%csl Yc4]} 16. Qxc4 Qb6 {[%cal Yg8g5] and Black has the advantage with his King relatively safe and a Rook bearing down on White's King.  Notice also that Black didn't castle, but his King certainly looks safer than White's.  Press the Delete Key to return to the main line. und aufgrund seiner relativ sicheren Königsstellung und des gegen den feindlichen König gericheten Turms ist Schwarz im Vorteil.  Beachten Sie: Schwarz hat zwar nicht rochiert, trotzdem aber steht sein König sicherer als der weiße.  Drücken von "ENTFERNEN" bringt Sie zur Partie zurück.}) 13... dxc4 (13... Rg8+ {Andrew Soltis} 14. Kh1 dxc4 15. Qf3 Ra7 16. Bf4 e5 17. Bxe5 fxe5 18. Rxe5+ Re7 19. Nc6 Qd3 20. Qxd3 cxd3 21. Nxe7 Bxe7 22. Rd5 Nc6 23. Rxd3 $15) 14. Qf3 {Ris,Robert: 'various annotators have tried to prove something in vain, as with correct play Black should be able to manage