{Wahls,Matthias: 'Inf.2/236 Andrew Soltis: 'It was at Havana that Fischer sprang his most important new idea of the 1960s, the improved Exchange Variation of the Ruy Lopez. He first used 5.O-O to beat Portisch in 34 moves, then two days later faced Gligoric, who mus thave been searching for a better defense. It didn't show. Fischer's third victim, Eleazar Jimenez, put up little resistance a week later and lost in 33 moves.''} 1. e4 {Wahls,Matthias Wahls,Matthias: 'Andrew Soltis Wahls Wahls'} e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Bxc6 {Wahls,Matthias: 'Andrew Soltis: ''!'''} ({At the Capablanca Memorial, Fischer thought two minutes - actually more because of the transmission delays - before playing} 4. Ba4 {(Wahls,Matthias) (Andrew Soltis) against Smyslov. Evidently he was considering 4.Bxc6 but decided to keep the secret, as it turned out, for another 14 months.}) 4... dxc6 (4... bxc6 {Wahls,Matthias} 5. d4 exd4 6. Qxd4 {Andrew Soltis: ''} Qf6 7. Qd3 $1 $14 {Andrew Soltis: '!'} (7. e5 Qg6 8. O-O Bb7 9. e6 $2 fxe6 10. Ne5 Qxg2+ {Andrew Soltis: '!'} 11. Kxg2 c5+ $19)) 5. O-O {Wahls,Matthias: 'Andrew Soltis: '!' Andrew Soltis: 'Lasker,Em; Bernstein,O; Barendregt,n''} (5. d4 {(Wahls,Matthias) Andrew Soltis}) 5... f6 {Wahls,Matthias: 'Andrew Soltis: ''!'''} ({Wahls,Matthias: 'Andrew Soltis: 'The opening books of the day ridiculed this and gave''} 5... Bg4 $6 {Wahls,Matthias: 'Andrew Soltis: '!' Andrew Soltis: 'and if '!?'''} 6. h3 h5 {Wahls,Matthias: 'Andrew Soltis: '!' Andrew Soltis: '. Isaac Boleslavsky, for example, only considered '!?'''} (6... Bxf3 {Wahls,Matthias} 7. Qxf3 Qf6 8. Qg3 Bd6 9. d3 Qg6 10. Be3 {Andrew Soltis: '!?'} Qxg3 11. fxg3 $14 {Hort,V-Kolarov/Polanica Zdroj/1967/1-0/34/ Andrew Soltis: 'Hort,V-Koralov,n POL 1967'}) 7. d4 $1 (7. d3 $1 {(Wahls,Matthias) Andrew Soltis: ''!''} Qf6 {Andrew Soltis: 'Nevertheless, 5.O-O had been the favorite line of the Dutch master Barendregt who kept trying to bolster White's chances. His efforts seemed doomed after he lost a 1962