{Andrew Soltis: 'Fischer's late comeback made the Piatigorsky Cup a battle between him and Spassky, who recalled how up to 1500 spectators (in a hall that seated 800) were on hand for the final rounds. The following game was Fischer's last victory and tied him for first place. But in the next round he could only draw with Spassky, who finished ahead of him by winning on the last day.'} {Chess Informant Ftacnik,L: 'Ivkov,B: 'Chess Informant''} 1. e4 {Andrew Soltis Ftacnik Ftacnik,L: 'Ivkov,B' Ftacnik,L: 'Ftacnik,Lubomir Ivkov,B Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Ivkov,Borislav''} c5 2. Nf3 Nc6 {Andrew Soltis: 'This was Najdorf's first game against Fischer with Black since the debacle in Varna. He wrote in the tournament book that he "did not consider it wise to try" the Najdorf Variation against Fischer because he "is one of the greatest specialists in this opening."'} 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 e6 (4... Nf6 {Ftacnik} 5. Nc3) 5. Nb5 {Andrew Soltis: 'Fischer never allowed his opponents to steer into the Scheveningen variation.'} (5. c4 {(Ftacnik)  Alekhine,A} Nf6 6. Nc3 Bb4 $10) 5... d6 6. Bf4 {Ftacnik: '!?' Ftacnik,L: '!?' '!?' '!?' Ftacnik,Lubomir: '!?'} (6. c4 $142 {Ftacnik}) 6... e5 (6... Ne5 $5 {Ftacnik} 7. N1a3 $1 {Bronstein,D} (7. Qd4 {Euwe,M} a6 8. Nxd6+ $4 Bxd6 9. Bxe5 Qa5+ $1 {Zuckerman,B})) 7. Be3 Nf6 ({Andrew Soltis: 'Now on'} 7... a6 {Ftacnik} 8. N5c3 Nf6 {Andrew Soltis: 'Fischer got excellent play against Badilles, in one of the 1967 exhibition games in Manila with'} 9. Bg5 {Andrew Soltis: 'Ftacnik'} (9. Bc4 $1 {Andrew Soltis: '. Play continued'} Be7 10. Nd5 $1 {Andrew Soltis: 'Ftacnik: '!''} Nxd5 11. Bxd5 O-O 12. Nc3 {× d5; Fischer,R-Badilles,G/Meralco/1967/ Andrew Soltis: 'Ftacnik: '× d5; Fischer,R-Badilles,G/Meralco/1967/''} Kh8 {Andrew Soltis} 13. O-O Be6 14. Bb3 Na5 15. Nd5) 9... Be7) 8. Bg5 $5 {Ftacnik: 'Bronstein,D' Andrew Soltis: 'Ftacnik: '!?' Ftacnik: 'Bronstein,D''} (8. Bc4 {Ftacnik} Be6 $1 (8... Nxe4 $4 9. Qd5 Be6 10. Qxe4 d5 11. Bxd5 $1 $18) 9. Bxe6 fxe6 10. c4 $1 