. Nf2 Re8 13. e4 $1 (13. cxd5 $6 Bxd3 14. Qxd3 cxd5 15. c4 dxc4 16. Qxc4 Rc8 17. Qa4 exd4 18. Qxd4 Nc5 19. Qxd8 Rexd8 20. Bb2 $6 Nd5 21. Rfe1 b5 $15 22. Rab1 a6 23. h4 h6 24. g4 $6 {×f3} Nb6 $1 25. Bd4 Nc4 26. Bxc5 Rxc5 $17 27. Rbc1 Rcc8 $1 28. Ra1 Rd2 29. f4 Rc2 30. e4 Rc3 31. a4 b4 $19 32. Rec1 Nd2 33. Rd1 Rc2 34. Nd3 b3 35. Nb4 Nf3+ 36. Kf1 Rh2 37. Rab1 b2 38. Nd3 {Illincic-Abramovic/Jugoslavia-ch/1994} (38. Nd3 Rcc2 $19)) 13... h6 (13... dxe4 14. fxe4 c5 (14... Nf8 15. Be3 Ne6 16. d5 $14) 15. d5 $14) 14. Be3 exd4 15. cxd4 dxe4 16. fxe4 c5 17. d5 Ne5 $13) 7. cxd5 exd5 (7... Nxd5 {(Ripperger) Lin-Agdestein Gheorghiu/RR: '?' Gheorghiu/RR: 'Mednis'} 8. c4 $16 {Gheorghiu/RR}) 8. e3 Nh5 {'?!' This move was considered adequate based on the game Gligoric-Averbakh, Saltsjobaden IZ 1952. By threatening a check on h4, Black hopes to weaken White's kingside.} 9. Qc2 {Gheorghiu/RR: '!' '!' Now 9...Qh4+ is countered by 10 Qf2 with a favourable endgame for White.} (9. g3 {Gheorghiu/RR} f5 10. Bd3 b6 11. Ne2 Ba6 12. Bxa6 Nxa6 13. Qd3 Qc8 14. c4 $14 {Gheorghiu-Averbach/Mar del Plata/1964}) 9... Re8 (9... Qh4+ {Gheorghiu/RR} 10. Qf2 $16 { Mednis}) 10. g4 {Gheorghiu/RR: '!' '!'} Nf4 11. h4 {Ripperger: '!' '!' Ripperger: '[The Romanian grandmaster plays very strong, so that Black has no chances.]' Ripperger: '[Der rumänische Großmeister spielt sehr stark, so daß Schwarz keinen Durchbruch erzwingen kann.]'} c5 12. Kf2 {'!' A colourful position - without developing a single minor piece and already having begun a pawn offensive on the kingside, White now makes a move with his king! Amazingly, he also stands better!} Ng6 13. Bd3 $1 ({In the aforementioned game Gligoric-Averbakh, Saltsjobaden IZ 1952 White adopted an incorrect plan which involved advancing the h-pawn and transferring the knight to f4:} 13. h5 $6 {and after} Nf8 14. Ne2 Nc6 15. Nf4 Ne6 16. Nxe6 Bxe6 17. Bd3 h6 {Black has good play.}) 13... Nc6 14. Ne2 Be6 ({In various opening reference works Black's last move is considered to be the root cause of his problems and} 14... Nf8 15. Kg3 Be6 {(Kogan-B.Vladimirov, Leningrad 1960) 'with a promising position for Black' is instead suggested. I believe that this is a misunderstanding - the plan of attacking with a kingside pawn-storm followed by a breakthrough in the centre as in our main game makes Black's defensive task very difficult indeed.}) 15. g5 {Gheorghiu/RR: '!' Gheorghiu/RR: 'Gheorghiu offered a draw.' '!' After making this strong move, Gheorghiu offered a draw! Of course, this was not based on any displeasure with his position but rather on the strength of his opponent and his brilliant performance in the Olympiad. Without thinking, Fischer declined.} (15. h5 {Gheorghiu/RR} Nf8 $11 {Gligoric-Averbach/Stockholm izt/1952}) 15... Rc8 16. h5 Nf8 17. g6 {Gheorghiu/RR: '!' '!'} fxg6 (17... Qf6 $142 {Gheorghiu/RR}) 18. hxg6 h6 $16 19. Qb1 {Gheorghiu/RR: '!'} Na5 20. Nf4 c4 {Gheorghiu/RR: '?'} (20... cxd4 {Gheorghiu/RR} 21. cxd4 $16 {Mednis}) 21. Bc2 (21. Bf5 $2 {Gheorghiu/RR} Nb3 22. Bxe6+ Nxe6 23. Qf5 Ng5 $1 $17) 21... Rc6 {White's following series of moves is aimed at improving the position of the a1-rook and the c1-bishop.} 22. Ra2 {Gheorghiu/RR: '!' '!'} Nd7 (22... Rb6 {Gheorghiu/RR} 23. Rb2 Rxb2 24. Qxb2 $16 { Mednis}) 23. a4 {'!'} Nf6 24. Ba3 {Gheorghiu/RR: '!'} Qd7 25. Rb2 b6 (25... Nb3 $142 {Gheorghiu/RR} 26. Bxb3 cxb3 27. Rxb3 $16 {}) 26. Rb5 {Gheorghiu/RR: '!' '!'} Nb7 $16 {Now everything is ready for a breakthrough in the centre.} 27. e4 {Gheorghiu/RR: '!' '!'} dxe4 28. Bxe4 {Ripperger: '!' Ripperger: '' Gheorghiu/RR: '!' Ripperger: '[Fischer must not take the bishop, because it would leave his pieces in total disarray.]' Ripperger: '[Fischer darf den Läufer nicht schlagen, da seine Figuren danach völlig desorganisiert sind.]'} (28. fxe4 $6 {Gheorghiu/RR}) 28... Rcc8 (28... Nxe4+ {Gheorghiu/RR} 29. Qxe4 $18 {'!' does not improve Black's situation.}) 29. Re5 {Gheorghiu/RR: '!' Gheorghiu/RR: '30.d5, 30.Lb7' '!'} Bg4 (29... Nd6 {Gheorghiu/RR loses to} 30. Bxd6 Qxd6 31. Rxe6 (31. Nxe6 Rxe6 32. Rxe6) 31... Rxe6 32. Nxe6 Qxe6 33. Bf5 $18) 30. Nd5 {Gheorghiu/RR: '+-!'} Rxe5 31. Nxf6+ gxf6 32. dxe5 Nc5 33. Bxc5 Qd2+ 34. Kg3 Bxf3 (34... Rxc5 {Gheorghiu/RR} 35. Qc1 $18) 35. Bxf3 Rxc5 36. Qc1 Qxc1 37. Rxc1 {The remaining moves were played through inertia:} Rxe5 38. Kf4 Kg7 39. Be4 h5 40. Rd1 Re7 41. Rd5 Kh6 42. Rd6 Kg7 43. Rc6 h4 44. Rxc4 h3 45. Kg3 Kh6 46. Bb1 {Gheorghiu/RR: '!'} Re3+ 47. Kh2 Re1 48. Bd3 Re3 49. Rh4+ Kg5 50. g7 {As a result of Gheorghiu's superb victory, 8...Nh5 almost totally disappeared from tournament play.} 1-0

