tis: 'ChessBase: 'loses to''} (31... Qf6 32. Qg3 $1 {Andrew Soltis: '. This last one requires some amplification:'} Re8 $1 33. Bb1 $1 Ra7 34. Bg5 $1 Qxa1 35. Bh6+ Kh8 36. Qxg6 {with crushing threats.}) (31... gxf5 32. Qg5+ Kh7 33. e7 Qe8 34. Re6 $1) 32. Qe7+ Kg8 33. Qd8+ Kg7 34. Qc7+ Kg8 35. e7 $18) 30... Qxf4 31. Bxf4 Re8 $2 {Maric,Rudolf: 'Ftacnik,L: '?'' Andrew Soltis: 'Time trouble. Better is 31...Rxa2. Now White wins material and the rest is a matter of technique.' Andrew Soltis: 'Time trouble. Better is 31...Rxa2. Now White wins material and the rest is a matter of technique. Garry Kasparov: 'An error in reply.''} (31... Rxa2 $1 {Maric,Rudolf: 'Ftacnik,L: '!' '!'' Andrew Soltis: 'ChessBase'} 32. Rxa2 {Maric,Rudolf: 'Ftacnik,L'} ({Andrew Soltis: '. "On'} 32. Rad1 Ra7 {Ftacnik,L Andrew Soltis: 'holds.'}) (32. Z0) 32... Nxa2 33. Ne5 g5 34. Bg3 {Maric,Rudolf: '' Ftacnik,L: '' "behält Weiß die Initiative, aber Schwarz hat Remischancen." (Fischer)} Nb4 $1 {he achieves his goal:} 35. Nxc4 (35. Ng6 Re8) 35... bxc4 36. Be5+ Bf6 37. Bd6 Re8 38. Bxc5 Nd3 39. Bxd3 cxd3 {, aiming for the exchange of his d-pawn for the e-pawn and an ending with three pawns against two on one wing.}) ({Andrew Soltis: 'Stein believed that' Andrew Soltis: 'ChessBase: 'Stein believed that''} 31... Ra6 {Ftacnik,L Andrew Soltis: 'would have drawn. But ChessBase: 'Andrew Soltis'' Andrew Soltis: 'ChessBase: 'would have drawn. But''} 32. Rad1 (32. a3 {offers good winning chances and Fischer's Andrew Soltis: 'ChessBase: 'offers good winning chances and Fischer's''}) 32... Rxe6 33. Rd7 { g5}) 32. Rad1 $1 {Andrew Soltis: 'ChessBase: '!'' Andrew Soltis: 'ChessBase: '!' '!'' Andrew Soltis: 'ChessBase: '!' '!' Garry Kasparov: '!'' Die Drohung d7 ist tödlich. Andrew Soltis: 'ChessBase: 'Die Drohung d7 ist tödlich.''} Ra6 (32... Rxa2 {Andrew Soltis: 'ChessBase' Andrew Soltis: 'ChessBase Garry Kasparov: 'is now too late in view of''} 33. Rd7 Ra6 34. Bb1 {Andrew Soltis: 'Garry Kasparov: '!''} Nc6 35. Bg5 Nb6 36. Be4 $3 Nc8 37. Nh4 {, winning. The mobility of the 'Spanish' bishop is fantastic!}) 33. Rd7 {Maric,R: '!' Maric,Rudolf: '!'} ({Andrew Soltis: 'Much faster is' Andrew Soltis: 'ChessBase: 'Much faster is''} 33. Bb7 $142 $1 {Ftacnik,L Andrew Soltis: '!' '!' '!' Andrew Soltis: 'ChessBase: 'Andrew Soltis''} Ra7 (33... Z0) ({. While after} 33... Rxa2 34. Rd7 Nb6 {White wins by} 35. Bc7 Nc4 36. Bd8 Kf6 ({or} 36... Kf8 37. Bxe7+ Rxe7 38. Nh4 $1) 37. Bxe7+ Rxe7 38. g4 $1 {. But the move in the game is also very strong.}) 34. Rd7 {Andrew Soltis: 'Garry Kasparov: '." (Fischer)''} Nb6 35. Bd6 $1) 33... Rxe6 {Andrew Soltis: '!' '!' '!''ChessBase: 'Andrew Soltis: '!'''} 34. Ng5 Rf6 {Andrew Soltis: 'Equally inadequate is 34...Ra6 35. Bb1 Kf6 36. Ne4+ Kf7 37. Nxc5.'} (34... Ra6 {Ftacnik,L} 35. Bb1 Kf6 36. Ne4+ Kf7 37. Nxc5 $18) 35. Bf3 {Maric,R: '+-!' Maric,Rudolf'ChessBase: 'Andrew Soltis: '!''' 'ChessBase: 'Andrew Soltis: '!' '!''' : '+-!' Maric,Rudolf: 'Ftacnik,L: '!' '!'' Andrew Soltis: '!' '!'} ({Both} 35. Bb7) ({and} 35. g3 {would also have won}) ({but the most elegant way was} 35. a3 $1 Nxa3 36. Be5 Nc4 37. Ba1 $1 Nb6 38. Rb7 Nc8 39. Bb1 $1 {(amazing dances by the bishops again!).}) 35... Rxf4 ({Andrew Soltis: 'there is no way to save material' Andrew Soltis: 'ChessBase: 'there is no way to save material''} 35... Kf8 {Ftacnik,L Andrew Soltis: 'ChessBase: 'Andrew Soltis''} 36. Nh7+ {Andrew Soltis: '. Fischer navigated through the final traps' Andrew Soltis: 'ChessBase: '. Fischer navigated through the final traps''}) 36. Ne6+ Kf6 37. Nxf4 Ne5 38. Rb7 ({Brilliancy such as} 38. a3 $5 Nxd7 39. axb4 Nf8 40. bxc5 {is not required. As it is, the outcome is obvious: White accurately converts his exchange advantage.}) 38... Bd6 39. Kf1 Nc2 ({Andrew Soltis: 'oR'} 39... Nxf3 {Ftacnik,L} 40. Rxe8 Nd2+ 41. Ke2 Bxf4 42. Rf8+ Kg5 (42... Ke5 43. Rxf4) 43. Rxf4 Kxf4 44. Kxd2 $18) 40. Re4 {Maric,R: '!' Maric,Rudolf: 'ChessBase: 'Andrew Soltis: '!''' 'ChessBase: 'Andrew Soltis: '!' '!''' '!' Andrew Soltis: '!' '!'} Nd4 41. Rb6 {Maric,R: '!' Maric,Rudolf: 'ChessBase: 'Andrew Soltis: '!''' 'ChessBase: 'Andrew Soltis: '!' '!''' '!' Andrew Soltis: '!' '!'} Rd8 42. Nd5+ Kf5 43. Ne3+ {Maric,Rudolf: 'Ftacnik,L: '' ''' Andrew Soltis: 'Garry Kasparov: 'The sealed move. The adjournment session did not last long.''} Ke6 ({Andrew Soltis: 'If'} 43... Kf6 {Ftacnik,L Andrew Soltis: 'White was intending'} 44. Be2 {Andrew Soltis: '!'} b4 45. f4 $18 { c4 Andrew Soltis: 'and then Bc4.'}) 44. Be2 {Maric,Rudolf: 'Ftacnik,L: ''ChessBase: 'Andrew Soltis: '!''' 'ChessBase: 'Andrew Soltis: '!' '!''' +-!' '+-!' Ftacnik,L: 'Kmoch,H:  f2-f4; xb5'' Andrew Soltis: '!' '!'} Kd7 45. Bxb5+ Nxb5 46. Rxb5 Kc6 47. a4 Bc7 48. Ke2 g5 49. g3 Ra8 50. Rb2 Rf8 51. f4 gxf4 52. gxf4 Nf7 53. Re6+ Nd6 {Andrew Soltis: 'If 53...Bd6 54. Rf6! ends resistance.'} (53... Bd6 {Ftacnik,L} 54. Rf6 $1) 54. f5 Ra8 55. Rd2 {Maric,Rudolf: 'Ftacnik,L: ''ChessBase: 'Andrew Soltis: '!''' 'ChessBase: 'Andrew Soltis: '!' '!''' !' '!'' Andrew Soltis: '!' '!'} Rxa4 56. f6 {Andrew Soltis: 'Black Resigns.' Quelle: Fischer "Meine 60 denkwürdigen Partien" (dt. Fassung) Andrew Soltis: 'ChessBase: 'Quelle: Fischer "Meine 60 denkwürdigen Partien" (dt. Fassung) ''} Rf4 57. Nd5 $1 {Maric,Rudolf: 'Ftacnik,L: '+-' '+-'' Andrew Soltis: 'etc. A dramatic, fighting game!'} Re4+ 58. Rxe4 Nxe4 59. f7 1-0

