1. e4 {Ivkov,Borislav Ivkov,Borislav} e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Ba4 Nf6 5. O-O Be7 6. Re1 b5 7. Bb3 d6 8. c3 O-O 9. h3 h6 10. d4 Re8 11. Be3 Bf8 12. Nbd2 Bb7 13. Qb1 Qb8 {With the bishop on b7, this regrouping is too slow and allows White to consolidate his space advantage. With the bishop on b7, this regrouping is too slow and allows White to consolidate his space advantage.} (13... d5 $6 {Ivkov,Borislav: '!?' '!?' has been tried a couple of times, but is unsound. has been tried a couple of times, but is unsound.} 14. Nxe5 (14. dxe5 Nxe4 15. Nxe4 dxe4 16. Qxe4 Na5 17. Qg4 Nxb3 18. axb3 Bxf3 19. Qxf3 Rxe5 20. Bf4 Rxe1+ 21. Rxe1 $14 {Despite simplifications, Black cannot easily neutralise White's pressure. Despite simplifications, Black cannot easily neutralise White's pressure.} c5 22. Qb7 Qc8 23. Qxc8 Rxc8 24. Rd1 Be7 25. Be3 Rc7 26. g4 Kf8 27. Kg2 Ke8 28. Kf3 Rd7 29. Ra1 Rd6 30. Ke2 Re6 31. f4 Kd7 32. Kf3 Kc8 33. f5 Rc6 34. Ke4 $16 {Balashov,Y (2570)-Nikolaevsky,Y (2490)/Leningrad 1971/URS-ch (1-0, 61)}) 14... Nxe5 15. dxe5 Rxe5 16. Bd4 (16. f4 Rxe4 $1 $44) 16... Rxe4 $6 {This gives up the exchange for nothing. This gives up the exchange for nothing.} (16... Re8 {would have required from White the taking of some risks in order to maintain the initiative. would have required from White the taking of some risks in order to maintain the initiative.} 17. e5 c5 18. exf6 Rxe1+ 19. Qxe1 cxd4 20. fxg7 Bxg7 21. cxd4 Bxd4 22. Rd1 {[%cal Gd2f3]} Bxb2 23. Ne4 $36) 17. Nxe4 Nxe4 18. Qd1 $14 {Spassky,B-Medina Garcia,A/Palma de Mallorca 1969/MCD (1-0, 30)}) (13... Qd7 $5 {may be a worthy try to prepare d6-d5, but further practice is needed. may be a worthy try to prepare d6-d5, but further practice is needed.} 14. a3 {White clearly needs an improvement over this standard continuation. Things do not look too good if White answers a developing move with a modest pawn advance. White clearly needs an improvement over this standard continuation. Things do not look too good if White answers a developing move with a modest pawn advance.} (14. a4 $5 {may be a try. In any case, the opening of the centre does not favour Black anymore: may be a try. In any case, the opening of the centre does not favour Black anymore:} d5 15. dxe5 Nxe5 16. Nxe5 Rxe5 17. Bd4 Re6 18. axb5 axb5 19. Rxa8 Bxa8 20. e5 $36) 14... d5 $5 15. dxe5 Nxe5 16. Nxe5 Rxe5 17. Bd4 (17. f4 Rxe4 $1 18. Nxe4 Nxe4 $44 {The weakness of the e4-square and of the whole white kingside offers Black excellent compensation for the sacrificed exchange. The weakness of the e4-square and of the whole white kingside offers Black excellent compensation for the sacrificed exchange.}) 17... Re6 18. e5 Rae8 $1 {The main idea of the move 13...d7 is revealed. The connection of the rooks is possible at once. The main idea of the move 13...d7 is revealed. The connection of the rooks is possible at once.} 19. f4 c5 20. Be3 Nh5 21. Bd1 d4 22. Bxh5 dxe3 23. Nf1 (23. Nf3 $16 {Balashov}) 23... c4 { c5  c5} 24. Qd1 Qc7 25. Nxe3 Bc5 $36 {Murrey,J (2450)-Balashov,Y (2590)/Moskva (open) 1991 (0-1, 45)}) (13... Nb8 {Ivkov,Borislav}) 14. a3 {Ivkov,Borislav: 'N!' 'N!'} (14. a4 {(Ivkov,Borislav) Ü 7/272}) 14... Nd8 15. Bc2 c6 16. b4 {Ivkov,Borislav: '' ''} Qc7 17. Bd3 Ne6 18. Qc2 Rac8 19. a4 $14 {A dream position for Fischer. Black has absolutely no counterplay and has to wait for the execution. A dream position for Fischer. Black has absolutely no counterplay and has to wait for the execution.} Nd7 20. Qb3 Nf4 {Ivkov,Borislav: '?' '?'} 21. Bxf4 exf4 22. c4 {Ivkov,Borislav: '' ''} bxc4 23. Bxc4 d5 {Ivkov,Borislav: '!' '!'} 24. Bd3 Rb8 25. Qc3 Qb6 {Ivkov,Borislav: '??' '??'} (25... Ba8 {Ivkov,Borislav} 26. Reb1 Qb7 $16) 26. Reb1 {Ivkov,Borislav: '!' '!'} Ba8 27. a5 Qa7 (27... Bxb4 {Ivkov,Borislav} 28. axb6 Bxc3 29. Rxa6 $18) 28. e5 Rb7 {Ivkov,Borislav: '?' '?'} 29. Qxc6 {Ivkov,Borislav: '+-!' '+-!'} Bxb4 30. Qxa6 Qb8 31. Bc2 {Ivkov,Borislav: '!' '!'} Re6 32. Qd3 Nf8 {Ivkov,Borislav: '?' '?'} (32... g6 {Ivkov,Borislav}) 33. Qf5 Ra6 34. Nb3 g6 {Ivkov,Borislav: '?!' '?!'} 35. Qxf4 Bc3 36. Nc5 Rxa5 37. Nxb7 Rxa1 38. Rxa1 Ne6 39. Qf6 {Ivkov,Borislav: '!' '!'} Bxa1 40. Nd6 Qc7 41. Bxg6 Qc1+ 42. Ne1 {Ivkov,Borislav: '!' '!'} Qxe1+ 43. Kh2 Ng5 44. Bxf7+ 1-0

