Rxg8 33. g3 Rg4 {. He thinks that he can achieve more.}) 31... f5 {Garry Kasparov: '!'} 32. Re1 {Garry Kasparov: '!' Garry Kasparov: 'For the moment a tough struggle between two worthy opponents is in progress. White is pressing on the weaknesses and skilfully maintaining the tension.'} ({The variation} 32. Kg1 {Garry Kasparov} d5 33. cxd5 Bxd5 34. Be2 $1 ({but not} 34. g4 $6 fxg4 35. Rxf8 Rxf8 36. Rxg4 Rf3 37. Rd4 b5 $1) 34... Rc8 35. g4 Rc2 36. Rh5+ Kg7 37. Rg5+ {would have led to a draw (since} Kf6 $2 38. gxf5 {is bad for Black).}) 32... Rf7 $15 33. b5 {ChessBase: '=' ChessBase: 'Suetin'} (33. Kh2 Rg7 $15) 33... axb5 34. cxb5 Bd7 (34... Bd5 $2 {Garry Kasparov} 35. Bxf5) 35. g4 $2 {Garry Kasparov: 'Fischer has achieved his aim: White has come out of cover and begun pressing over the entire board. In reply Black is prepared for a counterattack.'} (35. a4 $15 {ChessBase: '' ChessBase: 'Suetin'}) 35... Ra8 $17 {Garry Kasparov: '!'} ({Of course not} 35... fxg4 $2 {Garry Kasparov} 36. Bg6 $1 {.}) 36. gxf5 exf5 {Garry Kasparov: 'In this position the fate of the game was decided, and essentially that of the entire match.'} 37. Bc4 {ChessBase: '??' Garry Kasparov: '??' Garry Kasparov: 'In time-trouble Larsen makes an aggressive move, allowing a cunning counter by his opponent.'} ({Garry Kasparov: 'After the obvious'} 37. Reg1 {ChessBase Garry Kasparov: ', Fischer would have had to find a couple of accurate moves in order to extinguish the opponent's initiative:'} Ra4 {Garry Kasparov: '!'} (37... Rf6 38. Be2 Be8 39. Rg8 $18) ({Garry Kasparov: 'not'} 37... Rxa3 {Garry Kasparov: '?'} 38. Rg6+ Kh7 {Garry Kasparov: 'on account of'} (38... Kh5 39. Be2+ $18) 39. Rxd6 $16 { 40.d7:} (39. Bc4 $1 {Garry Kasparov} Rh3+ 40. Kg2 Kxg6 41. Kxh3+)) 38. Rg6+ Kh7 39. Rxd6 Rxh4+ 40. Kg2 $10 {Garry Kasparov: ', and now'} Bxb5 $1 {Garry Kasparov} ({avoiding the slightly inferior endgame after} 40... Rg7+ {Garry Kasparov} 41. Kf2) {, with a pretty perpetual check –} 41. Bxb5 Rg7+ 42. Kf2 Rf