in} (38. Rb8 Bf7 39. e8=Q Bxe8 40. Rxe8 b1=Q 41. Rc8+) 38... Kxb2 39. Kd4 Bf7 40. Kc5 Kc3 41. Kd6 Kd4 42. Kd7) 38. Kd4 b1=Q 39. Rxb1 Kxb1 40. Kc5 Kc2 41. Kd6 {ChessBase: 'Andrew Soltis: 'This was the Fischer that fans remembered. When the world's newest grandmaster, Bu Xiangzi, was interviewed in 2002 he recalled that his favorite book when he was growing up was a Chinese translation of My 60 Memorable Games. "His games were fantastic."'' ChessBase: 'Quelle: Ftacnik in 'Mega 2000' Timman in New in Chess' 8/1992'} Kd3 42. Kd7 Ke4 43. e8=Q+ Bxe8+ 44. Kxe8 Kf4 45. Kf7 Kg5 46. Ke6 $18 {1-0 (46) Fischer,R (2785)-Spassky,B (2560) Belgrade 1992 100 Jahre Schach [ChessBase]} 1-0

