1. e4 {Ftacnik} c5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 e6 5. Nb5 d6 6. c4 Nf6 7. N5c3 (7. N1c3 {- 55/(209)}) 7... Be7 8. g3 $146 {Matanovic,A: 'N'} (8. Be2 {Ü 49/(219) Matanovic,A: '- 49/(219)' Ü 49/(219) Ü 49/(219) Ü 49/(219) Matanovic,A: '- 49/(219)'}) 8... O-O (8... b6 {Ftacnik} 9. Bg2 Bb7 10. O-O O-O 11. b3 a6 12. Ba3 Qb8 13. Nd2 b5 $1 14. Bb2 Ne5 15. Qe2 bxc4 16. Nxc4 Nxc4 17. Qxc4 Rc8 18. Qd4 Ne8 $10 {Bronstein-Osnos/URS/1980/}) 9. Bg2 a6 10. O-O Rb8 11. Na3 Qc7 12. Be3 Bd7 13. Rc1 Ne5 14. h3 Rfc8 15. f4 Ng6 (15... Nxc4 {Ftacnik} 16. Nxc4 Qxc4 17. Nd5 $1) 16. Qd2 $14 { Matanovic,A: ''    Matanovic,A: ''} Be8 17. Rfd1 b6 18. Qf2 h6 {MIKHALCHISHIN: 'Diagram '} 19. Kh2 $6 {MIKHALCHISHIN: 'useful move , but Whites' main problem in this position is to include into the game Knight on a3. At this moment it was possible to do ,while pawn c4 is poisoned'} (19. Nab1 $1 Bc6 (19... Qxc4 20. b3 $1 (20. Nd5 Qxa2 $13) (20. Bf1 Qb4 21. a3 Qb3 $13) 20... Qb4 (20... Qc7 21. Nd5) 21. Rd4 Qc5 (21... Qa5 22. f5 exf5 (22... Ne5 23. b4 $18) 23. exf5 Nf8 24. b4 Qe5 25. Re1 $18) 22. Rc4 Qh5 23. Bxb6 $16) 20. a4 Qb7 21. Nd2 a5 (21... Nd7 22. b4) 22. Re1 Nd7 23. Nb3 $16) 19... Qa7 20. Qe2 Qc7 21. Bf3 $6 ({MIKHALCHISHIN: 'it was time to start protecting own pawn.'} 21. Re1 $5) 21... Bc6 $1 {MIKHALCHISHIN: 'Diagram '} 22. Nab1 {MIKHALCHISHIN: '?!' '?!' '?!'} ({MIKHALCHISHIN: 'More active and better was'} 22. Nd5 {Ftacnik: '!'} Qb7 23. Nxe7+ Nxe7 24. Rxd6 Bxe4 25. Bxe4 Qxe4 26. Rd4 Qg6 27. Rd3 Ne4 28. Qg4 Qxg4 29. hxg4 b5 30. b3 {with very tense end.}) ({It was possible to start action on the Queens side} 22. b4) 22... Qb7 23. Nd2 b5 $17 24. cxb5 (24. a3 {was another typical option of fighting against b7-b5.}) 24... axb5 25. b4 Qa8 (25... Ra8 {Ftacnik} 26. Qd3 d5 $1 $132) 26. Rc2 {MIKHALCHISHIN: 'Diagram '} d5 ({MIKHALCHISHIN: 'More direct attack on the Queens side was preferable'} 26... Qa3 $1 {MIKHALCHISHIN: '!?' '!?' '!?'} 27. Rb1 (27. Rdc1 Bf8 28. Ncb1 Qa8 29. Nc3 Qa3 30. Ncb1 {with repetition.}) 27... Bxe4 $1 28. Ndxe4 (28. Bxe4 Rxc3 29. Rxc3 Qxc3 $17) 28... Nxe4 $17) 27. e5 Ne4 $1 ({MIKHALCHISHIN: 'Of course active approach-Russians never go back!'} 27... Nd7 28. Rb1 Nb6 {Ftacnik: ''} 29. Bd4 $13 (29. Bxb6 Rxb6 30. Qe3 Qb8 31. Ne2 {with mutual chances.})) 28. Bxe4 dxe4 29. Bc5 $8 ({Maybe better strategy would be attack of the e4 pawn.} 29. Rb1 Bd5 30. Bf2) 29... Bxc5 30. bxc5 Rd8 $1 31. Re1 {MIKHALCHISHIN: 'Diagram '} Ne7 $1 {MIKHALCHISHIN: '!?' '!?' '!?'} ({Similar idea could be conducted differently} 31... e3 $5 32. Qxe3 Ne7 33. Qf2 Nf5 34. Nce4 Nd4 35. Rb2 Qa3 {with initiative.}) 32. Ncxe4 Nf5 33. Nb3 Nd4 34. Nxd4 Rxd4 35. Nd6 Qa4 (35... Qa3 $5) ({Two other options were more direct} 35... Ra4) 36. f5 $8 (36. Rb2 {Ftacnik} Rxf4 $1 37. gxf4 Qxf4+ 38. Kg1 Qg3+ 39. Kf1 Qxh3+ 40. Kf2 Qh2+ 41. Ke3 $2 Qxe5+ 42. Kd3 Qd5+) 36... Ra8 $2 ({MIKHALCHISHIN: 'Better was'} 36... Rd5 $1 37. Rb2 (37. Rd2 Ra8 38. Rb2 exf5 39. Nxf5 Rxc5 {with very tense position.}) 37... Qd4 $1 $17) (36... exf5 {Ftacnik} 37. e6 $1 $40) 37. Rb2 $1 (37. f6 {was very unpleasant for Black.}) 37... Qa3 (37... Rb4 {was much better chance,eliminating the defence of pawn a2.}) 38. fxe6 fxe6 39. Nxb5 Bxb5 40. Qxb5 Rd3 41. Rg2 $14 {MIKHALCHISHIN: 'Diagram  White protected everything and their free pawns are ready to run.'} (41. Ree2 {Ftacnik} Rxg3 42. Rb3 Rxb3 43. Qxb3 Qa6 44. Rc2 $16) 41... Qc3 (41... Rc3 {Ftacnik} 42. Qd7 Ra6 43. Rf1 Qxc5 44. Qe8+ Kh7 45. Rf8 $18) 42. Ree2 (42. Re4 {was more powerful - young Bobby would play it!}) 42... Ra3 43. Rc2 Qxe5 44. Rce2 (44. Rb2 Kh7 45. Rbe2 Qd5 46. Qb4 Rac3 47. Qe4+ Qxe4 48. Rxe4 Rxc5 49. Rxe6 Ra5 {was close to draw.}) 44... Re3 (44... Qc3 {Ftacnik} 45. Rxe6 Rxg3 $2 46. Qb8+ Kh7 47. Qxg3 $18) 45. Rxe3 Rxe3 46. a4 Rc3 47. c6 $1 {MIKHALCHISHIN: 'Fischer decides to sacrifice its c pawn and starts to prepare run of another,more dangerous one.'} Qd6 (47... Rc5 {Ftacnik} 48. c7 Rxc7 49. Qe8+ Kh7) 48. c7 Rxc7 (48... Qxc7 {Ftacnik} 49. Qe8+ Kh7 50. Qxe6 Ra3 51. Qe4+ Kh8 52. Qb4 $16) 49. Qb8+ Kh7 50. a5 h5 $1 51. h4 {MIKHALCHISHIN: 'Diagram '} Qc5 $2 ({MIKHALCHISHIN: 'It was very difficult way to draw'} 51... Rc6 $1 52. Qxd6 (52. Qb1+ Kh6 53. Rc2 (53. Qe1 Rc4) 53... Rxc2+ 54. Qxc2 Qa3 $11) 52... Rxd6 53. Ra2 Ra6 54. Kg2 Kg6 55. Kf3 Kf5 56. Ra3 e5 57. Ra4 e4+ 58. Ke3 Kg4 59. Kxe4 Kxg3 60. Kd5 (60. Kf5 g6+ 61. Ke5 Kf3 62. Kd5 Kg3 63. Kc5 g5 64. hxg5 h4 65. g6 h3 {with draw.}) 60... g5 $11) 52. a6 Rf7 (52... Ra7 53. Qb1+ {Ftacnik: '!?'} (53. Ra2 {Ftacnik} Rxa6 54. Qb1+ $1 Kh6 55. Rxa6 $18) 53... Kh6 (53... g6 {Ftacnik} 54. Rb2 $1 Rxa6 55. Rb7+ Kh6 56. Qb2 $18) (53... Kg8 {Ftacnik} 54. Rc2 $1 Qf5 55. Rc8+ Kf7 56. Qxf5+ exf5 57. Rc6 $18) 54. Rc2 Qf5 55. Qc1+ Kh7 56. Ra2 {was stiil winning for White.}) (52... Qe7 {Ftacnik} 53. Ra2 Ra7 54. Qe5 g6 55. Rc2 Qf7 56. Kg2 Rd7 $16) 53. Qb1+ Kh6 (53... Kh8 {Ftacnik} 54. Qa2 Qb6 55. Re2 Re7 56. Rb2 Qa7 57. Qb1 $18) (53... Rf5 {Ftacnik} 54. Qb7 Rf2 55. a7 Rxg2+ 56. Kxg2 Qc2+ 57. Kf3 Qd3+ 58. Kf4 $18) 54. Qa2 Re7 55. Qd2+ $1 Kg6 56. Re2 $1 (56. Rf2 {was not bad.}) (56. Qc2+ $5 {Ftacnik} Qxc2 57. Rxc2 Ra7 58. Ra2 Kf5 59. Ra4 Ke5 60. Kg2 Kd5 61. Kf3 Kc5 62. Kf4 Kb5 63. Ra2 $18) 56... Kh7 (56... Qb5 {Ftacnik} 57. Qc2+ Kh6 58. a7 Qa5 59. Re5 Qxa7 60. Rg5 $18) (56... Kf7 $1 $16 {Ftacnik}) 57. Qc2+ $18 {MIKHALCHISHIN: 'transposition into winning Rook end.'} Qxc2 58. Rxc2 Kg6 59. Ra2 Ra7 60. Ra5 e5 61. Kg2 Kf6 (61... Kf5 {Ftacnik} 62. Kf2 {1-0 (67) Fischer,R (2785)-Spassky,B (2560) Belgrade 1992 CBM 31 [Ftacnik]} Ke4 {Ftacnik} (62... Kg4 {Ftacnik} 63. Kg2 $1 g6 {Ftacnik} 64. Rxe5 Rxa6 65. Rg5#) 63. Ke2 g6 64. Ra4+ Kd5 65. Ke3 Kc5 66. Ke4 $18) 62. Kf2 Ke6 63. Ke3 Kf5 64. Kf3 g6 65. Ra3 $1 g5 (65... Kf6 {Ftacnik} 66. Ke4 Ke6 67. Ra4 Kd6 68. Ra5 $1 $18) 66. hxg5 Kxg5 67. Ke4 {MIKHALCHISHIN: '1-0 '} Kg4 {Ftacnik} (67... Kf6 {Ftacnik} 68. Ra5 $18) 68. Kxe5 Rxa6 69. Rxa6 Kxg3 70. Rg6+ $18 1-0

