ws. Myers Marin Purdy Soltis: '='}) 33... Nf6 $2 {Myers Marin Purdy Soltis: '?!' Myers Marin Purdy Soltis: 'Marin: Under no circumstances should Tal have allowed the enemy king to infiltrate via f4.'} ({Tal misses another sacrifice, a temporary one -} 33... Kd7 $1 34. Rxd5+ (34. Bxg7 Kd6) 34... Ke6 35. Ra5 b6) (33... Rc5 $142 {Marin} 34. Bxg7 Kd7 35. g3 Ke6 36. Re1+ Kf7 37. Ba1 $11 {Myers}) (33... Nc3 $142 $1 {Myers} 34. Rd2 g6 35. Bd4 Ne4 36. Rb2 Rc4 $17 {Myers}) 34. Kf4 $1 g6 (34... Rc4+ {Myers Marin Purdy Soltis: '?!'} 35. Bd4 {with good winning chances} (35. Kxf5 $2 {Myers Marin Purdy Soltis: '!'} Rxh4 (35... Rc2 $1 36. Rf1 Ng4 37. Bxg7 $14 {Myers})) 35... Ra4 $1 $15) (34... Rc2 $6 35. Bd4 (35. Kxf5 Rxa2 $1 $17) (35. Bxf6 gxf6 36. Rf1 Rc5 $15) 35... Rxa2 36. Kxf5 b5 37. Kg6 $14 {Marin}) 35. f3 $1 Nd7 36. Bd6 Rc2 {Myers Marin Purdy Soltis: '?'} (36... b5 $5) (36... Nb6 $142 $5 37. Kg5 Nc4 38. Be7 Ne5 39. Bf6 Nd7 40. Bb2 b6 41. Bc1 Ne5 42. Kh6 $1 Re6 $15 {Myers}) 37. g3 {This is what White had in mind after 34.Kf4. Even though two pawns up, Black would lose following 37. ...Rxa2? 38.Kg5 or 38.Rc1+ first Myers Marin Purdy Soltis: '!'} Re2 (37... Rxa2 $2 38. Kg5 $1 {Purdy} (38. Re1 $2 b5 $1 39. Rc1+ Kd8 40. Kg5 Re2 41. Bc7+ Ke7 42. Kxg6 Ne5+ 43. Kxh5 Nxf3 44. Kg6 Nd4 $132) 38... Rf2 (38... Re2 39. Kxg6 Ne5+ 40. Kxh5 Nxf3 41. Kg6 a5 42. h5 $16) 39. Rc1+ $1 Kd8 40. Bc7+ Ke8 41. Re1+ Kf7 42. Bd6 Nf8 43. Re7+ Kg8 44. Re8 $18 {Myers}) 38. Kg5 {Myers Marin Purdy Soltis: '!'} Re6 39. Bf4 {Myers Marin Purdy Soltis: '!'} Nf8 40. Rd6 $1 a5 $1 41. Kh6 $1 {Now Kg7 is a lethal threat e.g. 41. ...b5 42.Kg7 Rxd6 43.Bxd6 Ne6+ 44.Kxg6} ({the pawn ending is drawn after} 41. Rxe6 {Myers Marin Purdy Soltis: '?'} Nxe6+ 42. Kxg6 Nxf4+ 43. gxf4 b5 44. Kxf5 $8 (44. Kxh5 $4 b4 45. Kg5 a4 46. h5 b3 47. axb3 a3 $1 $19) 44... b4 45. Ke4 a4 46. Kd4 Kd7 47. Kc4 b3 48. axb3 axb3 49. Kxb3 Ke6 50. Kc3 Kf5 51. Kd3 Kxf4 52. Ke2 Kg3 53. Ke3 Kxh4 54. Kf4 Kh3 55. Kg5 $11 {Tal}) 41... Re2 (41... b5 42. K