 22... Rc2 23. g3 Qh6 24. Qd3 Rxa2 25. f4 (25. fxg4 Kg7 $1 26. Qf3 Qg6 27. Bd3 Ra4 $19) 25... Qg6) 23. gxf3 ({of course Agur: 'Andrew Soltis: 'of course''} 23. Bxf3 {is desirable but after Black stops the nuisance checks with Agur: 'Andrew Soltis: 'is desirable but after Black stops the nuisance checks with''} Kg7 {he can pick up a loose pawn with ...Rc5 Agur: ' 24... c5 -+' Agur: 'Andrew Soltis: 'he can pick up a loose pawn with ...Rc5''} 24. Qd7 Qe3+ 25. Kh1 Rc1 $19) 23... Kh8 $1 (23... Rc2 {is poor because of Agur: '?' '?' Agur: 'Andrew Soltis: 'is poor because of''} 24. Kh1 Rxe2 $4 {Agur: 'Andrew Soltis: '??''} (24... Kg7 25. Rg1+ Kh6 26. Qd1 $1) 25. Rg1+ {Agur: '+-' '+-'} Kh8) 24. Kh1 Ba6 $1 {Without this trick (25.Bxa6?? Qxf3+ and ...Rg8 mates) Black has a lot of work to do Agur: 'Andrew Soltis: 'Without this trick (25.Bxa6?? Qxf3+ and ...Rg8 mates) Black has a lot of work to do''} 25. Qf2 (25. Bxa6 $4 Qxf3+ 26. Kg1 Rg8#) 25... Bxe2 26. Qxe2 Qxe5 {Agur: '-+'} 27. Rg1 f5 $1 {To win, Black (a) eliminates threats to his king by controlling the a1-h8 diagonal, (b) ties White's queen to e4, and that frees him to (c) create a passed queenside pawn. Agur: 'Andrew Soltis: '!'' Agur: 'Andrew Soltis: 'To win, Black (a) eliminates threats to his king by controlling the a1-h8 diagonal, (b) ties White's queen to e4, and that frees him to (c) create a passed queenside pawn.''} 28. Qd3 fxe4 29. fxe4 Rf8 30. Qc2 Qf6 ({Part of Fischer lore is that he spent the previous night playing speed games for substantial stakes against a Midwestern expert, Norbert Leopoldi, and his caution Agur: 'Part of Fischer lore is that he spent the previous night playing speed games for substantial stakes against a Midwestern expert, Norbert Leopoldi, and his caution'} 30... b5 $1 {is a symptom of his tiredness. Agur: 'is a symptom of his tiredness.'}) 31. Rg2 Qd4 32. h3 Qa1+ 33. Rg1 Qe5 34. Qe2 ({White loses the pawn ending after Agur: 'White loses the pawn ending after'} 34. Rg2 Rf1+ 35. Rg1 Rx