1. d4 {Gligoric: In preparation for his 1992 match with Spassky], Bobby asked if I could play a training match with him.  At first I didn't want to, but I had to give in to his wishes. He was panicking about how theory had developed during his twenty-year absence from chess. That was why he came up with his own version of chess, where the starting position would be determined by the drawing of lots. And he began to torment me with persistent requests to write a book about it.} Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 Bg7 4. e4 d6 5. Nf3 O-O 6. Be2 e5 7. O-O Na6 8. Be3 Ng4 9. Bg5 f6 10. Bc1 (10. Bh4 Nh6 (10... Qe8 11. Qc2 (11. a3 h5 12. h3 Nh6 13. dxe5 dxe5 14. b4 c6 15. c5 Be6 16. Nd2 Rd8 17. Qc1 Qf7) 11... h5 12. h3 Nh6 13. Rfd1 Kh8 14. a3 Be6 15. b4 g5 16. Bg3 Rd8 17. d5 Bc8 18. Nb5 Bd7 19. Rab1 Qg6) (10... g5 11. Bg3 Nh6 12. dxe5 fxe5 13. Ne1 Nc5 14. Nc2 Ne6 15. Ne3 Nd4 16. h3 Kh8 17. Bg4 Ng8) 11. a3 (11. dxe5 dxe5) 11... g5 (11... c6 12. d5 c5 13. Nd2 Qd7 (13... Nf7 14. Bg4) 14. Rb1 f5 15. f3 Nf7 16. b4 b6 (16... Bh6 17. Bf2) 17. Bd3) 12. Bg3 f5 (12... g4 13. Nh4 exd4 14. Qxd4 f5 15. Qd5+ Kh8 16. Nxf5 Nxf5 17. exf5 Rxf5 18. Qd2) 13. exf5 g4 14. Ne1 exd4 15. Nb5 Qf6 16. Bxg4 Nxg4 17. Qxg4 Bxf5) 10... c6 (10... Kh8 11. h3 Nh6 12. dxe5 fxe5 13. Be3 Nf7 14. Qd2 Nc5 15. Ng5 Nxg5 16. Bxg5 Bf6 17. Be3) (10... Qe8 11. c5 (11. h3 Nh6 12. dxe5 dxe5 13. b3 Be6 {[%cal Gg2g4]} 14. Ba3 Rf7 $5 15. Qc2 {[%cal Gf4f7,Gg2g4]} Bf8 16. Bxf8 Qxf8 17. a3 Rd7 {[%cal Gf5d6]}) 11... exd4 (11... dxc5 12. Bxa6 bxa6 13. h3 $6 Nh6 (13... exd4 14. Nd5 Ne5 15. Nxc7) 14. dxe5) 12. Nxd4 dxc5 (12... Nxc5 13. Bxg4) 13. Nb3 Qe6 (13... Ne5 14. Bxa6 bxa6 15. Nxc5) 14. Nd5 c6 15. Nf4 Qd7 $15 16. Bxa6 bxa6 17. Qxd7 Bxd7 $44 18. Nxc5) (10... Nh6 11. Rb1 (11. a3 Qe8 12. b4 c6 13. h3 Nf7 14. d5 c5 15. Rb1 f5 16. Ne1 Qe7 17. Nd3 Qh4 18. Bf3 b6 19. Kh2 Ng5 20. Bxg5 Qxg5 21. bxc5 Nxc5 {Danielian,O-Brenjo,S (2320)/Leningrad 1991/CBM 023 ext/½-½ (50)} 22. Nxc5 bxc5 23. Qe2 {1-0 Gurevich,M (2630)-Ivanchuk,V (2625) Reggio Emilia-A 8889 31st 1988} Bh6) 11... Nf7 (11... exd4 $40 12. Nxd4 $2 Nc5 (12... f5 13. Bxh6 Bxh6 14. exf5) 13. b4 Ne6) (11... Qe8) (11... c6) 12. dxe5 (12. b4 exd4 13. Nxd4 Nxb4 14. Rxb4 c5) 12... dxe5 13. b4 c6 14. b5 Nc7 (14... Qxd1 15. Bxd1 cxb5 16. cxb5 Nc7 17. Bb3 Be6 18. Be3) 15. Ba3 Re8 16. bxc6 bxc6 17. Qa4 $13 Bd7 $5 18. Rfd1) 11. h3 (11. Rb1) 11... Nh6 {[%csl Rb4]} 12. Rb1 $146 (12. Be3 Nf7 13. dxe5 dxe5 14. c5 Nc7 15. Bc4 Be6 16. Nd2 (16. Qe2 Qe7 17. b4 Bh6 18. Bxh6 Nxh6 19. Nd2 Nf7 20. Nb3 $1 Rfd8 21. Rfd1) 16... Qe7 17. Qb3 {[%csl Rg2]} Rfb8 18. Bxe6 Nxe6 19. Qc4 (19. Nc4 Nxc5 20. Qa3 Bf8) 19... Bh6 20. Bxh6 Nxh6 21. Nb3 {Menace de gagner une seconde qualité mais les Noirs vont trouver des ressources tactiques} Nf7 $132 22. Rad1 Rd8 23. g3) 12... Nf7 13. dxe5 (13. b4 exd4 14. Nxd4 Nxb4 15. Rxb4 c5) 13... dxe5 14. b4 $5 {Les Blancs auront des compensations pour le  sacrifié} Qxd1 (14... Qe7) 15. Rxd1 Be6 16. c5 (16. b5 cxb5 17. cxb5 Nc5 18. Ba3 {[%csl Ge6][%cal Gh3g5,Gg5e6]} Rfc8) (16. Be3 $1 {[%csl Rf6,Rf7][%cal Gg2g4,Gh3f2]}) 16... Rfd8 17. Rxd8+ $1 $44 {[%csl Gb2,Rg7,Rg8]} Rxd8 18. a3 Bh6 1/2-1/2

