1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e5 3. dxe5 Ng4 4. Bf4 Nc6 5. Nf3 Bb4+ 6. Nbd2 (6. Nc3 Bxc3+ {Black is completely tied up.} 7. bxc3 Qe7 8. Qd5 f6 $1 9. exf6 Nxf6 10. Qd3 d6 11. e3 O-O 12. Be2 Ne4) 6... Qe7 7. e3 Ngxe5 8. Nxe5 Nxe5 9. Be2 b6 (9... O-O 10. O-O d6 11. Nb3) 10. O-O Bb7 (10... Bxd2 11. Qxd2 Bb7 12. Rac1 d6 13. b4 O-O 14. c5 dxc5 15. bxc5 Rad8 16. Qc3) 11. Nf3 (11. Nb3 O-O 12. a3 $18 {The point of 16.h5. 1-0 Kolpakov,M-Nikitin,A/Moscow 1963/EXT 99 (27)}) 11... Bxf3 (11... f6 12. Nxe5 fxe5 13. Bf3 exf4 14. Bxb7 fxe3 15. fxe3 (15. Bxa8 e2) 15... Rb8 (15... Qxe3+ $1) 16. Bf3 $19 {0-1 Rotstein,J-Sakharov,Y/Kiev 1963/EXT 2003 (35)}) 12. Bxf3 Rd8 $6 (12... Nxf3+ 13. Qxf3 O-O 14. Qb7) (12... c6 13. Be2 O-O $2 14. a3 Bd6 15. Qc2 Bc7 16. Rad1) 13. Be2 $1 Bd6 (13... O-O) 14. Qc2 h5 (14... O-O $138 15. Rad1 $1 Rfe8 (15... a5)) 15. Rad1 c6 (15... h4 16. Rd4 (16. h3 O-O) 16... h3) (15... g5) 16. Rd4 $2 {The wrong place for the queen.} Bc7 17. h4 g6 18. Bg5 f6 19. f4 fxg5 20. fxe5 Qg7 {White has not enough resources to harass the black king.} 21. Rf6 Bxe5 22. Rxg6 Qe7 23. Bxh5 Bh2+ 24. Kh1 0-1

