1. d4 {Marin,Mihail} Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 d5 4. Bg5 Ne4 5. Bh4 Nxc3 6. bxc3 dxc4 7. e3 Be6 8. Nf3 c5 9. Be2 Bg7 10. O-O O-O 11. Rb1 {Marin,Mihail: 'This anticipates Black's massive attack, but commits the knight a bit too soon.'} cxd4 (11... Bd5) 12. Nxd4 Bd5 {Marin,Mihail: '?!' Marin,Mihail: 'This justifies White's previous move.'} 13. Qc2 Qd7 14. Rfd1 (14. e4 Bc6 $132 {The position is quite interesting, but the relative lack of safety of the white king is a bit annoying.} {Only not} 15. Bxc4 $6 Bxd4 16. cxd4 $2 Qxd4 17. Rbd1 Qxe4 18. Qxe4 Bxe4 19. Rfe1 Bf5 20. Bxe7 Re8 21. f3 Nc6 22. Bf6 Rxe1+ 23. Rxe1 Be6 24. Bxe6 Re8 $13 {White surely has some compensation for the missing pawn, due to his advance in development and the weakness of the f5-square, but Black should be OK.} 25. Bxf7+ Kxf7) 14... Bxd4 15. cxd4 (15. Rxd4 Nc6 16. Rdd1 (16. Rd2 Qe6 17. Rxb7 Rfb8) 16... Qe6 $11 17. Rxb7 $1 Nd4 (17... Rfb8 18. Rc7 Be4 $16 19. Qa4 $1 {Marin,Mihail was called for, even though Black more or less wastes a tempo.}) 18. Rxd4 Bxb7 19. Bxc4 $44 {[%csl Rc2,Rf2,Rh2][%cal Gh1h2]} Qc6 20. Bd5 {Marin,Mihail} Qc7 21. Bg3 Qb6 22. Rb4 Bxd5 23. Rxb6 axb6 24. h4 Bxa2 25. Qe4 Rfe8 $16 {Spraggett,K (2580)-Zapata,A (2515) Cienfuegos 1997 (1-0, 46)} 26. h5 {Marin,Mihail}) 15... Qe6 16. Bf3 (16. Qc3 Nd7 17. f3 Nb6 18. Rb5 (18. e4 f5) (18. Rd2 Rfc8 19. e4 Bxe4 20. fxe4 Qxe4 21. Rxb6 axb6 $1 22. Be1 b5) (18. Re1 f5 19. Bd1 $2) 18... f5 19. Rdb1 Rac8 20. Bd1 Na8 21. Bc2 $6 Nc7 22. Ra5 a6 23. e4 fxe4 24. fxe4 b5 (24... Qg4 25. Qe1 Rf4 26. Bg3 Rxe4 27. Bxe4 Qxe4 28. Qxe4 Bxe4 29. Re1) 25. exd5) 16... Bxf3 17. gxf3 Nd7 18. Qe4 (18. Rxb7 Rfb8 19. Rdb1 Rxb7 20. Rxb7 Rc8) 18... b6 19. Rdc1 (19. Qxe6 fxe6 20. Bxe7 Rxf3 {[%cal Gd6d5]}) 19... Rac8 20. Rb4 {Marin,Mihail: ''} c3 21. Rb3 Nf6 22. Qxe6 fxe6 23. Bxf6 (23. Rbxc3 Rxc3 24. Rxc3 Nd5 25. Rc6 Rxf3 {[%csl Re6]} 26. Rxe6) (23. Bxf6 exf6 24. Rbxc3 Rxc3 25. Rxc3 Rf7 26. Rc6 Re7 27. f4 Kf7 28. Kg2 Rb7) 0-1

