1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Ba4 Nf6 5. O-O Be7 6. Re1 b5 7. Bb3 O-O 8. c3 d5 9. exd5 Nxd5 10. Nxe5 Nxe5 11. Rxe5 c6 12. Re1 Bd6 13. d4 Qh4 {With the bishop on b7, this regrouping is too slow and allows White to consolidate his space advantage.} 14. g3 Qh3 15. Qe2 Bd7 16. Qf1 Qf5 (16... Rae8 17. Qxh3 Rxe1+ 18. Qf1 Rfe8 19. Bd2 Rxf1+ { c5} 20. Kxf1 Nb6 21. Be3 Nd5 $36 {Murrey,J (2450)-Balashov,Y (2590)/Moskva (open) 1991 (0-1, 45)} 22. Bd2 $16 {Balashov} Nb6 23. Be3 $1 Nd5 24. a4 $44 {The weakness of the e4-square and of the whole white kingside offers Black excellent compensation for the sacrificed exchange.} Nxe3+ $5 {may be a try. In any case, the opening of the centre does not favour Black anymore:} 25. fxe3 Rxe3 26. axb5 axb5 27. Ra6 Bf8 28. Kf2 Re8 29. Nd2 c5 30. Nf3 c4 $36 31. Bd1) 17. Be3 (17. Nd2 Rae8 18. f3 Nf6 19. a4 c5 20. Rxe8 Rxe8 21. Ne4 Rxe4 22. fxe4 Qxe4 23. Bf4 Bc6 24. d5 c4 $16 {Balashov,Y (2570)-Nikolaevsky,Y (2490)/Leningrad 1971/URS-ch (1-0, 61)} 25. Bxd6 $5 {may be a worthy try to prepare d6-d5, but further practice is needed.} Qxd5 {White clearly needs an improvement over this standard continuation. Things do not look too good if White answers a developing move with a modest pawn advance.} 26. Bd1 $5 Qh1+ 27. Kf2 Qxh2+ 28. Ke1 Qxb2 29. Ra3 Ne4 30. Qf4 $1 {The main idea of the move 13...d7 is revealed. The connection of the rooks is possible at once.} Qg2 31. Be2 Qg1+) 17... Rae8 18. Nd2 Re7 19. a4 $14 {A dream position for Fischer. Black has absolutely no counterplay and has to wait for the execution.} (19. Qg2 {[%cal Gd2f3]} Rfe8 20. Qf3 $36 Qg6 21. Bxd5 $1 $44 cxd5 22. a4 bxa4 23. Qxd5 h6 24. Nf3 Qf6 25. Ne5 Bxe5 26. dxe5 Qg6 27. Qd6 Qf5 28. Bd4 Bc8 $14 {Despite simplifications, Black cannot easily neutralise White's pressure.} 29. Re3 Bb7 30. e6 Rxe6 31. Rxe6 Qxe6 32. Qxe6 Rxe6 33. Be3 Rd6) 19... Rfe8 20. axb5 axb5 21. Qg2 h5 22. Nf3 Be6 23. Nh4 Qf6 (23... Qh7 {would have required from White the taking of some risks in order to maintain the initiative.} 24. Bd2 Qd3 25. Bg5 f6 26. Rad1 Qh7 27. Bd2 g5 28. Nf3 Qg6) 24. Bd2 Nf4 25. Rxe6 Rxe6 (25... Nxg2 26. Rxf6 Nxh4 27. Rxd6) (25... Nxe6 $6 {This gives up the exchange for nothing.} 26. Qxc6) (25... fxe6 26. Qxc6 $14 {Spassky,B-Medina Garcia,A/Palma de Mallorca 1969/MCD (1-0, 30)}) 26. gxf4 Qxh4 27. Bxe6 Rxe6 28. f5 Re4 29. h3 Bf4 30. Re1 (30. Qxe4 $6 {has been tried a couple of times, but is unsound.} Bh2+) 30... Rxe1+ 31. Bxe1 Kh7 (31... Bc1 32. b3 (32. Qxc6 Qg5+ 33. Kf1 Qxf5) 32... Qf4 33. Qxc6 Qg5+ 34. Kf1 Qxf5) 32. Kf1 (32. b3) 32... Bc1 33. b3 Qf4 34. Qxc6 Qxf5 35. Kg2 Qg5+ 36. Kf1 Qf5 37. Kg2 Qg5+ 38. Kf1 1-0

