1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 d6 3. Nc3 Nbd7 4. e4 (4. Nf3 e5 5. Bg5 Be7 $17 {0-1 Opl,K (2270)-Stohl,I (2550)/Austria 1991/EXT 1997 (39)} 6. e3 O-O 7. Qc2 c6 8. Bd3 h6 9. Bh4 Re8 10. O-O-O (10. O-O)) 4... e5 5. Nf3 Be7 6. Be2 O-O 7. O-O c6 8. Re1 (8. Qc2) (8. Be3) 8... a6 9. Bf1 Qc7 (9... b5 $16 {White's queen and knight are worth more than Black's uncoordinated forces.} 10. a3 Bb7 $1 11. h3 Re8 12. Be3 (12. Bg5 h6 13. Bh4 Qb8 14. Bg3 Bf8) 12... exd4 13. Nxd4 Bf8 {- see 19...xf7.} 14. Nf5 $2 Ne5 $1 15. cxb5 cxb5 16. Bg5 h6) 10. h3 (10. a3) (10. Bg5) 10... Re8 (10... b5 {- see 19...xf7.} 11. a3) 11. a3 b5 12. Be3 (12. Bg5 Bb7 13. Rc1) 12... Bb7 13. Rc1 Qb8 14. b4 exd4 (14... Bf8) 15. Nxd4 $2 {This sacrifice does not work in this case.} Bf8 16. Nf5 Ne5 (16... Nxe4 17. Nh6+ gxh6 18. Qg4+ Ng5 $1 19. Qxd7) 17. Bg5 Nfd7 (17... Nxc4 $1 18. Bxc4 (18. Bxf6 $6 gxf6 $1 19. Bxc4 bxc4 $1 {[%cal Gd2d8]}) 18... bxc4 19. Bxf6 gxf6 20. Re3 (20. Qg4+ $18)) (17... bxc4) 18. c5 (18. cxb5 axb5 $18 19. a4) 18... dxc5 19. f4 cxb4 {Without this check Black would simply resign. The queen now protects f8.} (19... h6) 20. fxe5 Nxe5 $1 {The only defence, but sufficient. White's attack evaporates.} 21. axb4 Bxb4 22. Qb3 a5 23. Red1 $2 Bc8 24. Ne2 Nc4 (24... Be6) 25. Ned4 h6 $18 {½-½ Pujol Sans,M-Natalucci,F/Groningen 1971/EXT 2001 (69)} 26. Rxc4 $5 {This one is sufficient only for equality. This position was a matter of discussion in the mid 60's.} (26. Bh4 Rxe4 27. Bg3) 26... bxc4 $1 27. Bxc4 Ra7 (27... Qb7 28. Bxh6 Bxf5 (28... gxh6 29. Qg3+) 29. Qg3 $18 {1-0 Byrne,R-Evans,L/New York 1965/MCL (36)} Bf8 30. Bxg7) (27... Rxe4 28. Nxh6+ gxh6 29. Bxf7+ Kg7 30. Bg6 $2 Rf4 $16 {1-0 Mazzoni,G-Bobotsov,M/Le Havre 1966/EXT 1998 (80)}) (27... Bxf5 28. Bxf7+ Kh8 29. exf5) 28. Nxc6 Bc5+ 29. Be3 Qxb3 30. Bxb3 Bxf5 (30... Bxe3+) 31. Bxc5 Rb7 32. Ne7+ (32. Nxa5) 32... Rexe7 33. Bxe7 (33. exf5 Rec7 (33... Rxb3 34. Bxe7) 34. Bd6 Rd7 35. Ba4) 33... Bxe4 34. Rd8+ Kh7 35. Bxf7 {½-½ Hartston,W-Mecking,H/Hastings 1966/MCL} Rx