{[%evp 0,128,21,21,21,25,21,-2,35,0,29,-9,11,11,27,23,23,36,59,14,27,22,27,22,37,-23,7,7,26,39,63,45,99,78,66,28,72,62,78,43,43,43,23,23,18,45,118,30,107,100,83,83,97,84,110,80,132,115,115,115,157,169,166,171,171,134,150,160,160,89,95,57,51,51,46,46,40,31,47,-36,-23,-71,-60,-46,17,-11,0,0,0,0,0,-71,-48,-74,-75,-93,-94,-94,-94,-100,-92,-104,-108,-121,-121,-121,-104,-104,-105,-219,-219,-219,-219,-252,-259,-306,-276,-328,-306,-437,-394,-472,-444,-444,-380,-472,-380,-837,-454,-1125,-2079]} {Time control was forty moves in two hours.} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Ba4 d6 5. c3 Bd7 6. O-O g6 ({Black decides to fianchetto his Bishop. The alternative is} 6... Nf6 7. Re1 Be7 8. d4 $16) 7. d4 Bg7 8. Bg5 ({Slightly preferable is} 8. Re1) 8... f6 (8... Nf6 {is slightly preferable.}) 9. Bh4 $6 ({Bishop on h4-d8 diagonal is not best placed. Better was} 9. Be3 $14 {From the e3 square Bishop controls both wings.}) 9... Nh6 ({After} 9... h5 $1 {we can see that the Bishop is not well placed on h4. The position is unclear:} 10. Bg3 g5 11. h4 g4 12. Ne1 Nge7 $13) 10. Nbd2 (10. Na3 $5) 10... Nf7 ({After a better} 10... g5 11. Bg3 O-O {the position is unclear.}) 11. Re1 O-O (11... g5 $5 12. Bg3 h5 $13) 12. Nf1 Qe8 ({Threatenning xd4. The alternative is} 12... Kh8) 13. Bb3 Kh8 14. Ne3 $14 g5 $6 ({Dubious move. Preferable was} 14... Ne7 $14) 15. Bg3 Ne7 16. h4 (16. a4 $16) 16... g4 17. Nh2 h5 18. f3 $6 ({Unnecessary move which only helps Black. Preferable was a typical} 18. Nd5 Nxd5 19. Bxd5 $14) 18... Nh6 19. fxg4 hxg4 $13 20. Nhxg4 Nxg4 21. Nxg4 Qg6 22. Ne3 (22. Nh2 $13 {is an alternative.}) 22... Bh6 ({Of course,} 22... Qxe4 {would be bad because of} 23. Bc2 {with next h5.}) 23. Bf2 (23. Kh2 {is an alternative:} Bxe3 24. Rxe3 f5 25. exf5 Nxf5 $13) 23... Rad8 $6 ({Stronger was} 23... Bc6 24. Bc2 Rg8 25. Qf3 Raf8 $13) 24. Bc2 (24. Qf3 {Was more sensitive:} Qh7 25. Bc2 $14) 24... Rg8 25. Qf3 Bf4 $13 26. Kh1 Rg7 $2 ({Preferable was} 26... Bxe3 27. Bxe3 Rdf8 $13) 27. g3 $2 ({White misses a very strong move} 27. Rg1 $1 {[%csl Yg3][%cal Yg2g3] after which he keeps a slight edge:} Rf8 28. dxe5 dxe5 29. Rad1 $14) 27... Bh6 $2 ({The position is extremely complex and it is hard to find strong moves. Better was} 27... Bxe3 28. Rxe3 Bg4 29. Qg2 {and after a nice} Nd5 {the position is completely unclear.}) 28. Nf5 $1 $16 Nxf5 29. exf5 Qe8 $2 (29... Qh7 30. Be4 $16) 30. Be4 $18 {White is wining. He is a pawn up and his e4 dominates.} b6 31. dxe5 ({The alternative is} 31. Rad1) 31... dxe5 32. g4 ({I am sure that in his prime age Fischer would play} 32. Rad1 {without thinking.}) 32... Rh7 33. Rad1 Qe7 34. Bc6 $2 ({Fischer loses a huge part of his adantage. Better was} 34. Bg3 $18) 34... Bxc6 35. Rxd8+ $2 ({Another wrong exchange. After a better} 35. Qxc6 {White has a clear edge.}) 35... Qxd8 36. Qxc6 Bg5 $1 $11 37. h5 Rd7 38. Qe4 Rd2 39. Be3 Bxe3 40. Qxe3 Qd5+ 41. Qe4 Qxa2 {Although the position is even White has to fight for draw.} (41... Qxe4+ {also leads to an even play:} 42. Rxe4 Rxb2 43. Kg1 (43. g5 $5) 43... Rxa2 44. g5 fxg5 45. Rxe5 Ra1+ 46. Kg2 Ra5 47. Re7 Rxf5 48. Rxc7 a5 49. Ra7 Rc5 50. Kg3 Rxc3+ 51. Kg4 Rc4+ 52. Kxg5 $11) 42. Qc6 Qd5+ {Objectively, Rook endgame is even.} 43. Qxd5 Rxd5 44. Kg2 Kg7 45. g5 $6 ({Unnecessary idea. Easier was} 45. Kf3 Kh6 46. Rh1 $11) 45... fxg5 46. Kf3 Kf6 47. Ke4 Rd7 48. Rh1 a5 49. h6 Rh7 50. c4 g4 51. Rg1 $2 ({Clear mistake which loses the game. After} 51. Rh5 {preventing g5, the position is even.}) 51... Kg5 52. Rf1 ({More resilient is} 52. Rd1 {although it loses after} Rxh6 {Possible line is:} 53. Rd7 Rh2 54. Rg7+ Kf6 55. Rg6+ Kf7 56. Kxe5 Rxb2 57. Rxg4 a4 58. Rg3 Rb3 59. Rg1 a3 60. Ra1 Rd3 61. Ke4 Rc3 62. Kd4 Rh3 63. Kd5 Kf6 64. Kc6 Rc3 65. Kxc7 b5 66. Kc6 b4 67. Kc5 Rc1 68. Rxc1 b3 69. Rb1 a2 70. Rxb3 a1=Q $19) 52... Rxh6 53. Kxe5 Rf6 54. Rf4 Rf8 55. Rf1 Re8+ 56. Kd5 Kf6 57. Kc6 Re7 58. Kd5 Re5+ 59. Kc6 Rc5+ 60. Kd7 Rxc4 61. Rf2 Rc5 62. Rf4 Kg5 63. b4 axb4 64. f6 Kxf4 0-1

