{[%evp 0,20,17,24,23,13,22,-4,26,10,2,-19,-20,-10,-8,-13,-12,-10,-10,15,16,21,13]} 1. e4 c5 2. b3 {White tries to avoid theory. The game move leads to an even play.} Nc6 3. Bb2 e5 ({Limiting the scope of b2. The alternative is} 3... d6) 4. Nf3 (4. Bc4 {is a good alternative.}) 4... d6 5. Nc3 (5. Bc4 $5) 5... f5 $5 ({Even being young, Fischer played sharp chess. More positional is} 5... Nf6) 6. d3 $6 ({Too cautious. Better was} 6. Bc4 $11) 6... f4 (6... Nf6 {was preferable. Fischer gains space, which is interesting.}) 7. h4 $6 ({This move only weakens White's position. Better was} 7. Nd5 $11) 7... Bg4 8. Be2 Nf6 9. Nd5 Be7 10. Nxe7 $2 ({Unnecessary exchange. After a better} 10. c3 {the position is even.}) 10... Qxe7 $17 11. Nd4 $2 ({Loses a pawn. Better was} 11. Rc1 $17) 11... Nxd4 12. Bxg4 Nxc2+ $1 13. Kf1 $2 (13. Qxc2 {is stronger, although after} Nxg4 {White is a pawn down.}) 13... Nxa1 $19 14. Bxa1 Nxg4 15. Qxg4 O-O 16. Bc3 b5 17. Qe2 a5 18. f3 b4 0-1

