1. d4 {Prusikin,Michael Prusikin,Michael Prusikin,Michael: 'Gligoric,Svetozar'} Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. Nf3 c5 5. e3 Nc6 {Prusikin,Michael: '!' '!' Prusikin,Michael: 'The exact move order. If Black is aiming for the so-called Huebner Variation I think it is advisable for him to postpone castling.' Prusikin,Michael: 'The exact move order. If Black is aiming for the so-called Huebner Variation I think it is advisable for him to postpone castling. The exact move order. If Black is aiming for the so-called Huebner Variation I think it is advisable for him to postpone castling.'} 6. Bd3 Bxc3+ 7. bxc3 d6 8. e4 e5 9. d5 Ne7 10. Nh4 {Prusikin,Michael: '!?' '!?' Prusikin,Michael: 'The main line.'} (10. O-O {(Prusikin,Michael) The most natural move, but on the other hand it is imprecise: Prusikin,Michael: 'The most natural move, but on the other hand it is imprecise: The most natural move, but on the other hand it is imprecise:'} h6 $1 11. Ne1 $5 (11. Nh4 $6 g5 12. Nf5 Nxf5 13. exf5 e4 $1 14. Re1 Bxf5 15. f3 O-O 16. fxe4 Bg4 17. Qc2 Nd7 $17 {L'Ami,Alina 2359 - Benderac,Ana 2299, Calvia (ol) 2004 Prusikin,Michael: 'L'Ami,Alina 2359 - Benderac,Ana 2299, Calvia (ol) 2004 L'Ami,Alina 2359 - Benderac,Ana 2299, Calvia (ol) 2004'}) 11... g5 12. g3 Bh3 13. Ng2 Qd7 14. f3 O-O-O $15 {Kozma,Julius - Huebner,Robert, CSSR - BR Deutschland (m) 1969}) (10. Nd2 $5 {(Prusikin,Michael) is an interesting alternative:} Ng6 11. h4 $5 (11. g3 Bh3) (11. h3 $5 {A new move.}) 11... Bd7 (11... Nf4 12. Bf1) 12. g3 $14 {Li, Chao B 2744 - Rapport,Richard 2675, Tbilisi (m/1) 2017 Prusikin,Michael: 'Li, Chao B 2744 - Rapport,Richard 2675, Tbilisi (m/1) 2017 Li, Chao B 2744 - Rapport,Richard 2675, Tbilisi (m/1) 2017'}) 10... h6 $1 {Prusikin,Michael: 'Gligoric,Svetozar: '!''} (10... Ng6 11. Nf5 $1 {Prusikin,Michael: 'might be a little bit better for White.' Prusikin,Michael: 'might be a little bit better for White. might be a little bit better for White. Gligoric,Svetozar: '!''}) 11. f4 $5 $146 {Prusikin,Michael: 'Spassky comes up with a novelty, but...' Prusikin,Michael: 'Spassky comes up with a novelty, but... Spassky comes up with a novelty, but...'} (11. f3 g5 {Prusikin,Michael} 12. Nf5 Nxf5 13. exf5 Qe7 $15 {Piorun,Kacper 2580 - Laznicka,Viktor 2673, Deizisau 2014 Prusikin,Michael: 'Piorun,Kacper 2580 - Laznicka,Viktor 2673, Deizisau 2014 Piorun,Kacper 2580 - Laznicka,Viktor 2673, Deizisau 2014'}) {Prusikin,Michael: 'Diagram [#] Fischer is even here well prepared and uncorks an amazing move:' Prusikin,Michael: 'Diagram [#] Fischer is even here well prepared and uncorks an amazing move: Diagram [#] Fischer is even here well prepared and uncorks an amazing move:'} 11... Ng6 $1 {Prusikin,Michael: '!!' '!!' Prusikin,Michael: 'A surprising, but incredibly powerful move. Due to the forced exchange of knights, White's initiative on the kingside is contained, the position remains closed, which reduces the value of White's pair of bishops. The resulting defects in Black's pawn structure, on the other hand, are irrelevant because White has no way to exploit them.' Prusikin,Michael: 'A surprising, but incredibly powerful move. Due to the forced exchange of knights, White's initiative on the kingside is contained, the position remains closed, which reduces the value of White's pair of bishops. The resulting defects in Black's pawn structure, on the other hand, are irrelevant because White has no way to exploit them. A surprising, but incredibly powerful move. Due to the forced exchange of knights, White's initiative on the kingside is contained, the position remains closed, which reduces the value of White's pair of bishops. The resulting defects in Black's pawn structure, on the other hand, are irrelevant because White has no way to exploit them. Gligoric,Svetozar: '!''} ({Prusikin,Michael: 'The variation'} 11... exf4 $5 {Prusikin,Michael: '?' '?' Prusikin,Michael: 'Gligoric,Svetozar: '!?''} 12. Bxf4 g5 13. e5 $1 {Prusikin,Michael: '+-!' '+-!' Prusikin,Michael: 'shows how