1. e4 e6 {Prepared in advance by Tal and Koblenz for this encounter despite Tal's indifferent success with the French Defense. They reasoned -- correctly -- that Fischer was not totally at ease with the Winawer.} 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. e5 c5 5. a3 Ba5 6. b4 cxd4 7. Qg4 Ne7 8. bxa5 dxc3 9. Qxg7 Rg8 10. Qxh7 Nbc6 {'!'} (10... Nd7 11. Nf3 Qc7 12. Bb5 a6 13. Bxd7+ Bxd7 14. O-O d4 $5 15. Nxd4 (15. Bg5 Bc6 16. Bxe7 Kxe7 17. Qh4+ Ke8 18. Ng5 Qxe5 19. f4 $14 {Euwe ECO 2.Auflage 16/17 Fußnote 80} Qf5 $17) 15... Qxe5 16. Qd3 $16 {Fischer / HÜbner} Qg7 (16... O-O-O 17. Qc4+ (17. Qxc3+ $2 Bc6 $19) (17. g3 Nd5 (17... Bb5 $2 18. Qxc3+ Nc6 19. Nxb5 $18) 18. Rb1 Qc7 $15) 17... Kb8 18. Bf4 Rxg2+ 19. Kh1 (19. Kxg2 Qxf4 $40 {-+  20... e5}) 19... Rxh2+ 20. Bxh2 Rh8 21. f4 (21. Nf3 Bc6 22. Qxc6 Rxh2+ $17) 21... Qe4+ 22. Rf3 Nf5 23. Qd3 (23. Qe2 $2 Ng3+ $19) 23... Qxd4 $19) (16... Rd8 17. Qe3 Qg7 (17... Qd5 18. f3 Ba4 19. Ne2 Nf5 20. Qxc3 (20. Qf2 Qc4 $17 21. Bf4 Bxc2 22. Rac1 Rd2) 20... Bb5 21. Nf4 Qd4+ 22. Qxd4 Nxd4 23. Rf2 Nb3 $19) 18. g3 e5 (18... Nd5 19. Qe4 $10) (18... Ba4 19. Ne2 Nd5 (19... Bxc2 20. Qxc3) 20. Qe4 Bb5 21. Re1 $10 (21. a4 $10)) 19. Nf3 $14) 17. g3 e5 18. Ne2 Bb5 19. Qf3 Qh7 20. Re1 Bc6 21. Qe3 O-O-O $17 22. Qxe5 $2 (22. Nxc3 $2 Nf5) 22... Qxh2+) 11. Nf3 (11. f4) 11... Qc7 (11... Qxa5 $1 12. Rb1 (12. Ng5 Rf8 13. f4 Bd7 14. Be2 {(Levy)}) 12... Qc7 13. Bf4 Bd7 14. Bg3 O-O-O {Damjanovic-Yudovich Yugoslavia 1963}) 12. Bb5 {'!' "Sharper and boosted by Fischer's advocacy but still not necessarily better than 12 B-KB4." (Wicker 79)} (12. Bf4 $1 {This move is recommended by Tal, although Fischer prefers 12 Bb5.}) 12... Bd7 {"Now both White's KNP, which Black seriously threatens to capture, and his KP are attacked. After lengthy reflection Fischer decided to give up his central pawn." (Tal 76)} (12... Rxg2 $2 13. Kf1 $1 Rg8 14. Rg1 $1 Rxg1+ 15. Kxg1 $16 {"... and Black's King remains hemmed in the center while White merely marches his KRP to victory." (Fischer 1969)}) 13. O-O (13. Bxc6 $6 Bxc6 14. O-O (14. Bf4 $6 Rg4 $2 (14... Bb5 $1 $17 {(Wicker 79)}) 15. Qh8+ Kd7 $2 (15... Rg8) 16. Qxa8 $18 {Selivanovsky-Zelevinsky Moscow 1958}) 14... d4 $1 15. Ng5 Qxe5 16. Qxf7+ Kd7 $17 {(Fischer 69)}) 13... O-O-O {Tal called this the "most critical moment of the game" and spent about 40 minutes in thought.} (13... Nxe5 {Petrosian,T} 14. Nxe5 Qxe5 15. Bxd7+ Kxd7 16. Qd3 $1 $16 {Fischer (eco 81)} Qe4 $2 {'!?' Fischer gives "16...Qe4?" and Hubner seems to agree. However, only Wicker extends the analysis beyond move 18.} (16... Rac8 17. Rb1 Kc7 (17... Rc7 18. Rb4 (18. Be3 Nc6 19. f4 Qd6 20. Bd4 Qxa3 21. Ra1 Qb4 22. Bxc3 Qc5+ 23. Rf2 a6 $10 {Balashov--Lputian/Uzgorod/1988/}) 18... Nc6 19. Rh4 Qg7 20. g3 {Horvath,Is-Luther,T/Szekszard op/1989/} Kc8 $10) 18. Rb5 {'!'} Kb8 19. Be3 $16 {Tal}) (16... d4 17. Rd1 $5 (17. Rb1 Qd5 18. f3 Rac8 19. Qe4 (19. Bf4 e5 20. Bg3 f6 $10 {Chandler-Vaganian/Naestved/1985/Inf. 40/367/}) 19... f5 (19... Kc6 20. Rb4 $16) 20. Rxb7+ Rc7 21. Rxc7+ Kxc7 22. Qxd5 Nxd5 23. Rd1 e5 24. f4 Kd6 {Schwarz sollte nicht verlieren.}) (17. Rb1) 17... Nf5 (17... Nc6 18. Qf3 Qd5 19. Qxd5+ exd5 20. Rb1 $16) (17... Qd5 18. Qxd4 Rxg2+ 19. Kf1 { 20.a4 +- Vaganian}) 18. Rb1 (18. Qf3 Qd5 19. Qxd5+ exd5 $10) 18... Qd5 19. f3 Rac8 (19... Nh4 20. Rb5 Rxg2+ 21. Kf1 Qd6 22. Be3 (22. Qxd4 $2 Rg1+) 22... e5 23. Qe4 $18) 20. Qe4 $16) (16... Nc6 $2 17. Rb1 Nxa5 (17... Kc7 18. Qf3 Qg7 19. Bf4+ e5 20. Bg3 d4 21. Rb5 f6 22. Rfb1 Rab8 23. Qd5 $16 { 24.b3, 24.f4} (23. Qd5 Rgd8 24. Qb3 Kc8 25. f4 {(Hubner 91)})) 18. Qb5+ Nc6 19. Qxb7+ Qc7 20. Bf4 $16 e5 $2 21. Bxe5 (21. Bxe5 Nxe5 22. Qxd5+ Kc8 23. Rb5)) (16... Rh8 17. h3 Rag8 18. Rb1 Kc8 19. Rb4 $14) (16... Kc7 17. Rb1 d4 18. Rb5 {(Wicker 79)}) 17. Qxe4 dxe4 18. f3 $1 {Mit Bauerngewinn Fischer} (18. f3 $1 {(Fischer 69)} exf3 19. Rxf3 f5 (19... Nf5 20. Rxc3 (20. Bf4 $142 {(Wicker 79)}) 20... Rac8 {(Wicker 79)}) 20. Bf4 (20. Rxc3 Rac8) 20... Nd5 21. Be5 Ke7 {"Black's position is quite satisfactory." (Wicker 79)}) (18. Rb1 b6 $1 19. axb6 axb6 20. Rxb6 Rgb8 {Niemand-Vesta corres 1962 "and Black stands quite well despite his pawns minus." (Wicker 79)})) 14. Bg5 {? Fischer '?!'} (14. Bxc6 $1 Bxc6 (14... Qxc6 15. Bg5 d4 16. h4 $1) (14... Nxc6 15. Re1 { g5, h2-h4 +-} (15. Re1 d4 16. Bg5 Rdf8 17. h4 $16 {(Wicker 79)})) 15. Qxf7 d4 (15... Rxg2+ $2 16. Kxg2 d4 17. Kg1 Rg8+ 18. Ng5 $18 {Fischer}) (15... Rdf8 16. Qxe6+ Bd7 17. Qxe7 Rxg2+ 18. Kh1 (18. Kxg2 Bh3+ 19. Kxh3 Qxe7 {In dieser Variante gewinnt Schwarz gegenüber der von Fischer ein Tempo.} 20. Kg2 Qh7 21. Ng5 Qxc2 $13 22. Be3 (22. e6 d4) 22... Qf5 { 23... d4, 23... e5} (22... Rg8 {Fleetwood-Crispin/corr/1987/0-1/})) 18... Rxf3 19. Bg5 (19. Be3 $6 d4 20. Bxd4 Qc6 { 21... h2}) 19... Rgxf2 (19... Rfxf2 $2 20. Qf8+) 20. Rxf2 Rxf2 21. Kg1 Rf5 22. Bf6 Kb8 23. Rd1 {/+-}) 16. Qxe6+ Bd7 (16... Kb8 17. Ng5 $18 {Fischer} Nd5 (17... Ba4 18. Qf6 (18. Nf7 Rg6 (18... Rdf8 19. Bh6 (19. Bg5 Rxf7) 19... Rg6 20. Qa2 Qc6 $17) 19. Nxd8 (19. Qa2 Bc6 20. Ng5 Bd5 21. Qb1 Qxe5 $19) (19. Qh3 Rdg8 20. g3 (20. Qd3 Rxg2+ 21. Kh1 Qc6 $19) 20... Bxc2 $19) 19... Rxe6 20. Nxe6 Qc4 $19 {Weiß verliert den Bauern c2.}) (18. Qh3 Bxc2 19. Ne6 Qd7 {Dies führt nicht zum gewünschten Ziel.}) (18. Ra2 $2 Bb5 { 19... c4-+}) 18... Rg6 (18... Nd5 $6 19. Qf5 {Weiß deckt c2 und konsolidiert sich.}) (18... Rgf8 19. Ne6 Rxf6 20. exf6 {/}) (18... Rdf8 19. Qd6 Qxd6 20. exd6 Nf5 21. Bf4 { 22.e6 }) (18... Bxc2 19. Ne6 Qc6 20. f3 (20. g3 Rd7 21. Nxd4 Rxd4 22. Qxe7 Qf3 23. Qf6 Bf5 24. e6 {Der weiße e-Bauer entwickelt bedrohliche Kraft.} (24. Re1 $2 Rf4 25. Bxf4 Bh3 $19)) 20... Rd7 21. Nxd4 Qc5 22. Be3 Rxd4 23. e6 (23. Rac1 $2 Rd2 $19) 23... Nf5 $17) 19. Qf7 Rdg8 (19... Bxc2 20. Ne6 (20. e6 Nd5) 20... Bb3 (20... Rxe6 21. Qxe6 Rg8 22. Qd6 $16 d3 23. Bf4 d2 24. e6) (20... Qc6 21. Nf4 Nd5 22. Nxg6 Bxg6 23. Qf3 d3 24. Rd1 $16 Qc4 25. Qg3) 21. Qxg6 Nxg6 22. Nxc7 Kxc7 23. Bg5 $16) 20. e6 Ka8 21. h4 (21. Bf4 Qd8 { 22... f8}) 21... Bxc2 $13) 18. Qh3 (18. f4 Qxa5 19. Rb1 Qc5 20. Rf2 {Mrdja-Dr.Reefschläger/Lugano op/1982/} d3 $40 {}) 18... Qxe5 (18... Rde8 19. Nf3 { × d4} (19. Qd3 $2 Qxe5 20. Nf3 Rxg2+)) 19. Nf7 $16) 17. Qxe7 Rxg2+ 18. Kxg2 Bh3+ 19. Kxh3 Qxe7 20. Bg5 $18 {Fischer}) 14... Nxe5 $1 {"Setting off a dazzling array of fireworks! I thought Tal was merely trying to confuse the issue." (Fischer 69)} 15. Nxe5 (15. Bxd7+ Rxd7 (15... Kxd7 {Tal} 16. Nxe5+ Qxe5 17. Bxe7 (17. f4 Qd4+ 18. Kh1 Rg7 19. Qh3 Rdg8) 17... Rh8 18. Rae1 Rxh7 19. Rxe5 Kxe7 $17) 16. Nxe5 (16. Bxe7 Nxf3+ 17. Kh1 Qxh2+ $1 (17... Qxh2+ $1 {(Fischer 69)} 18. Qxh2 Nxh2)) 16... Qxe5 17. Bxe7 Rh8 $1 18. Rae1 Rxh7 19. Rxe5 Rxe7 $17 {Fischer,Tal (Fischer 69, Tal 76)} 20. Rd1 (20. f4 f6 21. Re3 d4 22. Re4 e5 23. fxe5 fxe5 24. Rf5 Kd7 25. Rexe5 Rxe5 26. Rxe5 Kd6 { 27... d3} 27. Re4 Kd5 (27... Kc5 28. Re5+ Kc4 29. Re8 {Diese Variante ist nicht besser als die Hauptvariante für Schwarz.}) 28. Re8 Rh6 {/-+}) (20. Rfe1 Rh4 (20... Kd7 $2 21. R5e3 d4 22. Rd1 $16) (20... Rc7 21. f4 Kd7 22. f5 Rh6 $17) 21. Rxd5 exd5 22. Rxe7 Rd4 (22... Ra4 23. Kf1 Rxa3 24. Ke2) 23. Kf1 Kd8 24. Re3 Rd1+ 25. Re1 (25. Ke2 Rd2+ 26. Kf3 Rxc2 27. Rd3 Ke7 28. Rxd5 Ra2 $10) 25... Rd2 26. Re2 $10 (26. Rc1 {Ein Gewinnversuch}) (26. Rc1 {"attempting to win" (Hubner 91)})) 20... Rc7 (20... Rh4 21. Rdxd5 {Vgl. Variante 20.fe1 h4 21.d5}) 21. g3 (21. Rd3 Rh4) (21. f4 Rc4 22. g3 Ra4 $36) 21... Kd7 22. Rd3 Rh8 23. Ree3 Rhc8 24. h4 Kd6 25. f4 f6 26. Kg2 e5 27. fxe5+ fxe5 28. g4 $13) (15. Bxe7 $2 Nxf3+ 16. Kh1 Rh8 $19 {Fischer}) 15... Bxb5 {'=!' (eco 74/81)} (15... Qxe5 16. Bxe7 Rh8 (16... Bxb5 17. Bxd8 Rh8 18. Rae1 Qxe1 19. Rxe1 Rxh7 20. Bf6 {Tal}) 17. Rfe1 {'!'} (17. Rae1 Qb8 $19 {Fischer, Tal '!'} (17... Qxe1 $2 18. Bxd7+ Kxd7 19. Qxf7 $16) 18. Bxd7+ Kxd7 19. Bd6 {Schwarz darf nun den Bauern f7 nicht geben. "Now Black cannot give up the pawn on f7." (Hubner 91)} Rxh7 20. Bxb8 Rxb8 21. f4 Rc8 22. Rf3 $10) 17... Qxe1+ 18. Rxe1 Rxh7 19. Bxd8 Kxd8 (19... Bxb5 $2 20. Bf6 $1 {vgl. 16... b5}) 20. Bxd7 Kxd7 21. R