1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. e5 c5 5. a3 Bxc3+ 6. bxc3 Qc7 7. Nf3 Nc6 8. Be2 Bd7 9. O-O Nge7 10. a4 Na5 $6 (10... b6 11. Ba3 Na5) 11. Re1 cxd4 12. cxd4 Nc4 13. Bd3 $1 h6 (13... O-O $2 14. Bxh7+ Kxh7 15. Ng5+ Kg6 16. Qg4 {(Trifunovic 70)}) 14. Nd2 $1 $16 {(eco 81)} Nxd2 15. Bxd2 Nc6 16. Qg4 g6 17. Re3 O-O-O 18. Rg3 (18. Rf3 $1) 18... Kb8 $2 19. Rf3 $1 f5 $2 (19... Be8) 20. exf6 e5 {With this move Black seems to take the initiative. The white queen is under attack, Black threatens an eventual e5-e4, and White's d-pawn is endangered. On the contrary, Fischer has prepared a crushing counterstroke.} 21. Qg3 $1 Nxd4 (21... e4 22. Bf4 $18) 22. Re3 e4 23. Rxe4 $1 (23. Qxc7+ $2 {This is the variation Black was expecting when he played his 21st move.} Kxc7 24. Bf1 {(Florian 83)}) 23... Qxg3 24. Rxd4 $3 {"A quiet intermediate move, after which it becomes clear that in spite of her apparent freedom, the queen is doomed." (Florian 83)} Qg4 $6 (24... Qc7 25. Bf4 $18) (24... Qxd3 $5 {}) 25. Rxg4 Bxg4 26. Bxg6 {"White has radically changed the structure of the position with the temporary queen sacrifice and the subsequent sacrifice of the exchange. Black's menacing centre pawns have disappeared, and the f6 pawn has become a threat." (Florian)} Rhg8 27. Bh7 $1 Rh8 28. Bd3 Rde8 $2 (28... Rhf8 29. Bxh6 Rxf6 30. Bg5 $18 {(Trifunovic 70)}) (28... Bh5 $142) 29. f7 Re7 (29... Ref8 30. Bg6) 30. f8=Q+ $1 Rxf8 31. Bb4 Rff7 32. Bxe7 Rxe7 33. f3 Bd7 34. a5 $1 Kc7 35. Kf2 Rf7 36. Ke3 Kd6 37. g3 Kc5 38. f4 Bg4 39. Rb1 Re7+ 40. Kd2 b6 41. axb6 axb6 42. h3 $1 Bd7 (42... Bxh3 43. Rh1 Bd7 44. Rxh6 Rg7 45. Rg6 $18 {(Trifunovic 70)}) 43. g4 d4 44. f5 Re3 45. f6 Rf3 46. Rf1 Rxf1 47. Bxf1 Be6 1-0

