1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 dxe4 4. Nxe4 Nd7 5. Nf3 Ngf6 6. Nxf6+ Nxf6 7. Bd3 b6 8. O-O Bb7 9. Qe2 Be7 10. Rd1 O-O 11. c4 Qe8 ({Black wants to play ...c5, but needs to get his Queen off the d-file. Besides the text, another way to prepare ...c5 - though in fact it was never played - is} 11... Qc8 12. Bg5 h6 13. Bd2 Re8 14. b4 a5 15. b5 c6 16. bxc6 Qxc6 17. Rab1 Rab8 18. Bf4 Bd6 19. Bxd6 Qxd6 20. Ne5 Nd7 21. Qe3 $11 {Psakhis-Akopian, Halhidiki 1992}) 12. b3 c5 13. Bb2 Rd8 14. dxc5 Bxc5 15. a3 {GM Reshevsky used the plan of 15.Bxf6 gxf6 16.Be4 in an analogous position to try to steer for a better ending.} Qc6 16. b4 Bd6 17. Rac1 Rd7 $4 {Morris overlooks a tactic. Better was 17...Bf4 with complicated play.} 18. c5 $1 {Black has no good answer to the threats of 19.b5 and 19.Bb5.} Bb8 19. Bb5 $2 {Simply 19.b5, followed in most cases by 20.c6, wins material.} Rxd1+ 20. Rxd1 Qc7 21. cxb6 (21. c6 Bxc6 22. Rc1 Bxb5) 21... axb6 22. h3 (22. Ne5 {looks better.}) 22... Rd8 (22... Bxf3 23. Qxf3 Qh2+ 24. Kf1 Nd5 {threatens ...Nf4. White may be forced to meet this move with g3 pitching the h3 pawn, but seeking compensation in the Bishop pair, d-file and Black's off-side pieces.}) 23. Rxd8+ Qxd8 24. Bd3 Qd5 25. Bc4 Qf5 26. Qd3 Qxd3 27. Bxd3 Nd5 28. Bd4 Nf4 29. Bf1 {It might look illogical to surrender the Bishop pair when the opponent had a queenside majority, but 29...Bxf3 makes some sense as after 30.gxf3 the White King has a hard time becoming active.} Nxh3+ 30. gxh3 Bxf3 31. Bxb6 Bd6 {Morris stop Bobby from activating his majority with 32.a4.} 32. Bg2 Bxg2 {A difficult decision as 32...Bd1 makes it hard for White to activate his queenside pawns.} 33. Kxg2 Kf8 34. a4 ({White can go into a pawn endgame with} 34. Bc5 {but after} Bxc5 35. bxc5 Ke7 36. a4 Kd7 37. a5 Kc6 38. a6 g5 {it's hard for White to breakthrough. The best try might be 34.Kf3 bringing the King up the board to support the Queenside pawns with the Bishops on the board.}) 34... Bxb4 35. a5 Bxa5 36. Bxa5 f6 {The reduced material guarantees that sensible play will draw for Black.} 37. Kf3 Kf7 38. Ke4 Kg6 39. Bb4 Kf7 40. Kd4 Kg6 41. Bd6 Kf5 42. Bf8 g5 43. Be7 Kg6 44. Kc5 h5 45. Kd4 Kf5 46. Ke3 1/2-1/2

